 'Rounding up old cast members, a producer hopes to reverse the ill fortunes of the 1991 film “Shuttlecock” with added scenes and a new title, “Sins of a Father.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'Nearly 25 years ago, the producer Graham Leader made a film called “Shuttlecock.” Alan Bates had the starring role, as a British spy during World War II whose secrets inflict psychic damage on his son. The film opened the San Sebastián Film Festival in Spain in 1991 and was broadcast once on Channel 4 in Britain and on Canal Plus in France, where it had a brief theatrical release. It never found a distributor, however, and sank without a trace. ', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/01/arts/01SHUTTLECOCK1/01SHUTTLECOCK1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 403, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/02/01/arts/01SHUTTLECOCK1/01SHUTTLECOCK1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 403}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/01/arts/01SHUTTLECOCK1/01SHUTTLECOCK1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 688, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/01/arts/01SHUTTLECOCK1/01SHUTTLECOCK1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1375, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/01/arts/01SHUTTLECOCK1/01SHUTTLECOCK1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/02/01/arts/01SHUTTLECOCK1/01SHUTTLECOCK1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}