ives: Dr. King is arrested during protest after receiving Nobel Peace prize in 1965.', 'web_url': 'https://iht-retrospective.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/02/01/1965-dr-king-300-negroes-arrested-in-selma/', 'snippet': 'Highlights from the International Herald Tribune archives: Dr. King is arrested during protest after receiving Nobel Peace prize in 1965.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SELMA, Ala. — Civil-rights leader the Rev. Martin Luther King jr., was arrested today [Feb. 1] while attempting to lead a mass march of 300 Negroes on the Dallas county courthouse to protest voter-registration procedures. The Negroes, who were walking en masse from a church, were taken into custody on orders from Selma’s Public Safety Director Wilson Baker on charges of parading without a permit. Mr. Baker stopped the procession near the church, where the Negroes had assembled. He told them: ‘‘Each and every one of you is under arrest for parading without a permit.’’ After an hour of waiting in the jail, Dr. King was released without charges filed against him. But he was quickly rearrested when he did not obey an officer’s orders to leave the scene. This was the first time he has been arrested since he received the Nobel Peace prize last month. — New York Herald Tribune, European Edition, Feb. 2, 1965', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/01/blogs/01iht-old02-selma/01iht-old02-selma-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 437, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/02/01/blogs/01iht-old02-selma/01iht-old02-selma-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 437}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/01/blogs/01iht-old02-selma/01iht-old02-selma-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 582, 'width': 800, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/01/blogs/01iht-old02-selma/01iht-old02-selma-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 582, 'width': 800, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/01/blogs/01iht-old02-selma/01iht-old02-selma-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/02/01/blogs/01iht-old02-selma/01iht-old02-selma-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/01/blogs/01iht-old02-selma/01iht-old02-selma-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': '1965: Dr. King, 300 Negroes Arrested in Selma', 'kicker': 'IHT Retrospective', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Civil Rights Movement (1954-68)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'King, Martin Luther Jr', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'ALABAMA', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-02-01T15:50:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By International Herald Tribune', 'person': [{'firstname': 'International', 'middlename': 'Herald', 'lastname': 'Tribune', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/bcf3245c-f765-5a0c-97fe-a0ed9f7d61e1', 'word_count': 157, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bcf3245c-f765-5a0c-97fe-a0ed9f7d61e1'}, {'abstract': 'The central question posed by the 10-year budget is this: Should Washington worry about the rising gap between the rich and everyone else, or address a mountain of debt?', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/02/02/us/obama-budget-to-seek-to-stabilize-deficit-and-address-income-inequality.html', 'snippet': 'The central question posed by the 10-year budget is this: Should Washington worry about the rising gap between the rich and everyone else, or address a mountain of debt?', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — President Obama will propose a 10-year budget on Monday that stabilizes the federal deficit but does not seek balance, instead focusing on policies to address income inequality as he adds nearly $6 trillion to the debt.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/02/us/02BUDGET/02BUDGET-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 412, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/02/02/us/02BUDGET/02BUDGET-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 412}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/02/us/02BUDGET/02BUDGET-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 703, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/02/us/02BUDGET/02BUDGET-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1406, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/02/us/02BUDGET/02BUDGET-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/02/02/us/02BUDGET/02BUDGET-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'cred