osing is not only foolish, it can lead to permanent loss of teeth.', 'web_url': 'https://well.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/02/01/the-hazards-of-do-it-yourself-orthodonture/', 'snippet': 'Orthodontists warn that D.I.Y. teeth straightening or gap closing is not only foolish, it can lead to permanent loss of teeth.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Jamila Garza, 24, from Everett, Wash., has made no less than nine YouTube videos enthusiastically describing how she closed a gap between front teeth with $5 elastic bands. Ms. Garza is not a dental professional. Until recently, she was a fashion design student. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/02/science/02TEETH_COMBO/02TEETH_COMBO-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 280, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/02/02/science/02TEETH_COMBO/02TEETH_COMBO-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 280}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/02/science/02TEETH_COMBO/02TEETH_COMBO-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 479, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/02/science/02TEETH_COMBO/02TEETH_COMBO-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 957, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/02/science/02TEETH_COMBO/02TEETH_COMBO-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/02/02/science/02TEETH_COMBO/02TEETH_COMBO-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/02/science/02TEETH_COMBO/02TEETH_COMBO-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Do-It-Yourself Orthodonture: Don’t Try This at Home', 'kicker': 'Well', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Teeth and Dentistry', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-02-01T17:07:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Science', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': 'By Catherine Saint Louis', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Catherine', 'middlename': 'Saint', 'lastname': 'Louis', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/79cc4069-832e-5ea3-818c-28d5fc8dd7c6', 'word_count': 426, 'uri': 'nyt://article/79cc4069-832e-5ea3-818c-28d5fc8dd7c6'}, {'abstract': 'Some people who want to straighten their teeth for much less money are using a kit to make dental impressions and sending them back to companies that will provide their aligners. Critics say this process overlooks oral health issues.', 'web_url': 'https://well.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/02/01/a-trip-to-the-mail-box-not-the-orthodontist/', 'snippet': 'Some people who want to straighten their teeth for much less money are using a kit to make dental impressions and sending them back to companies that will provide their aligners. Critics say this process overlooks oral health issues.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When John Hofford, a 27-year-old digital media specialist, wanted to straighten his teeth, he wanted invisible plastic aligners that would correct his crowding, instead of conspicuous metal braces. But he couldn’t afford the clear aligners sold at his local orthodontist in Atlanta.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/31/science/02teeth2/02teeth2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/01/31/science/02teeth2/02teeth2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/31/science/02teeth2/02teeth2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/31/science/02teeth2/02teeth2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/31/science/02teeth2/02teeth2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/01/31/science/02teeth2/02teeth2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/31/science/02teeth2/02teeth2-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Straighter Teeth by Mail', 'kicker': 'Well', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Straighter Teeth, by Mail', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Teeth and Dentistry', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'CrystalBraces LLC', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'SmileCareClub Inc', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-02-01T17:08:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Science', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': 'By Catherine Saint Louis', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Catherine', 'middlename': 'Saint', 'lastname': 'Louis', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ce52d0a7-4d2d-5206-8751-eee1f6f86e94', 'word_count': 900, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ce52d0a7-4d2d-5206-8751-eee1f6f86e94'}, {'abstract': 'Everybody likes to talk about the weather, but meteorologists are expected to do it with unassailable certainty. Recent events show that is not always possible.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/02/02/nyregion/a-job-of-forecasts-unpredictable-by-nature.html', 'snippet': 'Everybody likes to talk about the weather, but meteorologists are expected to do it with unassailable certainty. Recent events show that is not always possible.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The meteorologist Steven DiMartino signed off Twitter at 11 p.m. last Monday, warning his followers that “intense heavy snow is approaching.” After 20 hours of blizzard-tracking for clients who pay him to predict how the weather will affect their travel, families and businesses, he finally took a nap in his chair.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/02/nyregion/02WORKING1/02WORKING1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 402, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/02/02/nyregion/02WORKING1/02WORKING1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 402}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/02/nyregion/02WORKING1/02WORKING1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 687, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/02/nyregion/02WORKING1/02WORKING1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1373, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/02/nyregion/02WORKING1/02WORKING1-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/02/02/nyregion/02WORKING1/02WORKING1-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/02/nyregion/02WORKING1/02WORKING1-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Job Filled With Forecasts That’s Unpredictable by Nature', 'kicker': 'The Working Life', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Job Filled With Forecasts That’s Unpredictable by Nature', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Swarns, Rachel L', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Weather', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AMERICAN METEOROLOGICAL SOCIETY', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Weather Service', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Snow and Snowstorms', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wysocki, Mark W', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York Metropolitan Area', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-02-01T17:42:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rachel L. Swarns', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rachel', 'middlename': 'L.', 'lastname': 'Swarns', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/05b049b5-ad70-5050-84b9-3daffb12ca4a', 'word_count': 821, 'uri': 'nyt://article/05b049b5-ad70-5050-84b9-3daffb12ca4a'}, {'abstract': '“American Sniper” topped the domestic movie box office, with an estimated $31.9 million in sales during its sixth weekend in theaters and third weekend in wide release.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/02/01/even-on-super-bowl-weekend-american-sniper-wins/', 'snippet': '“American Sniper” topped the domestic movie box office, with an estimated $31.9 million in sales during its sixth weekend in theaters and third weekend in wide release.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LOS ANGELES — Even the Super Bowl couldn’t crowd out Clint Eastwood’s “American Sniper,” which again topped the domestic movie box office, with an estimated $31.9 million in sales during its sixth weekend in theaters and third weekend in wide release. The strong haul — a record for any film during Super Bowl weekend, if the estimates hold — pushed total domestic sales for the reality-based Iraq war story to about $249 million.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Even on Super Bowl Weekend, ‘American Sniper’ Wins', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Another Super Weekend for ‘American Sniper’', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Super Bowl', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Binder, Mike', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Costner, Kevin', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-02-01T17:45:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael Cieply', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cieply', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/225ee63a-2018-5e1d-9e22-e17c0fdf4b8b', 'word_count': 348, 'uri': 'nyt://article/225ee63a-2018-5e1d-9e22-e17c0fdf4b8b'}, {'abstract': 'Before the Civil War even ended, Northerners were at odds over what post-Emancipation America should look like.', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/02/01/the-reconstruction-wars-begin/', 'snippet': 'Before the Civil War even ended, Northerners were at odds over what post-Emancipation America should look like.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On Jan. 26, 1865, the Massachusetts Anti-Slavery Society convened inside Boston’s Melodeon Theater, a mainstay of the city’s cultural, religious and civic life, for its annual meeting. A break from frigid temperatures and heavy snow led to high attendance. The Congregationalist minister Theodore Parker had often offered sermons at the Melodeon. In 1850, the antislavery Parker called for democracy “of all the people, by all the people, and for all the people.” After 30 years of labor, abolitionists now believed that they were in a position to push not only for the final destruction of slavery, but also for a new definition of who made up the “people.” With the bloody Civil War coming to a close, the future of the abolitionist cause, according to the Boston Brahmin Wendell Phillips, was inextricably linked to Reconstruction. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/04/25/opinion/opinionator-pog-disunion/opinionator-pog-disunion-thumbStandard.gif', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/04/25/opinion/opinionator-pog-disunion/opinionator-pog-disunion-thumbStandard.gif', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/04/25/opinion/opinionator-pog-disunion/opinionator-pog-disunion-thumbLarge.png', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Reconstruction Wars Begin', 'kicker': 'Disunion', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Civil War (US) (1861-65)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Reconstruction Era', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Slavery (Historical)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Thirteenth Amendment (US Constitution)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Douglass, Frederick', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Garrison, William Lloyd', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Boston (Mass)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-02-01T18:02:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Erik J. Chaput', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Erik', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'Chaput', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9aea96d1-6532-5a0c-b072-ad2a45fdeab1', 'word_count': 2261, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9aea96d1-6532-5a0c-b072-ad2a45fdeab1'}, {'abstract': 'Among the Kurds of the Syrian border town, pride in victory outweighs grief over losses, even amid the destruction wrought by an Islamic State siege.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/02/02/world/middleeast/in-liberated-kobani-pride-despite-the-devastation.html', 'snippet': 'Among the Kurds of the Syrian border town, pride in victory outweighs grief over losses, even amid the destruction wrought by an Islamic State siege.', 'lead_paragraph': 'KOBANI, Syria — Lasheen Abdulla steered her white minivan through the streets of her hometown, past the charred husks of bombed cars, the shattered storefronts, the unexploded mortar shells. Across the gray of destruction were streaks of color: the purple sheets hung to hide the Kurdish snipers who, for months, defended this city from the extremists of the Islamic State.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'In Liberated Kobani, Kurds Take Pride Despite the Devastation', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'In Liberated Kobani, Kurds Take Pride Despite the Devastation', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Arango, Tim', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Kobani (Syria)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Kurds', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Syria', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Islamic State in Iraq and Syria (ISIS)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Refugees and Displaced Persons', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Turkey', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-02-01T18:28:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tim Arango', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tim', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Arango', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e444063f-a193-5d37-bf11-74d8f6174369', 'word_count': 1410, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e444063f-a193-5d37-bf11-74d8f6174369'}, {'abstract': 'The destruction in Kobani, Syria, wrought by an Islamic State siege and the American-led air campaign, is so thorough 