niel Léveillé.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/02/02/arts/dance/daniel-leveilles-solitudes-solo-at-abrons-arts-center.html', 'snippet': 'Travelogues, a new series at Abrons Arts Center, began over the weekend with the American premiere of “Solitudes Solo,” by Daniel Léveillé.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When we watch a dance performance, we rarely think about where it has been and where it’s going. The dancers you see in New York today could have been halfway around the world last week. With a new series at Abrons Arts Center, Travelogues, the independent producer Laurie Uprichard (formerly a curator at Danspace Project and Dublin Dance Festival) frames performance as something that exists before and after we see it. The series began over the weekend with the American premiere of “Solitudes Solo” by Daniel Léveillé, whose company is based in Montreal. (Ms. Uprichard had seen the work in Montreal and Paris before bringing it to the Lower East Side.) This is a dance that, wherever it goes, plants itself firmly in that place — or at least it did on Friday in the intimate Experimental Theater at Abrons.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/02/arts/02DANIEL/02DANIEL-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 401, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/02/02/arts/02DANIEL/02DANIEL-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 401}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/02/arts/02DANIEL/02DANIEL-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 684, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/02/arts/02DANIEL/02DANIEL-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1368, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJum