, 'pub_date': '2015-02-02T05:21:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ken Belson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ken', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Belson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1491c101-75a9-5eb7-b103-3384ca685309', 'word_count': 555, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1491c101-75a9-5eb7-b103-3384ca685309'}, {'abstract': 'The new Louis Vuitton Foundation museum in Paris, designed by Frank Gehry, will feature an exhibition of modern masterpieces with loans from institutions around the world.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/02/02/arts/design/the-louis-vuitton-foundation-in-paris-will-display-modern-masterpieces.html', 'snippet': 'The new Louis Vuitton Foundation museum in Paris, designed by Frank Gehry, will feature an exhibition of modern masterpieces with loans from institutions around the world.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PARIS — When it opened in October, the Louis Vuitton Foundation museum was such an audacious addition to the landscape here that all eyes were on the architecture and its creator, Frank Gehry. At the time, it seemed that the art on view — from the foundation’s collection — was little more than an afterthought, and few details were disclosed about future programs. But it turns out that Suzanne Pagé, the foundation’s artistic director, was secretly working on an exhibition of modern masterpieces to open in April with loans from institutions around the world including Edvard Munch’s “The Scream,” Matisse’s “Dance” and Léger’s “Three Women (Le Grand Déjeuner).”', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/02/arts/02VUITTON/02VUITTON-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 437, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/02/02/arts/02VUITTON/02VUITTON-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 437}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/02/arts/02VUITTON/02VUITTON-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 745, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/02/arts/02VUITTON/02VUITTON-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1490, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/02/arts/02VUITTON/02VUITTON-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/02/02/arts/02VUITTON/02VUITTON-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/02/arts/02VUITTON/02VUITTON-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Bold Addition to Paris Skyline Gets Art to Match ', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Bold Addition to Paris Skyline Gets Art to Match', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Vogel, Carol', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ARCHITECTURE', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Louis Vuitton Foundation for Creation', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gehry, Frank', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Paris (France)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Museums', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-02-02T05:30:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Art & Design', 'byline': {'original': 'By Carol Vogel', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Carol', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Vogel', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f379bf55-0928-59b6-ac0d-256295076fdd', 'word_count': 1323, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f379bf55-0928-59b6-ac0d-256295076fdd'}, {'abstract': 'Edelman caught the game-winning touchdown, but questions lingered as to whether he should have been evaluated for a concussion earlier in the game.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/02/02/sports/football/hit-in-head-patriotsjulian-edelman-stays-in-leaving-questions.html', 'snippet': 'Edelman caught the game-winning touchdown, but questions lingered as to whether he should have been evaluated for a concussion earlier in the game.', 'lead_paragraph': 'GLENDALE, Ariz. — After a Super Bowl performance that had people raving about his toughness while questioning his team’s training staff, Julian Edelman of the New England Patriots is sure to be a hot topic in the coming weeks.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/02/sports/SUB-hoffman/SUB-hoffman-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 433, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/02/02/sports/SUB-hoffman/SUB-hoffman-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 433}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/02/sports/SUB-hoffman/SUB-hoffman-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 740, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'le