o the measured cadences of a funeral dirge, the leaders of the Soviet Union bore the ashes of Frol Romanovich Kozlov across the cobblestones of Red Square toward their final resting place in the Kremlin wall today [Feb. 2]. Leonid I. Brezhnev, first secretary of the Communist Party, and Premier Alexei N. Kosygin led the line of pallbearers that carried the urn at shoulder height, resting on a black pillow and covered by a canopy of white flowers. The funeral contained all the pomp the Soviet Communist Party, the government and the military could muster. — New York Herald Tribune, European Edition, Feb. 3, 1965', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '1965: Kozlov Ashes Put in Kremlin', 'kicker': 'IHT Retrospective', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Funerals and Memorials', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Moscow (Russia)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'USSR (Former Soviet Union)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-02-02T17:18:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By International Herald Tribune', 'person': [{'firstname': 'International', 'middlename': 'Herald', 'lastname': 'Tribune', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/212341f6-315e-563e-b760-9d1d137f304a', 'word_count': 110, 'uri': 'nyt://article/212341f6-315e-563e-b760-9d1d137f304a'}, {'abstract': 'The actor reiterates the critique that Oscars rarely go to performers of color who are the protagonists.', 'web_url': 'https://carpetbagger.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/02/02/david-oyelowo-says-academy-rewards-black-actors-in-subservient-roles/', 'snippet': 'The actor reiterates the critique that Oscars rarely go to performers of color who 