Peter J. Henning', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Peter', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'Henning', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/85d1e060-7c29-5edc-9958-26f0b8bc25ef', 'word_count': 980, 'uri': 'nyt://article/85d1e060-7c29-5edc-9958-26f0b8bc25ef'}, {'abstract': 'The World Meteorological Organization also said that 14 of the 15 warmest years on record had occurred in the 21st century.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/02/03/science/earth/un-weather-agency-confirms-2014-as-hottest-year.html', 'snippet': 'The World Meteorological Organization also said that 14 of the 15 warmest years on record had occurred in the 21st century.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The World Meteorological Organization reported on Monday that 2014 was the hottest year in a historical record of global temperature dating from 1880. That finding confirms an announcement made last month by two American scientific agencies and one in Japan.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'U.N. Weather Agency Confirms 2014 as Hottest Year', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Agency Confirms 2014 as Hottest, but Just Barely', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Global Warming', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gillis, Justin', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'World Meteorological Organization', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United Nations', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Weather', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-02-02T18:21:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'Science', 'subsection_name': 'Environment', 'byline': {'original': 'By Justin Gillis', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Justin', 