arts/dance/mariinsky-ballet-performs-at-the-kennedy-center-opera-house.html', 'snippet': 'The Mariinsky Ballet was at its most stylish in performances of the oldest work on its program, the Grand Pas from “Paquita,” at the Kennedy Center.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — The Mariinsky Ballet demonstrated on Saturday and Sunday that it is still one of the world’s supreme ballet companies. In the final week of its three-week visit to the United States, it produced its best dancing in the tour’s oldest ballet, the Grand Pas from “Paquita” (1881). In New York, the company’s way with classical style had seemed straitjacketed in its tempos and phrasing by its musical director, Valery Gergiev. He, however, stayed in New York to conduct the Metropolitan Opera and, at Carnegie Hall, the Mariinsky’s orchestra. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/03/arts/03MARIINSKY/03MARIINSKY-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 379, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/02/03/arts/03MARIINSKY/03MARIINSKY-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 379}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/03/arts/03MARIINSKY/03MARIINSKY-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 647, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/03/arts/03MARIINSKY/03MARIINSKY-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1294, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/03/arts/03MARIINSKY/03MARIINSKY-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/02/03/arts/03MARIINSKY/03MARIINSKY-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/03/arts/03MARIINSKY/03MARIINSKY-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Spirited Journey Backward, From Modernism to Classical', 'kicker': 'Dance Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Spirited Journey Backward, From Modernism to Classical', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dancing', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Mariinsky Ballet', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-02-02T22:04:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Dance', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alastair Macaulay', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alastair', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Macaulay', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/7cef7d3c-3ac9-56f2-a8dd-fda9378b64e9', 'word_count': 941, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7cef7d3c-3ac9-56f2-a8dd-fda9378b64e9'}, {'abstract': 'Syriza is making sense.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/02/02/whos-unreasonable-now/', 'snippet': 'Syriza is making sense.', 'lead_paragraph': 'OK, so as I understand the latest from the new Greek government, Yanis Varoufakis is saying that he and his colleagues don’t care what happens to the headline value of the debt — if you want to claim that there has been no write-off, OK. What they want instead is substantive but not outrageous relief from the burden of running primary surpluses (surpluses ex interest payments), reducing the amount of resources transferred to creditors from 4.5 to 1-1.5 percent of GDP; they also want flexibility to achieve these surpluses with a mix that includes more revenue and less spending austerity.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Who’s Unreasonable Now?', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2015-02-02T22:04:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/814941d7-76a3-5c3b-a81c-61b148f38d9a', 'word_count': 350, 'uri': 'nyt://article/814941d7-76a3-5c3b-a81c-61b148f38d9a'}, {'abstract': 'A weekly capsule of travel news curated by our writers and editors.', 'web_url': 'https://intransit.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/02/02/walkabout-kayak-adds-cuba-to-its-search-database/', 'snippet': 'A weekly capsule of travel news curated by our writers and editors.', 'lead_paragraph': ' New Destinations Kayak, the travel search engine, will now include Cuba hotel and flight information in its search function. Information will now be listed for flights to Havana, Santiago de Cuba and other cities. (Newsweek)', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/11/magazine/11havana-cuba_ss-slide-GW3L/11havana-cuba_ss-slide-GW3L-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 600, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/01/11/magazine/11havana-cuba_ss-slide-GW3L/11havana-cuba_ss-slide-GW3L-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 600}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/11/