'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/03/arts/03LAVETTE/03LAVETTE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/02/03/arts/03LAVETTE/03LAVETTE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/03/arts/03LAVETTE/03LAVETTE-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Struggle to Survive in Each Soulful Lyric', 'kicker': 'Music Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Struggle to Survive in Each Soulful Lyric', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Cafe Carlyle (Manhattan, NY)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'LaVette, Bettye', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-02-02T22:28:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Stephen Holden', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stephen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Holden', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/e1709e65-e7ec-5cda-ae1a-eac577ea9dcc', 'word_count': 359, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e1709e65-e7ec-5cda-ae1a-eac577ea9dcc'}, {'abstract': 'A diverse mix of Angelenos browsed 40,000 square feet of affordable zines, prints and editions over the weekend.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/02/02/la-art-book-fair-street-style/', 'snippet': 'A diverse mix of Angelenos browsed 40,000 square feet of affordable zines, prints and editions over the weekend.', 'lead_paragraph': 'This past weekend, Los Angeles hosted three very different art fairs in three very different locales: Art Los Angeles Contemporary in Santa Monica, Paramount Ranch in Agoura Hills and Printed Matter’s L.A. Art Book Fair downtown. With 40,000 square feet worth of affordable zines, prints and editions on offer, the latter event was the most populist, and populous. For three days, the normally quiet streets of Little Tokyo teemed with pedestrians as art lovers, thrill-seeking teenagers and curious onlookers migrating from the Hello Kitty exhibition next door crowded the Geffen Contemporary at MOCA. Live bands and food trucks lent a music-festival feel; fittingly, the fashion on view tended toward the grungy, with black-on-black layers and mom jeans (on both men and women) among the more visible trends. The style outliers, many of whom were exhibitors, took things a step further. Highlights included statement shoes, sparkling face paint and multiples of “symbolic jewelry” from the artist Tauba Auerbach, whose Diagonal Press hosted a booth at the fair. The photographer Laure Joliet was on hand to capture the action for T.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Grunge Aesthetic at the L.A. Art Book Fair', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Geffen Contemporary', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Los Angeles (Calif)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-02-02T22:30:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Eviana Hartman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Eviana', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hartman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0cb4c21a-6dc8-5ae7-8815-e9fa1bd486e7', 'word_count': 199, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0cb4c21a-6dc8-5ae7-8815-e9fa1bd486e7'}, {'abstract': 'Bob Dylan’s “Shadows in the Night,” an album of 10 songs that were all recorded by Frank Sinatra, is a tribute from one venerated American musician to another.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/02/03/arts/music/releases-from-bob-dylan-and-diana-krall.html', 'snippet': 'Bob Dylan’s “Shadows in the Night,” an album of 10 songs that were all recorded by Frank Sinatra, is a tribute from one venerated American musician to another.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It’s not a put-on. Bob Dylan’s “Shadows in the Night,” an album of 10 songs that were all recorded by Frank Sinatra, is a tribute from one venerated American musician to another, a reconsideration of a school of songwriting, a feat of technical nostalgia and a reckoning with love and death.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/03/arts/03NEWMUSIC/03NEWMUSIC-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 596, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/02/03/arts/03NEWMUSIC/03NEWMUSIC-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 596}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/03/arts/03NEWMUSIC/03NEWMUSIC-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1018, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/03/arts/03NEWMUSIC/03NEWMUSIC-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1490, 'width': 1499, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/03/arts/03NEWMUSIC/03NEWMUSIC-thumbStand