g-agenda-the-road-to-s-p-s-settlement/', 'snippet': 'S.&.P.’s settlement ends a heated, two-year fight with regulators. | President Obama’s corporate tax reform irks the business world. | Slump in oil prices brings pressure. | Ally chief steps down.', 'lead_paragraph': 'THE ROAD TO S.&P.’S SETTLEMENT | An overflow crowd of government regulators, including attorneys general from states across the country, spent a day in January ticking off their demands before eventually negotiating a $1.37 billion settlement with the giant ratings agency Standard & Poor’s, Ben Protess reports in DealBook. The settlement, expected to be announced on Tuesday, was the culmination of a heated, two-year fight between S.&P. and the Justice Department, according to an account assembled through interviews. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Morning Agenda: The Road to S.&P.’s Settlement', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2015-02-03T12:16:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sydney Ember', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sydney', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ember', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d59c1aac-1470-5bab-9ed2-b594da6a1c79', 'word_count': 2143, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d59c1aac-1470-5bab-9ed2-b594da6a1c79'}, {'abstract': 'The beloved triangle of Phil Jackson, the Knicks’ president, has so far been seen as a failed experiment, but ultimate success would burnish his basketball legacy beyond wins and losses.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/02/04/sports/basketball/phil-jackson-is-out-to-prove-that-his-signature-offense-still-fits.html', 'snippet': 'The beloved triangle of Phil Jackson, the Knicks’ president, has so far been seen as a failed experiment, but ultimate success would burnish his basketball legacy beyond wins and losses.', 'lead_paragraph': 'There were 60 million good reasons for Phil Jackson to accept the formidable challenge of rebuilding the Knicks along with one intangible benefit that could not be banked. Some might think the one he chose, however, borders on obsession: to resurrect his beloved triangle and prove to the world that it is an offense for the ages.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/04/sports/JACKSON/JACKSON-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 429, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/02/04/sports/JACKSON/JACKSON-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 429}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/04/sports/JACKSON/JACKSON-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 732, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/04/sports/JACKSON/JACKSON-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1464, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/04/sports/JACKSON/JACKSON-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/02/04/sports/JACKSON/JACKSON-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/04/sports/JACKSON/JACKSON-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {