y and stiff, loomed over the doctor, showing a number of troubling signs. The doctor noted poor posture, callused skin, limbs pocked with deep scars. He feared survival would hinge on drastic action, maybe even an amputation.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'For the Prickliest Patients, a Desert Doctor Makes House Calls', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'For the Prickliest Patients, a Doctor Makes House Calls', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Gardens and Gardening', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rojas, Rick', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'ARIZONA', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Leblanc, Rilee', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deserts', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-02-03T15:51:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rick Rojas', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rojas', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/eef327a4-0196-5db1-8310-b18e2a7768ec', 'word_count': 1114, 'uri': 'nyt://article/eef327a4-0196-5db1-8310-b18e2a7768ec'}, {'abstract': 'Highlights from the International Herald Tribune archives: French officials consider wartime food rationing in 1940.', 'web_url': 'https://iht-retrospective.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/02/03/1940-rationing-may-be-started/', 'snippet': 'Highlights from the International Herald Tribune archives: French officials consider wartime food rationing in 1940.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Paris newspapers yesterday [Feb. 3]\xa0 published articles intimating that ration\xa0 cards for at least a few food products\xa0 may be introduced in the capital, if not in\xa0 all of France. Thus far in the war, France\xa0 alone of the belligerents has not introduced the ration system. Several newspapers also announced the fact that the\xa0 Seine Department General Council on\xa0 December 30 passed a resolution asking\xa0 that ration cards for sugar, coffee, oil,\xa0 macaroni and spaghetti be issued within \xa0the department. At the same time, it was\xa0 revealed that ration cards were printed\xa0 by the government in 1937 and distributed to town halls throughout the nation.\xa0— New York Herald Tribune, European Edition, Feb. 4, 1940', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '1940: Rationing May Be Started', 'kicker': 'IHT Retrospective', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Food', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Rationing and Allocation of Resources', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'World War II (1939-45)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'France', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-02-03T16:03:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By International Herald Tribune', 'person': [{'firstname': 'International', 'middlename': 'Herald', 'lastname': 'Tribune', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/cb4221b8-f7ee-59c0-b510-5bcdbdbeda1c', 'word_count': 114, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cb4221b8-f7ee-59c0-b510-5bcdbdbeda1c'}, {'abstract': 'A new, supportive ad follows two rulings striking down Alabama’s same-sex marriage ban.', 'web_url': 'https://takingnote.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/02/03/marriage-equality-in-alabama/', 'snippet': 'A new, supportive ad follows two rulings striking down Alabama’s same-sex marriage ban.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A television ad now airing across Alabama delivers a well-timed message about the human costs of denying gay couples the right to marry.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Marriage Equality in Alabama', 'kicker': 'Taking Note', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Same-Sex Marriage, Civil Unions and Domestic Partnerships', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Moore, Roy S', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wolfson, Evan', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'ALABAMA', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-02-03T16:04:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dorothy J. Samuels', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dorothy', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'Samuels', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/32e514dd-77ac-56e1-a8db-74465d4fac40', 'word_count': 328, 'uri': 'nyt://article/32e514dd-77ac-56e1-a8db-74465d4fac40'}, {'abstract': 'The new book, “Go Set a Watchman,” focuses on the character of Scout as an adult, and was written in the 1950s. It will be published in July.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/02/04/books/harper-lee-author-of-to-kill-a-mockingbird-is-to-publish-a-new-novel.html', 'snippet': 'The new book, “Go Set a Watchman,” focuses on the character of Scout as an adult, and was written in the 1950s. It will be published in July.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For more than half a century, “To Kill a Mockingbird” has stood apart as a singular American literary masterpiece, a perennial best seller that has provoked countless classroom discussions about racial and social injustice. It brought instant and overwhelming fame to its enigmatic author, Harper Lee, who soon retreated from the spo