officer for the Navy, was arrested Tuesday and charged with conspiracy to commit bribery in a scandal involving ship-supply contracts in the Pacific. Federal prosecutors said Mr. Simpkins, 60, accepted several hundred thousand dollars in cash, trips and the services of prostitutes from Leonard Francis, a Malaysian businessman who recently pleaded guilty to bribing Navy officials for help in overbilling the services by at least $35 million. Prosecutors said Mr. Simpkins, who pleaded not guilty, overruled a subordinate who wanted to drop a contract with Mr. Leonard in Thailand that included “many exceedingly high cost” items. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '17', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Ex-Contractor Charged in Navy Bribery Case', 'kicker': 'National Briefing | Military', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Ex-Contractor Charged in Navy Bribery Case', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Drew, Christopher', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Defense Contracts', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bribery and Kickbacks', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Simpkins, Paul', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Francis, Leonard', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-02-04T00:45:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Christopher Drew', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Christopher', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Drew', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/7ebb6624-364a-593d-a777-e21615f49700', 'word_count': 102, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7ebb6624-364a-593d-a777-e21615f49700'}, {'abstract': 'In one of the best-received proposals in his State of the City address, Mayor Bill de Blasio announced 