ubtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/03/multimedia/opdoc-curse/opdoc-curse-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 576, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/03/multimedia/opdoc-curse/opdoc-curse-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1080, 'width': 1920, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/03/multimedia/opdoc-curse/opdoc-curse-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/02/03/multimedia/opdoc-curse/opdoc-curse-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/03/multimedia/opdoc-curse/opdoc-curse-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Our Curse', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parenting', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Babies and Infants', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Documentary Films and Programs', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-02-04T01:10:08+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Opinion', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'Tomasz Śliwiński', 'person': [{'firstname': '', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Video', '_id': 'nyt://video/030e6bd6-b74e-580f-8ed6-dc4fd43472d6', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://video/030e6bd6-b74e-580f-8ed6-dc4fd43472d6'}, {'abstract': 'W tym krótkim, nominowanym do Oscara filmie dokumentalnym młoda para zmaga się z koszmarem każdego nowego rodzica: dzieckiem urodzonym z zagrażającą życiu chorobą.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/02/04/opinion/nasza-klatwa.html', 'snippet': 'W tym krótkim, nominowanym do Oscara filmie dokumentalnym młoda para zmaga się z koszmarem każdego nowego rodzica: dzieckiem urodzonym z zagrażającą życiu chorobą.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Cztery lata temu, u mojego nowonarodzonego syna Leo zdiagnozowano bardzo rzadką i nieuleczalną chorobę, tak zwaną Klątwę Ondyny. Znana jest również jako zespół wrodzonej ośrodkowej hipowentylacji.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '‘Nasza klątwa’', 'kicker': 'Op-Docs', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2015-02-04T01:13:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tomasz Śliwiński', 'person': [{'firstname': '', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/5300494c-800b-5ff1-9df9-52cedcf94a3f', 'word_count': 335, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5300494c-800b-5ff1-9df9-52cedcf94a3f'}, {'abstract': 'In this Oscar-nominated documentary, a young couple struggles to overcome every new parent’s worst nightmare: a child born with a life-threatening illness.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/02/02/opinion/our-curse.html', 'snippet': 'In this Oscar-nominated documentary, a young couple struggles to overcome every new parent’s worst nightmare: a child born with a life-threatening illness.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Four years ago, my newborn son, Leo, was given a diagnosis of a very rare and incurable disorder known as Ondine’s Curse. Also called  Congenital Central Hypoventilation Syndrome (C.C.H.S.), the disorder prevents the thousand or so people known to have been born with it from breathing while asleep, and sometimes also while awake. Though the disorder is manageable when treated, our son is likely to need a ventilator for the rest of his life.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '‘Our Curse’', 'kicker': 'Op-Docs', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Children and Childhood', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicine and Health', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parenting', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-02-04T01:13:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tomasz Śliwiński', 'person': [{'firstname': '', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/e300292d-e3f9-5b30-a5f2-cce49ab11e91', 'word_count': 405, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e300292d-e3f9-5b30-a5f2-cce49ab11e91'}, {'abstract': 'Middle Eastern and developing countries have long kept oil cheap for political reasons, but a new global energy picture presents an opportunity to stop.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/02/04/business/low-energy-prices-offer-opening-for-subsidy-cuts.html', 'snippet': 'Middle Eastern and developing countries have long kept oil cheap for political reasons, but a new global energy picture presents an opportunity to stop.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In Saudi Arabia, drivers pay roughly 45 cents a gallon to fill up their cars, and in Venezuela even less. Energy is so inexpensive in Kuwait and Qatar that residents chill their enormous swimming pools in the summer and typically leave their air-conditioners on at full blast while they are away on vacation.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/04/business/04SUBSIDIES/04SUBSIDIES-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 408, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/02/04/business/04SUBSIDIES/04SUBSIDIES-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 408}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/04/business/04SUBSIDIES/04SUBSIDIES-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 696, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/04/business/04SUBSIDIES/04SUBSIDIES-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1392, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/04/business/04SUBSIDIES/04SUBSIDIES-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/02/04/business/04SUBSIDIES/04SUBSIDIES-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/04/business/04SUBSIDIES/04SUBSIDIES-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Low Energy Prices Offer Opening for Subsidy Cuts', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Low Energy Prices Offer Opening for Subsidy Cuts', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Oil (Petroleum) and Gasoline', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Krauss, Clifford', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Prices (Fares, Fees and Rates)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'International Trade and World Market', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Middle East', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Third World and Developing Countries', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-02-04T01:13:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Energy & Environment ', 'byline': {'original': 'By Clifford Krauss', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Clifford', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krauss', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3e897460-fa6c-556a-81c2-fa8f696f2694', 'word_count': 1114, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3e897460-fa6c-556a-81c2-fa8f696f2694'}, {'abstract': 'Cuba temporarily detained 178 political prisoners in January, the State Department’s senior human rights official said Tuesday. There were 489 such detentions in December.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/02/04/world/americas/us-official-says-cubas-political-detentions-declined.html', 'snippet': 'Cuba temporarily detained 178 political prisoners in January, the State Department’s senior human rights official said Tuesday. There were 489 such detentions in December.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — Cuba temporarily detained 178 political prisoners in January, Tom Malinowski, the State Department’s senior human rights official, said Tuesday. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'U.S. Official Says Cuba’s Political Detentions Declined', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'U.S. Official Says Cuba’s Political Detentions Declined', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Political Prisoners', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Cuba', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-02-04T01:21:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Americas', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael R. Gordon', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': 'R.', 'lastname': 'Gordon', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c479da15-abaf-5f83-8c32-70d29c00966c', 'word_count': 463, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c479da15-abaf-5f83-8c32-70d29c00966c'}, {'abstract': 'Alexis Tsipras, the newly elected prime minister of Greece, and his finance minister are making fashion statements as they visit European capitals to lobby for relief from the country’s bailout debt.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/02/04/world/on-tour-greek-leaders-wear-no-ties-and-aim-for-looser-belts.html', 'snippet': 'Alexis Tsipras, the newly elected prime minister of Greece, and his finance minister are making fashion statements as they visit European capitals to lobby for relief from the country’s bailout debt.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ROME — Less than two weeks after taking power in national elections, Greece’s leftist-led government is now taking Europe. Fashion critics in London are debating whether the Greek finance minister is an arbiter of cool chic or looks like a nightclub bouncer. Politicians in Brussels and Berlin are mulling whether the new Greek prime minister is a radical looking to bring down the eurozone or a canny operator looking for a deal.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/04/world/04GREECE/04GREECE-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 390, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'lega