glocations', 'value': 'Detroit (Mich)', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Kentucky', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-02-04T12:00:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/dbd42422-d2a8-5365-ad42-988257c79160', 'word_count': 1501, 'uri': 'nyt://article/dbd42422-d2a8-5365-ad42-988257c79160'}, {'abstract': 'S.&P.’s settlement leaves the future unclear for ratings. | A lesson for deal makers. | Smucker announces it will buy Big Heart Pet Brands. | Staples and Office Depot are in advanced talks to combine.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2015/02/04/morning-agenda-what-s-p-s-settlement-means/', 'snippet': 'S.&P.’s settlement leaves the future unclear for ratings. | A lesson for deal makers. | Smucker announces it will buy Big Heart Pet Brands. | Staples and Office Depot are in advanced talks to combine.', 'lead_paragraph': ' WHAT S.&P.’S SETTLEMENT MEANS | Standard & Poor’s $1.37 billion settlement with prosecutors, announced on Tuesday, will settle an array of government lawsuits against the giant rating agency. But it does not represent closure for the broader ratings business, DealBook’s Ben Protess and Nathaniel Popper report. An uncertain future still lies ahead for S.&P., as well as its main rivals, Moody’s and Fitch.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Morning Agenda: What S.&P.’s Settlement Means', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2015-02-04T12:09:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sydney Ember', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sydney', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ember', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/582249ce-71ba-5159-a6af-533b1ddb248e', 'word_count': 2030, 'uri': 'nyt://article/582249ce-71ba-5159-a6af-533b1ddb248e'}, {'abstract': 'Regulators shot down a combination of Staples and Office Depot about 18 years ago, but since then, the competitive landscape has changed, with both companies now facing rivals in Walmart, Target, Amazon and others.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2015/02/04/staples-to-buy-office-depot-for-6-3-billion/', 'snippet': 'Regulators shot down a combination of Staples and Office Depot about 18 years ago, but since then, the competitive landscape has changed, with both companies now facing rivals in Walmart, Target, Amazon and others.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Updated, 6:48 p.m. | In planning a $6.3 billion merger, Staples and Office Depot are betting that 18 years was long enough for government regulators to change their minds about how consumers buy office supplies.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/05/business/05SKYBOX1/05SKYBOX1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 372, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/02/05/business/05SKYBOX1/05SKYBOX1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 372}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/05/business/05SKYBOX1/05SKYBOX1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 635, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/05/business/05SKYBOX1/05SKYBOX1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1271, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumb