e': None, 'lastname': 'Blinder', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4bab4740-2ef7-5a51-a1d2-f7fc3712fc34', 'word_count': 1170, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4bab4740-2ef7-5a51-a1d2-f7fc3712fc34'}, {'abstract': 'The Times reporter Anahad O’Connor writes about the connection between his 2013 Science Times article about herbal supplements and an investigation by the New York attorney general’s office.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/times-insider/2015/02/04/times-article-prompts-investigation-into-herbal-supplements/', 'snippet': 'The Times reporter Anahad O’Connor writes about the connection between his 2013 Science Times article about herbal supplements and an investigation by the New York attorney general’s office.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On Feb. 3, Anahad O’Connor wrote an article about findings that major retailers may be selling herbal supplements that contain little more than cheap fillers like powdered rice, asparagus and houseplants, and in some cases substances that could be dangerous to those with allergies. As he tells Insiders, Mr. O’Connor had some familiarity with these accusations.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Times Article Prompts Investigation Into Herbal Supplements', 'kicker': 'Times Insider', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dietary Supplements and Herbal Remedies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Frauds and Swindling', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Labeling and Labels', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Schneiderman, Eric T', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Times', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-02-04T15:53:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'secti