 the museums, hôtels particuliers and showrooms of Paris, another fashion show was taking place halfway across the world on the sun-baked, hard-surface tennis courts of the Australian Open.', 'print_section': 'E', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Fashion Takes Center Court at the Australian Open     ', 'kicker': 'Noted', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Tennis in Australia Is Back in Fashion', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Emmrich, Stuart', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tennis', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Australian Open (Tennis)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wozniacki, Caroline', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Williams, Serena', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sharapova, Maria', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'NIKE Inc', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'ADIDAS AG', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bouchard, Eugenie', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Azarenka, Victoria', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-02-04T18:09:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Styles', 'section_name': 'Fashion & Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Stuart Emmrich', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stuart', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Emmrich', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/42d9438c-c121-5524-a534-a32c8248bea5', 'word_count': 412, 'uri': 'nyt://article/42d9438c-c121-5524-a534-a32c8248bea5'}, {'abstract': 'The three circles of anti-vaccine sentiment.', 'web_url': 'https://douthat.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/02/04/among-the-anti-vaxxers/', 'snippet': 'The three circles of anti-vaccine sentiment.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I’m hopeful that the briefly-popular idea\xa0that\xa0vaccination is about to become a partisan issue turns out to be a one-week wonder: It was floated thanks to Chris Christie and (especially) Rand Paul’s rhetorical malpractice, eagerly grasped at by liberals and narrative-seeking journalists, and then — God willing — given last rites by\xa0Paul’s booster shot yesterday. But the related and largely nonpartisan debate over how best to argue with/persuade/shame the kind of parents who decide not to vaccinate their kids (see this piece from Conor Friedersdorf, and this one from Slate’s Phil Plait, for interesting discussions) is\xa0likely to remain relevant for quite a while … at least as long as we keep having disease\xa0outbreaks\xa0that seem to cluster in areas with clear pockets of strong anti-vaccine sentiment.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Among the Anti-Vaxxers', 'kicker': 'Ross Douthat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Autism', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Epidemics', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Measles', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Vaccination and Immunization', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hillenbrand, Laura', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kohn, Sally', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Paul, Rand', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Sweden', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-02-04T18:09:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ross Douthat', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ross', 'middlename':