rrier regulations have played a vital role in the growth of the Web.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Listening to large cable and phone companies might lead some people to conclude that the Federal Communications Commission is about to unleash the technological equivalent of the bubonic plague upon the Internet, or what some are calling “utility regulation.” Don’t believe the hype.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'No, the F.C.C. Isn’t Destroying the Internet', 'kicker': 'Taking Note', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Net Neutrality', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wheeler, Thomas E', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Comcast Corporation', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Federal Communications Commission', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Verizon Communications Inc', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-02-04T19:14:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Vikas Bajaj', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Vikas', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bajaj', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b20ef8db-06bf-5fa5-896b-9762d42809f6', 'word_count': 324, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b20ef8db-06bf-5fa5-896b-9762d42809f6'}, {'abstract': 'The defeat of the Islamist militants suggests that momentum in the nearly six-year war against Boko Haram may finally be shifting.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/02/05/world/africa/boko-haram-pushed-from-nigerian-town-by-chad-military.html', 'snippet': 'The defeat of the Islamist militants suggests that momentum in the nearly six-year war against Boko Haram may finally be shifting.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ABUJA, Nigeri