rs are increasingly teaming up in ways both large and small.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/02/05/arts/music/at-lincoln-center-cultural-institutions-team-up.html', 'snippet': 'At Lincoln Center, institutions that once competed, sometimes bitterly, over audiences, resources and donors are increasingly teaming up in ways both large and small.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It was a day of rehearsals all around Lincoln Center, and plenty of well-known artists were hard at work — but not in their usual places. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/05/arts/05PLAZA/05PLAZA-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 450, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/02/05/arts/05PLAZA/05PLAZA-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 450}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/05/arts/05PLAZA/05PLAZA-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 769, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/05/arts/05PLAZA/05PLAZA-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1537, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/05/arts/05PLAZA/05PLAZA-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/02/05/arts/05PLAZA/05PLAZA-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/05/arts/05PLAZA/05PLAZA-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Making Overtures Across the Plaza', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Making Overtures Across the Plaza', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cooper, Michael', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Lincoln Center for the Performing Arts', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Metropolitan Opera', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Opera', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dancing', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Culture (Arts)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Philharmonic', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York City Ballet', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-02-04T22:35:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael Cooper', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cooper', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e182a958-6592-5a1c-8957-af9ec8df17af', 'word_count': 1021, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e182a958-6592-5a1c-8957-af9ec8df17af'}, {'abstract': 'The inquiries are reminiscent of an investigation started in 2002, when the district attorney conducted a large-scale review of potential fraud in sales tax payments on art purchases.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/02/05/arts/design/galleries-records-are-subpoenaed.html', 'snippet': 'The inquiries are reminiscent of an investigation started in 2002, when the district attorney conducted a large-scale review of potential fraud in sales tax payments on art purchases.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Several art galleries and dealers have received subpoenas from the Manhattan district attorney’s office requesting sales and shipping records, according to lawyers for the businesses, suggesting that investigators may be revisiting the issue of whether galleries and collectors are properly paying sales tax for art sold in New York, the lawyers said.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Galleries’ Records Are Subpoenaed', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Galleries’ Records Are Subpoenaed', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bowley, Graham', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tax Evasion', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Subpoenas', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-02-04T22:38:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Art & Design', 'byline': {'original': 'By Graham Bowley and Robin Pogrebin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Graham', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bowley', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Robin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pogrebin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/47472631-c870-5b76-a10f-145ae17243cf', 'word_count': 861, 'uri': 'nyt://article/47472631-c870-5b76-a10f-145ae17243cf'}, {'abstract': 'Gaylord Schanilec’s “Lac DesPleurs,” a book made with centuries-old woodblock printing methods, suggests how such artisanry is experiencing a golden era.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/02/08/arts/design/artists-find-an-audience-for-painstaking-letterpress-printing.html', 'snippet': 'Gaylord Schanilec’s “Lac DesPleurs,” a book made with centuries-old woodblock printing methods, suggests how such artisanry is experiencing a golden era.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SAN MARCOS, TEX. — On the day before New Year’s Eve, after making the 19-hour drive to Texas from Wisconsin, the writer and artisan Gaylord Schanilec began checking the status of the precious cargo that had been sitting, uninsured, in the bed of his Chevy Silverado. In the home studio of Craig Jensen, a bookbinder here, Mr. Schanilec plucked more than half a million dollars out of Rubbermaid storage bins. The money was in the form of 100 bubble-wrapped copies of “Lac Des Pleurs,” Mr. Schanilec’s ode to Lake Pepin, near his home in Stockholm, Wis., population 69. The going rate for each copy is $5,000. ', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '26', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/08/arts/08LETTERPRESS1/08LETTERPRESS1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 486, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/02/08/arts/08LETTERPRESS1/08LETTERPRESS1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 486}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/08/arts/08LETTERPRESS1/08LETTERPRESS1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 829, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/08/arts/08LETTERPRESS1/08LETTERPRESS1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1657, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/08/arts/08LETTERPRESS1/08LETTERPRESS1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/02/08/arts/08LETTERPRESS1/08LETTERPRESS1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/08/arts/08LETTERPRESS1/08LETTERPRESS1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Grain by Wood Grain, a Movable Feast', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Grain by Wood Grain, a Movable Feast', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hoinski, Michael', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Schanilec, Gaylord (1955- )', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Book Trade and Publishing', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wood and Wood Products', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Texas', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-02-04T22:38:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Art & Design', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael Hoinski', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hoinski', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4d0a6bfc-29e9-5aaa-bd42-523124ce51e6', 'word_count': 1227, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4d0a6bfc-29e9-5aaa-bd42-523124ce51e6'}, {'abstract': '“Allegiance,” on NBC, joins the FX drama “The Americans,” the Showtime series “Homeland” and NBC’s own “State of Affairs” in the prime-time espionage sweepstakes.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/02/05/arts/television/hope-davis-stars-in-allegiance-on-nbc.html', 'snippet': '“Allegiance,” on NBC, joins the FX drama “The Americans,” the Showtime series “Homeland” and NBC’s own “State of Affairs” in the prime-time espionage sweepstakes.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The heroine of “Allegiance” has a brilliant son who works at the C.I.A. and has no idea that his mother is a Russian spy. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/05/arts/05ALLEGIANCEJP1/05ALLEGIANCEJP1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 667, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/02/05/arts/05ALLEGIANCEJP1/05ALLEGIANCEJP1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 667}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/05/arts/05ALLEGIANCEJP1/05ALLEGIANCEJP1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 922, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/05/arts/05ALLEGIANCEJP1/05ALLEGIANCEJP1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2000, 'width': 1799, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/05/arts/05ALLEGIANCEJP1/05ALLEGIANCEJP1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/02/05/arts/05ALLEGIANCEJP1/05ALLEGIANCEJP1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/05/arts/05ALLEGIANCEJP1/05ALLEGIANCEJP1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Homeland Insecurities ', 'kicker': 'Television Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Homeland Insecurities', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Stanley, Alessandra', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Allegiance (TV Program)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Davis, Hope', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Broadcasting Co', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-02-04T22:41:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alessandra Stanley', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alessandra', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Stanley', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/d9d3b9ff-0524-5173-8471-abeb3575ef9b', 'word_count': 885, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d9d3b9ff-0524-5173-8471-abeb3575ef9b'}, {'abstract': 'The late Civil War saw a booming market in recruiting fraud.', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/02/04/men-is-cheap/', 'snippet': 'The late Civil War saw a booming market in recruiting fraud.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In February 1865, The New York Times announced sensational news: 27 recruitment and bounty brokers had been arrested after a federal government investigation into allegations of huge military recruitment fraud. Spearheaded by Lafayette C. Baker, the government’s detective in chief, the investigation laid bare a nationwide network of malfeasance, implicating businessmen, local government officials, military officers and soldiers engaged in a concerted effort to fraudulently help communities achieve their draft quotas by forging enlistment documents, and then surreptitiously pocketing the commissions paid for reaching those numbers. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/04/25/opinion/opinionator-pog-disunion/opinionator-pog-disunion-thumbStandard.gif', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/04/25/opinion/opinionator-pog-disunion/opinionator-pog-disunion-thumbStandard.gif', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/04/25/opinion/opinionator-pog-disunion/opinionator-pog-disunion-thumbLarge.png', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': '‘Men Is Cheap’', 'kicker': 'Disunion', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Civil War (US) (1861-65)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Draft and Recruitment (Military)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Frauds and Swindling', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-02-04T22:43:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Brian P. Luskey', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Brian', 'middlename': 'P.', 'lastname': 'Luskey', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0469abac-7697-50d1-b2fb-8934050013f4', 'word_count': 1129, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0469abac-7697-50d1-b2fb-8934050013f4'}, {'abstract': 'Some A-listers have joined a growing outcry against the objectification of women on the red carpet.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/02/05/movies/awardsseason/on-the-red-carpet-a-revolt-builds-over-the-p