formance to ask citizens to speak about their visions for Cuba, said Wednesday that she had not been able to find a lawyer willing to defend her and that prosecutors had been given 60 more days to decide whether to charge her. The charges being considered include inciting public disorder. She has been released, but her passport has been confiscated. She said six lawyers had refused to represent her because they believed that her case was a lost cause or feared that defending her might hurt their careers. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Cuba: Artist Awaits Decision on Charges', 'kicker': 'World Briefing', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Cuba: Artist Awaits Decision on Charges', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Burnett, Victoria', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Cuba', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bruguera, Tania', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Demonstrations, Protests and Riots', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-02-05T04:32:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Americas', 'byline': {'original': 'By Victoria Burnett', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Victoria', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Burnett', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/0a026b84-4336-5652-b053-4ca05f7a83f7', 'word_count': 111, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0a026b84-4336-5652-b053-4ca05f7a83f7'}, {'abstract': 'A panel of judges ruled Wednesday that the leader of the neo-fascist party Golden Dawn and more than a dozen party lawmakers are among 72 people who would stand trial on charges that include participation in a criminal organization, murder and assault.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/02/05/world/europe/greece-rightists-ordered-to-stand-trial.html', 'snippet': 'A panel of judges ruled Wednesday that the leader of the neo-fascist party Golden Dawn and more than a dozen party lawmakers are among 72 people who would stand trial on charges that include participation in a criminal organization, murder and ass...', 'lead_paragraph': ' A panel of judges ruled Wednesday that the leader of the neo-fascist party Golden Dawn and more than a dozen party lawmakers are among 72 people who would stand trial on charges that include participation in a criminal organization, murder and assault. The ruling followed a 15-month investigation into the party, which is widely regarded as one of Europe’s most violent far-right groups. The defendants include 18 Golden Dawn lawmakers who were elected to Greece’s Parliament in the 2012 general elections, including two who have since left the party, as well as 54 members or supporters of Golden Dawn. Golden Dawn dismissed the charges, saying the party and its supporters are victims of “persecution” and a “political frame-up.” ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Greece: Rightists Ordered to Stand Trial', 'kicker': 'World Briefing', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Greece: Rightists Ordered to Stand Trial', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kitsantonis, Niki', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Greece', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fringe Groups and Movements', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Golden Dawn (Greece)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Europe', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Decisions and Verdicts', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-02-05T04:34:46+0000', 'document_ty