 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Classified Information and State Secrets', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Terrorism', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lynch, Stephen F (1955- )', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-02-05T04:39:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Carl Hulse', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Carl', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hulse', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1a37152d-416e-51aa-a23a-e6323f59e6a8', 'word_count': 1122, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1a37152d-416e-51aa-a23a-e6323f59e6a8'}, {'abstract': 'Matt Ferchen, an associate professor of international relations at Tsinghua University in Beijing, discusses how oil prices will affect China’s relations with other countries and its transition to a more energy-efficient future.', 'web_url': 'https://sinosphere.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/02/04/q-and-a-matt-ferchen-on-china-and-the-price-of-oil/', 'snippet': 'Matt Ferchen, an associate professor of international relations at Tsinghua University in Beijing, discusses how oil prices will affect China’s relations with other countries and its transition to a more energy-efficient future.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The recent global drop in oil prices has made winners of consumers in places like the United States and Japan, and losers of countries that depend heavily on oil exports such as Russia, Iran and Venezuela. China, a leading crude oil importer and the world’s largest energy consumer, has responded to the fall in oil prices — the steepest since 2009 — by going on a buying spree to ensure that its strategic oil reserves at the end of 2014 were twice what they were the year before. Last month, in another move to bolster the country’s supplies, China’s top economic planning agency, the National Development and Reform Commission, directed domestic oil refiners to stock up on crude oil and to provide the government with monthly updates on their inventories.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/02/blogs/02SINO-FERCHEN/02SINO-FERCHEN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 923, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/02/02/blogs/02SINO-FERCHEN/02SINO-FERCHEN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 923}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/02/blogs/02SINO-FERCHEN/02SINO-FERCHEN-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 666, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/02/blogs/02SINO-FERCHEN/02SINO-FERCHEN-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1331, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/02/blogs/02SINO-FERCHEN/02SINO-FERCHEN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/02/02/blogs/02SINO-FERCHEN/02SINO-FERCHEN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/02/blogs/02SINO-FERCHEN/02SINO-FERCHEN-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Q. and A.: Matt Ferchen on China and the Price of Oil', 'kicker': 'Sinosphere', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Oil (Petroleum) and Gasoline', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Reserves (Natural Resources)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'BRICS Group', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Development and Reform Commission (China)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Tsinghua University', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iran', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Russia', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-02-05T04:53:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jess Macy Yu', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jess', 'middlename': 'Macy', 'lastname': 'Yu', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a216122f-ece2-5c5c-9091-644d7db86e26', 'word_count': 1385, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a216122f-ece2-5c5c-9091-644d7db86e26'}, {'abstract': 'Dancer injured, Justin Peck fills in during debut of his work at New York City Ballet', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/02/04/justin-peck-finds-a-sub-for-injured-dancer-himself/', 'snippet': 'Dancer injured, Justin Peck fills in during debut of his work at New York City Ballet', 'lead_paragraph': 'Justin Peck does not lack for causes of anxiety. As the resident choreographer for New York City Ballet, the 27-year-old is perpetually auditioning for the role of rightful heir to George Balanchine. So imagine what Mr. Peck must have felt when he learned that Andrew Veyette, one of the lead dancers in his “Rodeo: Four Dance Episodes” was injured and could not perform on Wednesday evening at its premiere at the David H. Koch Theater. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Justin Peck  Finds a Sub for Injured Dancer: Himself', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dancing', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Peck, Justin', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York City Ballet', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-02-05T04:58:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Brian Seibert', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Brian', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Seibert', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8ba68579-7f78-5197-b4ca-f92440f53a01', 'word_count': 245, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8ba68579-7f78-5197-b4ca-f92440f53a01'}, {'abstract': 'The Puerto Rican-born artist makes pieces that feel completely modern, sometimes tweaking the patina with an accidental coffee spill or cigarette ash.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/02/05/t-magazine/kiko-lopez-mirrors-glass.html', 'snippet': 'The Puerto Rican-born artist makes pieces that feel completely modern, sometimes tweaking the patina with an accidental coffee spill or cigarette ash.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Kiko Lopez makes mirrors that combine an 18th-century technique with a renegade spirit. Using the painstaking process of verre églomisé, he covers engraved glass with gold and silver leaf, a skill he mastered in the South of France while apprenticing for several retired artisans after, he says, “they realized I was serious and wasn’t just going to make reproductions.” Although he’s committed to respecting tradition, the Puerto Rican-born artist makes pieces that feel completely modern, sometimes tweaking the patina with an accidental coffee spill or cigarette ash. Decorators such as Alberto Pinto, Chahan Minassian and Caroline Sarkozy have commissioned his work, which includes lustrous large-scale mirrors and Jean-Michel Frank-inspired glass fireplaces, and which is now available in America through the New York design shop Maison Gerard.', 'print_section': 'M2', 'print_page': '110', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/15/t-magazine/15womens-look-lopez/15womens-look-lopez-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/02/15/t-magazine/15womens-look-lopez/15womens-look-lopez-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/15/t-magazine/15womens-look-lopez/15womens-look-lopez-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/15/t-magazine/15womens-look-lopez/15womens-look-lopez-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1000, 'width': 1500, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/15/t-magazine/15womens-look-lopez/15womens-look-lopez-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/02/15/t-magazine/15womens-look-lopez/15womens-look-lopez-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/15/t-magazine/15womens-look-lopez/15womens-look-lopez-thumbLarge