w York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Annie Correal and Andy Newman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Annie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Correal', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Andy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Newman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c67029b1-ad44-52ab-8a72-729e7418af62', 'word_count': 843, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c67029b1-ad44-52ab-8a72-729e7418af62'}, {'abstract': 'The French president said that the country would fight Islamic radicalism, train imams and reinforce the curriculum in schools to foster a stronger sense of civic identity.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/02/06/world/europe/hollande-vows-to-defend-frances-republican-ideals.html', 'snippet': 'The French president said that the country would fight Islamic radicalism, train imams and reinforce the curriculum in schools to foster a stronger sense of civic identity.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PARIS — President François Hollande of France on Thursday sought to reassure a nation still shaken by the recent terrorist attacks in and around Paris, saying that the country would not be cowed by terrorists and would defend its republican ideals of liberty and free expression against those who sought to undermine them.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/05/blogs/05WATCHING-hollande/05WATCHING-hollande-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/02/05/blogs/05WATCHING-hollande/05WATCHING-hollande-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/05/blogs/05WATCHING-hollande/05WATC