ster said it was an effort to make good on pledges to “make life easier for Iraqis in liberated areas.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/02/06/world/middleeast/overnight-curfew-to-be-canceled-in-baghdad.html', 'snippet': 'A spokesman for Iraq’s prime minister said it was an effort to make good on pledges to “make life easier for Iraqis in liberated areas.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'BAGHDAD — Seeking to normalize life in the embattled capital, Iraq’s prime minister said on Thursday that the authorities would lift a nighttime curfew in Baghdad that has been in force, with some interruptions, for over a decade.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Decade-Long Night Curfew to Be Lifted in Baghdad', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Curfew, in Place for Decade, to Be Lifted in Baghdad', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Fahim, Kareem', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iraq', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Abadi, Haider al-', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Curfews', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Baghdad (Iraq)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Islamic State in Iraq and Syria (ISIS)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-02-05T14:39:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kareem Fahim', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kareem', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fahim', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3c1af202-be52-51c7-bcd1-f87e5e715143', 'word_count': 309, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3c1af202-be52-51c7-bcd1-f87e5e715143'}, {'abstract': 'In Berlin, as in Frankfurt, Greece’s new finance minister receives few signs that creditors are open to renegotiating his country’s bailout loans.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/02/06/business/international/finance-ministers-for-greece-and-germany-find-little-commonality.html', 'snippet': 'In Berlin, as in Frankfurt, Greece’s new finance minister receives few signs that creditors are open to renegotiating his country’s bailout loans.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BERLIN — An attempt by Greece to shift the country’s debt narrative away from austerity ran into a wall of inflexibility during a two-day trip to Germany.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/06/business/06eugreece-web/06eugreece-web-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 384, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/02/06/business/06eugreece-web/06eugreece-web-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 384}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/06/business/06eugreece-web/06eugreece-web-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 656, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/06/business/06eugreece-web/06eugreece-web-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1312, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/06/business/06eugreece-web/06eugreece-web-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/02/06/business/06eugreece-web/06eugreece-web-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}},