gs.nytimes.com/2015/02/05/1915-germans-threaten-shipping/', 'snippet': 'Highlight from the International Herald Tribune archives: Germany “declares war” on neutral commerce in 1915.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON — Amplifying its programme of attempting to torpedo hospital ships and sink merchantmen without warning and without giving a chance to their non- combatants aboard to escape, Germany has now issued the following amazing proclamation, which is in effect a declaration of war on the neutral commerce, and therefore on the neutral nations of the world: ‘‘The seas surrounding Great Britain and Ireland, including the whole of the English Channel, are hereby declared to be a military zone. On and after February 18, the merchant shipping of the belligerent nations navigating these waters will be destroyed, even when it may not be possible to preserve the crews and passengers from danger.’’ — The New York Herald, European Edition, Feb. 6, 1915', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '1915: Germans Threaten Shipping', 'kicker': 'IHT Retrospective', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Ships and Shipping', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'World War I (1914-18)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Germany', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-02-05T15:32:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By International Herald Tribune', 'person': [{'firstname': 'International', 'middlename': 'Herald', 'lastname': 'Tribune', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8ea995df-2818-58f9-99db-68deae5c3ea0', 'word_count': 123, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8ea995df-2818-58f9-99db-68deae5c3ea0'}, {'abstract': 'Before Sam Smith can b