ials continue to say they think the drug should be illegal, and that they won’t consider rescheduling it even though it’s in the same category as heroin. The nominee for attorney general, Loretta Lynch, suggested at her confirmation hearing that marijuana was more dangerous than alcohol, an opinion that goes against available evidence.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '‘Marijuana Can Be Helpful,’ Admits Surgeon General', 'kicker': 'Taking Note', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Marijuana', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Surgeon General (US)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-02-05T18:23:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Juliet Lapidos', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Juliet', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lapidos', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2cceaf96-edf1-5bce-b211-61161d11341f', 'word_count': 214, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2cceaf96-edf1-5bce-b211-61161d11341f'}, {'abstract': 'The 70-year-old former glam rocker, whose real name is Paul Gadd, was found guilty of sexually abusing three girls decades ago and could spend the rest of his life in prison.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/02/06/world/europe/singer-gary-glitter-convicted-of-sexual-abuse-in-britain.html', 'snippet': 'The 70-year-old former glam rocker, whose real name is Paul Gadd, was found guilty of sexually abusing three girls decades ago and could spend the rest of his life in prison.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON — The former glam rocker Gary Glitter was found guilty on Thursday of sexually abusing three young girls decades ago, and he could spend the rest of his life in prison.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '9', 's