ating and Relationships', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-02-05T20:00:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Styles', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Daniel Jones', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Daniel', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Jones', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5b525eb8-cc19-57ac-860f-dfe4a90de76d', 'word_count': 1371, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5b525eb8-cc19-57ac-860f-dfe4a90de76d'}, {'abstract': 'A new bill would improve access to family planning counseling.', 'web_url': 'https://takingnote.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/02/05/contraceptive-coverage-for-women-in-the-military/', 'snippet': 'A new bill would improve access to family planning counseling.', 'lead_paragraph': '“We owe female service members the same access to contraception and family planning services as the women they fight to protect,” said Representative Jackie Speier of California, summing up the principle behind a bill she and another Democrat, Senator Jeanne Shaheen of New Hampshire, introduced on Wednesday.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Contraceptive Coverage for Women in the Military', 'kicker': 'Taking Note', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Birth Control and Family Planning', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Shaheen, Jeanne', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Speier, Jackie', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-02-05T20:04:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dorothy J. Samuels', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dorothy', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'Samuels', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization':