t://article/3afd65cd-428b-5aac-a44b-e2e4fa640907'}, {'abstract': 'As the National Gallery essentially digests the Corcoran Gallery, the process is unlike anything an American museum has undertaken before.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/02/06/arts/design/corcoran-gallery-art-transforms-national-gallery.html', 'snippet': 'As the National Gallery essentially digests the Corcoran Gallery, the process is unlike anything an American museum has undertaken before.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — In the six months since a court allowed the Corcoran Gallery of Art here to dissolve, a victim of financial struggles, about 17,000 works in the museum’s overall collection — by masters like Degas, Sargent, Albert Bierstadt and Cy Twombly — have been in a highly unusual institutional limbo. Their fate is being adjudicated by a group of veteran curators from the National Gallery of Art, which agreed last February to bring as many Corcoran pieces under the museum’s own roof as appropriate and to help find homes for others in Washington-area public collections.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '29', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Corcoran Gallery Art Transforms National Gallery', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'In Death, a Gallery Reshapes Another', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Corcoran Gallery of Art', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Gallery of Art', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Museums', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Washington (DC)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-02-05T20:24:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Art & Design', 'byline': {'original': 'By Randy Kennedy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Randy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kennedy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/543308fa-17a0-5336-b220-50e1d5c4c52c', 'word_count': 1500, 'uri': 'nyt://article/543308fa-17a0-5336-b220-50e1d5c4c52c'}, {'abstract': '“Gang of Seven,” Mike Nelson’s exhibition at 303 Gallery, includes works made from driftwood, skulls and other items found off the coast of British Columbia.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/02/06/arts/design/mike-nelson-gang-of-seven.html', 'snippet': '“Gang of Seven,” Mike Nelson’s exhibition at 303 Gallery, includes works made from driftwood, skulls and other items found off the coast of British Columbia.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The British artist and two-time Turner Prize nominee Mike Nelson has filled the spacious 303 Gallery with a lively crowd of lyrical sculptural assemblages made of flotsam and jetsam collected from the coastal waters of British Columbia. (The exhibition’s title, “Gang of Seven,” refers to a collective of early-20th-century Canadian landscape painters known as the Group of Seven.) They’re made of bottles, driftwood, chunks of plastic foam, lengths of frayed rope, bald tires, pieces of rusted iron, animal skulls and many other sorts of detritus.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '31', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/06/arts/06MIKENELSONGALLERY5/MIKENELSON-GALLERY5-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 789, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/02/06/arts/06MIKENELSONGALLERY5/MIKENELSON-GALLERY5-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 789}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/06/arts/06MIKENELSONGALLERY5/MIKENELSON-GALLERY5-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 779, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/06/arts/06MIKENELSONGALLERY5/MIKENELSON-GALLERY5-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1557, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/06/arts/06MIKENELSONGALLERY5/MIKENELSON-GALLERY5-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/02/06/arts/06MIKENELSONGALLERY5/MIKENELSON-GALLERY5-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/06/arts/06MIKENELSONGALLERY5/MIKENELSON-GALLERY5-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Mike Nelson: ‘Gang of Seven’', 'kicker': 'Art in Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Mike Nelson', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Nelson, Mike', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-02-05T20:27:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Art & Design', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ken Johnson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ken', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Johnson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/5ff1c590-a0f1-5581-99df-f273e851e951', 'word_count': 267, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5ff1c590-a0f1-5581-99df-f273e851e951'}, {'abstract': 'In honor of Valentine’s Day, we debut our first guest pinner.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/02/05/t-pinterest-aerin-lauder-valentines-day/', 'snippet': 'In honor of Valentine’s Day, we debut our first guest pinner.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In honor of Valentine’s Day, Aerin Lauder donned her rosiest lenses to curate a Pinterest board exclusively for T. It’s filled with inspired objects, delectable eats and swoonworthy fashion —\xa0all things pink, red, heart-shaped and sweet. Lauder, T’s first guest pinner — whose own eponymous lifestyle label just released a new rose-scented parfum in time for the holiday — shows that from the runway to the kitchen, love really is all around us.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/05/t-magazine/5beddie_pinterest/5beddie_pinterest-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/02/05/t-magazine/5beddie_pinterest/5beddie_pinterest-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/05/t-magazine/5beddie_pinterest/5beddie_pinterest-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/05/t-magazine/5beddie_pinterest/5beddie_pinterest-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1333, 'width': 2000, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/05/t-magazine/5beddie_pinterest/5beddie_pinterest-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/02/05/t-magazine/5beddie_pinterest/5beddie_pinterest-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/05/t-magazine/5beddie_pinterest/5beddie_pinterest-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'T’s Newest Pinterest Board: Full of Love, Courtesy of Aerin Lauder', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': "Valentine's Day", 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lauder, Aerin', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Pinterest', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'T: The New York Times Style Magazine', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-02-05T20:30:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By T Magazine', 'person': [{'firstname': '', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4df8cca6-036c-5ef9-b4b1-9abcb1e3e6a3', 'word_count': 116, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4df8cca6-036c-5ef9-b4b1-9abcb1e3e6a3'}, {'abstract': 'Three moving-image installations by James Benning and Peter Hutton make up “Nature Is a Discipline.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/02/06/arts/design/james-benning-and-peter-hutton-nature-is-a-discipline.html', 'snippet': 'Three moving-image installations by James Benning and Peter Hutton make up “Nature Is a Discipline.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'In the 1990s and 2000s, when celluloid film was being eclipsed by digital technology, there was an efflorescence of 16-millimeter film installations, with loud projectors and richly colored images, and a revival of interest in deceased pioneers like Paul Sharits and Hollis Frampton. One thing curiously absent — at least in galleries — was work by living artists revealing how they had (or hadn’t) made the switch from film to video.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '31', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/06/arts/06BENNINGHUTTON2GALLERY7/06BENNINGHUTTON2GALLERY7-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 451, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/02/06/arts/06BENNINGHUTTON2GALLERY7/06BENNINGHUTTON2GALLERY7-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 451}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/06/arts/06BENNINGHUTTON2GALLERY7/06BENNINGHUTTON2GALLERY7-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 769, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/06/arts/06BENNINGHUTTON2GALLERY7/06BENNINGHUTTON2GALLERY7-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1539, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/06/arts/06BENNINGHUTTON2GALLERY7/06BENNINGHUTTON2GALLERY7-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/02/06/arts/06BENNINGHUTTON2GALLERY7/06BENNINGHUTTON2GALLERY7-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/06/arts/06BENNINGHUTTON2GALLERY7/06BENNINGHUTTON2GALLERY7-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'James Benning and Peter Hutton: ‘Nature Is a Discip