: 'The New Museum’s Triennial show focuses on artists for whom the Internet is the air they breathe and the world they see.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It is early 2009. Hope and change are in the air. President Obama stands before the camera delivering his Inaugural Address, but within seconds something seems off. The speech is not the pragmatic one he gave on that cold January day but a fiery message in which he excoriates “peddlers of hate whose stock-in-trade is xenophobia, homophobia, racism, sexism and isolationism, and who define America by our differences rather than our common bonds.”', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Where Virtual Equals Real ', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Where Virtual Equals Real', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New Museum of Contemporary Art', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kline, Josh', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Trecartin, Ryan', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cornell, Lauren (1978- )', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-02-05T21:50:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Art & Design', 'byline': {'original': 'By Randy Kennedy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Randy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kennedy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6e5d7409-0f19-5bfa-a707-9e581117f02a', 'word_count': 1797, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6e5d7409-0f19-5bfa-a707-9e581117f02a'}, {'abstract': 'Andrew Napier’s “Mad as Hell,” a documentary about the commentator Cenk Uygur, takes an admiring approach toward his combative style and political philosophy.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/02/06/movies/mad-as-hell-a-documentary-about-the-pundit-cenk-uygur.html', 'snippet': 'Andrew Napier’s “Mad as Hell,” a documentary about the commentator Cenk Uygur, takes an admiring approach toward his combative style and political philosophy.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Andrew Napier’s “Mad as Hell” takes its title from Howard Beale’s famous rant in “Network” exhorting viewers to vent their anger. But the reference sets the stakes a little high: Will this documentary about the political pundit Cenk Uygur have as much to say about the media as Sidney Lumet’s 1976 classic, “Network,” did?', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Righteous Ranter, Howling at Left and Right ', 'kicker': 'Movie Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Mad as Hell', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rapold, Nicolas', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Napier, Andrew (1988- )', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Mad As Hell (Movie)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Uygur, Cenk', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Documentary Films and Programs', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-02-05T21:57:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nicolas Rapold', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nicolas', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rapold', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/1ec19a10-2729-5af0-b688-933c025d5e65', 'word_count': 257, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1ec19a10-2729-5af0-b688-933c025d5e65'}, {'abstract': 'A new study receives widespread attention, but its conclusions are based on the deaths of only 17 runners.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/02/06/upshot/no-more-running-probably-isnt-bad-for-you.html', 'snippet': 'A new study receives widespread attention, but its conclusions are based on the deaths of only 17 runners.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Don’t run less hard. Don’t run less often. Don’t run less distance. And don’t be persuaded by underpowered medical studies — a habit that really could harm your health.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/06/upshot/06UP-Sample/06UP-Sample-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 375, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/02/06/upshot/06UP-Sample/06UP-Sample-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 375}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/06/upshot/06UP-Sample/06UP-Sample-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 640, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/06/upshot/06UP-Sample/06UP-Sample-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1279, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/06/upshot/06UP-Sample/06UP-Sample-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/02/06/upshot/06UP-Sample/06UP-Sample-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/06/upshot/06UP-Sample/06UP-Sample-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'l