fier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/c38e62e1-db24-5c80-bef1-998468634246', 'word_count': 280, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c38e62e1-db24-5c80-bef1-998468634246'}, {'abstract': 'Refsnyder, a second baseman in the Yankees’ farm system, may become an even greater inspiration to adopted children and adoptive parents if he reaches the kind of success he and the Yankees expect.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/02/06/sports/baseball/on-deck-for-the-yankees-from-south-korea-rob-refsnyder.html', 'snippet': 'Refsnyder, a second baseman in the Yankees’ farm system, may become an even greater inspiration to adopted children and adoptive parents if he reaches the kind of success he and the Yankees expect.', 'lead_paragraph': 'TAMPA, Fla. — At the end of all those baseball showcases in Orange County, Calif., the format would often be the same. Few of the coaches and children who had come together for the day knew one another. The director would stand in front of the players and call out the names of those who had excelled that day: the best fielder, the best arm, the best hitter.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'On Deck for the Yankees, From South Korea, Rob Refsnyder', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Impressing Yanks, and Inspiring Adoptees', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Waldstein, David', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Refsnyder, Robert (1991- )', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ADOPTIONS', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'South Korea', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Yankees', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '