k” astonishes most by its appearance in an actual theater. But it’s February, and pickings are slim, so this soulless, sterile romantic comedy has slipped under the wire to give audiences a headache and Matt LeBlanc’s reputation a relapse.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/06/arts/LOVESICK/LOVESICK-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 776, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/02/06/arts/LOVESICK/LOVESICK-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 776}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/06/arts/LOVESICK/LOVESICK-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 792, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/06/arts/LOVESICK/LOVESICK-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1185, 'width': 916, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/06/arts/LOVESICK/LOVESICK-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/02/06/arts/LOVESICK/LOVESICK-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/06/arts/LOVESICK/LOVESICK-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'He’s Smitten, and That’s the Problem', 'kicker': 'Movie Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Lovesick', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Matheny, Luke (1976- )', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'LeBlanc, Matt', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Larter, Ali', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'LovesIck (Movie)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-02-05T22:29:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jeannette Catsoulis', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jeannette', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Catsoulis', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/56c31a85-c04a-52a1-8bad-ea290c801f5f', 'word_count': 252, 'uri': 'nyt://article/56c31a85-c04a-52a1-8bad-ea290c801f5f'}, {'abstract': 'Mexico City’s most established art fair, Zona Maco, kicked off last night and is accompanied by several smaller, hipper fairs elsewhere in the city.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/02/05/zona-maco-mexico-city-art-fairs/', 'snippet': 'Mexico City’s most established art fair, Zona Maco, kicked off last night and is accompanied by several smaller, hipper fairs elsewhere in the city.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On the heels of Los Angeles’s expanding art week, sun-chasing aesthetes push south to Mexico City’s Distrito Federal for Zona Maco and all the festivities organized around the city’s most established art fair. The main event was inaugurated last night at the Centro Banamex, an imposing conference complex on the outskirts of the posh northern regions of the city. Now on view to the public until Sunday, the fair counts David Zwirner, Zurich’s Mai 36, Bogotá’s Casas Riegner and local heavyweights like Kurimanzutto, Labor and OMR among its exhibitors. With sections siloed for new galleries, the southern hemisphere, modern art and design, Maco models itself after the department-store variety of mega-events like Art Basel and Frieze, where all of the visitors’ shopping needs are met under the roof of one neighborhood-sized building.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/05/t-magazine/05mexico-mcgarry/05mexico-mcgarry-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 399, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/02/05/t-magazine/05mexico-mcgarry/05mexico-mcgarry-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 399}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/05/t-magazine/05mexico-mcgarry/05mexico-mcgarry-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 681, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/05/t-magazine/05mexico-mcgarry/05mexico-mcgarry-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1363, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/05/t-magazine/05mexico-mcgarry/05mexico-mcgarry-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/02/05/t-magazine/05mexico-mcgarry/05mexico-mcgarry-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/05/t-magazine/05mexico-mcgarry/05mexico-mcgarry-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Art Fair Scene Heads South of the Border', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None},