r identity at the center of almost every conversation.', 'lead_paragraph': '“Boy Meets Girl,” or — as the subtitle should say, “Everything You Always Wanted to Know About Being Transgender” — is a romantic comedy that’s so progressive it hurts. Placing sex and gender identity at the center of almost every conversation, the writer and director, Eric Schaeffer, is so keen to demythologize that the film’s potentially most affecting moments are too often smothered by the hackneyed characters and setups that surround them.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/06/arts/06BOYMEETS/BOYMEETS-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 322, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/02/06/arts/06BOYMEETS/BOYMEETS-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 322}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/06/arts/06BOYMEETS/BOYMEETS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 549, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/06/arts/06BOYMEETS/BOYMEETS-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1099, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/06/arts/06BOYMEETS/BOYMEETS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/02/06/arts/06BOYMEETS/BOYMEETS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/06/arts/06BOYMEETS/BOYMEETS-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150