_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Investigation Finds Problems With Work on New York City 911 System', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Investigation of Problems With Work on 911 System', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Nine-One-One (911) (Emergency Phone Number)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Government Employees', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Department of Investigation (NYC)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-02-06T05:10:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nikita Stewart', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nikita', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Stewart', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/930cf061-bf57-56b0-8994-f400bc61bb98', 'word_count': 584, 'uri': 'nyt://article/930cf061-bf57-56b0-8994-f400bc61bb98'}, {'abstract': 'Television highlights.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/02/06/arts/whats-on-tv-friday.html', 'snippet': 'Television highlights.', 'lead_paragraph': '9 P.M. (13) SHAKESPEARE UNCOVERED Morgan Freeman, who played Petruchio in “The Taming of the Shrew” in the Public Theater’s 1990 Shakespeare in the Park production, looks at some famous Petruchios (Richard Burton, John Cleese and Raul Julia) and Kates (Elizabeth Taylor, Fiona Shaw, Sinead Cusack and Meryl Streep) and reunites with his own sparring partner, Tracey Ullman (above with Mr. Freeman). Julia Stiles reflects on her role in the 1999 teenage comedy adaptation of the work, “10 Things I Hate About You.” And the Royal Shakespeare Company takes the play to a school near where Shakespeare grew up to find out what children make of the adult shenanigans. At 10, David Harewood, the first black actor to star in the title role of “Othello” at the National Theater in London, looks at the history behind the play; talks to Adrian Lester, the National Theater’s latest Othello, about the reaction to the 1825 performance of Ira Aldridge, the first black man to play the role in Britain; and ponders Laurence Olivier’s use of blackface in his acclaimed film portrayal in 1965.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '27', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What’s On TV Friday', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'What’s On TV Friday', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-02-06T05:23:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kathryn Shattuck', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kathryn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shattuck', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Schedule', '_id': 'nyt://article/31109662-d47d-5bca-97ed-621b9e375d43', 'word_count': 717, 'uri': 'nyt://article/31109662-d47d-5bca-97ed-621b9e375d43'}, {'abstract': 'Mr. Rubino accompanied Charles Van Doren, his legal client, to Washington in 1959, when he admitted before a congressional subcommittee that he was fed answers on the NBC show “Twenty-One.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/02/06/nyregion/carl-j-rubino-100-is-dead-served-as-lawyer-in-quiz-show-scandal.html', 'snippet': 'Mr. Rubino accompanied Charles Van Doren, his legal client, to Washington in 1959, when he admitted before a congressional subcommittee that he was fed answers on the NBC show “Twenty-One.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'In October 1959, a tormented 33-year-old named Charles Van Doren returned to his Greenwich Village apartment after driving around New England for days to escape the paparazzi camped on his doorstep. A letter from a complete stranger suggested a self-evident solution to his crisis of conscience: Just tell the truth.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/06/us/05rubino-obit/05rubino-obit-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 501, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/02/06/us/05rubino-obit/05rubino-obit-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 501}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/06/us/05rubino-obit/05rubino-obit-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 855, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/06/us/05rubino-obit/05rubino-obit-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1710, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/06/us/05rubino-obit/05rubino-obit-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/02/06/us/05rubino-obit/05rubino-obit-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/06/us/05rubino-obit/05rubino-obit-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Carl J. Rubino, Lawyer in Quiz-Show Scandal, Dies at 100', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Carl Rubino, 100, Lawyer in Quiz-Show Case, Dies', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Obituaries)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rubino, Carl J (1914-2015)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Van Doren, Charles (1926- )', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-02-06T05:32:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sam Roberts', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Roberts', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Obituary (Obit)', '_id': 'nyt://article/42560850-d26e-5c90-85e3-42707ec59158', 'word_count': 960, 'uri': 'nyt://article/42560850-d26e-5c90-85e3-42707ec59158'}, {'abstract': 'The embattled prime minister urged members of his Liberal Party on Friday to choose “stability” after a junior lawmaker called for a vote to contest him.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/02/07/world/asia/tony-abbott-australian-premier-vows-to-fight-leadership-challenge.html', 'snippet': 'The embattled prime minister urged members of his Liberal Party on Friday to choose “stability” after a junior lawmaker called for a vote to contest him.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SYDNEY, Australia — Australia’s embattled prime minister, Tony Abbott, said Friday that he would fight an attempt to contest his leadership next week, after a junior politician from his conservative Liberal Party called for the vote.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/07/world/07australia02/07australia02-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 404, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/02/07/world/07australia02/07aus