 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/02/06/opinion/a-game-of-chicken.html', 'snippet': 'Europe faces a moment of truth as it deals with a debt-ridden Greece.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On Wednesday, the European Central Bank announced that it would no longer accept Greek government debt as collateral for loans. This move, it turns out, was more symbolic than substantive. Still, the moment of truth is clearly approaching.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '23', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/12/opinion/krugman-circular/krugman-circular-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 591, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/11/12/opinion/krugman-circular/krugman-circular-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 591}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/12/opinion/krugman-circular/krugman-circular-jumbo-v5.jpg', 'height': 1008, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/12/opinion/krugman-circular/krugman-circular-superJumbo-v5.jpg', 'height': 1852, 'width': 1881, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/12/opinion/krugman-circular/krugman-circular-thumbStandard-v5.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/11/12/opinion/krugman-circular/krugman-circular-thumbStandard-v5.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/12/opinion/krugman-circular/krugman-circular-thumbLarge-v7.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Game of Chicken', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Columnist', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Game of Chicken', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Krugman, Paul', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Greece', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Europe', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'European Central Bank', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'European Union', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Germany', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'European Sovereign Debt Crisis (2010- )', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'International Relations', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Merkel, Angela', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-02-06T08:27:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/ac171494-4b43-52b3-afa7-6cb96c1eee90', 'word_count': 806, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ac171494-4b43-52b3-afa7-6cb96c1eee90'}, {'abstract': 'Some of the country’s largest retailers, counting on the stupidity of consumers, are selling dietary-supplement junk, a step removed from sawdust.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/02/06/opinion/the-politics-of-fraudulent-dietary-supplements.html', 'snippet': 'Some of the country’s largest retailers, counting on the stupidity of consumers, are selling dietary-supplement junk, a step removed from sawdust.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SALT LAKE CITY — One pill makes you smarter. One pill makes you thin. One pill makes you happy. Another keeps you energized. And so what if tests conducted by scientists in New York and Canada have found that the substances behind these miracle enhancements may contain nothing more than powdered rice or houseplants. If enough people believe they’ll be healthier, well, it’s a nice racket.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/01/opinion/egan-circular/egan-circular-jumbo-v2.png', 'height': 228, 'width': 228, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/01/opinion/egan-circular/egan-circular-superJumbo-v2.png', 'height': 228, 'width': 228, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/01/opinion/egan-circular/egan-circular-thumbStandard-v2.png', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/11/01/opinion/egan-circular/egan-circular-thumbStandard-v2.png', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/01/opinion/egan-circular/egan-circular-thumbLarge-v4.png', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Stupid Pills', 'kicker': 'Contributing Op-Ed Writer', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dietary Supplements and Herbal Remedies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hatch, Orrin G', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Schneiderman, Eric T', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Utah', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Regulation and Deregulation of Industry', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-02-06T08:27:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Timothy Egan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Timothy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Egan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/def73dec-f34a-547d-8865-431d47e2ba61', 'word_count': 957, 'uri': 'nyt://article/def73dec-f34a-547d-8865-431d47e2ba61'}, {'abstract': 'Don’t try to punish them. Just make getting an exemption harder.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/02/06/opinion/how-to-handle-the-vaccine-skeptics.html', 'snippet': 'Don’t try to punish them. Just make getting an exemption harder.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ATLANTA — THE alarming number of measles cases — a record 644 last year, and 102 last month, the most since the disease was declared eliminated in the United States in 2000 — has focused scrutiny on parents who refuse vaccinations for their children. There are some who want state and local governments to sue, or even criminally charge, such parents. A bill in California would end all nonmedical exemptions to immunization requirements.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '23', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'How to Handle the Vaccine Skeptics', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Contributor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'How to Handle the Vaccine Skeptics', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Omer, Saad B', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Vaccination and Immunization', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'States (US)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Children and Childhood', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parenting', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Measles', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Law and Legislation', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-02-06T08:27:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Saad B. Omer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Saad', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/f36809a1-f0ba-57e0-b11a-b8dc2e3e917a', 'word_count': 770, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f36809a1-f0ba-57e0-b11a-b8dc2e3e917a'}, {'abstract': 'With global warming, you truly can’t step in the same river twice.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/02/06/opinion/global-warming-changes-everything.html', 'snippet': 'With global warming, you truly can’t step in the same river twice.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SANTIAGO, Chile — I HAVE recently been able to confirm, through sad and indisputable evidence, that Heraclitus was right when he wrote that we can never step into the same river twice. I doubt, of course, that that pre-Socratic philosopher, when coining the phrase two and a half millenniums ago about the implacable flux of time, had in mind the ecological destruction of the planet, the abyss toward which our greed and inability to courageously confront global warming are leading us. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '23', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'captio