web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/02/08/education/edlife/skipping-class-at-harvard.html', 'snippet': 'How many are actually going to lectures.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Secret cameras trained on Harvard lecture halls to study attendance raised quite a stir last fall. To some professors, the research methodology used by the Harvard Initiative for Learning and Teaching clearly invaded the sanctity of the classroom, despite a noble goal: to find out how often students skip lectures. So how hot, or cold, were the seats? Results are out.', 'print_section': 'ED', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/04/education/edlife/edl-08-attendance/edl-08-attendance-jumbo.png', 'height': 315, 'width': 351, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/04/education/edlife/edl-08-attendance/edl-08-attendance-superJumbo.png', 'height': 315, 'width': 351, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/04/education/edlife/edl-08-attendance/edl-08-attendance-thumbStandard.png', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/02/04/education/edlife/edl-08-attendance/edl-08-attendance-thumbStandard.png', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/04/education/edlife/edl-08-attendance/edl-08-attendance-thumbLarge.png', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Skipping Class at Harvard', 'kicker': 'Blackboard', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'And You Thought You Wouldn’t Be Missed!', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Colleges and Universities', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Harvard University', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-02-06T10:45:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'EdLife', 'section_name': 'Education', 'subsection_name': 'Education Life', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e5bdf509-7191-59f7-afc6-6e6bb77e2eed', 'word_count': 61, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e5bdf509-7191-59f7-afc6-6e6bb77e2eed'}, {'abstract': 'Cauliflower is a versatile vegetable that can be marianted, mashed like a potato or smashed into a delicious vegetarian patty, writes Martha Rose Shulman.', 'web_url': 'https://well.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/02/06/cauliflower-marinated-mashed-and-smashed/', 'snippet': 'Cauliflower is a versatile vegetable that can be marianted, mashed like a potato or smashed into a delicious vegetarian patty, writes Martha Rose Shulman.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Cauliflower is a vegetable that I have no qualms about buying on impulse. It keeps very well in the refrigerator – I have made perfectly good meals using florets I found lingering in my produce drawer that had been there for more than a week. Not that I recommend this approach, but it is good to know that you need not use it up right away, especially when you find large heads weighing anywhere from 1 1/2 to 2 pounds. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/31/science/recipehealthwellpromo/recipehealthwellpromo-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/01/31/science/recipehealthwellpromo/recipehealthwellpromo-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0