iginal': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a6794235-45c3-5ecc-a20c-030600e711bc', 'word_count': 133, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a6794235-45c3-5ecc-a20c-030600e711bc'}, {'abstract': 'Chinese state news media reported that an ethnic Kazakh herder had stumbled across an enormous gold nugget, which weighed 17 pounds and was shaped like a map of China.', 'web_url': 'https://sinosphere.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/02/06/chinese-herder-strikes-gold/', 'snippet': 'Chinese state news media reported that an ethnic Kazakh herder had stumbled across an enormous gold nugget, which weighed 17 pounds and was shaped like a map of China.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The mountains of the remote Altay area of northwestern China have a storied history of gold mining. People in the region talk about mines that Russians helped build and operate in the first half of the 20th century. The Russians left the area after the People’s Liberation Army took over the vast Xinjiang region. Altay sits near the borders with Russia, Mongolia and Kazakhstan, and it is a place from which legends travel far.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Herder Strikes Gold, in the Shape of China', 'kicker': 'Sinosphere', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Gold', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cixi, Empress Dowager of China (1835-1908)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Xinjiang (China)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-02-06T11:39:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Edward Wong', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Edward', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wong', 'qualifier': No