/25cover_text-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1683, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/25/magazine/25cover_text/25cover_text-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/01/25/magazine/25cover_text/25cover_text-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/25/magazine/25cover_text/25cover_text-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Reply All: The 1.25.15 Issue', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Reply All: The 1.25.15 Issue', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2015-02-06T11:58:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/781c3302-a469-5aff-ac63-c82255fb149d', 'word_count': 682, 'uri': 'nyt://article/781c3302-a469-5aff-ac63-c82255fb149d'}, {'abstract': 'Trying to undo the damage of our hubris.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/02/08/magazine/can-we-reverse-engineer-the-environment.html', 'snippet': 'Trying to undo the damage of our hubris.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Across the top of the map, above the Arctic’s Mer Glaciale, there floats a banner inscribed with a legend that in translation reads “New Discovery of Many Nations in New France in the years 1673 and 1674.” This legend is a bit misleading. Although the terrestrial features seem to have been distorted by a fun-house mirror, the aquatic features are strikingly recognizable and strikingly out of scale, as if we were peering down through a magnifying glass poised over the Great Lakes. Read the semi-legible calligraphic names along the coasts and riverbanks, and you begin to perceive that this isn’t really a map of North America nor of New France. It’s a navigation chart and a relic of a time when waterways assumed out-of-scale proportions in our geographies.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/08/magazine/08lede1/08mag-08lede.t_CA1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/02/08/magazine/08lede1/08mag-08lede.t_CA1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/08/magazine/08lede1/08mag-08lede.t_CA1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/08/magazine/08lede1/08mag-08lede.t_CA1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1367, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/08/magazine/08lede1/08mag-08lede.t_CA1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/02/08/magazine/08lede1/08mag-08lede.t_CA1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/08/magazine/08lede1/08mag-08lede.t_CA1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Can We Reverse-Engineer the Environment?', 'kicker': 'Essay', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Reverse Engineering', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Engineering and Engineers', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hohn, Donovan', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Invasive Species', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Chicago (Ill)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Environment', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Mississippi River', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Lake Michigan', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Canals', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Great Lakes', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-02-06T11:58:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Donovan Hohn', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Donovan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hohn', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/514433b9-76ba-5367-8b73-1cee9266b118', 'word_count': 1641, 'uri': 'nyt://article/514433b9-76ba-5367-8b73-1cee9266b118'}, {'abstract': 'Defining true agency.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/02/08/magazine/the-hazards-of-other-planets.html', 'snippet': 'Defining true agency.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The company Mars One is trying to establish colonies on Mars by offering one-way trips there within the next 10 years. I’ve gotten into heated debates about the ethical implications of sending people on these trips. Even though the people selected signed up knowing they would never return to Earth, I believe the entire endeavor is unethical because they will not really have a full grasp of what they’ve signed up for until they get to Mars, at w