ear.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BATON ROUGE, La. — In recent weeks, the office of Gov. Bobby Jindal of Louisiana has issued news releases about the “mindless naïveté” of Hillary Rodham Clinton, the folly of opening diplomatic relations with Cuba and the threat of radical Islam in Europe, prompting a flurry of commentary about what it all might mean to Republican voters in Iowa and South Carolina should Mr. Jindal decide, as has long been expected, to run for president.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/07/us/07JINDALWEB/07JINDALWEB-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/02/07/us/07JINDALWEB/07JINDALWEB-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/07/us/07JINDALWEB/07JINDALWEB-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/07/us/07JINDALWEB/07JINDALWEB-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/07/us/07JINDALWEB/07JINDALWEB-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/02/07/us/07JINDALWEB/07JINDALWEB-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/07/us/07JINDALWEB/07JINDALWEB-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'As Jindal’s G.O.P. Profile Grows, So Do Louisiana’s Budget Woes', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'As Jindal’s G.O.P. Profile Grows, So Do Louisiana’s Budget Woes', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jindal, Bobby', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Louisiana', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'State Legislatures', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tax Credits, Deductions and Exemptions', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Budgets and Budgeting', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2016', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-02-06T12:26:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Campbell Robertson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Campbell', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Robertson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a116fc78-3e58-5031-9604-cb7ec96fb017', 'word_count': 1219, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a116fc78-3e58-5031-9604-cb7ec96fb017'}, {'abstract': 'A 10-year-old tournament in Minnesota has grown from a curiosity into a phenomenon, but without a single national champion, the attractions are bragging rights, camaraderie and beer.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/02/07/sports/in-pond-hockey-no-reason-to-have-one-big-fish.html', 'snippet': 'A 10-year-old tournament in Minnesota has grown from a curiosity into a phenomenon, but without a single national champion, the attractions are bragging rights, camaraderie and beer.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MINNEAPOLIS — For one long weekend every January, nearly 1,500 men and women in skates converge on frozen Lake Nokomis to revisit their childhoods. ', 'print_section': 'SP', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'In Pond Hockey, No Reason to Have One Big Fish', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Pond Hockey Doesn’t Need a Big Fish', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hockey, Ice', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Borzi, Pat', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Minneapolis (Minn)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Lakes', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'USA Hockey', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-02-06T12:30:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Hockey', 'byline': {'original': 'By Pat Borzi', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Pat', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Borzi', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fdd624de-e506-5b40-a1bb-5d8be273f0e3', 'word_count': 1165, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fdd624de-e506-5b40-a1bb-5d8be273f0e3'}, {'abstract': 'Even if saying that makes you furious.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/02/06/debt-is-money-we-owe-to-ourselves/', 'snippet': 'Even if saying that makes you furious.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Antonio Fatas, commenting on recent work on deleveraging or the lack thereof, emphasizes one of my favorite points: no, debt does not mean that we’re stealing from future generations. Globally, and for the most part even within countries, a rise in debt isn’t an indication that we’re living beyond our means, because as Fatas puts it, one person’s debt is another person’s asset; or as I equivalently put it, debt is money we owe to ourselves — an obviously true statement that, I have discovered, has the power to induce blinding rage in many people.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Debt Is Money We Owe To Ourselves', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2015-02-06T12:32:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/25e420f1-e03e-5560-b9c4-6ad7338a7bd7', 'word_count': 303, 'uri': 'nyt://article/25e420f1-e03e-5560-b9c4-6ad7338a7bd7'}, {'abstract': 'Mr. Small, a policy researcher at the German Marshall Fund of the United States in Washington, explores China’s ties with Pakistan, past and present, in a new book.', 'web_url': 'https://sinosphere.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/02/06/q-and-a-andrew-small-on-the-china-pakistan-relationship/', 'snippet': 'Mr. Small, a policy researcher at the German Marshall Fund of the United States in Washington, explores China’s ties with Pakistan, past and present, in a new book.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Andrew Small, a policy researcher at the German Marshall Fund of the United States in Washington, explores China’s ties with Pakistan in a new book that delves into the relationship’s history, the Chinese origins of Pakistan’s nuclear weapons, extremism in the two countries and how the future might develop as the United States recedes from Pakistan and Afghanistan.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/05/blogs/05sino-small01/05sino-small01-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 730, 'width': 481, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02