 proved cathartic for its writer-director, Damián Szifron.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Emerging from a bakery where he has just bought a birthday cake for his daughter, a man discovers his car has been towed. At her wedding reception, a bride realizes her new husband has been cheating on her. On an empty highway, the drivers of an Audi and a jalopy jockey for position and insult each other. Each of the six episodes in “Wild Tales,” an Argentine movie nominated for the Oscar for best foreign-language film, begins with a disagreeable incident drawn from daily life — but escalates from there into an almost baroque tale of revenge.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Revenge Tales Drawn from Everyday Indignities', 'kicker': 'Carpetbagger', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Through a Lens Darkly: Foreign Directors on Their Films', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Academy Awards (Oscars)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'ALMODOVAR, PEDRO', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Sony Pictures Entertainment', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'ARGENTINA', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-02-06T14:00:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Larry Rohter', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Larry', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rohter', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a2c95755-c9b4-5507-9b9b-70ae3b204782', 'word_count': 1108, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a2c95755-c9b4-5507-9b9b-70ae3b204782'}, {'abstract': 'The “Sex and the City” alum will premiere “Rasheeda Speaking” with the New Group theater company on Wednesday.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/02/06/cynthia-nixon-rasheeda-speaking-interview/', 'snippet': 'The “Sex and the City” alum will premiere “Rasheeda Speaking” with the New Group theater company on Wednesday.', 'lead_paragraph': 'This Wednesday, Feb. 11, the New Group theater company will open “Rasheeda Speaking,” an exquisitely tense (and often cringingly funny) portrait of racial paranoia in a small doctor’s office, starring the incomparable Tonya Pinkins and Dianne Wiest. The play also marks the directorial debut of the “Sex and the City” veteran Cynthia Nixon, who since the release of the franchise’s second film in 2010 has appeared on Broadway in “Wit” and on TV in “The Big C,” and has crusaded hard for marriage equality and for the election, in 2014, of New York City Mayor Bill de Blasio. Nixon chatted with T about launching her career as a director, the other projects that will keep her busy this year — and, of course, the latest news about Miranda.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/06/t-magazine/06nixon-murphy-1/06nixon-murphy-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 600, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/02/06/t-magazine/06nixon-murphy-1/06nixon-murphy-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 600}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/06/t-magazine/06nixon-murphy-1/06nixon-murphy-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 888, 'width': 888, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/06/t-magazine/06nixon-murphy-1/06nixon-murphy-1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 888, 'width': 888, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/06/t-magazine/06nixon-murphy-1/06nixon-murphy-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/02/06/t-magazine/06nixon-murphy-1/06nixon-murphy-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/06/t-magazine/06nixon-murphy-1/06nixon-murphy-1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Cynthia Nixon on Her Directorial Debut, De Blasio and How Miranda’s Doing These Days', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Race and Ethnicity', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Johnson, Joel Drake', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Nixon, Cynthia', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Pinkins, Tonya', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wiest, Dianne', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New Group Theater Co', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Rasheeda Speaking (Play)', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-02-06T14:00:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tim Murphy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tim', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Murphy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f1425f34-1c59-5698-9109-ebe8a50f5856