Good news in today’s jobs report, and the dollar shot higher. But a stronger dollar will make US goods less competitive, and act as a brake on further recovery. So how do we think about this? How much of the US recovery will be diffused to other countries via dollar strength and a bigger trade deficit?', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Dollar and the Recovery (Wonkish)', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2015-02-06T16:00:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e9b774dd-a7da-5af2-9a74-59b65d7f0ed8', 'word_count': 715, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e9b774dd-a7da-5af2-9a74-59b65d7f0ed8'}, {'abstract': 'When making chocolate confections, let luscious be the beacon. Then bump up the chocolate content. (Article plus video.)', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/02/11/dining/recipes-for-chocolate-pudding-poundcake-and-icebox-cake.html', 'snippet': 'When making chocolate confections, let luscious be the beacon. Then bump up the chocolate content. (Article plus video.)', 'lead_paragraph': 'I once baked heart-shaped chocolate shortbreads for my sweetie at the time. The cookies were a recipe of my own invention — crisp, crumbly, seasoned with sea salt and near-black cocoa powder, and utterly delicious. ', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Bittersweet Kiss of Chocolate ', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Bittersweet Kiss of Chocolate', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Clark, Melissa', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cooking and Cookbooks', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Chocolate', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Pudding', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Recipes', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cakes', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-02-06T16:06:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'By Melissa Clark', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Melissa', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Clark', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1af057eb-bca3-5bf9-a517-e1a0a106b0dd', 'word_count': 488, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1af057eb-bca3-5bf9-a517-e1a0a106b0dd'}, {'abstract': 'Len Rix, who translated Magda Szabo’s novel “The Door,” decided to pick up Hungarian at the age of 47.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/02/08/books/review/translating-in-tongues.html', 'snippet': 'Len Rix, who translated Magda Szabo’s novel “The Door,” decided to pick up Hungarian at the age of 47.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Hungarian language, or Magyar, is notoriously difficult to learn for nonnative speakers: Meanings are tucked away in multiple suffixes; word order often has more to do with context than predictable rules of syntax; and as part of the Finno-Ugric language group, Hungarian has few linguistic relatives.', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/08/books/review/08openbook/08openbook-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 225, 'width': 510, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'ima