'nyt://article/f8b058d1-c4c0-58f2-b4f2-2e6daec30cf6'}, {'abstract': 'Three senators sent letters to the Federal Trade Commission and the Federal Communications Commission, saying that the tracking technology may violate consumers’ privacy and asking regulators to investigate Verizon’s practices.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/02/06/lawmakers-call-for-investigation-into-verizons-use-of-mobile-supercookies/', 'snippet': 'Three senators sent letters to the Federal Trade Commission and the Federal Communications Commission, saying that the tracking technology may violate consumers’ privacy and asking regulators to investigate Verizon’s practices.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Three Democratic lawmakers on the influential Senate Committee on Commerce, Science and Transportation are calling on federal regulators to investigate Verizon for its practice of using unique customer codes to track the online activities of its wireless subscribers. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/06/business/06bits-mcadam/06bits-mcadam-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 528, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/02/06/business/06bits-mcadam/06bits-mcadam-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 528}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/06/business/06bits-mcadam/06bits-mcadam-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 902, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/06/business/06bits-mcadam/06bits-mcadam-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1804, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/06/business/06bits-mcadam/06bits-mcadam-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/02/06/business/06bits-mcadam/06bits-mcadam-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/06/business/06bits-mcadam/06bits-mcadam-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Lawmakers Call for Investigation Into Verizon’s Use of Mobile ‘Supercookies’', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Privacy', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Telephones and Telecommunications', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wireless Communications', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Federal Communications Commission', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Federal Trade Commission', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Verizon Communications Inc', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-02-06T16:25:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Natasha Singer and Brian X. Chen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Natasha', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Singer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Brian', 'middlename': 'X.', 'lastname': 'Chen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8f3232b7-89e1-585c-b190-b4b95854595a', 'word_count': 441, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8f3232b7-89e1-585c-b190-b4b95854595a'}, {'abstract': 'On Saturday, voters in New Delhi are due to elect their 70-member legislative assembly.', 'web_url': 'https://takingnote.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/02/06/can-narendra-modi-keep-his-clout/', 'snippet': 'On Saturday, voters in New Delhi are due to elect their 70-member legislative assembly.', 'lead_paragraph': 'NEW DELHI – Narendra Modi became India’s prime minister after his Bharatiya Janata Party won a parliamentary election in May, crushing the Indian National Congress that had controlled Indian politics for most of the past 60 years. \xa0Propelled by his popularity, the BJP then extended its mandate by sweeping a succession of state elections.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Can Narendra Modi Keep Winning?', 'kicker': 'Taking Note', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kejriwal, Arvind', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Modi, Narendra', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Bharatiya Janata Party', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Indian National Congress', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'India', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-02-06T16:25:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Carol Giacomo', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Carol', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Giacomo', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8e873a54-1a61-5be8-8e5d-2c0fd11fc776', 'word_count': 469, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8e873a54-1a61-5be8-8e5d-2c0fd11fc776'}, {'abstract': 'Bernard Wilhelm opens a show at MOCA, in which he presents his fall/winter 2015 collection.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/02/06/bernhard-willhelm-moca-exhibit/', 'snippet': 'Bernard Wilhelm opens a show at MOCA, in which he presents his fall/winter 2015 collection.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The German designer Bernhard Willhelm may have grown up near the Bauhaus stronghold Ulm School of Design, where lecturers included Mies van der Rohe and Buckminster Fuller, but he’s since become the fashion world’s champion of form following a different sort of function. In Willhelm’s hands, geometric cuts and experimental textiles explore not utility, but the sometimes messy rules of attraction —\xa0and he’s quick to cite the adage that we put on clothes hoping someone else will take them off later. “I think if you have sex with somebody it’s very, very important that you have a little laugh together,” says Willhelm, noting that he was the first cover boy for the magazine Butt. “When sex gets too serious it’s unbearable, and that’s the same with sexy fashion.” This good-humored dedication to liberation is on full display in Willhelm’s exhibition “When Fashion Shows the Danger Then Fashion Is the Danger,” co-conceived with his longtime collaborator Jutta Kraus, and opening this weekend at the\xa0Museum of Contemporary Art in Los Angeles.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/06/t-magazine/06bernard-wu/06bernard-wu-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/02/06/t-magazine/06bernard-wu/06bernard-wu-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/06/t-magazine/06bernard-wu/06bernard-wu-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/06/t-magazine/06bernard-wu/06bernard-wu-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/06/t-magazine/06bernard-wu/06bernard-wu-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/02/06/t-magazine/06bernard-wu/06bernard-wu-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/06/t-magazine/06bernard-wu/06bernard-wu-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Fashion Designer Stages an Erotic Exhibition in Lieu of a Runway', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Design', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Willhelm, Bernhard', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Los Angeles Museum of Contemporary Art', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Los Angeles (Calif)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-02-06T16:30:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Su Wu', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Su', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wu', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/65ae4596-da34-51e5-9c56-2153a0b50ff1', 'word_count': 494, 'uri': 'nyt://article/65ae4596-da34-51e5-9c56-2153a0b50ff1'}, {'abstract': 'Highlights from the International Herald Tribune archives: A Canadian ship was lost in the war in 1940.', 'web_url': 'https://iht-retrospective.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/02/06/1940-canadian-ship-torpedoed/', 'snippet': 'Highlights from the International Herald Tribune archives: A Canadian ship was lost in the war in 1940.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON — The first Canadian ship of the war to be lost, the 9,874-ton Beaverburn, of the Canadian Pacific Steamship Company, was torpedoed by a German submarine off the southern coast of Ireland today [Feb. 6]. Other ships in the vicinity hurried to the scene and rescued all but one of the seventy-seven members of the crew. Constructed in 1928, the Beaverburn was one of the fastest Canadian freighters and carried the most modern equipement for fruit refrigeration. Its attacker was believed to be the same submarine unofficially reported in the trans-Atlantic shipping lane off Cornwall peninsula. Fifty-four members of the 100-man crew of the 875-ton British minesweeper Sphinx were lost when it foundered yesterday as it was being towed to port, after having been attacked by German planes. The captain and four seamen were killed during the attack and the other forty-nine were drowned. During the week ending February 5, eight British merchant-ships, totaling 25,069 tons, and six neutral ships totaling 17,546 tons, were lost by enemy action. — New York Herald Tribune, European Edition, Feb. 7, 1940', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/07/blogs/07iht-oldfeb07-ship/07iht-oldfeb07-ship-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 366, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/02/07/blogs/07iht-oldfeb07-ship/07iht-oldfeb07-ship-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 366}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/07/blogs/07ih