'uri': 'nyt://article/6c6b0cfa-9cf8-5068-a2b4-e4aae316d35f'}, {'abstract': 'This week, Adelle Waldman discusses Clancy Martin’s “Love and Lies”; Alexandra Alter has news from the publishing world; Dana Goldstein talks about Anya Kamenetz’s “The Test”; and Gregory Cowles has best-seller news. Pamela Paul is the host.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/audio/2015/02/06/books/review/08books_pod.html', 'snippet': 'This week, Adelle Waldman discusses Clancy Martin’s “Love and Lies”; Alexandra Alter has news from the publishing world; Dana Goldstein talks about Anya Kamenetz’s “The Test”; and Gregory Cowles has best-seller news. Pamela Paul is the host.', 'lead_paragraph': 'This week, Adelle Waldman discusses Clancy Martin’s “Love and Lies”; Alexandra Alter has news from the publishing world; Dana Goldstein talks about Anya Kamenetz’s “The Test”; and Gregory Cowles has best-seller news. Pamela Paul is the host.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Inside The New York Times Book Review: ‘Love and Lies’', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-02-06T16:41:24+0000', 'document_type': 'audio', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Books', 'subsection_name': 'Book Review', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://audio/7d4ac4b0-066e-59b5-817a-911103ec3daa', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://audio/7d4ac4b0-066e-59b5-817a-911103ec3daa'}, {'abstract': 'The Islamic State said Friday that Jordanian bombings in Syria intended to avenge the immolation of a captured pilot had killed an American hostage, Kayla Mueller, who was held by the group.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/02/07/world/middleeast/isis-claims-american-hostage-killed-by-jordanian-retaliation-bombings.html', 'snippet': 'The Islamic State said Friday that Jordanian bombings in Syria intended to avenge the immolation of a captured pilot had killed an American hostage, Kayla Mueller, who was held by the group.', 'lead_paragraph': 'She had always been the unidentified, lone female American hostage of the Islamic State. For nearly 17 months, while her fellow American captives were beheaded one after another in serial executions posted on YouTube, Kayla Mueller’s name remained a closely guarded secret, whispered among reporters, government officials and hostage negotiators — all fearing that any public mention might imperil her life.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/07/world/HOSTAGE/HOSTAGE-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 714, 'width': 457, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/07/world/HOSTAGE/HOSTAGE-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 714, 'width': 457, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/07/world/HOSTAGE/HOSTAGE-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/02/07/world/HOSTAGE/HOSTAGE-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/07/world/HOSTAGE/HOSTAGE-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'ISIS Declares Airstrike Killed a U.S. Hostage', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'ISIS Declares Airstrike Killed a U.S. Woman', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Islamic State in Iraq and Syria (ISIS)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mueller, Kayla (1988-2015)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Kidnapping and Hostages', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Jordan', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Syria', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-02-06T16:51:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rukmini Callimachi and Rick Gladstone', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rukmini', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Callimachi', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Rick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gladstone', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6822bece-42d9-588b-9d3e-6751a5357b9c', 'word_count': 1386, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6822bece-42d9-588b-9d3e-6751a5357b9c'}, {'abstract': 'After an audit revealed a questionable $12 million surplus, a company hired a law firm to help it get rid of the money by giving it away.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/02/07/your-money/finding-the-right-way-to-dispose-of-ill-gotten-gains.html', 'snippet': 'After an audit revealed a questionable $12 million surplus, a company hired a law firm to help it get rid of the money by giving it away.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SEVERAL years ago, a large European company asked Thomas M. DiBiagio to run an internal audit on its South African operations. The company suspected that something might be amiss. And it was right. In the course of the audit, he discovered about $12 million that might best be described as ill-gotten gains.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'ra