 representative, Michael B. Froman, a Harvard Law School classmate of President Obama’s, is scrambling to complete the one big deal that appears ripe for compromise between Republicans and Democrats — the Trans-Pacific Partnership with a dozen countries from Canada to New Zealand. The deal, being negotiated, forms the core of Mr. Obama’s much-promoted “pivot” toward Asia.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Politics of Trade: The Top U.S. Negotiator Answers 10 Questions ', 'kicker': 'Q. and A.', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Politics of Trade: The Top U.S. Negotiator Answers 10 Questions', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'International Trade and World Market', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Harwood, John', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Trans-Pacific Partnership', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Froman, Michael B', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-02-06T19:37:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By John Harwood', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Harwood', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Question', '_id': 'nyt://article/1626d32c-7ac2-5de4-8f6a-5947b9576054', 'word_count': 1041, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1626d32c-7ac2-5de4-8f6a-5947b9576054'}, {'abstract': 'Tina Maze of Slovenia captured the women’s downhill at the Alpine world ski championships in Beaver Creek, Colo., to earn her second medal there. She has hopes of three more.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/02/07/sports/skiing/tina-maze-wins-womens-downhill-at-alpine-worl