 'Basketball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Basketball Assn', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lopez, Felipe', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-02-06T20:01:39+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'New York', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Slideshow', '_id': 'nyt://slideshow/5545d3d6-cce0-5172-ba5e-0665f1e19fd6', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://slideshow/5545d3d6-cce0-5172-ba5e-0665f1e19fd6'}, {'abstract': 'Mr. Lopez, a former St. John’s star and professional player who works with teenagers through N.B.A. Cares, attends Sunday services at his evangelical church and, later, at St. Patrick’s.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/02/08/nyregion/for-felipe-lopez-a-basketball-ambassador-a-day-to-pray.html', 'snippet': 'Mr. Lopez, a former St. John’s star and professional player who works with teenagers through N.B.A. Cares, attends Sunday services at his evangelical church and, later, at St. Patrick’s.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Felipe Lopez has a special place in New York’s basketball pantheon: a gravity-defying phenom at Rice High School in Manhattan in the early ’90s, a star at St. John’s University in Queens. His National Basketball Association career, less prolific, lasted five journeyman seasons before an injury cut it short. Now, as the N.B.A. All-Star festivities return to New York Feb. 13 to 15, Mr. Lopez will be making a different kind of star turn, working with city teenagers as an ambassador for the league’s N.B.A. Cares program. “The goal is to reach over a million kids in the five boroughs,” Mr. Lopez, 40, said. He also runs a free Saturday basketball clinic at the Evangelical Spanish Church, near his childhood home in the Bronx. He moved to Astoria, Queens, last year with his girlfriend, Marija Kero, 30, a math teacher at Mott Hall Charter School in the Bronx.', 'print_section': 'MB', 'pr