 'On a slushy Saturday morning, Ashley Brazenor, 30, was babysitting for 2-year-old Beckett Abbott at Roots Cafe. She ordered a cold-brew iced coffee and a tofu scramble with vegan cheese — no toast, extra Sriracha — while Beckett nibbled on a berry muffin. Bluegrass riffs bounced off walls lined with washboards, acoustic guitars and mounted driftwood. A line snaked almost to the door, as patrons waited to order ginger apple cider or egg-and-cheese burritos slathered with mashed avocados and black beans. ', 'print_section': 'MB', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Cozy Living Room With a Barista: Roots Cafe in the South Slope', 'kicker': 'Neighborhood Joint', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Cozy Living Room With a Barista', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'South Park Slope (Brooklyn, NY)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Restaurants', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Roots Cafe (Brooklyn, NY, Restaurant)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-02-06T20:37:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jessica Leigh Hester', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jessica', 'middlename': 'Leigh', 'lastname': 'Hester', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/239dc1f6-a3e6-5cf3-846f-6b2d35035dd2', 'word_count': 594, 'uri': 'nyt://article/239dc1f6-a3e6-5cf3-846f-6b2d35035dd2'}, {'abstract': 'It’s good for casual sex — and serious relationships.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/02/08/opinion/sunday/in-defense-of-tinder.html', 'snippet': 'It’s good for casual sex — and serious relationships.', 'lead_paragraph': 'IS the smartphone revolution sullying the online dating world?', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page