4', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://slideshow/5af39b20-f751-585e-be38-f95a9c1b9734'}, {'abstract': 'Photos from Ukraine, Mexico, Jordan and Taiwan.', 'web_url': 'https://lens.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/02/06/feb-6-2015-pictures-of-the-day/', 'snippet': 'Photos from Ukraine, Mexico, Jordan and Taiwan.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Photos from Ukraine, Mexico, Jordan and Taiwan.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Feb. 6, 2015 — Pictures of the Day', 'kicker': 'Lens', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Photography', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Jordan', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Mexico', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Taiwan', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Ukraine', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-02-06T21:22:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Multimedia/Photos', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e1c7da70-4533-5d4b-a737-e69d8109ba7d', 'word_count': 12, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e1c7da70-4533-5d4b-a737-e69d8109ba7d'}, {'abstract': 'Kishin Shinoyama took the snapshots, one of which became the cover of the album “Double Fantasy,” just months before Lennon’s death in 1980.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/02/06/john-lennon-yoko-ono-new-pictures-kishin-shinoyama/', 'snippet': 'Kishin Shinoyama took the snapshots, one of which became the cover of the album “Double Fantasy,” just months before Lennon’s death in 1980.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A little over 30 years ago, the Japanese photographer Kishin Shinoyama walked through Central Park with one of the most famous couples in the world. It was sunset, autumn; they sat on a bench just in front of the pond, bordered by trees, a sliver of New York skyline visible in the distance, including the building where they lived. He asked them to kiss, and he clicked the shutter. Three months later, on Dec. 8, 1980, John Lennon was fatally shot at the entrance to the Dakota, home to him and his wife, Yoko Ono. Just three weeks prior to Lennon’s death, Shinoyama’s photograph of John and Yoko’s kiss at Central Park Pond had appeared on the cover of what would be their final studio album, “Double Fantasy.” Shinoyama made other photographs that day, of course — 800 in all, in fact — but many of them have never been shown until now, on the occasion of Taschen’s forthcoming publication of “Kishin Shinoyama. John Lennon & Yoko Ono. Double Fantasy” ($700), out this month. A video trailer for the book premieres here.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'In a New Book, Never-Before-Seen Photos of John Lennon and Yoko Ono', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Photography', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Rock Music', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lennon, John', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ono, Yoko', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Shinoyama, Kishin', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Taschen Books', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Central Park (Manhattan, NY)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-02-06T21:30:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rebecca Bengal', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rebecca', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bengal', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f00456d8-b757-56bd-b42b-22e4faf44b21', 'word_count': 553, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f00456d8-b757-56bd-b42b-22e4faf44b21'}, {'abstract': 'Judy Kuhn sang music from three generations of the Richard Rodgers dynasty as part of Lincoln Center’s American Songbook series.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/02/07/arts/music/judy-kuhns-homage-to-a-family-of-composers-in-the-american-songbook-series.html', 'snippet': 'Judy Kuhn sang music from three generations of the Richard Rodgers dynasty as part of Lincoln Center’s American Songbook series.', 'lead_paragraph': 'From father to daughter to grandson: The Lincoln Center American Songbook program “Judy Kuhn Sings Richard Rodgers, Mary Rodgers and Adam Guettel” on Wednesday evening convincingly portrayed the lineage of the composer Richard Rodgers as more than bloodline; it is a proudly romantic musical tradition. The performer making the connections was that top-of-the-line singer Judy Kuhn, whose approach to theater music might be described as one of passionate restraint.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Saluting the Rodgers Songwriting Dynasty ', 'kicker': 'Music Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Saluting the Rodgers Songwriting Dynasty', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'American Songbook (Music Series)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Lincoln Center for the Performing Arts', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kuhn, Judy', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-02-06T21:38:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Stephen Holden', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stephen', 'middlename': Non