pet': 'The way men handled the snow and slush on Feb. 4 spoke volumes about their sartorial habits.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The way men handled the snow and slush on Wednesday spoke volumes about their sartorial habits. Men who were otherwise conservatively clothed refused to change their dress shoes to storm-appropriate footwear. Meanwhile, men exploring fashion frontiers had a new dare: loafers without socks. For the first time, the Bryant Park fountain’s base froze with mini-icebergs forming in the corners.', 'print_section': 'ST', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Bill Cunningham | Men’s\xa0Winter Wear', 'kicker': 'On the Street', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Winter Wear', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Shoes and Boots', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cunningham, Bill', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Snow and Snowstorms', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Men and Boys', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-02-06T23:18:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Styles', 'section_name': 'Fashion & Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bill Cunningham and Joanna Nikas', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bill', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cunningham', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Joanna', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Nikas', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9c5d6be5-7570-524c-92c8-143c42c8fe7d', 'word_count': 61, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9c5d6be5-7570-524c-92c8-143c42c8fe7d'}, {'abstract': 'As social media platforms value ever-smaller snippets, Internet fame is shrinking from micro to nano.', 