-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 444, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/02/07/sports/CITY-IRISH-1/CITY-IRISH-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 444}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/07/sports/CITY-IRISH-1/CITY-IRISH-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 757, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/07/sports/CITY-IRISH-1/CITY-IRISH-1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1515, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/07/sports/CITY-IRISH-1/CITY-IRISH-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/02/07/sports/CITY-IRISH-1/CITY-IRISH-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/07/sports/CITY-IRISH-1/CITY-IRISH-1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Thriving After a Ban, Notre Dame’s Jerian Grant Impresses a Hall of Famer', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Notre Dame Star Thrives After a Ban', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Basketball (College)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Casey, Tim', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Grant, Jerian', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'University of Notre Dame', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-02-07T01:22:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'College Basketball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tim Casey', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tim', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Casey', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/144af892-1825-590d-b228-57856c2d5ca6', 'word_count': 1057, 'uri': 'nyt://article/144af892-1825-590d-b228-57856c2d5ca6'}, {'abstract': 'When he mentioned the Crusades in condemning Islamic terrorists this week, the president ignited a firestorm on television and social media about the validity of his observations.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/02/07/us/obama-trying-to-add-context-to-speech-faces-backlash-over-crusades.html', 'snippet': 'When he mentioned the Crusades in condemning Islamic terrorists this week, the president ignited a firestorm on television and social media about the validity of his observations.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — President Obama personally added a reference to the Crusades in his speech this week at the National Prayer Breakfast, aides said, hoping to add context and nuance to his condemnation of Islamic terrorists by noting that people also “committed terrible deeds in the name of Christ.”', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Obama, Trying to Add Context to Speech, Faces Backlash Over ‘Crusades’', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Obama, Trying to Add Context to Speech, Faces Backlash Over ‘Crusades’', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Islamic State in Iraq and Syria (ISIS)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Religion and Belief', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Christians and Christianity', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Muslims and Islam', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Crusades (Christianity)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Speeches and Statements', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-02-07T01:24:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael D. Shear', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ba4aa25f-afee-594d-adc1-b7fc9f091d5a', 'word_count': 904, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ba4aa25f-afee-594d-adc1-b7fc9f091d5a'}, {'abstract': 'The Security Council resolution, which could be adopted next week, is intended to choke the terrorist group’s ability to trade in oil, antiquities and hostages.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/02/07/world/middleeast/un-prepares-resolution-to-confront-islamic-state-on-oil-and-antiquities.html', 'snippet': 'The Security Council resolution, which could be adopted next week, is intended to choke the terrorist group’s ability to trade in oil, antiquities and hostages.', 'lead_paragraph': 'UNITED NATIONS — In a show of unity by the world powers against the Islamic State, the United Nations Security Council is preparing to adopt a legally binding resolution intended to choke the terrorist group’s ability to trade in oil, antiquities and hostages.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'U.N. Prepares Resolution to Confront Islamic State on Oil and Antiquities', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Terrorism', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Embargoes and Sanctions', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Kidnapping and Hostages', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Security Council (UN)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Islamic State in Iraq and Syria (ISIS)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Syria', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-02-07T01:28:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Somini Sengupta', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Somini', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sengupta', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/09e6f812-8c0c-543e-9ace-4b4463ff596e', 'word_count': 446, 'uri': 'nyt://article/09e6f812-8c0c-543e-9ace-4b4463ff596e'}, {'abstract': 'Out of my 25 new Catholic cousins, only one is still practicing.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/02/07/opinion/jennifer-finney-boylan-can-the-church-return-to-the-faithful.html', 'snippet': 'Out of my 25 new Catholic cousins, only one is still practicing.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I ONCE had a friend with a boomerang. One day we took it to the Jersey Shore and I watched as he whupped it around. It was beautiful: the young man and the boomerang, the bright sun and the water. Then, late in the day, he tossed it out over the ocean, and the boomerang didn’t come back. For a while we stood together, looking out, wondering whether we might just have lost sight of it. We glanced around nervously, on the off chance that it might yet clock us on the head, returning from a direction we had not anticipated.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '19', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/08/0