'pub_date': '2015-02-07T19:30:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'subsection_name': 'Sunday Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/9d08e2e2-dddc-5ed4-ad84-24ad2625a783', 'word_count': 725, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9d08e2e2-dddc-5ed4-ad84-24ad2625a783'}, {'abstract': 'Colleges have to resist misguided federal policies. The solution is to work with the local police.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/02/08/opinion/sunday/the-best-way-to-address-campus-rape.html', 'snippet': 'Colleges have to resist misguided federal policies. The solution is to work with the local police.', 'lead_paragraph': 'THE campus rape debate took another hairpin turn last week when The Daily Beast published an interview with Paul Nungesser, the Columbia student accused of raping a fellow student, Emma Sulkowicz. She has been carrying a mattress around the campus to raise awareness about sexual assault and to protest the school’s failure to expel Mr. Nungesser, who was cleared by a campus tribunal.', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/03/16/opinion/Shulevitz-Judith-circular/Shulevitz-Judith-circular-articleLarge-v4.png', 'height': 300, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/03/16/opinion/Shulevitz-Judith-circular/Shulevitz-Judith-circular-articleLarge-v4.png', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 300}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/03/16/opinion/Shulevitz-Judith-circular/Shulevitz-Judith-circular-jumbo-v4.png', 'height': 512, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJu