 'uri': 'nyt://article/a0d305c4-8a1e-5077-8daa-85505db6872f'}, {'abstract': 'After voters in the district approved legalization last fall, a federal provision seeking to block it may hang on the interpretation of a single word.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/02/08/us/politics/district-of-columbia-sees-loophole-in-congresss-move-to-halt-marijuana-law.html', 'snippet': 'After voters in the district approved legalization last fall, a federal provision seeking to block it may hang on the interpretation of a single word.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — Last fall, voters in the District of Columbia chose to join a handful of states in legalizing the growth and possession of small amounts of marijuana. But unlike in the states, the free will of district voters — no matter how overwhelmingly expressed — is never the end of the story.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '15', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'District of Columbia Sees Loophole in Congress’s Move to Halt Marijuana Law', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'District of Columbia Sees Loophole in Congress’s Move to Halt Marijuana Law', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Marijuana', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Washington (DC)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Law and Legislation', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-02-07T20:36:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jennifer Steinhauer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jennifer', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Steinhauer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 