 a Keeper', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Weddings and Engagements', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-02-08T05:15:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Society', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rosalie R. Radomsky', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rosalie', 'middlename': 'R.', 'lastname': 'Radomsky', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/58584c28-9867-5bcb-aee0-0df6615e3016', 'word_count': 640, 'uri': 'nyt://article/58584c28-9867-5bcb-aee0-0df6615e3016'}, {'abstract': 'Television highlights.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/02/08/arts/whats-on-tv-sunday.html', 'snippet': 'Television highlights.', 'lead_paragraph': '8 P.M. (CBS) THE 57TH ANNUAL GRAMMY AWARDS L L Cool J (above) returns as host of this ceremony honoring artists in country, hip-hop, jazz, pop and rock and broadcast live from the Staples Center in Los Angeles. Leading the pack with six nominations each are Sam Smith, Pharrell Williams and Beyoncé, who, with 53 nominations now has more than any other female performer in the award’s history. Iggy Azalea, Jay Z, Sia, Usher, Jack White, Miranda Lambert, Beck, Drake, Eric Church, Gordon Goodwin and the engineer Tom Coyne follow with four. George Harrison, Buddy Guy and the Bee Gees will be honored as this year’s lifetime achievement recipients. After six years, Kanye West will return to the Grammy stage in a solo performance as well as in a collaboration with Paul McCartney and Rihanna on her new single, “FourFiveSeconds.” Paired performers include Tony Bennett and Lady Gaga; Hozier and Annie Lennox; Jessie J and Tom Jones; and Adam Levine and Gwen Stefani. Katy Perry, AC/DC, Common, John Legend, Mary J. Blige, Juanes, Ariana Grande, Madonna and Ed Sheeran are also scheduled to take the stage. Pre-event coverage begins at 4 on E!; Pop joins the red carpet at 5; and E! moves to the after-party at 11:30.', 'print_section': 'SP', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What’s On TV Sunday', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'What’s On TV Sunday', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2015-02-08T06:00:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kathryn Shattuck', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kathryn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shattuck', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4fe2ace4-b605-57f0-9182-0ba26bf069d0', 'word_count': 692, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4fe2ace4-b605-57f0-9182-0ba26bf069d0'}, {'abstract': 'Corrections appearing in print on Sunday, February 8, 2015.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/02/08/pageoneplus/corrections-february-8-2015.html', 'snippet': 'Corrections appearing in print on Sunday, February 8, 2015.', 'lead_paragraph': 'INTERNATIONAL', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Corrections: February 8, 2015', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Corrections', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2015-02-08T07:10:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Summary', 'section_name': 'Corrections', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Correction', '_id': 'nyt://article/bd732966-3600-5226-b6df-b3ac1c7b3f21', 'word_count': 852, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bd732966-3600-5226-b6df-b3ac1c7b3f21'}, {'abstract': 'In a Chilean youth orchestra, a conductor and a young musician learn how music lifts them up and changes their lives.', 'web_url': 'https://lens.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/02/08/two-lives-in-harmony/', 'snippet': 'In a Chilean youth orchestra, a conductor and a young musician learn how music lifts them up and changes their lives.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Under skies as cloudy as her future, Melody Jerez, a young Chilean girl, discovered music, and with it a world of possibility. Years later, she took over a youth orchestra in an even smaller town, where another child, Georgina Ávila, was similarly entranced.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Two Lives, in Harmony', 'kicker': 'Lens', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Photography', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sundance Film Festival (Park City, Utah)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rivas, Marialy', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Sundance Institute', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Chile', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-02-08T08:00:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Multimedia/Photos', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e7375cb8-01d9-5cae-854e-cda2a4d33955', 'word_count': 201, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e7375cb8-01d9-5cae-854e-cda2a4d33955'}, {'abstract': 'A security technology meant to keep communications private is being used to do things like stream Netflix in countries where it is not available.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/02/08/in-ways-legal-and-illegal-vpn-technology-is-erasing-international-borders/', 'snippet': 'A security technology meant to keep communications private is being used to do things like stream Netflix in countries where it is not available.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Rod Drury, an entreprene