Poitras also win for “Citizenfour.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Directors Guild of America on Saturday gave its top prize to Alejandro G. Iñárritu for “Birdman,” his backstage tale of a washed-up movie star seeking a comeback on Broadway. He beat out a field that included Richard Linklater (“Boyhood”) and Clint Eastwood (“American Sniper”). In the documentary category, Laura Poitras took the honors for “Citizenfour,” her film about Edward J. Snowden and his revelations about snooping by the National Security Agency.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Iñárritu Takes Directors Guild Prize', 'kicker': 'Carpetbagger', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Directors Guild Gives Prize to Iñárritu', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Inarritu, Alejandro G', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Poitras, Laura', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Directors Guild of America', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-02-08T14:20:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Stephanie Goodman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stephanie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Goodman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c76a2c4d-4e39-5ec1-a80f-1989980e479f', 'word_count': 72, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c76a2c4d-4e39-5ec1-a80f-1989980e479f'}, {'abstract': 'Smith built the Tar Heels into a perennial national power in his 36 years at Chapel Hill and became one of the game’s most respected figures.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/02/09/sports/ncaabasketball/dean-smith-longtime-university-of-north-carolina-basketball-coach-dies-at-83.html', 'snippet': 'Smith built the Tar Heels into a perennial national power in his 36 years at Chapel Hill and became one of the game’s most respected figures.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Dean Smith, who built the University of North Carolina men’s basketball team into a perennial national power in his 36 years at Chapel Hill and became one of the game’s most respected figures for qualities that transcended the court, died on Saturday in Chapel Hill, N.C. He was 83.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/08/obituaries/09SMITHOBIT/09SMITHOBIT-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 407, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/02/08/obituaries/09SMITHOBIT/09SMITHOBIT-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 407}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/08/obituaries/09SMITHOBIT/09SMITHOBIT-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 694, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/08/obituaries/09SMITHOBIT/09SMITHOBIT-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1156, 'width': 1706, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/08/obituaries/09SMITHOBIT/09SMITHOBIT-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/02/08/obituaries/09SMITHOBIT/09SMITHOBIT-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/08/obituaries/09SMITHOBIT/09SMITHOBIT-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150,