n Them All? The Globetrotters Beg to Differ', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Basketball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Harlem Globetrotters', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-02-08T17:33:49+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Basketball', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Slideshow', '_id': 'nyt://slideshow/b27736a8-b5ab-53ff-9ea1-345601b47ea2', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://slideshow/b27736a8-b5ab-53ff-9ea1-345601b47ea2'}, {'abstract': 'Despite an almost certain outcome, the beloved exhibition team has kept its routine fresh for nearly 90 years.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/02/09/sports/basketball/globetrotters-say-you-can-win-them-all.html', 'snippet': 'Despite an almost certain outcome, the beloved exhibition team has kept its routine fresh for nearly 90 years.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ROCHESTER — Lou Dunbar seems happy. He smiles a lot. He laughs constantly. He claims that his job has never felt like a job because he enjoys it too much. And it all begins to make sense once you consider that Dunbar, who goes by Sweet Lou, is the winningest basketball coach in the world.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Can’t Win ’Em All? Globetrotters Come Close', 'kicker': 'Not the Knicks', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Can’t Win ’Em All? Globetrotters Come Close', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Basketball', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Harlem Globetrotters', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Washington Generals', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Dunbar, Louis