t of cooperation in lawmaking.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/02/09/arts/design/edward-m-kennedy-institute-aims-to-teach-collaboration.html', 'snippet': 'The Edward M. Kennedy Institute in Boston, opening next month, mirrors the senator’s spirit of cooperation in lawmaking.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When it opens next month in Boston, the Edward M. Kennedy Institute for the United States Senate will be aiming to restore respect for Congress at a time when rancor and partisanship have seriously damaged its reputation.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'In the Mold of a Senator Who Bartered', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'In the Mold of a Senator Who Bartered', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Kennedy, Edward M, Institute for the United States Senate', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kennedy, Edward M', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Senate', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Boston (Mass)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'University of Massachusetts', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Vinoly, Rafael', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ARCHITECTURE', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-02-08T22:13:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Art & Design', 'byline': {'original': 'By Robin Pogrebin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Robin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pogrebin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/aabafcec-ab8f-5da1-bc4e-7fe5101d1575', 'word_count': 1241, 'uri': 'nyt://article/aabafcec-ab8f-5da1-bc4e-7fe5101d1575'}, {'abstract': 'Rosie O’Donnell is leaving ABC’s “The View” at the end of the week to focus on her health and family.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/02/09/arts/television/odonnell-saying-goodbye-to-the-view.html', 'snippet': 'Rosie O’Donnell is leaving ABC’s “The View” at the end of the week to focus on her health and family.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Rosie O’Donnell is leaving ABC’s “The View” at the end of the week to focus on her health and family. Cindi Berger, Ms. O’Donnell’s publicist, told the The New York Post’s Page Six that the 52-year-old comedian and actress wanted to spend more time with her five children after separating from her second wife, Michelle Rounds, in November. “Rosie has teens and an infant at home that need her attention,” Ms. Berger said. “This has been a very stressful situation. She is putting her personal health and family first.” Ms. O’Donnell won’t be walking out of the spotlight completely. “Rosie O’Donnell: A Heartfelt Stand Up,” her HBO Documentary special about cardiac health (she suffered a heart attack in 2012), premieres Feb. 14. And a Tweet posted on “The View” Twitter account said Ms. O’Donnell would “be back often with her unique point of view and updates on her work and family.”', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/09/arts/09ARTS3/09ARTS3-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 795, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/02/09/arts/09ARTS3/09ARTS3-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 795}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/09/arts/09ARTS3/09ARTS3-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 774, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/09/arts/09ARTS3/09ARTS3-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1547, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/09/arts/09ARTS3/09ARTS3-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/02/09/arts/09ARTS3/09ARTS3-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/09/arts/09ARTS3/09ARTS3-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'O’Donnell Saying Goodbye to ‘The View’', 'kicker': 'Arts, Briefly', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'O’Donnell Saying Goodbye to ‘The View’', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': "O'Donnell, Rosie", 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'The View (TV Program)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-02-08T22:40:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'Compiled by Lori Holcomb-Holland', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lori', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Holcomb-Holland', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/40e653ae-bbde-5727-8d3e-9a65bd7828f3', 'word_count': 151, 'uri': 'nyt://article/40e653ae-bbde-5727-8d3e-9a65bd7828f3'}, {'abstract': 'From Ruby Keeler to Judy Garland, singers retrace a movie-musical history in “Here’s to the Girls!: Hollywood’s Leading Ladies,” at the 92nd Street Y.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/02/09/arts/heres-to-the-girls-at-the-92nd-street-y.html', 'snippet': 'From Ruby Keeler to Judy Garland, singers retrace a movie-musical history in “Here’s to the Girls!: Hollywood’s Leading Ladies,” at the 92nd Street Y.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In the giddy, goofy history of the movie musical as traced in “Here’s to the Girls!: Hollywood’s Leading Ladies,” the 92nd Street Y’s Lyrics and Lyricists program on Saturday, each major studio had its own pantheon and signature style. One of the most clearly defined, identified as the Warner Bros. Dames, were brassy streetwise characters played by the likes of Ruby Keeler and Joan Blondell. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'With Dream-Girl Stand-Ins, a Riotous Heyday Recalled', 'kicker': 'Music Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'With Dream-Girl Stand-Ins, a Riotous Heyday Recalled', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': '92nd Street Y', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Busch, Charles', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Andress, Carl', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-02-08T22:41:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Stephen Holden', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stephen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Holden', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/19023bc9-280a-5371-8f8c-05132ed74346', 'word_count': 310, 'uri': 'nyt://article/19023bc9-280a-5371-8f8c-05132ed74346'}, {'abstract': 'The mezzo-soprano Elina Garanca and the tenor Roberto Alagna reunited for the first time since 2009 in Bizet’s “Carmen,” and the spectacle was largely unchanged.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/02/09/arts/elina-garanca-reprises-her-role-in-carmen.html', 'snippet': 'The mezzo-soprano Elina Garanca and the tenor Roberto Alagna reunited for the first time since 2009 in Bizet’s “Carmen,” and the spectacle was largely unchanged.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As she has risen to stardom over the past decade the Latvian mezzo-soprano Elina Garanca has been one of the most frustrating singers in opera. There are few voices as sheerly lovely as hers: a smooth, evenly produced instrument, rich but not heavy, with high notes that penetrate without blaring.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/09/arts/09CARMEN/09CARMEN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 473, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/02/09/arts/09CARMEN/09CARMEN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 473}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/09/arts/09CARMEN/09CARMEN-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 807, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/09/arts/09CARMEN/09CARMEN-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1614, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/09/arts/09CARMEN/09CARMEN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/02/09/arts/09CARMEN/09CARMEN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/09/arts/09CARMEN/09CARMEN-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Saucy Temptress Keeps the Temperature Cool ', 'kicker': 'Opera Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Saucy Temptress Keeps the Temperature Cool', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Opera', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Woolfe, Zachary', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Metropolitan Opera', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Garanca, Elina', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Perez, Ailyn', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Eyre, Richard', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'ALAGNA, ROBERTO', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Carmen (Opera)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-02-08T22:43:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Zachary Woolfe', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Zachary', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Woolfe', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/f620a6a9-0410-5f33-9ec7-5462659db9da', 'word_count': 413, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f620a6a9-0410-5f33-9ec7-5462659db9da'}, {'abstract': '“Word of Mouth” by Timo Andres, performed by Orpheus Chamber Orchestra at Carnegie Hall, is a chamber symphony suffused with optimism but also conflicting ambitions.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/02/09/arts/music/orpheus-chamber-orchestra-at-carnegie-hall.html', 'snippet': '“Word of Mouth” by Timo Andres, performed by Orpheus Chamber Orchestra at Carnegie Hall, is a chamber symphony suffused with optimism but also conflicting ambitions.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In 1842 Charles Dickens published “American Notes,” a travelogue detailing impressions formed during a six-month journey up and down the Eastern Seaboard. “American Notes” is also the title of this season’s commissioning program by the Orpheus Chamber Orchestra, which invites composers to write works that take the temperature of the country today — not quite a State of the Union, perhaps, so much as a national selfie.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/09/arts/09ORPHEUS/09ORPHEUS-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 409, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/02/09/arts/09ORPHEUS/09ORPHEUS-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 409}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/09/arts/09ORPHEUS/09ORPHEUS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 698, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/09/arts/09ORPHEUS/09ORPHEUS-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1396, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/09/arts/09ORPHEUS/09ORPHEUS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/02/09/arts/09ORPHEUS/09ORPHEUS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/09/a