'Business Day', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'International Business', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Slideshow', '_id': 'nyt://slideshow/8edd6506-fca2-5c9a-bce8-053088ce60a6', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://slideshow/8edd6506-fca2-5c9a-bce8-053088ce60a6'}, {'abstract': 'The play “The Listeners” centers on two drifters, contradictions and shifting identities.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/02/09/theater/the-listeners-a-matthew-freeman-drama-at-the-brick.html', 'snippet': 'The play “The Listeners” centers on two drifters, contradictions and shifting identities.', 'lead_paragraph': 'To break the fourth wall at “The Listeners,” Matthew Freeman’s new play at the Brick, you’ll need a battering ram. The set is an enclosed, roofless room in the middle of the Brick’s black-box space. Audience members can peer at the play through letterbox slits sliced into the walls. If you come early enough to grab a chair in front of one of the two panels of one-way glass, you’ll enjoy the rare luxury of seeing two or even three characters at once.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/09/arts/09LISTENERS/09LISTENERS-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 701, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/02/09/arts/09LISTENERS/09LISTENERS-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 701}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/09/arts/09LISTENERS/09LISTENERS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 876, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/09/arts/09LISTENERS/09LISTENERS-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1487, 'w