n their multitudes, these birds renew our faith in doing things together.', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/02/09/swan-lovers/', 'snippet': 'In their multitudes, these birds renew our faith in doing things together.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I’m not Leda, so it’s perhaps odd that swans should be involved in my love life, but I happen to live near the Magee Marsh National Wildlife Refuge in Oak Harbor, Ohio. The refuge is not only the self-styled Warbler Capital of the World in spring — when every warbler on Peterson’s list of “Confusing Warblers” flies through, making crowded birders jostle one another’s camera tripods — but is also, during the winter, a way station for thousands of migrating tundra swans.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/09/opinion/09menagerieWEB/09menagerieWEB-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 397, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/02/09/opinion/09menagerieWEB/09menagerieWEB-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 397}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/09/opinion/09menagerieWEB/09menagerieWEB-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 678, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/09/opinion/09menagerieWEB/09menagerieWEB-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 927, 'width': 1400, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/09/opinion/09menagerieWEB/09menagerieWEB-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/02/09/opinion/09menagerieWEB/09men