icle/da010de8-6744-5586-a81d-b874fc3f1de1'}, {'abstract': 'There’s a disconnect between what we think kills children and what actually does. In the U.S., it makes sense to focus on accidents, homicide and suicide.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/02/10/upshot/how-to-prioritize-and-save-young-lives.html', 'snippet': 'There’s a disconnect between what we think kills children and what actually does. In the U.S., it makes sense to focus on accidents, homicide and suicide.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In an ad during the Super Bowl last week, Nationwide Insurance chillingly reminded us that accidents are the No. 1 killer of children. Aside from the odd setting for the commercial, one of the reasons that it shocked so many people in the United States is that we have a disconnect between what we think kills children and what really does.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/05/upshot/10up-health-1423080620962/10up-health-1423080620962-articleLarge.png', 'height': 486, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/02/05/upshot/10up-health-1423080620962/10up-health-1423080620962-articleLarge.png', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 486}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/05/upshot/10up-health-1423080620962/10up-health-1423080620962-jumbo.png', 'height': 830, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/05/upshot/10up-health-1423080620962/10up-health-1423080620962-superJumbo.png', 'height': 1361, 'width': 1679, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/05/upshot/10up-health-1423080620962/10up-health-1423080620962-thumbStandard.png', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/02/05/upshot/10up-health-1423080620962/10up-health-1423080620962-thumbStandard.png', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/05/upshot/10up-health-1423080620962/10up-health-1423080620962-thumbLarge.png', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'How to Prioritize and Save Young Lives', 'kicker': 'The New Health Care', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Children and Childhood', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Traffic Accidents and Safety', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Teenagers and Adolescence', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Suicides and Suicide Attempts', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Murders, Attempted Murders and Homicides', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Denmark', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-02-09T11:38:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Upshot', 'section_name': 'The Upshot', 'byline': {'original': 'By Aaron E. Carroll', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Aaron', 'middlename': 'E.', 'lastname': 'Carroll', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/527a05cd-506f-5832-869a-95697a87badf', 'word_count': 803, 'uri': 'nyt://article/527a05cd-506f-5832-869a-95697a87badf'}, {'abstract': 'The Davos set loses its leverage.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/02/09/greece-the-tie-that-doesnt-bind/', 'snippet': 'The Davos set loses its leverage.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Relations between Greece and its creditors are not improving. Was this bad diplomacy on the part of Tsipras/Varoufakis? Maybe, but my guess is that there was nothing they could do to avoid a bitter confrontation short of immediate betrayal of the voters who put them in office. And creditor-country officials are acting as if they still expect that to happen, just as it has repeatedly over the past five years.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Greece: The Tie That Doesn’t Bind', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2015-02-09T11:43:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d239ebeb-3846-5d3e-bdb5-82826aedd318', 'word_count': 565, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d239ebeb-3846-5d3e-bdb5-82826aedd318'}, {'abstract': 'Before making an advance directive, talk with your doctor and your caregiver about just how far end-of-life care should go at the cost of comfort.', 'web_url': 'https://well.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/02/09/know-the-hard-choices-prolonging-life-entails/', 'snippet': 'Before making an advance directive, talk with your doctor and your caregiver about just how far end-of-life care should go at the cost of comfort.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Virgie Divinigracia had the kind of death last month that most Americans say they want: at home, relieved of physical and mental pain, surrounded by those she loved, “a beautiful death” as those present described it. Alas, this is true for too few Americans. Most still die in costly medical facilities tethered to machines, often unable to communicate, in a futile attempt to prolong their lives.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/07/science/06brody/06brody-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 481, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/02/07/science/06brody/06brody-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 481}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/07/science/06brody/06brody-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 822, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/07/science/06brody/06brody-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1170, 'width': 1458, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/07/science/06brody/06brody-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/02/07/science/06brody/06brody-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/07/science/06brody/06brody-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Seeking a ‘Beautiful Death’', 'kicker': 'Well', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Keeping the End in Clear Sight', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Death and Dying', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Health Insurance and Managed Care', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Livi