ri': 'nyt://article/0009554b-ebc2-50a7-9903-0a7fc1827a07'}, {'abstract': 'The Consumer Financial Protection Bureau seeks to limit payday lenders. | The prime minister of Greece says he will carry out his campaign to roll back austerity. | Hidden cash is flowing into high-end real estate. | Shares of HSBC fall on tax avoidance claims.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2015/02/09/morning-agenda-u-s-takes-on-payday-lenders/', 'snippet': 'The Consumer Financial Protection Bureau seeks to limit payday lenders. | The prime minister of Greece says he will carry out his campaign to roll back austerity. | Hidden cash is flowing into high-end real estate. | Shares of HSBC fall on tax avo...', 'lead_paragraph': ' U.S. TAKES ON PAYDAY LENDERS | The Consumer Financial Protection Bureau will soon release the first draft of federal regulations to govern a wide range of short-term loans made by the $46 billion payday loan industry, Jessica Silver-Greenberg reports in DealBook. The rules are expected to address expensive credit backed by car titles and some installment loans that stretch longer than the traditional two-week payday loan, according to industry lawyers, consumer groups and government authorities briefed on the discussions.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Morning Agenda: U.S. Takes On Payday Lenders', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2015-02-09T12:08:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sydney Ember', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sydney', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ember', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/17eea246-7774-5a71-8e88-84a5bf03532e', 'word_count': 1986, 'uri': 'nyt://article/17eea246-7774-5a71-8e88-84a5bf03532e'}, {'abstract': 'This red carpet vs. stage vs. exit quick-change thing has gotten out of control.', 'web_url': 'https://runway.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/02/09/from-beyonce-to-sam-smith-clothing-changes-become-the-grammys-worst-trend/', 'snippet': 'This red carpet vs. stage vs. exit quick-change thing has gotten out of control.', 'lead_paragraph': 'There were many folks who looked surprisingly good at the Grammy Awards on Sunday, managing to combine rock ’n’ roll edge with actual elegance (chief among them in my book: Nicki Minaj in Tom Ford, Iggy Azalea in Armani Privé, and Gwen Stefani in her Versace jumpsuit), but really, who could keep track?', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/09/fashion/09runway-A/09runway-A-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 399, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/02/09/fashion/09runway-A/09runway-A-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 399}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/09/fashion/09runway-A/09runway-A-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 681, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/09/fashion/09runway-A/09runway-A-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1361, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/09/fashion/09runway-A/09runway-A-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/02/09/fashion/09runway-A/09runway-A-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 