hey had begun a search immediately.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/02/10/world/asia/after-criticism-india-police-arrest-8-in-haryana-rape-murder.html', 'snippet': 'Opposition lawmakers have seized on the case, and the victim’s sister said the police could have saved her life if they had begun a search immediately.', 'lead_paragraph': 'NEW DELHI — Under mounting criticism for their slow response to a missing persons report filed last week, the police in the Indian state of Haryana arrested eight men on Monday suspected of raping and murdering a mentally impaired woman whose battered body was found in a field.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'After Criticism, India Police Arrest 8 in Haryana Rape-Murder', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'India: Eight Are Arrested in Rape and Killing', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Murders, Attempted Murders and Homicides', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kumar, Hari', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sex Crimes', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'India', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Haryana (India)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Intellectual Disabilities', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-02-09T16:58:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Hari Kumar', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Hari', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kumar', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a74f8183-0a44-543b-9a05-f1fe1414e056', 'word_count': 243, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a74f8183-0a44-543b-9a05-f1fe1414e056'}, {'abstract': 'The use of an airbag safety device has not gained acceptance among the sport’s professionals yet, despite the risk of serious injury that competitors face in violent crashes.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/02/10/sports/airbag-is-approved-but-ski-racers-are-largely-shunning-it-for-now.html', 'snippet': 'The use of an airbag safety device has not gained acceptance among the sport’s professionals yet, despite the risk of serious injury that competitors face in violent crashes.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MOLVENA, Italy — Broken collarbones. Shattered shoulders. Internal bleeding. Punctured lungs. Those injuries, and worse, are possible every time a world-class skier plunges out of a starting gate and slides down a snowy racecourse.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/10/sports/10SKIBAGweb5/10SKIBAGweb5-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 393, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/02/10/sports/10SKIBAGweb5/10SKIBAGweb5-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 393}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/10/sports/10SKIBAGweb5/10SKIBAGweb5-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 671, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/10/sports/10SKIBAGweb5/10SKIBAGweb5-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1341, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/10/sports/10SKIBAGweb5/10SKIBAGweb5-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/02/10/sports/10SKIBAGweb5/10SKIBAGweb5-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/10/sports/10SKIBAGweb5/10SKIBAGweb5-thumbLarge-v3.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Airbag Is Approved, but Ski Racers Are Largely Shunning It for Now', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Airbag Is Approved, but Ski Racers Are Largely Shunning It for Now', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Skiing', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Borden, Sam', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sports Injuries', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sporting Goods and Equipment', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'World Cup (Skiing)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ALPINE SKIING', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Dainese SpA', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Miller, Bode', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-02-09T17:00:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Skiing', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sam Borden', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Borden', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ada784d6-10d2-538d-bab5-c9bea42eff91', 'word_count': 1171, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ada784d6-10d2-538d-bab5-c9bea42eff91'}, {'abstract': 'A machine drops balls into bins. When should you stop the machine in order to maximize your winnings? Test your logic with this original puzzle by Dutch mathematician Henk Tijms.', 'web_url': 'https://wordplay.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/02/09/tijms/', 'snippet': 'A machine drops balls into bins. When should you stop the machine in order to maximize your winnings? Test your logic with this original puzzle by Dutch mathematician Henk Tijms.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Our puzzle this week was suggested by Henk Tijms, a Dutch mathematician and emeritus professor at the VU University Amsterdam. We first met Dr. Tijms about a year ago through his Devil’s Penny. This new puzzle has a similar feel, but is a bit more challenging. Let’s play\xa0—', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Henk Tijms: Dropping Balls Into Bins', 'kicker': 'Wordplay', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Crossword Puzzles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mathematics', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-02-09T17:00:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Crosswords & Games', 'byline': {'original': 'By Gary Antonick', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Gary', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Antonick', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/284d35ac-01df-55fb-a8de-a7cd169817f8', 'word_count': 1094, 'uri': 'nyt://article/284d35ac-01df-55fb-a8de-a7cd169817f8'}, {'abstract': 'It will take years to repair banks’ credibility enough to produce someone who can move as easily from banking to public service, Antony Currie and Rob Cox of Reuters Breakingviews write.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2015/02/09/john-whiteheads-storied-career-is-hard-to-reproduce/', 'snippet': 'It will take years to repair banks’ credibility enough to produce someone who can move as easily from banking to public service, Antony Currie and Rob Cox of Reuters Breakingviews write.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The storied career that John C. Wh