ore, officials said.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/02/10/world/europe/migrants-die-after-rescue-by-italys-coast-guard.html', 'snippet': 'More than 100 migrants were rescued in rough seas, but the others perished before the Italian Coast Guard could get them to shore, officials said.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ROME — Twenty-nine migrants who were rescued alive in rough seas off the Libyan coast died before the Italian Coast Guard could get them to shore, officials said on Monday.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Migrants Are Plucked From Sea Off Libya, but 29 Die Aboard Italian Rescue Ships', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Migrants Are Plucked From Sea Off Libya, but 29 Die Aboard Italian Rescue Ships', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Pianigiani, Gaia', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Italy', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Libya', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Immigration and Emigration', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Maritime Accidents and Safety', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Fatalities)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Mare Nostrum', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Mediterranean Sea', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Lampedusa (Italy)', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Ships and Shipping', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-02-09T20:13:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Gaia Pianigiani and Jim Yardley', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Gaia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pianigiani', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Jim', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Yardley', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/eed25a0a-e6dd-53e8-b963-84bfdaf5edee', 'word_count': 643, 'uri': 'nyt://article/eed25a0a-e6dd-53e8-b963-84bfdaf5edee'}, {'abstract': 'This Thursday, Julian Wasser’s images of the iconic American author will be on display at New York City’s Danziger Gallery.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/02/09/joan-didion-julian-wasser-photography-exhibition/', 'snippet': 'This Thursday, Julian Wasser’s images of the iconic American author will be on display at New York City’s Danziger Gallery.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Last month, an online fracas erupted when Céline released its campaign featuring a sunglass-shaded, 80-year-old Joan Didion photographed by Juergen Teller. Was the image a step forward for feminism, or had Didion’s personal style eclipsed the substance of her work? Julian Wasser, for his part, was merely perplexed. “I don’t know how that happened,” says the photographer from his home in Los Angeles. “I don’t know how she fit into that, because she’s just a down-to-earth, regular person.”', 'print_section': 'ST', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Joan Didion: From the Face of Céline to the Subject of a New Photography Exhibition', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'On View: Joan Didionu2019s Close-Up', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Photography', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Didion, Joan', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Chelsea (Manhattan, NY)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-02-09T20:15:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Eviana Hartman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Eviana', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hartman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/017f432f-721a-5c48-952f-b13c1c361e98', 'word_count': 526, 'uri': 'nyt://article/017f432f-721a-5c48-952f-b13c1c361e98'}, {'abstract': 'In an experimental carbon storage process, gas emissions and water are injected into volcanic rock, turning the mixture into minerals.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/02/10/science/burying-a-mountain-of-co2.html', 'snippet': 'In an experimental carbon storage process, gas emissions and water are injected into volcanic rock, turning the mixture into minerals.', 'lead_paragraph': 'HENGILL, Iceland — In a cramped work trailer not far from Iceland’s largest geothermal power plant, a researcher pored over a box of core samples — cylinders of rock that a drilling rig had pulled from deep underground just a few minutes before.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/10/science/10CARBONCOMBO/10CARBONCOMBO-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 576, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/02/10/science/10CARBONCOMBO/10CARBONCOMBO-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 576}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/10/science/10CARBONCOMBO/10CARBONCOMBO-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 982, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/10/science/10CARBONCOMBO/10CARBONCOMBO-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1965, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo'