city of Ahmedabad.', 'lead_paragraph': 'More than a decade after he spent his meandering postcollegiate years on the Indian subcontinent studying Sufi mysticism and following a musical guru, the Austrian artist Matthias Kaiser returns today to open a pop-up ceramics shop under a neem tree in Ahmedabad, India. He’s stocked the roadside stall with art made, as always, of loosely interpreted recollections: a kiln’s worth of functional vessels carrying the echoes of papaya and potato chaat, Le Corbusier and Pierre Jeanneret’s modernist city of Chandigarh and “hairless dogs, three-wheeled tractors and giant moving haystacks that had a truck hidden somewhere underneath,” Kaiser explains.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/09/t-magazine/09kaiser-wu/09kaiser-wu-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 360, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/02/09/t-magazine/09kaiser-wu/09kaiser-wu-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 360}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/09/t-magazine/09kaiser-wu/09kaiser-wu-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 614, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/09/t-magazine/09kaiser-wu/09kaiser-wu-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1229, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/09/t-magazine/09kaiser-wu/09kaiser-wu-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/02/09/t-magazine/09kaiser-wu/09kaiser-wu-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbna