', '_id': 'nyt://article/e2197ec4-7141-5fbd-988d-5a80284edf9f', 'word_count': 1130, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e2197ec4-7141-5fbd-988d-5a80284edf9f'}, {'abstract': 'Legal experts said Alabama’s clash of federal and state authority on the issue would almost surely end with state officials honoring the decision by a Federal District Court judge allowing the unions.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/02/10/us/supreme-court-undercuts-alabama-chief-justices-argument-to-delay-same-sex-marriages.html', 'snippet': 'Legal experts said Alabama’s clash of federal and state authority on the issue would almost surely end with state officials honoring the decision by a Federal District Court judge allowing the unions.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Until Monday, Chief Justice Roy S. Moore of Alabama had what some legal experts called a plausible argument for delaying the onset of same-sex marriage in the state, which had been ordered by a Federal District Court judge. After all, the United States Supreme Court will decide the issue for the entire nation in coming months and it made sense, Chief Justice Moore and other opponents of same-sex marriage said, to freeze things until the highest court ruled. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Supreme Court Undercuts Alabama Chief Justice’s Argument to Delay Same-Sex Marriages', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Supreme Court Undercuts Alabama Chief Justice’s Argument to Delay Unions', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Supreme Court (US)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Eckholm, Erik', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'ALABAMA', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Same-Sex Marriage, Civil Unions and Domestic Partnerships', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Moore, Roy S', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'