s considerable power in Washington, veterans may be let down. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'When Colleges Use Veterans as Pawns', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'When Colleges Use Veterans as Pawns', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'For-Profit Schools', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Veterans', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Consumer Protection', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Law and Legislation', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Corinthian Colleges Inc', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Senate', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-02-10T08:27:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/b6bd4fb5-b948-5061-9440-1faa8206f8b2', 'word_count': 493, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b6bd4fb5-b948-5061-9440-1faa8206f8b2'}, {'abstract': 'To right its anemic performance, the World Health Organization has endorsed changes to respond more quickly to the next outbreak.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/02/10/opinion/reform-after-the-ebola-debacle.html', 'snippet': 'To right its anemic performance, the World Health Organization has endorsed changes to respond more quickly to the next outbreak.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The World Health Organization’s anemic performance in handling the Ebola outbreaks in West Africa may yield one positive outcome: sweeping, and long overdue, institutional reforms to improve its ability to respond more quickly to the next outbreak of a lethal infectious disease. Scrambling to a