, 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/02/11/world/asia/kenji-ekuan-japanese-designer-who-gave-soy-sauce-its-curves-dies-at-85.html', 'snippet': 'Mr. Ekuan’s work included some of the products most closely associated with postwar Japan, including Yamaha motorcycles and bullet trains.', 'lead_paragraph': 'TOKYO — Kenji Ekuan, a Japanese industrial designer whose instantly recognizable soy sauce bottle — red-capped and elegantly teardrop-shaped — became one of his country’s most ubiquitous postwar exports, died here on Sunday. He was 85.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '15', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/11/world/11ekuan/11ekuan-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 793, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/02/11/world/11ekuan/11ekuan-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 793}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/11/world/11ekuan/11ekuan-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 776, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/11/world/11ekuan/11ekuan-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1551, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/11/world/11ekuan/11ekuan-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/02/11/world/11ekuan/11ekuan-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/11/world/11ekuan/11ekuan-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Kenji Ekuan, Who Gave Soy Sauce Its Graceful Curves, Dies at 85', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Kenji Ekuan, 85; Gave Soy Sauce Its Graceful Curves', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Obituaries)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Soble, Jonathan', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ekuan, Kenji (1929-2015)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Japan', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Design', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-02-10T10:24:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jonathan Soble', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jonathan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Soble', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Obituary (Obit)', '_id': 'nyt://article/d7157d41-d095-50c8-a1b5-669cbc5de05b', 'word_count': 644, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d7157d41-d095-50c8-a1b5-669cbc5de05b'}, {'abstract': 'A handful of upstart sites is striving to disrupt the vacation rental market by appealing to families with children or jet-setters seeking luxury villas.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/02/15/travel/giving-airbnb-a-run-for-its-money.html', 'snippet': 'A handful of upstart sites is striving to disrupt the vacation rental market by appealing to families with children or jet-setters seeking luxury villas.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When travelers think about vacation rentals, they almost always think of Airbnb. The easy-to-use site, founded in 2008 and now with more than a million listings worldwide, is the first stop for many tourists — which means properties are snapped up fast, especially during major events such as concerts, games and conferences. Yet a handful of new contenders is striving to disrupt the vacation rental market by targeting specific kinds of travelers, be it families with children or jet-setters seeking luxury villas and airport transfers by helicopter. Below, a guide to some of the upstarts and, at the end of this column, a reminder of some veteran sites that all too often end up in the shadow of Airbnb.', 'print_section': 'TR', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/15/travel/15GETAWAY/15GETAWAY-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 504, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/02/15/travel/15GETAWAY/15GETAWAY-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 504}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/15/travel/15GETAWAY/15GETAWAY-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 860, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/15/travel/15GETAWAY/15GETAWAY-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1649, 'width': 1964, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/15/travel/15GETAWAY/15GETAWAY-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/02/15/travel/15GETAWAY/15GETAWAY-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/15/travel/15GETAWAY/15GETAWAY-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Giving Airbnb a Run for Its Money', 'kicker': 'The Getaway', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Beyond Airbnb: A Guide to New Vacation Rental Sites', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rosenbloom, Stephanie', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Renting and Leasing (Real Estate)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hotels and Travel Lodgings', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-02-10T10:45:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Travel', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By Stephanie Rosenbloom', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stephanie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rosenbloom', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3428e8f0-0fdc-5b04-a93e-6e37a4f8aa2a', 'word_count': 1122, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3428e8f0-0fdc-5b04-a93e-6e37a4f8aa2a'}, {'abstract': 'A decades-long film career has taken the iconic Italian actress around the world. She shares her favorite places.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/02/15/travel/sophia-loren-on-her-life-in-hotels.html', 'snippet': 'A decades-long film career has taken the iconic Italian actress around the world. She shares her favorite places.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The actress Sophia Loren is a symbol of Italy to generations of moviegoers. Born in Rome on Sept. 20, 1934, as Sofia Villani Scicolone, she was raised outside Naples and suffered intense deprivation during World War II. As Italy entered the postwar “Dolce Vita” era, she became a star of Cinecittá, Rome’s film industry center. She won an Oscar in 1962 for her performance in “La Ciociara,” or “Two Women,” about wartime Italy. Her memoir, “Yesterday, Today, Tomorrow: My Life,” was published late last year by Atria Books. She is the mother of Carlo Jr. and Edoardo, with her husband, the producer Carlo Ponti, who died in 2007. Following are edited excerpts from a conversation with Ms. Loren.', 'print_section': 'TR', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/15/travel/15QNA/15QNA-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 726, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/02/15/travel/15QNA/15QNA-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 726}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/15/travel/15QNA/15QNA-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 847, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/15/travel/15QNA/15QNA-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1694, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/15/travel/15QNA/15QNA-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/02/15/travel/15QNA/15QNA-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/15/travel/15QNA/15QNA-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Sophia Loren on Her Life in Hotels', 'kicker': 'Q&A', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Sophia Loren on Travel, and Wanting to Be a Tourist', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N