c3-5af7-9552-223786d44083'}, {'abstract': 'The Justice Department is pushing banks to plead guilty to settle a currency inquiry. | A disproportionate number of companies led by women are the targets of activist investors. | Puerto Rico’s debt plan is in jeopardy. | Profit at UBS rises.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2015/02/10/morning-agenda-u-s-presses-banks-for-guilty-pleas/', 'snippet': 'The Justice Department is pushing banks to plead guilty to settle a currency inquiry. | A disproportionate number of companies led by women are the targets of activist investors. | Puerto Rico’s debt plan is in jeopardy. | Profit at UBS rises.', 'lead_paragraph': 'U.S. SEEKS FELONY PLEAS BY BIG BANKS | The Justice Department is pushing some of the biggest banks on Wall Street, including American institutions, to plead guilty to criminal charges that they manipulated the prices of foreign currencies, Ben Protess and Jessica Silver-Greenberg report in DealBook. In the final stages of a long-running investigation into corruption in the world’s biggest financial market, federal prosecutors have recently informed Barclays, JPMorgan Chase, the Royal Bank of Scotland and Citigroup that they must enter guilty pleas to settle the cases, according to lawyers briefed on the matter. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Morning Agenda: U.S. Presses Banks for Guilty Pleas', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2015-02-10T12:21:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sydney Ember', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sydney', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ember', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/50d9c936-ea11-510b-85e7-28ed1b80fbf5', 'word_count': 2273, 'uri': 'nyt://article/50d9c936-ea11-510b-85e7-28ed1b80fbf5'}, {'abstract': 'The boundary-pushing comedian/author/actor is now a jumpsuit designer.', 'web_url': 'https://runway.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/02/10/the-olsen-twins-victoria-beckham-margaret-cho-this-is-not-a-joke/', 'snippet': 'The boundary-pushing comedian/author/actor is now a jumpsuit designer.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Thanks to the successful transitions of Mary-Kate and Ashley Olsen and Victoria Beckham from celebrities to full-fledged fashion designers respected by the style community at large, the idea that an actress/singer/what-have-you might credibly make some clothes has gained a certain amount of traction these days. So perhaps it should come as no surprise that just in time for fashion week, which begins on Thursday, there’s a new crossover candidate: Margaret Cho — boundary-pushing comedian/author/actor and, now, jumpsuit designer.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/10/fashion/10runway-A/10runway-A-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 351, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/02/10/fashion/10runway-A/10runway-A-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 351}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/10/fashion/10runway-A/10runway-A-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 599, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/10/fashion/10runway-A/10runway-A-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1199, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/10/fashion/10runway-A/10runway-A-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height'