tract': 'Once again, readers have spotted a succession of mysterious strangers wandering through the tops of our stories.', 'web_url': 'https://afterdeadline.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/02/10/surrounded-by-strangers/', 'snippet': 'Once again, readers have spotted a succession of mysterious strangers wandering through the tops of our stories.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Once again, readers have spotted a succession of mysterious strangers wandering through the tops of our stories.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Surrounded by Strangers', 'kicker': 'After Deadline', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2015-02-10T13:00:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Times Topics', 'byline': {'original': 'By PHILIP B. CORBETT', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Philip', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/db6700f5-4a99-5ba7-bdab-c8e8f44c4197', 'word_count': 1166, 'uri': 'nyt://article/db6700f5-4a99-5ba7-bdab-c8e8f44c4197'}, {'abstract': 'The up\xad-and\xad-coming soprano sings an excerpt from Micaëla’s aria.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/02/10/in-performance-ailyn-prez-of-carmen/', 'snippet': 'The up\xad-and\xad-coming soprano sings an excerpt from Micaëla’s aria.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Ailyn Pérez, an up\xad-and\xad-coming soprano who has been making the rounds of major opera houses in Vienna, London, Berlin and Milan, made her Metropolitan Opera debut this month as Micaëla in a revival of Bizet’s “Carmen.” Ms. Pérez, who won the 2012 Richard Tucker Award, was praised for her performance by Zachary Woolfe, who wrote in The New York Times that she was a “confident, forthright presence in a role that can fade into merely demure.” Here she is singing a decidedly non\xad