ghlights from the International Herald Tribune archives: Viet Cong bomb G.I. barracks in 1965.', 'web_url': 'https://iht-retrospective.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/02/10/1965-bomb-hits-g-i-barracks/', 'snippet': 'Highlights from the International Herald Tribune archives: Viet Cong bomb G.I. barracks in 1965.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SAIGON — Communist Viet Cong terrorists blew up a U.S. Army barracks tonight [Feb. 10], inflicting heavy loss of life, a U.S. military spokesman reported. One American has already been found dead and 14 others were wounded. Another 30 Americans were missing in the blast and were believed dead under the wreckage. About 60 men lived in the four-story hotel used as a barrack at Qui Nhon, 250 miles northeast of here, but several of them were away when the explosion occurred, the spokesman said. He said the hotel was ‘‘completely destroyed.’’— New York Herald Tribune, European Edition, Feb. 11, 1965', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/11/blogs/11iht-oldfeb11-vietnam/11iht-oldfeb11-vietnam-articleLarge.png', 'height': 453, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/02/11/blogs/11iht-oldfeb11-vietnam/11iht-oldfeb11-vietnam-articleLarge.png', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 453}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/11/blogs/11iht-oldfeb11-vietnam/11iht-oldfeb11-vietnam-jumbo.png', 'height': 772, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/11/blogs/11iht-oldfeb11-vietnam/11iht-oldfeb11-vietnam-superJumbo.png', 'height': 1080, 'width': 1432, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'ty