 her corpse as proof of death.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For one tortured weekend, the parents of Kayla Mueller refused to believe that their daughter was dead. From their home in Prescott, Ariz., they issued an impassioned plea to the Islamic State, which had held her captive since August 2013, and urged the extremist organization to contact them privately with proof of her death. The militants acquiesced and sent at least three photographs of her corpse. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/11/world/11KAYLA/11KAYLA-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 322, 'width': 596, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/11/world/11KAYLA/11KAYLA-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 322, 'width': 596, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/11/world/11KAYLA/11KAYLA-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/02/11/world/11KAYLA/11KAYLA-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/11/world/11KAYLA/11KAYLA-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'With Proof From ISIS of Her Death, Family Honors Kayla Mueller', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Proof of Death in Hand, Family Honors Hostage', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Schmitt, Eric', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Islamic State in Iraq and Syria (ISIS)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Kidnapping and Hostages', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mueller, Kayla (1988-2015)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Syria', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Jordan', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-02-10T15:31:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rukmini Callimachi and Eric Schmitt', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rukmini', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Callimachi', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Eric', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schmitt', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/bb67d521-24aa-5a0d-b9bc-401baddd0722', 'word_count': 1247, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bb67d521-24aa-5a0d-b9bc-401baddd0722'}, {'abstract': 'Don’t judge politicians by how they come across.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/02/10/up-close-and-delusional/', 'snippet': 'Don’t judge politicians by how they come across.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Jonathan Chait notes that people are still trying to cast Paul Ryan as reasonable and moderate — hey, he visits bookstores favored by liberals. As Chait says, this sort of political evaluation by personal style is unreliable at best; and Ryan quite clearly deliberately exploits it, too, making moderate noises without ever giving an inch on his hard-line right-wing policies. Remember, this is the guy who pretended to offer a budget based on fiscal responsibility, but when you took out the magic asterisks it was really tax cuts for the rich, severe benefit cuts for the poor, and overall would actually increase the deficit.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Up Close And Delusional', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2015-02-10T15:33:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/67b0d9f0-f192-5c46-aef0-4e28e8ce978e', 'word_count': 506, 'uri': 'nyt://article/67b0d9f0-f192-5c46-aef0-4e28e8ce978e'}, {'abstract': 'Rahm Emanuel instructed David Axelrod to draft a statement that could be read in place of an inauguration address if an attack turned out to be imminent.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/politics/first-draft/2015/02/10/obama-had-statement-to-read-if-terror-halted-inauguration/', 'snippet': 'Rahm Emanuel instructed David Axelrod to draft a statement that could be read in place of an inauguration address if an attack turned out to be imminent.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The night before President Obama was inaugurated in 2009, David Axelrod got a call from an agitated Rahm Emanuel, the president-elect’s chief of staff, according to Mr. Axelrod’s book, “Believer,” which was released on Tuesday.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/10/us/politics/10firstdraft-obama-inauguration/10firstdraft-obama-inauguration-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/02/10/us/politics/10firstdraft-obama-inauguration/10firstdraft-obama-inauguration-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'ima