tted a group of uniformed Marines paying for snacks. “Mommy!” she exclaimed, “look at ALL those daddies!” We’re never really alone.', 'web_url': 'https://parenting.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/02/10/the-military-marriage-trapeze-act/', 'snippet': 'Stopping at a highway rest stop, my 4-year-old spotted a group of uniformed Marines paying for snacks. “Mommy!” she exclaimed, “look at ALL those daddies!” We’re never really alone.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I clipped in my harness, took a deep breath at the base of the metal ladder and slowly started the long, precarious, 23-foot climb. As the ladder gently swayed with every movement, I tried to create the illusion of composure while getting to the platform at the top as quickly as possible. The mixture of adrenaline and fear is my version of a Long Island iced tea: seems like such a good combination, until you get sick or black out. I remind myself that people (like me) actually pay for this feeling. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/09/us/motherlode-trapeze/motherlode-trapeze-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 396, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/02/09/us/motherlode-trapeze/motherlode-trapeze-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 396}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/09/us/motherlode-trapeze/motherlode-trapeze-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 592, 'width': 896, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/09/us/motherlode-trapeze/motherlode-trapeze-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 592, 'width': 896, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'im