e': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Late-Night Host Seamlessly Mixing Analysis, Politics and Humor', 'kicker': 'Critic’s Notebook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Late-Night Host Seamlessly Mixing Analysis, Politics and Humor', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Stewart, Jon', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Comedy and Humor', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'The Daily Show with Jon Stewart (TV Program)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Comedy Central', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'News and News Media', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-02-11T02:24:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jason Zinoman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jason', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Zinoman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/58d1d292-e7ac-5308-a6a9-872b431c4a52', 'word_count': 794, 'uri': 'nyt://article/58d1d292-e7ac-5308-a6a9-872b431c4a52'}, {'abstract': 'Under Jon Stewart, “The Daily Show” became an important incubator of comedic talent.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/02/10/jon-stewart-and-the-daily-show-a-comedy-family-tree/', 'snippet': 'Under Jon Stewart, “The Daily Show” became an important incubator of comedic talent.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Just over 16 years ago, Jon Stewart took over “The Daily Show,” which has served as a primary source of news and satire for a generation. His mission: to skewer, mock and fact-check what he saw as the inanities of American politics and media. In the process, “The Daily Show” served as a launching pad for some of comedy’s most notable talents to go onto other shows or projects. Jon Stewart must be a happy papa.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': "Jon Stewart and ‘The Daily Show': A Comedy Launchpad", 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Carell, Steve', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Colbert, Stephen', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Corddry, Rob', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Helms, Ed', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Oliver, John', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Stewart, Jon', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wilmore, Larry', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Comedy Central', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-02-11T02:24:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Gilbert Cruz', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Gilbert', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cruz', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/da57b862-b9a9-5cad-9644-5f630f36ce08', 'word_count': 345, 'uri': 'nyt://article/da57b862-b9a9-5cad-9644-5f630f36ce08'}, {'abstract': 'Gov. Charlie Baker of Massachusetts deployed National Guard troops to help with snow removal as the state tried to dig out from its third major winter storm in two weeks.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/video/us/100000003502206/boston-buried-in-near-record-snowfall.html', 'snippet': 'Gov. Charlie Baker of Massachusetts deployed National Guard troops to help with snow removal as the state tried to dig out from its third major winter storm in two weeks.', 