mages/2015/02/11/world/10SCHOOLS/10SCHOOLS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/02/11/world/10SCHOOLS/10SCHOOLS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/11/world/10SCHOOLS/10SCHOOLS-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'French Teachers, on the Front Lines', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'French Teachers, on the Front Lines', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Education (K-12)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Donadio, Rachel', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'France', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Freedom of Religion', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Freedom of Speech and Expression', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Teachers and School Employees', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Terrorism', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Muslims and Islam', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Paris (France)', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Charlie Hebdo', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-02-11T04:13:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rachel Donadio', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rachel', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Donadio', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f2f64f3d-3ae5-575e-9814-7903dd6c32c7', 'word_count': 1244, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f2f64f3d-3ae5-575e-9814-7903dd6c32c7'}, {'abstract': 'The St. Louis County prosecutor asked a federal judge on Monday to dismiss a lawsuit from a grand juror who wants to speak publicly about the case of Darren Wilson, the Ferguson police officer who fatally shot Michael Brown.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/02/11/us/missouri-prosecutor-seeks-dismissal-of-grand-jurors-lawsuit.html', 'snippet': 'The St. Louis County prosecutor asked a federal judge on Monday to dismiss a lawsuit from a grand juror who wants to speak publicly about the case of Darren Wilson, the Ferguson police officer who fatally shot Michael Brown.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The St. Louis County prosecutor, with the backing of Missouri’s attorney general, asked a federal judge on Monday to dismiss a lawsuit from a grand juror who wants to speak publicly about the case of Darren Wilson, the Ferguson police officer who fatally shot an unarmed black man last summer and was not indicted. Missouri law prevents grand jurors from discussing their work in most instances, and the 12-member panel that decided not to indict Mr. Wilson for killing Michael Brown, 18, has remained anonymous. One juror sued last month seeking protection from the restrictions, naming the prosecutor, Robert P. McCulloch, as the defendant. That lawsuit, which said that the public’s understanding of the grand jury was “not entirely accurate,” indicated a willingness to discuss what happened during the hearings and “advocate for legislative change to the way grand juries are conducted.” In the lawsuit, the grand juror, who is represented by the American Civil Liberties Union of Missouri, indicated a fear of being prosecuted if he or she spoke publicly. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Missouri: Prosecutor Seeks Dismissal of Grand Juror’s Lawsuit ', 'kicker': 'National Briefing | Midwest', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Missouri: Prosecutor Seeks Dismissal of Grand Juror’s Lawsuit', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wilson, Darren (1986- )', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Brown, Michael (1996-2014)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Ferguson (Mo)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Police Brutality, Misconduct and Shootings', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Jury System', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Missouri', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McCulloch, Robert P (1951- )', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-02-11T04:15:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mitch Smith', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mitch', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Smith', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/4463514e-85b0-5d87-96cf-c4ecefbeac03', 'word_count': 271, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4463514e-85b0-5d87-96cf-c4ecefbeac03'}, {'abstract': 'The decrees governing bakeries play into a serious debate about whether the country can change its work rules and make other adjustments to counter high unemployment and a morose economy.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/02/11/world/decrees-governing-frances-bakeries-prompt-a-wider-debate-on-work-rules.html', 'snippet': 'The decrees governing bakeries play into a serious debate about whether the country can change its work rules and make other adjustments to counter high unemployment and a morose economy.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PARIS — Stéphane Cazenave, a baker in Saint-Paul-lès-Dax in southwestern France, was awarded a prize last year for best traditional baguette, in a contest organized by the confederation of French bakers. Back home, business was good, and Mr. Cazenave kept his bakery open seven days a week.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Decrees Governing France’s Bakeries Prompt a Wider Debate on Work Rules', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Decrees Governing France’s Bakeries Prompt a Wider Debate on Work Rules', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Breeden, Aurelien', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'France', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Working Hours', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bakeries and Baked Products', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Shopping and Retail', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wages and Salaries', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Income', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cazenave, Stephane', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-02-11T04:27:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Aurelien Breeden', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Aurelien', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Breeden', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/90b0dcb5-034c-58e9-83ac-6099936665b0', 'word_count': 714, 'uri': 'nyt://article/90b0dcb5-034c-58e9-83ac-6099936665b0'}, {'abstract': 'Alexis Tsipras said his government would seek a short-term “bridge” agreement to a new deal and a “necessary” reduction of his country’s debt.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/02/11/world/europe/greek-prime-minister-tsipras-wins-confidence-vote-before-talks-with-creditors.html', 'snippet': 'Alexis Tsipras said his government would seek a short-term “bridge” agreement to a new deal and a “necessary” reduction of his country’s debt.', 'lead_paragraph': "ATHENS — With Greece preparing for tough talks with creditors in Brussels, Prime Minister Alexis Tsipras's government easily won a confidence vote in Parliament early Wednesday with assurances that it would reverse an economic program that has slashed living standards.", 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Greek Prime Minister Tsipras Wins Confidence Vote Before Talks With Creditors', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Tsipras, Alexis', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Greece', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'European Sovereign Debt Crisis (2010- )', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Eurozone', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-02-11T04:30:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Niki Kitsantonis', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Niki', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kitsantonis', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1d1ef555-c383-5cd5-9a23-0f6c100bf87b', 'word_count': 385, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1d1ef555-c383-5cd5-9a23-0f6c100bf87b'}, {'abstract': 'The auction site Paddle8 has partnered with the design firm Homepolish to create a pop-up series of interiors vignettes at the Ace Hotel and Swim Club.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/02/11/t-magazine/palm-springs-modernism-week-desert-living.html', 'snippet': 'The auction site Paddle8 has partnered with the design firm Homepolish to create a pop-up series of interiors vignettes at the Ace Hotel and Swim Club.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In the coming days, design and art lovers will descend on the desert east of Los Angeles for the 10th edition of Palm Springs Modernism Week. Among the lectures, house tours, exhibitions and fairs this year, one unofficial event stands out — and even offers the chance for the snowbound to get in on the action. The auction site Paddle8 has partnered with the design firm Homepolish to create “Desert Living: Icons of Modern Design,” a pop-up series of interiors vignettes at the Ace Hotel and Swim Club’s 4,000-square-foot clubhouse space. The four installations, says Jason Stein, Paddle8’s senior design specialist, reflect “what our favorite homes in Palm Springs would be; a setting we’d want to live in.” And though midcentury art and design are, as expected, well represented, the collectibles on offer extend far beyond the “Mad Men”-era nostalgia typically associated with the region. One California-themed tableau includes Frank Gehry’s cardboard chair, Bill Curry’s “Cattail” lamp, John Baldessari prints and an Ed Ruscha painting; another explores the notion of opulence through such pieces as a chrome 1970s Gucci wine cooler and a Helmut Newton nude photograph. And a future-themed area features Gerald McCabe’s seven-stemmed “Daisy” table and artwork by Kenny Scharf, Sam Francis and David Hockney. The environments will be accessible to visitors this weekend and are, Stein promises, “really layered”; for those stuck in less salubrious climes, everything is up for auction starting Wednesday on the Paddle8 site.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/11/t-magazine/11paddle-hartman-2/11paddle-hartman-2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 402, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/02/11/t-magazine/11paddle-hartman-2/11paddle-hartman-2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 402}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/11/t-magazine/11paddle-hartman-2/11paddle-hartman-2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 687, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/11/t-magazine/11paddle-hartman-2/11paddle-hartman-2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1374, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/11/t-magazine/11paddle-hartman-2/11paddle-hartman-2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/02/11/t-magazine/11paddle-hartman-2/11paddle-hartman-2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/11/t-magazine/11paddle-hartman-2/11paddle-hartman-2-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Midcentury Modernism Arrives in the California Desert', 'kicker': 'By Design', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2015-02-11T05:00:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TDesign', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Eviana Hartman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Eviana', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hartman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/00afbe80-c5e2-5b8d-9552-019df2169fe2', 'word_count': 293, 'uri': 'nyt://article/00afbe80-c5e2-5b8d-9552-019df2169fe2'}, {'abstract': 'Just in time for Valentine’s Day, indie purveyors of artisanal scoops offer new flavors to be shipped statewide.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/02/11/t-magazine/small-batch-ice-cream.html', 'snippet': 'Just in time for Valentine’s Day, indie purveyors of artisanal scoops offer new flavors to be shipped statewide.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It may seem unlikely given the time of year, but a handful of indie ice cream makers across the country introduced new, handcrafted flavors this month. And the small-batch pints, created in collaboration with other American purveyors of artisanal goods and available to be shipped anywhere in the U.S., are a welcome relief from the traditional Valentine’s Day sweets this time of year.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/11/t-magazine/11cream-donnelly/11cream-donnelly-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 450, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/02/11/t-magazine/11cream-donnelly/11cream-donnelly-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 450}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/11/t-magazine/11cream-donnelly/11cream-donnelly-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 706, 'width': 941, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/11/t-magazine/11cream-donnelly/11cream-donnelly-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 706, 'width': 941, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/11/t-magazine/11cream-donnelly/11cream-donnelly-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/02/11/t-magazine/11cream-donnelly/11cream-donnelly-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/11/t-magazine/11cream-donnelly/11cream-donnelly-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Perfect Pint (of Ice Cream)', 'kicker': 'Food Matters', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2015-02-11T05:00:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TLiving', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kate Donnelly', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kate', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Donnelly', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/61ec95c6-9a41-5fb0-b107-5a644108547a', 'word_count': 234, 'uri': 'nyt://article/61ec95c6-9a41-5fb0-b107-5a644108547a'}, {'abstract': 'Subodh Gupta\'s "Seven Billion Light Years" includes ready-made and appropriated objects that reflect on Indian culture.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/02/11/t-magazine/subodh-gupta-seven-billion-light-years-new-york.html', 'snippet': 'Subodh Gupta\'s "Seven Billion Light Years" includes ready-made and appropriated objects that reflect on Indian culture.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Many of the objects in Subodh Gupta’s career-spanning new exhibition, “Seven Billion Light Years,” are ordinary: The works on display include kitchen utensils piled together as part of a sculpture, a window buried in the ground and a broken stove attached to a painting. But Gupta thinks of them as more than discards; these are also someone else’s memories on display. Because he transforms certain objects into larger-than-life, sometimes shocking sculptures, Gupta has been called the “Damien Hirst of New Delhi”; alternately, his methods of appropriating and displaying other people’s objects could be described as Duchampian. The truth is, Gupta is a sentimentalist at heart. His objects, whether gilded or left as-is, are intimately bound up with Indian culture — agriculture and cooking traditions that are fading away from modern society.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The ‘Damien Hirst of New Delhi’ Brings a Personal Exhibition to New York', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2015-02-11T05:00:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sylvia Rupani-Smith', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sylvia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rupani-Smith', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8034d097-bbba-596c-b815-aadf1cb8c951', 'word_count': 445, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8034d097-bbba-596c-b815-aadf1cb8c951'}, {'abstract': 'The backstage beauty expert explains how to get the no-makeup makeup look in 10 steps.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/02/11/t-magazine/makeup-lessons-pat-mcgrath.html', 'snippet': 'The backstage beauty expert explains how to get the no-makeup makeup look in 10 steps.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The makeup artist Pat McGrath is a master of creating bold, hashtag-worthy looks with her whimsical use of sequins, glitter and Crayola-like color, but her most impressive trompe l’oeil might be when her handiwork is completely invisible to the eye. When she’s not pushing the avant-garde with wild materials, McGrath’s makeup can be so subtle that it appears as if the models aren’t wearing any at all. As it turns out, achieving this no-makeup makeup effect (seen on many a runway — and surely many more in the weeks to come during the fall/winter 2015 fashion shows), requires the right mix of products (11 to be exact) and ample blending. Here, McGrath reveals the secrets behind her stealth technique that results in casual perfection.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/15/t-magazine/15womens-look-mcgrath-1/15womens-look-mcgrath-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 450, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/02/15/t-magazine/15womens-look-mcgrath-1/15womens-look-mcgrath-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 450}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/15/t-magazine/15womens-look-mcgrath-1/15womens-look-mcgrath-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 768, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/15/t-magazine/15womens-look-mcgrath-1/15womens-look-mcgrath-1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1536, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/15/t-magazine/15womens-look-mcgrath-1/15womens-look-mcgrath-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/02/15/t-magazine/15womens-look-mcgrath-1/15womens-look-mcgrath-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/15/t-magazine/15womens-look-mcgrath-1/15womens-look-mcgrath-1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Lesson in Natural Makeup From the Masterful Pat McGrath', 'kicker': 'On Beauty', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline':