ith its two sequels, has sold more than 100 million copies worldwide despite being ridiculed by virtually every critic who has read it. (Salman Rushdie, for one, said that it “made ‘Twilight’ look like ‘War and Peace.’\xa0”) ', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/15/arts/1550GREY1/1550GREY1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 397, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/02/15/arts/1550GREY1/1550GREY1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 397}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/15/arts/1550GREY1/1550GREY1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 678, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/15/arts/1550GREY1/1550GREY1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1356, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/15/arts/1550GREY1/1550GREY1-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/02/15/arts/1550GREY1/1550GREY1-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/15/arts/1550GREY1/1550GREY1-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': '‘Fifty Shades of Grey,’ the Movie, as a Fairy Tale', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Seeing the Fairy-Tale Romance in Pain', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lyall, Sarah', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Taylor-Wood, Sam', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'James, E L', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Dornan, Jamie', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Johnson, Dakota', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Fifty Shades of Grey (Book)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Fifty Shades of Grey (Movie)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-02-11T13:00:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sarah Lyall', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sarah', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lyall', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d8862467-0724-547f-bbf1-34f630c3a902', 'word_count': 1338, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d8862467-0724-547f-bbf1-34f630c3a902'}, {'abstract': 'Two recent articles show the need for evolving style guidelines', 'web_url': 'https://publiceditor.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/02/11/the-times-and-transgender-issues-part-one-of-two-on-pronouns/', 'snippet': 'Two recent articles show the need for evolving style guidelines', 'lead_paragraph': 'In August 2013, soon after Chelsea Manning announced that she identified as a woman and no longer wanted to be known as Bradley Manning, The Times made a quick – and I thought appropriate – adjustment. Articles began referring to Private Manning with the feminine pronoun and the use of the name Chelsea. It caused a bit of a scramble at the time, because editors were concerned about clarity for readers when referring to the high-profile soldier who had just been sentenced to prison for leaking classified information. But in the end, a ruling principle – the preference of the individual – held sway.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Times and Transgender Issues (Part 1 of 2): On Pronouns', 'kicker': 'The Public Editor&#039;s Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2015-02-11T13:00:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Margaret Sullivan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Margaret', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sullivan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6c39d017-a0ca-5920-965f-ab4dc136f663', 'word_count': 946, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6c39d017-a0ca-5920-965f-ab4dc136f663'}, {'abstract': 'The company, which specializes in letting clients sell and manage online software systems, plans to expand its staff worldwide.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2015/02/11/cloud-software-start-up-appdirect-raises-50-million/', 'snippet': 'The company, which specializes in letting clients sell and manage online software systems, plans to expand its staff worldwide.', 'lead_paragraph': 'AppDirect, a start-up focused on helping customers sell software online, said on Wednesday that it had raised $50 million in new financing to help it expand its staff worldwide.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Cloud Software Start-Up AppDirect Raises $50 Million', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Start-Up Financing', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Venture Capital', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AppDirect Inc', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Mithril Capital Management', 'rank': 4, '