 'snippet': 'This collection of 50 years of Amiri Baraka’s poetry shows the firmness of his beliefs and the heat of his fury.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Amiri Baraka eulogized James Baldwin on Dec. 8, 1987, by saying: “He was all the way live, all the way conscious, turned all the way up, receiving and broadcasting. . . . He always made us know we were dangerously intelligent and as courageous as the will to be free.”', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/15/books/review/15RANKINE/15rankine-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 524, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/02/15/books/review/15RANKINE/15rankine-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 524}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/15/books/review/15RANKINE/15rankine-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 895, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/15/books/review/15RANKINE/15rankine-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1790, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/15/books/review/15RANKINE/15RANKINE-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/02/15/books/review/15RANKINE/15RANKINE-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/15/books/review/15RANKINE/15RANKINE-thumbLarge-v3.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Amiri Baraka’s ‘S O S’', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Truth to Power', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Baraka, Amiri', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Poetry and Poets', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'S O S: Poems 1961-2013 (Book)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-02-11T15:00:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'BookReview', 'section_name': 'Books', 'subsection_name': 'Book Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Claudia Rankine', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Claudia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rankine', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/d77e0d0b-35d2-5745-8b46-a615a04984b8', 'word_count': 1185, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d77e0d0b-35d2-5745-8b46-a615a04984b8'}, {'abstract': 'Robert L. Grenier, a C.I.A. station chief, had a ringside seat for the early days of the Afghan war.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/02/15/books/review/robert-l-greniers-88-days-to-kandahar.html', 'snippet': 'Robert L. Grenier, a C.I.A. station chief, had a ringside seat for the early days of the Afghan war.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As America’s longest war draws to a close, journalists and diplomats, spooks and soldiers keep turning out books attempting to explain what was lost and won over the last 14 years in Afghanistan. While none so far have synthesized the disparate worlds of American civilian policy, military action and Afghan realities, the latest entry, “88 Days to Kandahar: A CIA Diary,” by Robert L. Grenier, adds another on-the-ground view of how the early events actually unfolded. Grenier, who retired in 2006 after 27 years with the C.I.A., was the station chief in Islamabad, Pakistan, from 1999 to 2002, with practical responsibility for Taliban-dominated \xadareas of southern and eastern Afghanistan during the crucial early months of the war. The book’s title refers to the period between Sept. 11 and Dec. 7, when an anti-Taliban tribal leader named Hamid Karzai made a perilous return to Afghanistan to rally Pashtun opposition to the Taliban, which culminated in their surrender.', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/15/books/review/15RUBIN/15RUBIN-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 1710, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/02/15/books/review/15RUBIN/15RUBIN-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 1710}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/15/books/review/15RUBIN/15RUBIN-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 360, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/15/books/review/15RUBIN/15RUBIN-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 719, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/15/books/review/15RUBIN/15RUBIN-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/02/15/books/review/15RUBIN/15RUBIN-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/15/books/review/15RUBIN/15RUBIN-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarg