imes', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/13/arts/13FIFTY/13FIFTY-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 399, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/02/13/arts/13FIFTY/13FIFTY-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 399}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/13/arts/13FIFTY/13FIFTY-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/13/arts/13FIFTY/13FIFTY-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1364, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/13/arts/13FIFTY/13FIFTY-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/02/13/arts/13FIFTY/13FIFTY-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/13/arts/13FIFTY/13FIFTY-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Review: In ‘Fifty Shades of Grey’ Movie, Sex Is a Knotty Business', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'When Love Wears a Blindfold', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Taylor-Wood, Sam', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'James, E L', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Dornan, Jamie', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Johnson, Dakota', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Fifty Shades of Grey (Movie)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-02-11T15:36:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By A.O. Scott', 'person': [{'firstname': 'A.', 'middlename': 'O.', 'lastname': 'Scott', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/af10d944-2e68-5175-b8d9-a3b9fc4fa9a5', 'word_count': 1460, 'uri': 'nyt://article/af10d944-2e68-5175-b8d9-a3b9fc4fa9a5'}, {'abstract': 'A Chilean director explores a world of sinning priests sent into exile.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/02/11/chiles-pablo-larrain-presents-catholic-priest-film-at-berlin-festival/', 'snippet': 'A Chilean director explores a world of sinning priests sent into exile.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BERLIN — The Chilean director Pablo Larraín has a penchant for the dark side. His “Tony Manero” (2009) was about a serial killer, and “Post Mortem” (2012) and the Oscar-nominated “No” (2013) explored the complexities of Pinochet’s Chile. In “The Club,” which debuted at the Berlin Film Festival this week to strong reviews, the director has mined another troubling theme: errant Roman Catholic priests and the system that has helped cover up their misdeeds.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Chile’s Pablo Larraín Presents Film on Catholic Priests at Berlin Festival', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Berlin International Film Festival', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Larrain, Pablo', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizati