case to collect treasures for her line.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/02/11/irene-neuwirth-gem-show-diary/', 'snippet': 'Fifteen years after her first visit, the native Angeleno still makes the trip to the Tucson Gem, Mineral & Fossil Showcase to collect treasures for her line.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In 2001, Irene Neuwirth took her first trip to the Tucson Gem, Mineral & Fossil Showcase, a massive exhibition held every winter that spans various venues across the city. At the time, the native Angeleno was teaching horseback riding and picking up beads at her local hippie haunt that she would later turn into jewelry for fun. “I drove there, stayed at the airport Hilton, and had $300,” she says. “I spent $500 and thought I would be in debt for the rest of my life.” Upon returning to L.A., Neuwirth made 10\xa0necklaces, and sent them to Barneys with a note written in Magic Marker that read, “I hope you love them.” Today, her namesake\xa0line is one the department store’s best sellers and she has a fanciful Melrose Place flagship store to call her own.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Jewelry Designer Irene Neuwirth Goes to the Gem Show', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Jewels and Jewelry', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Neuwirth, Irene', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Tucson (Ariz)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-02-11T16:30:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Crystal Meers', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Crystal', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Meers', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 't