}], 'headline': {'main': '‘American Sniper’ Case Opens', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Murders, Attempted Murders and Homicides', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kyle, Chris (1974-2013)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Texas', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Stephenville (Tex)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-02-11T17:29:49+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'AP', 'person': [], 'organization': 'AP'}, 'type_of_material': 'Video', '_id': 'nyt://video/082ad94b-26e2-593e-92ba-284375ffef86', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://video/082ad94b-26e2-593e-92ba-284375ffef86'}, {'abstract': 'A close-up of the makeup artist.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/02/11/pat-mcgrath-facts-and-figures/', 'snippet': 'A close-up of the makeup artist.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In the beauty universe, you could say the world spins around Pat McGrath. Over the course of her three-decade career, the prolific, self-taught makeup artist has worked with in-demand models (Naomi, Gisele, Cara, Kendall), major fashion houses (Christian Dior, Versace, Prada) and the top photographers (Steven Meisel counts her among his closest collaborators). A backstage fixture, McGrath can set trends with a wave of her hands — she famously prefers to work with her fingers instead of with brushes — and is nothing if not extremely versatile: dewy, no-makeup skin, custom-made Swarovski crystal face masks and feather-adorned eyelids and brows are all in her wheelhouse. In 2004, she was made global creative design director for Procter & Gamble Beauty, and last spring, Queen Elizabeth II named her a Member of the Order of the British Empire for services to the fashion and beauty industries. (To celebrate, McGrath snapped her first selfie.) Here, a closer look at all things in McGrath’s orbit.', 'print_section': 'M2', 'print_page': '136', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/11/t-magazine/11btn-mcgrath/11btn-mcgrath-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 465, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/02/11/t-magazine/11btn-mcgrath/11btn-mcgrath-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 465}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/11/t-magazine/11btn-mcgrath/11btn-mcgrath-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 794, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/11/t-magazine/11btn-mcgrath/11btn-mcgrath-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1103, 'width': 1422, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/11/t-magazine/11btn-mcgrath/11btn-mcgrath-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/02/11/t-magazine/11btn-mcgrath/11btn-mcgrath-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/11/t-magazine/11btn-mcgrath/11btn-mcgrath-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The World of Pat McGrath', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'By the Numbers: Pat McGrath', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cosmetics and Toiletries', 'rank': 1, 'major'