n-baroqued.html', 'snippet': 'The experimental dance company’s program at New York Live Arts plays between ballet and hip-hop.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Despite its live music and the admirable skills of most of its dancers, “Baroque’d,” BalletNext’s program at New York Live Arts, is always less than good. It varies from the blandly vague (the first two items) to the amateurishly pseudo-experimental (the last). That last dance, “Something Sampled,” is sufficiently irksome to be considerably more memorable than the first two. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/12/arts/12BAROQUED/12BAROQUED-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 390, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/02/12/arts/12BAROQUED/12BAROQUED-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 390}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/12/arts/12BAROQUED/12BAROQUED-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 665, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/12/arts/12BAROQUED/12BAROQUED-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1330, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/12/arts/12BAROQUED/12BAROQUED-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/02/12/arts/12BAROQUED/12BAROQUED-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/12/arts/12BAROQUED/12BAROQUED-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Review: BalletNext Takes Risks in ‘Baroque’d’', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Pulsing Rhythm Binds Distinct Styles', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dancing', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Ballet Next Inc', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-02-11T21:37:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Dance', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alastair Macaulay', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alastair', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Macaulay', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/b9e73299-4fea-562b-972f-dbadf3f9f7a3', 'word_count': 570, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b9e73299-4fea-562b-972f-dbadf3f9f7a3'}, {'abstract': 'Ms. Jansen, a Dutch violinist, and Mr. Golan, an Israeli pianist, performed works including Prokofiev’s “Five Melodies for Violin and Piano” and Ravel’s Violin Sonata.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/02/12/arts/music/review-janine-jansen-and-itamar-golan-balance-power-and-nuance-at-zankel-hall.html', 'snippet': 'Ms. Jansen, a Dutch violinist, and Mr. Golan, an Israeli pianist, performed works including Prokofiev’s “Five Melodies for Violin and Piano” and Ravel’s Violin Sonata.', 'lead_paragraph': 'New York fans of the Dutch violinist Janine Jansen have had it rough in recent years. Illness caused her to bow out of high-profile concerts with the Budapest Festival Orchestra in 2013 and the New York Philharmonic last year. On Tuesday, she was back, in radiant form, with a recital at Zankel Hall alongside the Israeli pianist Itamar Golan, which proved that she is an artist worth the wait.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '2', 'source':