ount': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://video/ae7a50a0-fe19-5202-bfd1-4175f0d76c86'}, {'abstract': 'Brandon Sherrod, a starting forward for the Yale men’s basketball team, took off this school year to sing, perform and travel with the Whiffenpoofs, the university’s all-male a cappella group.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/02/12/sports/ncaabasketball/yale-forward-brandon-sherrod-takes-a-break-to-sing-with-whiffenpoofs.html', 'snippet': 'Brandon Sherrod, a starting forward for the Yale men’s basketball team, took off this school year to sing, perform and travel with the Whiffenpoofs, the university’s all-male a cappella group.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Approaching 10 p.m. on the eve of a recent blizzard, the Rockwood Music Hall, on the Lower East Side of Manhattan, was running low on breathing room, packed so tightly that each whoosh of cold air from the opening of the rear door brought sharp-eyed looks from those inside — no more, please. Even the stage was jammed: four musicians (drummer, keyboardist, two guitarists) and four singers, one of whom, stashed in the corner, slapping a tambourine against his hip, stood 6 feet 6 inches.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/12/sports/YALE1/YALE1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/02/12/sports/YALE1/YALE1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/12/sports/YALE1/YALE1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/12/sports/YALE1/YALE1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'supe