 year to help stabilize an economy reeling from political upheaval and a separatist uprising.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MOSCOW — The International Monetary Fund agreed on Thursday to throw a new $17.5 billion lifeline to Ukraine, hoping to stabilize the country as it teeters on the edge of default.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'I.M.F. Announces $17.5 Billion Package to Help Kiev Stabilize Economy', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'I.M.F. Announces $17.5 Billion Package to Help Kiev Stabilize Economy', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Ukraine', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'International Monetary Fund', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lagarde, Christine', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Yanukovych, Viktor F', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Russia', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-02-12T10:28:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By David M. Herszenhorn', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9def2815-e697-5ff6-bef8-10b467e0f86e', 'word_count': 851, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9def2815-e697-5ff6-bef8-10b467e0f86e'}, {'abstract': 'The move was the latest example of how the threat of deflation is pushing central bankers into unexplored territory on monetary policy.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/02/13/business/international/sweden-cuts-interest-rate-and-announces-bond-buying-program.html', 'snippet': 'The move was the latest example of how the threat of deflation is pushing central bankers into unexplored territory on monetary policy.', 'lead_paragraph': 'FRANKFURT — The Swedish central bank on Thursday put its benchmark interest rate in negative territory and announced a bond-buying program in bold moves to protect its economy from mounting economic and political uncertainty in Europe.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/13/business/13swedenrates-web1/13swedenrates-web1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 370, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/02/13/business/13swedenrates-web1/13swedenrates-web1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 370}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/13/business/13swedenrates-web1/13swedenrates-web1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 631, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/13/business/13swedenrates-web1/13swedenrates-web1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1262, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/13/business/13swedenrates-web1/13swedenrates-web1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/02/13/business/13swedenrates-web1/13swedenrates-web1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/13/business/13swedenrates-web1/13swedenrates-web1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Sweden Imposes Negative Interest Rate and Plans Bond-Buying Program', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Sweden Imposes Negative Interest Rate and Plans Bond-Buying Program', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Sweden', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Interest Rates', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Riksbank', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Inflation (Economics)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deflation (Economics)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-02-12T10:29:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'International Business', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jack Ewing', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jack', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ewing', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8d7c7202-fbe0-5348-9871-7669cb60b9ce', 'word_count': 686, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8d7c7202-fbe0-5348-9871-7669cb60b9ce'}, {'abstract': 'World Press Photo has announced its 2014 contest winners, with judges giving top honors to quieter moments.', 'web_url': 'https://lens.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/02/12/a-subtle-moment-becomes-the-world-press-photo-of-the-year/', 'snippet': 'World Press Photo has announced its 2014 contest winners, with judges giving top honors to quieter moments.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For the second year in a row, World Press Photo’s judges gave their top prize to an image from the contemporary issues category, bypassing news images from the conflict in Ukraine, the Ebola crisis in Sierra Leone and protests in Turkey.Mads Nissen’s photograph of two Russian gay men embracing was named the World Press Photo of the Year for 2014 in Amsterdam on Thursday. The winning image is part of a photo essay on the effects of an anti-gay law passed in Russia in 2013. Mr. Nissen is a staff photographer for the Danish newspaper Politiken and is represented by Panos Pictures.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Subtle Moment Becomes the World Press Photo of the Year', 'kicker': 'Lens', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Homosexuality and Bisexuality', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Photography', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hicks, Tyler', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McNally, Michele', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ponomarev, Sergey', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'World Press Photo Foundation', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'AFRICA', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'AMSTERDAM (NETHERLANDS)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Donetsk (Ukraine)', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Florida', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Italy', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Russia', 'rank': 13, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Sierra Leone', 'rank': 14, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-02-12T10:42:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Multimedia/Photos', 'byline': {'original': 'By James Estrin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'James', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Estrin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6b7e1a04-ab3a-576c-abb0-96fd574f88e3', 'word_count': 954, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6b7e1a04-ab3a-576c-abb0-96