ue': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mergers, Acquisitions and Divestitures', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mayer, Marissa', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Alibaba Group Holding Ltd', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Yahoo! Inc', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-02-12T17:12:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Robert Cyran', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Robert', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cyran', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/df493e1f-1734-578c-adb3-32e4066c8542', 'word_count': 396, 'uri': 'nyt://article/df493e1f-1734-578c-adb3-32e4066c8542'}, {'abstract': 'The conspiracy to avoid fiscal crisis.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/02/12/qe-truthers/', 'snippet': 'The conspiracy to avoid fiscal crisis.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Everyone knows about the infamous open letter warning Ben Bernanke not to engage in quantitative easing, lest he cause inflation and currency debasement; many are also familiar with the remarkable unwillingness of that letter’s signatories to admit, after more than four years of low inflation and a rising dollar, that they were wrong. But not many people seem to know about an opinion piece by John Taylor and Paul Ryan, released at about the same time, that is even more revealing about the GOP’s monetary madness.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'QE Truthers', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2015-02-12T17:14:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Pau