ng health insurance, tends to be viewed as the province of the very young. But for one group of mostly Brooklyn-based men in their 30s and 40s, many of whom came of age on the ramps and rails of lower Manhattan in the ’80s and ’90s, skating is still very much a way of life. And now, in a low-slung Long Island City warehouse, a group of 40 or so of them have erected a monument to their hobby: a secret, members-only DIY club reputed to be the largest and most elaborate skate park in town.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Secret Skate-Park Clubhouse for Grown-Up Brooklynites', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Organizations, Societies and Clubs', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Skateboarding', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Carson, John', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Brooklyn (NYC)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Long Island City (Queens, NY)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-02-12T19:00:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Eviana Hartman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Eviana', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hartman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/61f1a618-821d-53b0-9c04-0b5933d3ed06', 'word_count': 554, 'uri': 'nyt://article/61f1a618-821d-53b0-9c04-0b5933d3ed06'}, {'abstract': 'The amount of debris is likely to increase tenfold over the next decade unless nations start disposing of trash responsibly, new research suggests.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/02/13/science/earth/plastic-ocean-waste-levels-going-up-study-says.html', 'snippet': 'The amount of debris is likely to 