5-02-12T21:07:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Science', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': 'By Marie Tae McDermott', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Marie', 'middlename': 'Tae', 'lastname': 'McDermott', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/27e5d288-daef-58b4-8b3b-5ec50bdda6fc', 'word_count': 933, 'uri': 'nyt://article/27e5d288-daef-58b4-8b3b-5ec50bdda6fc'}, {'abstract': 'Scenes from the New York Fashion Week photo diary of Valerio Mezzanotti.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/02/12/new-york-fashion-week-creatures-of-the-wind-fall-winter-2015/', 'snippet': 'Scenes from the New York Fashion Week photo diary of Valerio Mezzanotti.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Scenes from the New York Fashion Week photo diary of Valerio Mezzanotti.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'New York Fashion Week: Creatures of the Wind Fall/Winter 2015', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'New York Fashion Week', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Women and Girls', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Creatures of the Wind (Fashion Label)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-02-12T21:10:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Valerio Mezzanotti', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Valerio', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mezzanotti', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/58803af9-0e82-5097-a779-99eb343da694', 'word_count': 41, 'uri': 'nyt://article/58803af9-0e82-5097-a779-99eb343da694'}, {'abstract': 'The Buddha-as-monk is a recurrent image in this Asia Society exhibit, which acknowledges the complexities of Myanmar cultural history and the yawning gaps in information available about the country.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/02/13/arts/design/art-of-devotion.html', 'snippet': 'The Buddha-as-monk is a recurrent image in this Asia Society exhibit, which acknowledges the complexities of Myanmar cultural history and the yawning gaps in information available about the country.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Religious images live switched-on, switched-off lives. I remember walking through the National Museum in Kyoto, Japan, some years back, taking in its rows of Buddhist sculpture, and being stopped by one piece, not because it was especially beautiful — it wasn’t — but because a vase with a single fresh flower had been placed in front of it, like an offering in a temple. I stayed with the image because someone — a guard? a visitor? — was telling me, in terms I don’t often think of in museums, that it was important, in a personal, spiritual way.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '27', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Review: Exploring ‘Buddhist Art of Myanmar’ at Asia Society', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Art of Devotion', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cotter, Holland', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Asia Society', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Buddhism', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Myanmar', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-02-12T21:18:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Art & Design', 'byline': {'original': 'By Holland Cotter', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Holland', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cotter', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/f1440ea1-4a2f-5a84-8131-99462f09fd49', 'word_count': 1375, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f1440ea1-4a2f-5a84-8131-99462f09fd49'}, {'abstract': 'A dog instead of a date? Yes, and at 90 percent off this weekend, at Best Friends Animal Society. For the commitment-averse, there’s comedy.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/02/13/nyregion/a-valentines-day-weekend-of-pet-adoptions-chocolate-and-improv.html', 'snippet': 'A dog instead of a date? Yes, and at 90 percent off this weekend, at Best Friends Animal Society. For the commitment-averse, there’s comedy.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Not long ago, one of the Miser’s single friends celebrated Valentine’s Day by adopting a puppy, a Chihuahua-pug mix named Whiskey. It seemed impulsive at the time, but Whiskey — we’re talking about the dog here — quickly became and remains a source of happy distractions. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '33', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/13/arts/13MISER/13MISER-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/02/13/arts/13MISER/13MISER-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/13/arts/13MISER/13MISER-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/13/arts/13MISER/13MISER-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumb