.html', 'snippet': 'A critical guide to productions in New York City, including shows in previews.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Approximate running times are in parentheses. Theaters are in Manhattan unless otherwise noted. Full reviews of current productions, additional listings, showtimes and ticket information are at nytimes.com/theater. A searchable, critical guide to theater is at nytimes.com/events.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/13/arts/13LISTINGS-THEATER/LISTINGS-THEATER-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 420, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/02/13/arts/13LISTINGS-THEATER/LISTINGS-THEATER-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 420}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/13/arts/13LISTINGS-THEATER/LISTINGS-THEATER-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 716, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/13/arts/13LISTINGS-THEATER/LISTINGS-THEATER-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1432, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/13/arts/13LISTINGS-THEATER/13LISTINGS-THEATER-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/02/13/arts/13LISTINGS-THEATER/13LISTINGS-THEATER-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/13/arts/13LISTINGS-THEATER/13LISTINGS-THEATER-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Theater Listings for Feb. 13-19', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Listings: Theater', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-02-12T23:55:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Theater', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Schedule', '_id': 'nyt://article/7f614d34-3dc2-5fe1-b153-008b6f15d240', 'word_count': 5270, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7f614d34-3dc2-5fe1-b153-008b6f15d240'}, {'abstract': 'This remake of Bill Gunn’s “Ganja and Hess” is a stylishly shot, coolly contemplative homage to the original.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/02/13/movies/review-da-sweet-blood-of-jesus-spike-lees-vampire-movie.html', 'snippet': 'This remake of Bill Gunn’s “Ganja and Hess” is a stylishly shot, coolly contemplative homage to the original.', 'lead_paragraph': '“Da Sweet Blood of Jesus,” Spike Lee’s new film, is a grisly and ghoulish vampire story. It is also an evident labor of love. The opening images — a solitary dancer undulating on the Red Hook waterfront, the Brooklyn Heights Promenade and other Kings County spots — offer a reminder that no filmmaker has shot this borough as beautifully and fondly as Mr. Lee. Martha’s Vineyard, where much of the action takes place, looks pretty good too. And though there are episodes of bloody mayhem and steamy sex, the mood is contemplative, at times almost serene. Mr. Lee has earned a reputation as a polemicist and provocateur, but he has also been, from the beginning, a sensualist and a visual stylist.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Review: ‘Da Sweet Blood of Jesus,’ Spike Lee’s Vampire Movie', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Laid-Back Vampires Ponder What’s for Lunch', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lee, Spike', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Da Sweet Blood of Jesus (Movie)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-02-12T23:56:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By A.O. Scott', 'person': [{'firstname': 'A.', 'middlename': 'O.', 'lastname': 'Scott', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/ff619ffc-b569-5645-a27d-e81064718a59', 'word_count': 550, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ff619ffc-b569-5645-a27d-e81064718a59'}, {'abstract': 'A college student with chronic headaches who suddenly became too dizzy to walk learned she had postural tachycardia syndrome — also called postural orthostatic tachycardia syndrome — a condition in which simply being upright causes lightheadedness and an elevated heart rate.', 'web_url': 'https://well.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/02/12/think-like-a-doctor-swept-off-her-feet-solved/', 'snippet': 'A college student with chronic headaches who suddenly became too dizzy to walk learned she had postural tachycardia syndrome — also called postural orthostatic tachycardia syndrome — a condition in which simply being upright causes lightheadedness...', 'lead_paragraph': 'On Wednesday, we challenged Well readers to take on the case of a 21-year-old college student with chronic headaches who suddenly became too dizzy to walk. She had a medical history that was complicated by back surgery and a subsequent infection, and chronic headaches after a car accident. More than 300 of you wrote in with suggested diagnoses, but only a handful of you noticed the clue that led the medical student who saw the patient to the right answer.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/10/health/tlad_well/tlad_well-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 592, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/10/health/tlad_well/tlad_well-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 592, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/10/health/tlad_well/tlad_well-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/02/10/health/tlad_well/tlad_well-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/10/health/tlad_well/tlad_well-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Think Like a Doctor: Swept Off Her Feet Solved', 'kicker': 'Well', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Blood Pressure', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Doctors', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Headaches', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Nerves and Nervous System', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-02-12T23:58:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Science', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lisa Sanders, M.D', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lisa', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sanders', 'qualifier': 'M.D', 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization':