large', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/13/arts/13OSCARHUNT1/13OSCARHUNT1-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 354, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/02/13/arts/13OSCARHUNT1/13OSCARHUNT1-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 354}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/13/arts/13OSCARHUNT1/13OSCARHUNT1-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 604, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/13/arts/13OSCARHUNT1/13OSCARHUNT1-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1208, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/13/arts/13OSCARHUNT1/13OSCARHUNT1-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/02/13/arts/13OSCARHUNT1/13OSCARHUNT1-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/13/arts/13OSCARHUNT1/13OSCARHUNT1-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'For Oscars Telecast, Few Black Nominees Mean Fewer Black Viewers', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Telecast in Search of Black Viewers', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Academy Awards (Oscars)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Blacks', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Black People', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Ratings (Audience Measurement)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-02-13T00:24:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'subsection_name': 'Awards Season', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael Cieply and Brooks Barnes', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cieply', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Brooks', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Barnes', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3e2ecfea-5c49-5f2a-aaeb-590c73165994', 'word_count': 1276, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3e2ecfea-5c49-5f2a-aaeb-590c73165994'}, {'abstract': 'Ronit Elkabetz plays a woman who is determined to escape her marriage, although the rabbinic power structure is stacked against her.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/02/13/movies/review-in-gett-the-trial-of-viviane-amsalem-a-woman-fights-for-her-freedom.html', 'snippet': 'Ronit Elkabetz plays a woman who is determined to escape her marriage, although the rabbinic power structure is stacked against her.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The hypnotic “Gett: The Trial of Viviane Amsalem” is the story of a woman wronged by men and God, if finally, in a sense, redeemed by cinema. Under Israeli law, a woman can be divorced only if her husband presents her with a religious bill of divorce called a gett (sometimes spelled get). No gett, no divorce. The long-suffering title character desperately wants to be free of her husband, who refuses to let her go. So year after year, Viviane pleads her case before a rabbinic court, waiting for her divorce as days slip into weeks and then months, her pacific face glazed with tears and her body occasionally rocked by a laugh tinged with knowing and madness. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/13/arts/13GETT/13GETT-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 341, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/02/13/arts/13GETT/13GETT-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 341}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/13/arts/13GETT/13GETT-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 581, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/13/arts/13GETT/13GETT-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1163, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/13/arts/13GETT/13GETT-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/02/13/arts/13GETT/13GETT-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/13/arts/13GETT/13GETT-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Review: In ‘Gett: The Trial of Viviane Amsalem,’ a Woman Fights for Her Freedom', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Tremulously Desperate, as the Rabbis Sit in Judgment', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Elkabetz, Ronit', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Elkabetz, Shlomi', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': '