 jihadist propaganda magazine, the interview is believed to be the first time the group has said anything concerning the whereabouts of Hayat Boumeddiene.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/02/13/world/middleeast/isis-releases-interview-with-woman-linked-to-amedy-coulibaly.html', 'snippet': 'Published in an English-language version of its online jihadist propaganda magazine, the interview is believed to be the first time the group has said anything concerning the whereabouts of Hayat Boumeddiene.', 'lead_paragraph': ' The Islamic State group said Thursday that a woman it described as the widow of the French gunman responsible for a deadly siege at a Paris supermarket last month — a woman who is now among France’s most wanted fugitives — was living among the group’s followers, presumably in Syria or Iraq. The assertion by the Islamic State, published in an English-language version of its online jihadist propaganda magazine, is believed to be the first time the group has said anything concerning the whereabouts of the woman, Hayat Boumeddiene, 26. French officials suspect that she was an accomplice of the gunman, Amedy Coulibaly, killed in a Jan. 9 shootout with the French police. The article asserted that Mr. Coulibaly had arranged for her travel to lands controlled by the Islamic State before the attack. She was quoted as saying that she was happy to be living in an area controlled by the Islamic State, also known as ISIS or ISIL, and was quoted as advising other women followers of the group to “be bases of support and safety for your husbands, brothers, fathers, and sons.” Turkish officials have said that Ms. Boumeddiene traveled to Turkey from Spain before the Paris attack and entered Syria through a Turkish border crossing on Jan. 8, one day before the supermarket siege. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'ISIS Releases Interview With Woman Linked to Amedy Coulibaly', 'kicker': 'World Briefing', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'ISIS Releases Interview With Woman Who Fled France', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Islamic State in Iraq and Syria (ISIS)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Boumeddiene, Hayat (1988- )', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'France', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Charlie Hebdo', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Terrorism', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iraq', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Syria', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Coulibaly, Amedy (1982-2015)', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fugitives', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-02-13T02:43:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rick Gladstone', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gladstone', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/9d78478c-8ce1-538b-8d41-53dad20acc3a', 'word_count': 218, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9d78478c-8ce1-538b-8d41-53dad20acc3a'}, {'abstract': 'The International Federation of Red Cross and Red Crescent Societies reported Thursday that its burial teams in Guinea have been attacked verbally or physically 10 times a month on average since March.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/02/13/world/africa/red-cross-faces-attacks-at-ebola-victims-funerals.html', 'snippet': 'The International Federation of Red Cross and Red Crescent Societies reported Thursday that its burial teams in Guinea have been attacked verbally or physically 10 times a month on average since March.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Red Cross vol