Kuka,” at 3LD Art & Technology Center, he reveals that when he was 10, his wealthy parents became bankrupt and suicidal. The family moved to a 40-square-foot room; Mr. Huang, feeling compelled to be a perfect child, masked his emotions to become the picture of obedience. In other words, a robot. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/13/arts/13HUANG/13HUANG-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/02/13/arts/13HUANG/13HUANG-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/13/arts/13HUANG/13HUANG-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/13/arts/13HUANG/13HUANG-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/13/arts/13HUANG/13HUANG-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/02/13/arts/13HUANG/13HUANG-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/13/arts/13HUANG/13HUANG-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Review: ‘Huang Yi &amp; Kuka,’ a Pas de Deux Between Human and Machine', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Steeled to Make Every Step Perfect', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dancing', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Huang Yi', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Robots and Robotics', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-02-13T04:01:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Dance', 'byline': {'original': 'By Gia Kourlas', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Gia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kourlas', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/a4cdad68-57f3-5d86-bc98-bc1d3712a76e', 'word_count': 431, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a4cdad68-57f3-5d86-bc98-bc1d3712a76e'}, {'abstract': 'In some cases, material was republished with no credit at all, while other articles made passing reference to outside sources but failed to give proper credit when passages were taken verbatim or with minor changes.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/02/13/business/media/news-director-at-mic-is-fired-after-plagiarism-accusations.html', 'snippet': 'In some cases, material was republished with no credit at all, while other articles made passing reference to outside sources but failed to give proper credit when passages were taken verbatim or with minor changes.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In the latest plagiarism scandal in journalism, Mic, a news site intended for the so-called millennial generation, has fired its news director after numerous examples surfaced showing that he had lifted material from other sources without proper attribution.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Mic News Director Is Fired After Plagiarism Accusations', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Plagiarism at News Site; Editor Fired', 'name': None, 'seo': N