ue': 'National Assn of Attorneys General', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-02-13T04:38:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Eric Lipton and Danielle Ivory', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Eric', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lipton', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Danielle', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ivory', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7b983dff-d076-5bab-a4a9-56033b973a9e', 'word_count': 1354, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7b983dff-d076-5bab-a4a9-56033b973a9e'}, {'abstract': 'The Baguette handbag will be artfully reimagined by five powerhouse women, including Rihanna and Sarah Jessica Parker, in celebration of the company’s new Madison Avenue flagship store.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/02/13/t-magazine/fendi-baguette-rihanna-sarah-jessica-parker.html', 'snippet': 'The Baguette handbag will be artfully reimagined by five powerhouse women, including Rihanna and Sarah Jessica Parker, in celebration of the company’s new Madison Avenue flagship store.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Fendi Baguette was a fashion-world success from the day it was released in 1997 and, thanks to being a favorite of Carrie’s on “Sex and the City,” it became a bona fide pop culture icon soon after. As of 2015, more than 1,000 versions of the design have been created ranging from rare limited editions to mass-market reimaginings. In celebration of Fendi’s new flagship store on Madison Avenue, the Italian brand has now teamed up with five powerhouse women to present yet another unique line of the famous shoulder bag. This time around, Rihanna, Jourdan Dunn, Rachel Feinstein, Leandra Medine and, yes, Sarah Jessica Parker, have each designed their own 3Baguette, the smaller version of the bag. Each piece will be auctioned online from February 13 through March 13 with proceeds going to a charity of each guest designer’s choosing, from the Brain Trauma Foundation (Parker) to the Naomi Berrie Diabetes Center (Feinstein).', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/13/t-magazine/13fendi-bobb/13fendi-bobb-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 450, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/02/13/t-magazine/13fendi-bobb/13fendi-bobb-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 450}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/13/t-magazine/13fendi-bobb/13fendi-bobb-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 768, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/13/t-magazine/13fendi-bobb/13fendi-bobb-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1536, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/13/t-magazine/13fendi-bobb/13fendi-bobb-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/02/13/t-magazine/13fendi-bobb/13fendi-bobb-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/13/t-magazine/13fendi-bobb/13fendi-bobb-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Style Icons Update a Fendi Classic for a Good Cause', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': 