urtain of Distraction has taken student-section antics to a new level — and it appears to be costing visiting teams one to two points per game.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/02/14/upshot/how-arizona-state-reinvented-free-throw-distraction.html', 'snippet': 'Arizona State’s Curtain of Distraction has taken student-section antics to a new level — and it appears to be costing visiting teams one to two points per game.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A shark attack. The return of Elvis. Twerking farm animals. A shirtless guitarist. Kissing unicorns. An old lady yelling at you to get off her lawn. Distracted yet? So, too, are college basketball players, who have tried — and often failed — to overcome the creative attempts of students at Arizona State to destroy the focus of free-throw shooters.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/11/upshot/11UP-Curtain/11UP-Curtain-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 385, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/02/11/upshot/11UP-Curtain/11UP-Curtain-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 385}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/11/upshot/11UP-Curtain/11UP-Curtain-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 658, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/11/upshot/11UP-Curtain/11UP-Curtain-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1315, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/11/upshot/11UP-Curtain/11UP-Curtain-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/02/11/upshot/11UP-Curtain/11UP-Curtain-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/11/upshot/11UP-Curtain/11UP-Curtain-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'How Arizona State Reinvented Free-Throw Distraction', 'kicker': 'Curtains for Visitors', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Bad Free Throw? Blame the Twerking Livestock', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Basketball (College)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'ARIZONA STATE UNIVERSITY', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'University of Arizona', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-02-13T05:24:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'The Upshot', 'byline': {'original': 'By Justin Wolfers', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Justin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wolfers', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f6b714e2-21cf-5e5c-a8f8-775032fbbee3', 'word_count': 1181, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f6b714e2-21cf-5e5c-a8f8-775032fbbee3'}, {'abstract': 'Twenty-two Marines and sailors were injured at a military base in the Southern California desert on Thursday when a fire-extinguisher system went off during a training exercise, the military said.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/02/13/us/california-22-hurt-in-military-training-as-vehicles-fire-extinguisher-goes-off.html', 'snippet': 'Twenty-two Marines and sailors were injured at a military base in the Southern California desert on Thursday when a fire-extinguisher system went off during a training exercise, the military said.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Twenty-two Marines and sailors were injured at a military base in the Southern California desert on Thursday when a fire-extinguisher system went off during a training exercise, the military said. The accident happened inside an amphibious assault vehicle at the Marine Corps Air Ground Combat Center in Twentynine Palms, east of Los Angeles, the Marine Corps said. Some of the Marines and sailors were taken to a hospital to be treated for inhaling the fire retardant, and they were in stable condition, according to the Marine Corps. None of the injuries were life-threatening, Capt. Maureen T. Krebs, a Marine Corps spokeswoman, said. The vehicle, which resembles a tank, is used to move troops from ships to land. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'California: 22 Hurt in Military Training as Vehicle’s Fire Extinguisher Goes Off', 'kicker': 'National Briefing | West', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'California: 22 Hurt in Military Training as Vehicle’s Fire Extinguisher Goes Off', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Accidents and Safety', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'California', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Traffic Accidents and Safety', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United States Marine Corps', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-02-13T05:41:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ashley Southall', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ashley', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Southall', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/3