 Tinder has not fundamentally changed the local dating scene so much as quickened and coarsened its already abrupt, aggressive nature.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On a recent night, with Valentine’s Day looming, I went out for drinks with a woman I know and a few of her friends. It was a Thursday, and the bar they chose, Bondurants, on the Upper East Side, was packed with people just like them: good-looking, semi-affluent millennials, downing craft beer and milling about in hungry-looking, monosexual clusters. ', 'print_section': 'MB', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/15/nyregion/15LOVE1/15LOVE1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 593, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/02/15/nyregion/15LOVE1/15LOVE1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 593}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/15/nyregion/15LOVE1/15LOVE1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1011, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/15/nyregion/15LOVE1/15LOVE1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2023, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/15/nyregion/15LOVE1/15LOVE1-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/02/15/nyregion/15LOVE1/15LOVE1-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/15/nyregion/15LOVE1/15LOVE1-thumbLarge-v3.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'On Tinder, Taking a Swipe at Love, or Sex, or Something, in New York', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Taking a Swipe at Love (or Something)', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Feuer, Alan', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Tinder (Mobile App)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Social Conditions and Trends', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dating and Relationships', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mobile Applications', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Single Persons', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Online Dating', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-02-13T10:00:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alan Feuer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Feuer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2ea8b98c-499b-5e19-a547-15c7e4159f98', 'word_count': 2522, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2ea8b98c-499b-5e19-a547-15c7e4159f98'}, {'abstract': 'Mr. Rudder, who met his wife in a “totally off-line” way, spends time on Sundays being a dad and playing basketball.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/02/15/nyregion/how-christian-rudder-a-founder-of-okcupid-spends-his-sunday.html', 'snippet': 'Mr. Rudder, who met his wife in a “totally off-line” way, spends time on Sundays being a dad and playing basketball.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The lovelorn this Valentine’s Day can take heart. The dating site OKCupid generates approximately 30,000 first dates every day around the United States. That’s an eye-catching number, even for Christian Rudder, a founder of the website and data geek, whose first book, “Dataclysm: Who We Are When We Think No One’s Looking,” was published in September. Yet Mr. Rudder, 39, met his wife, Reshma Patel, the owner of a public relations firm, in a “totally off-line” way. They hit it off in 1999 when his band was playing a show with her boyfriend’s band in Boston. The couple, who married in 2006, live in North Williamsburg with their 3-year-old daughter, Plum.', 'print_section': 'MB', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/15/nyregion/15ROUTINE1/15ROUTINE1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 470, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/02/15/nyregion/15ROUTINE1/15ROUTINE1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 470}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/15/nyregion/15ROUTINE1/15ROUTINE1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 802, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/15/nyregion/15ROUTINE1/15ROUTINE1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1604, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/15/nyregion/15ROUTINE1/15ROUTINE1-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/02/15/nyregion/15ROUTINE1/15ROUTINE1-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/15/nyregion/