e': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ea8034b3-ba13-516c-ba6f-3c5464e45002', 'word_count': 868, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ea8034b3-ba13-516c-ba6f-3c5464e45002'}, {'abstract': 'An exhibition of 54 works by 37 photographers at the Heckscher Museum of Art is a good reminder that experimental photography did not begin in the age of the digital camera.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/02/15/nyregion/in-huntington-an-exhibition-of-pioneering-photography-through-the-ages.html', 'snippet': 'An exhibition of 54 works by 37 photographers at the Heckscher Museum of Art is a good reminder that experimental photography did not begin in the age of the digital camera.', 'lead_paragraph': '“Modern Alchemy,” a small gem of an exhibition at the Heckscher Museum of Art in Huntington, is a good reminder that experimental photography did not begin in the age of the digital camera, although technology has certainly helped it evolve. A selection of diverse images, accompanied by thorough explanations of how various photographers worked, starting with Man Ray in the 1930s, supports this idea.', 'print_section': 'LI', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/15/nyregion/15ARTSLI1/15ARTSLI1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 456, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/02/15/nyregion/15ARTSLI1/15ARTSLI1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 456}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/15/nyregion/15ARTSLI1/15ARTSLI1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 779, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/15/nyregion/15ARTSLI