, 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/02/14/t-magazine/winter-skin-recipe-celebrity-facialist-joanna-vargas.html', 'snippet': 'Joanna Vargas, who prepped Julianne Moore and Maggie Gyllenhaal for the Golden Globes this weekend, shares at-home applications to combat dryness.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On the red carpet this weekend, the New York-based stars Julianne Moore and Maggie Gyllenhaal appeared untouched by winter as they arrived at the 2015 Golden Globe Awards. Their skin was radiant, almost dewy — not dry like most faces in Manhattan these days. And not coincidentally, they were each prepped for the evening by the celebrity facialist Joanna Vargas, who also counts Naomi Watts as a regular client. The expert, who just launched her newest anti-aging solution — the Forever Facial ($700), designed to improve the skin’s elasticity through the use of heat and radio waves (“they push your collagen fibers back together again and trigger collagen production,” she explains) — says the secret to great skin, no matter the time of year, is a facial once a month. “Nothing you do at home can replace a professional exfoliation, extraction and attention,” she says.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/14/t-magazine/14skin-mosci-1/14skin-mosci-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 300, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/01/14/t-magazine/14skin-mosci-1/14skin-mosci-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 300}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/14/t-magazine/14skin-mosci-1/14skin-mosci-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 512, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/14/t-magazine/14skin-mosci-1/14skin-mosci-1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/14/t-magazine/14skin-mosci-1/14skin-mosci-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/01/14/t-magazine/14skin-mosci-1/14skin-mosci-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/14/t-magazine/14skin-mosci-1/14skin-mosci-1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Celebrity Facialist’s Recipe for Remedying Winter Skin', 'kicker': 'On Beauty', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Skin', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Celebrities', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gyllenhaal, Maggie', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Moore, Julianne', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Watts, Naomi', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-02-14T05:00:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TDesign', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Renata Mosci', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Renata', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mosci', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ea34e226-25bc-5be3-b495-aa0c8f9cc5d8', 'word_count': 340, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ea34e226-25bc-5be3-b495-aa0c8f9cc5d8'}, {'abstract': 'Money and race issues simmer amid the turmoil in Danai Gurira’s latest play, “Familiar,” in New Haven.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/02/15/nyregion/a-review-of-familiar-in-new-haven.html', 'snippet': 'Money and race issues simmer amid the turmoil in Danai Gurira’s latest play, “Familiar,” in New Haven.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Every wedding weekend needs a family crisis, and the one in Danai Gurira’s “Familiar” is the arrival of an eccentric aunt from Zimbabwe with dollar signs in her eyes. But this play, having its world premiere at Yale Repertory Theater, already has other sources of tension: The bride is a 34-year-old virgin, and the groom, marrying into a Zimbabwean family, is white.', 'print_section': 'CT', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/15/nyregion/15ARTSCT1/15ARTSCT1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/02/15/nyregion/15ARTSCT1/15ARTSCT1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/15/nyregion/15ARTSCT1/15ARTSCT1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/15/nyregion/15ARTSCT1/15ARTSCT1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/15/nyregion/15ARTSCT1/15ARTSCT1-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/02/15/nyregion/15ARTSCT1/15ARTSCT1-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'cre