 expropriate all the earnings of Fannie Mae and Freddie Mac. What exactly is it trying to hide?', 'lead_paragraph': 'On Aug. 17, 2012, the federal government began expropriating all the earnings of Fannie Mae and Freddie Mac, the mortgage finance giants that succumbed to the 2008 crisis. ', 'print_section': 'BU', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'After the Housing Crisis, a Cash Flood and Silence', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'After Crisis, a Cash Flood and Silence', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Federal Home Loan Mortgage Corp (Freddie Mac)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Morgenson, Gretchen', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Federal National Mortgage Assn (Fannie Mae)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Treasury Department', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mortgages', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Law and Legislation', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Justice Department', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-02-14T17:19:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'SundayBusiness', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Gretchen Morgenson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Gretchen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Morgenson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a9ffc526-d9c1-5d86-9d77-cbe38e027372', 'word_count': 1124, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a9ffc526-d9c1-5d86-9d77-cbe38e027372'}, {'abstract': 'The Islamic State is expanding beyond its base in Syria and Iraq to establish militant affiliates in Afghanistan, Algeria, Eg