', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Smoking Toll Gets Much Worse', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Smoking Toll Gets Much Worse', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Smoking and Tobacco', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New England Journal of Medicine', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Research', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicine and Health', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cancer', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AMERICAN CANCER SOCIETY', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Cancer Institute', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-02-14T19:30:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'subsection_name': 'Sunday Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/bb35256a-6310-58b8-9c20-8c75420f4828', 'word_count': 502, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bb35256a-6310-58b8-9c20-8c75420f4828'}, {'abstract': 'A much larger budget is needed to stem the illicit trade in rhino horn, ivory and other prized animal parts.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/02/15/opinion/sunday/wildlife-slaughter-goes-unabated.html', 'snippet': 'A much larger budget is needed to stem the illicit trade in rhino horn, ivory and other prized animal parts.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As the world’s booming black market for body parts from endangered species continues to elude effective policing, rhinoceros deaths quadrupled in four years to the 1,215 killed by African smugglers in 2014. These magnificent animals were slaughtered so that urbanites in places like China and Vietnam can take a dose of powdered rhino horn, which fetches tens of thousands of dollars a pound as a luxury cure for hangovers. ', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/15/opinion/15sun3WEB/15sun3WEB-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 437, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/02/15/opinion/15sun3WEB/15sun3WEB-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 437}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/15/opinion/15sun3WEB/15sun3WEB-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 747, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/15/opinion/15sun3WEB/15sun3WEB-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1493, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/15/opinion/15sun3WEB/15sun3WEB-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/02/15/opinion/15sun3WEB/15sun3WEB-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/15/opinion/15sun3WEB/15sun3WEB-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Wildlife Slaughter Goes Unabated', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Wildlife Slaughter Goes Unabated', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Poaching (Wildlife)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Endangered and Extinct Species', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Black Markets', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Rhinoceroses', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Ivory', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-02-14T19:30:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'subsection_name': 'Sunday Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/93bcba3e-3e3a-531a-aaf6-e3df73ddce30', 'word_count': 417, 'uri': 'nyt://article/93bcba3e-3e3a-531a-aaf6-e3df73ddce30'}, {'abstract': 'The growth and radicalization of Islamist groups raise the possibility that large parts of Libya could become a satellite of the Islamic State.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/02/15/opinion/sunday/what-libyas-unraveling-means.html', 'snippet': 'The growth and radicalization of Islamist groups raise the possibility that large parts of Libya could become a satellite of the Islamic State.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Largely overshadowed by the crises in Syria, Iraq and Ukraine, Libya’s unraveling has received comparatively little attention over the past few months. As this oil-rich nation veers toward complete chaos, world leaders would be wise to redouble efforts led by the United Nations to broker a power-sharing deal among warring factions.', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/15/opinion/15sun1WEB/15sun1WEB-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 393, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/02/15/opinion/15sun1WEB/15su