type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew C. Revkin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': 'C.', 'lastname': 'Revkin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6b031498-407b-5a1d-b712-6ee29fc6df97', 'word_count': 749, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6b031498-407b-5a1d-b712-6ee29fc6df97'}, {'abstract': 'Comparable devastation.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/02/15/weimar-and-greece-continued/', 'snippet': 'Comparable devastation.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Try to talk about macroeconomics, and you’re sure to encounter accusations that your policies would turn us into Weimar Germany; those wheelbarrows full of cash remain the ultimate bogeymen for many, despite years of being wrong about everything. As some of us have noted, however, there’s a peculiar selectivity in the use of Weimar as cautionary tale: it’s always about the hyperinflation of 1923, never about the deflationary effects of the gold standard and austerity in 1930-32, which is, you know, what brought you-know-who to power. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Weimar and Greece, Continued', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2015-02-15T14:56:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/bd3971be-3db8-5138-bf21-6646d3949aa3', 'word_count': 207, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bd3971be-3db8-5138-bf21-6646d3949aa3'}, {'abstract': 'Mr. Levy’s career went into a spiral after the failure of “Mourning Becomes Electra,” and he was imprisoned for two years for his role in a drug ring.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/02/15/arts/music/marvin-david-levy-opera-composer-who-became-a-felon-is-dead-at-82.html', 'snippet': 'Mr. Levy’s career went into a spiral after the failure of “Mourning Becomes Electra,” and he was imprisoned for two years for his role in a drug ring.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It was only after he entered Dante’s Inferno — his name for the series of federal penitentiaries that became his home for two years — that the composer Marvin David Levy marshaled the resolve to write the kind of music he had always wanted.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '26', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/15/arts/15levy-obit/15levy-obit-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 465, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/02/15/arts/15levy-obit/15levy-obit-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 465}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/15/arts/15levy-obit/15levy-obit-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 794, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/15/arts/15levy-obit/15levy-obit-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1588, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/15/arts/15levy-obit/15levy-obit-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/02/15/arts/15levy-obit/15levy-obit-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'