'snippet': 'Coming in second were Chilean director Pablo Larraín’s “The Club,” about a home for errant priests, which took the grand jury prize, the Silver Bear, and “Ixcanul Volcano,” by the Guatemalan director Jayro Bustamante.', 'lead_paragraph': '“Taxi,” in which the Iranian director Jafar Panahi mounted a dashboard camera in a yellow cab and drove it around Tehran, took the top prize, the Golden Bear, at the 65th Annual Berlin Film Festival on Saturday. Mr. Panahi’s young niece, who appears in the film and steals the show with her luminous curiosity, accepted the award on her uncle’s behalf.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '‘Taxi’ by Jafar Panahi Takes Top Prize at Berlin Film Festival', 'kicker': 'Carpetbagger', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'ARONOFSKY, DARREN', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Haigh, Andrew', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Herzog, Werner', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Panahi, Jafar', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rampling, Charlotte', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Berlin (Germany)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-02-15T15:34:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rachel Donadio', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rachel', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Donadio', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/efd27792-329a-5a6b-80c1-80dbb3cc3aab', 'word_count': 432, 'uri': 'nyt://article/efd27792-329a-5a6b-80c1-80dbb3cc3aab'}, {'abstract': 'Mr. Levine’s work was vibrantly, angrily and often painfully alive with the sound, smell and sinew of heavy manual labor.', 'web_url': 'https://www.n