, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Slideshow', '_id': 'nyt://slideshow/c946ccdd-0da6-50dc-aa6e-d61e24588aea', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://slideshow/c946ccdd-0da6-50dc-aa6e-d61e24588aea'}, {'abstract': 'Mr. Levine’s spare, ironic poems of the industrial heartland evoked the drudgery and hardships of working-class life in America.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/02/16/books/an-appraisal-the-poet-philip-levine-an-outsider-archiving-the-forgotten.html', 'snippet': 'Mr. Levine’s spare, ironic poems of the industrial heartland evoked the drudgery and hardships of working-class life in America.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Della and Tatum, Sweet Pea and Packy, Ida and Cal. You met a lot of unpretentious people in Philip Levine’s spare, ironic poems of the industrial heartland. Mr. Levine had toiled in auto plants as a young man. “I saw that the people that I was working with,” he told Detroit Magazine, “were voiceless in a way.” ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/16/arts/16APPRECIATIONJP/16APPRECIATIONJP-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 807, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/02/16/arts/16APPRECIATIONJP/16APPRECIATIONJP-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 807}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/16/arts/16APPRECIATIONJP/16APPRECIATIONJP-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 762, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/16/arts/16APPRECIATIONJP/16APPRECIATIONJP-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1523, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'le