tween the two sides.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/02/16/nyregion/cablevision-and-union-reach-brooklyn-contract-deal.html', 'snippet': 'A two-year contract agreement gives the company’s 262 Brooklyn technicians considerable pay raises and ends a three-year standoff between the two sides.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Cablevision and the Communications Workers of America have reached a two-year contract agreement that gives the company’s 262 Brooklyn technicians considerable pay raises and ends a three-year standoff between the two sides.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Cablevision and Union Reach Brooklyn Contract Deal', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Cablevision and Union Reach Brooklyn Contract Deal', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Cablevision Systems Corporation', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Communications Workers of America', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Organized Labor', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wages and Salaries', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Brooklyn (NYC)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-02-16T03:24:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nikita Stewart', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nikita', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Stewart', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e7c2df52-53e6-5deb-94f7-567776ddff92', 'word_count': 483, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e7c2df52-53e6-5deb-94f7-567776ddff92'}, {'abstract': 'The low temperature dipped to 3 degrees in Central Park on Monday morning, missing the record set for that date, but the wind chills in the city were below minus