etailers, many of whom have struggled to adapt to the technological age they helped usher in.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/02/16/opinion/goodbye-to-the-electronics-store.html', 'snippet': 'Internet-based retailers, especially Amazon, have had a particularly devastating impact on electronics retailers, many of whom have struggled to adapt to the technological age they helped usher in.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I was assembling a home audio system recently and needed speaker wires. A friend recommended RadioShack. I went to two — in Manhattan and in Brooklyn — but, to my surprise, neither carried any. How could RadioShack, the place Americans go to for cables, connectors, circuits and all kinds of other electronic doodads, not have speaker wires?', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/16/opinion/16mon3web/16mon3web-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/02/16/opinion/16mon3web/16mon3web-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/16/opinion/16mon3web/16mon3web-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/16/opinion/16mon3web/16mon3web-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/16/opinion/16mon3web/16mon3web-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/02/16/opini