dynamic search model to explain why “most single people are crazy” is brilliant — and I don’t just say that because it starts with homage to a classic forerunner.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Good Odds But Odd Goods', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2015-02-16T12:57:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4141039c-06a0-53dd-8f54-0be0f673496f', 'word_count': 63, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4141039c-06a0-53dd-8f54-0be0f673496f'}, {'abstract': 'Some of Chávez’s best-known works — including his “Sinfonía india” and “H.P.,” a ballet symphony — will be played, along with works by Silvestre Revueltas, Alberto Ginastera, Heitor Villa-Lobos, and an overview of Mexican choral music.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/02/16/bard-summerscape-to-feature-work-of-the-composer-carlos-chvez/', 'snippet': 'Some of Chávez’s best-known works — including his “Sinfonía india” and “H.P.,” a ballet symphony — will be played, along with works by Silvestre Revueltas, Alberto Ginastera, Heitor Villa-Lobos, and an overview of Mexican choral music.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The music of Carlos Chávez, a key 20th-century Mexican composer whose works blended modern, folk and pre-Columbian influences, will be explored this summer at the Bard SummerScape Festival in Annandale-on-Hudson, N.Y., the festival announced Monday. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Bard SummerScape to Feature Work of the Composer Carlos Chávez', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Bard SummerScape To Focus on Chávez', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bard SummerScape Festival', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Classical Music', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Botstein, Leon', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Annandale-on-Hudson (NY)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-02-16T13:01:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael Cooper', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cooper', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fec8c521-f9d5-52ab-876f-e52b718f197f', 'word_count': 253, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fec8c521-f9d5-52ab-876f-e52b718f197f'}, {'abstract': 'Highlights from the International Herald Tribune archives: Women’s rights activist calls for action in 1940.', 'web_url': 'https://iht-retrospective.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/02/16/1940-women-called-to-new-fight/', 'snippet': 'Highlights from the International Herald Tribune archives: Women’s rights activist calls for action in 1940.', 'lead_paragraph': 'NEW YORK — A call to leaders of American women to meet in New York next fall for a Woman’s Centennial Congress to make plans for a campaign to extend feminine rights during the next century was issued today [Feb. 16] by Mrs. Carrie Chapman Catt, president of the National American Woman’s Suffrage Association. Mrs. Catt announced that the congress was also intended to commemorate ‘‘the almost unbelievable changes that have taken place in the status of women’’ in the last 100 years. She said the fight for women’s rights had been so successful in this period that it might well be called the ‘‘Women’s Century.’’ — New York Herald Tribune, European Edition, Feb. 17, 1940', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/17/blogs/17iht-oldfeb17-carrie/17iht-oldfeb17-carrie-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 583, 'width': 459, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/17/blogs/17iht-oldfeb17-carrie/17iht-oldfeb17-carrie-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 583, 'width': 459, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/17/blogs/17iht-oldfeb17-carrie/17iht-oldfeb17-carrie-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/02/17/blogs/17iht-oldfeb17-carrie/17iht-oldfeb17-carrie-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/17/blogs/17iht-oldfeb17-carrie/17iht-oldfeb17-carrie-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': '1940: Women Called to New Fight', 'kicker': 'IHT Retrospective', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': "Women's Rights", 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-02-16T13:01:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By International Herald Tribune', 'person': [{'firstname': 'International', 'middlename': 'Herald', 'lastname': 'Tribune', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/df4050d6-6a64-56fc-a26b-43b2360ae763', 'word_count': 116, 'uri': 'nyt://article/df4050d6-6a64-56fc-a26b-43b2360ae763'}, {'abstract': 'Some surprising good news.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/02/16/new-york-diversifies/', 'snippet': 'Some surprising good news.', 'lead_paragraph': 'One thing I learned from Ed Glaeser’s fine work on the economy of New York was that the city, after a complex past, had become essentially a monoculture. That is, its export sector — the part of the economy that sells to other locations, as opposed to providing local, nontraded goods and services — was basically finance and nothing else.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'New York Diversifies', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2015-02-16T13:08:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ae29ac1b-3417-51d1-9194-724d4b996454', 'word_count': 211, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ae29ac1b-3417-51d1-9194-724d4b996454'}, {'abstract': 'Unlike more freewheeling ceremonies of the past, this year’s awards were a buttoned-down affair.', 'web_url': 'https://carpetbagger.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/02/16/imitation-game-grand-budapest-hotel-and-decorum-win-over-writers-guild/', 'snippet': 'Unlike more freewheeling ceremonies of the past, this year’s awards were a buttoned-down affair.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Stories of freewheeling Writers Guild Awards ceremonies of yore was one of the reasons the Bagger traveled to the tourist-chocked confines of Midtown Manhattan on a frigid Saturday