l': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/02/16/new-york-fashion-week-trend-buttons-fall-winter-2015-shows/', 'snippet': 'Oversize buttons are shaping up to be fall wardrobe fixtures.', 'lead_paragraph': 'What is in a button? It’s functional and fastens, usually without being noticed — until now. On the fall/winter 2015 runways in New York, the utilitarian little notions have been upgraded from behind the scenes to front and center. We saw them first at Victoria Beckham, who sewed large horn buttons onto knit shift dresses and sculpted outerwear. A few hours later, Derek Lam introduced double-breasted vests fastened with oversize white buttons and turtlenecks dotted with black ones. And at Edun, buttons embellished extra-large pea coats and the necks of dresses. Practical or not, they’re poised to be a fixture for fall.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/16/t-magazine/16trend-button-gilchrist/16trend-button-gilchrist-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 450, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/02/16/t-magazine/16trend-button-gilchrist/16trend-button-gilchrist-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 450}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/16/t-magazine/16trend-button-gilchrist/16trend-button-gilchrist-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 768, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/16/t-magazine/16trend-button-gilchrist/16trend-button-gilchrist-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1536, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/16/t-magazine/16tr