e', 'news_desk': 'Science', 'section_name': 'Science', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Letter', '_id': 'nyt://article/06425ceb-4be0-5a71-bd4f-0c7ddbfe22a8', 'word_count': 587, 'uri': 'nyt://article/06425ceb-4be0-5a71-bd4f-0c7ddbfe22a8'}, {'abstract': 'Models at Coach, DKNY and Cushie et Ochs all appeared with boldly outlined eyes.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/02/16/black-eyeliner-fall-2015-beauty/', 'snippet': 'Models at Coach, DKNY and Cushie et Ochs all appeared with boldly outlined eyes.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Black lines are defining the eyes in unexpected ways at the fall/winter 2015 shows. Last Thursday at Coach’s presentation, a seamless, symmetrical cat-eye immediately drew attention; the black stroke went across the top lid and back down halfway along\xa0the lower lid, with just enough of a pull at the corner of the eye. DKNY explored the trend with a little more adventurous oomph, outlining the outskirts of the eye with a thick black line; and at Cushnie et Ochs, it was more rock-n-roll, a smoky eye that stole the beauty moment – thick and smeared, with a slight interruption at each corner that separated the top and the bottom portion of the eye like the ends of a brushstroke.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/16/t-magazine/16trend-eye-mosci/16trend-eye-mosci-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 360, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/02/16/t-magazine/16trend-eye-mosci/16trend-eye-mosci-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 360}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/16/t-magazine/16trend-eye-mosci/16trend-eye-mosci-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 614, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/16/t-magazine/16trend-eye-mosci/16trend-eye-mosci-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1229, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/16/t-magazine/16trend-eye-mosci/16trend-eye-mosci-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/02/16/t-magazine/16trend-eye-mosci/16trend-eye-mosci-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/16/t-magazine/16trend-eye-mosci/16trend-eye-mosci-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'On the Fall 2015 Runways, Fresh Takes on an Old Standby: Black Eyeliner', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Beauty (Concept)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Eyes and Eyesight', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Cushnie et Ochs', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Karan, Donna, International', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-02-16T22:05:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Renata Mosci', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Renata', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mosci', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ca079f09-f032-5afc-829d-ab2933579afd', 'word_count': 147, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ca079f09-f032-5afc-829d-ab2933579afd'}, {'abstract': 'The orchestra’s residency last week again raised a question of whether London could be Mr. Rattle’s next stop.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/02/17/arts/music/review-berlin-philharmonic-goes-to-london-in-simon-rattle-homecoming.html', 'snippet': 'The orchestra’s residency last week again raised a question of whether London could be Mr. Rattle’s next stop.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON — Whenever the conductor Simon Rattle takes his Berlin Philharmonic Orchestra to London, there’s a sense of reckoning: about the boy who went away, made good and is now bringing home the proof. For British audiences, the very idea that a conductor from England — what Germans used to call “the land without music” — is in charge of Germany’s flagship orchestra is a continuing source of national delight. British music lovers are always curious to know how the relationship has worked out. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/17/arts/17RATTLE/17RATTLE-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 423, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/02/17/arts/17RATTLE/17RATTLE-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 423}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/17/arts/17RATTLE/17RATTLE-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 722, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/17/arts/17RATTLE/17RATTLE-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1443, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type'