, religious belief.', 'lead_paragraph': 'You know what would make Baba Brinkman happy this weekend? If just one winner would get up at the Oscars and make an acceptance speech that began not with an expression of gratitude to God but with “I want to thank Charles Darwin.”', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/17/arts/17RAPGUIDE/17RAPGUIDE-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 401, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/02/17/arts/17RAPGUIDE/17RAPGUIDE-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 401}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/17/arts/17RAPGUIDE/17RAPGUIDE-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 684, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/17/arts/17RAPGUIDE/17RAPGUIDE-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1369, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/17/arts/17RAPGUIDE/17RAPGUIDE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/02/17/arts/17RAPGUIDE/17RAPGUIDE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/17/arts/17RAPGUIDE/17RAPGUIDE-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Review: ‘Rap Guide to Religion’ Examines Why Humanity Created God', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Why Humanity Created God', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gates, Anita', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Brinkman, Baba', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'SoHo Playhouse', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Rap Guide to Religion (Play)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-02-16T22:12:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Theater', 'byline': {'original': 'By Anita Gates', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Anita', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gates', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/1a80a4ac-8728-51a3-bf79-2174709b0d1d', 'word_count': 311, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1a80a4ac-8728-51a3-bf79-2174709b0d1d'}, {'abstract': 'The string quartet played a program of Mozart, Ravel and Brahms at the Frick Collection’s Music Room on Sunday afternoon.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/02/17/arts/auryn-quartet-forges-a-radiance-at-the-frick.html', 'snippet': 'The string quartet played a program of Mozart, Ravel and Brahms at the Frick Collection’s Music Room on Sunday afternoon.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A warm sound is invariably an appealing attribute of solo or ensemble playing — and as temperatures plummeted on Sunday afternoon, it felt particularly welcome to bask in the Auryn Quartet’s glowing timbres in the snug acoustical cocoon of the Frick Collection’s intimate Music Room. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/17/arts/17AURYNSUB/17AURYNSUB-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 377, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/02/17/arts/17AURYNSUB/17AURYNSUB-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 377}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/17/arts/17AURYNSUB/17AURYNSUB-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 643, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/17/arts/17AURYNSUB/17AURYNSUB-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1285, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/17/arts/17AURYNSUB/17AURYNSUB-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/02/17/arts/17AURYNSUB/17AURYNSUB-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/17/arts/17AURYNSUB/17AURYNSUB-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Review: Auryn Quartet Forges a Radiance at the Frick', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Cozy Radiance That Old Hands Can Forge', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Schweitzer, Vivien', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Classical Music', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Frick Collection', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Auryn Quartet', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-02-16T22:24:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Vivien Schweitzer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Vivien', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schweitzer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/5d3b16e7-9daf-5e70-8d87-3fbce1745edc', 'word_count': 264, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5d3b16e7-9daf-5e70-8d87-3fbce1745edc'}, {'abstract': 'The oxblood color is reminiscent of the red leather Doc Martens popular in the late ’80s and early ’90s.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/02/16/phillip-lim-fall-2015-beauty/', 'snippet': 'The oxblood color is reminiscent of the red leather Doc Martens popular in the late ’80s and early ’90s.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It’s unquestionable (and understandable) that designers have lately preferred to keep their beauty looks simple, and the choice to eschew that effortless style in favor of a bold one feels innovative and inspired. During a season that’s so far been filled with natural-looking lips, it’s refreshing to see a color speak for itself, as we did at 3.1 Phillip Lim’s fall 2015 show today. Backstage, the makeup artist Francelle Daly professed her love affair with Nars Cosmetics’ newest lip color, VIP Red, taking us down a nostalgic burgundy punk path. “I fell in love with this shade when they showed it to me,” Daly said. “I remember in the ’90s and late ’80s, it was all about my red leather Dr. Martens boots.” The oxblood red lipstick is also the perfect complement to the clothing Lim showed: “It really fits into all these beautiful gold, brown and green tones that you see in the collection,” Daly said.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/16/t-magazine/16beauty-lim-gilchrist/16beauty-lim-gilchrist-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 800, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/201