wn as the radically independent mind behind art-house classics like “Down by Law” and “Dead Man,” the filmmaker is also a member of the “amorphous” post-rock group known as Sqürl. (The band composed the scores to the recent Jarmusch films “The Limits of Control” and “Only Lovers Left Alive.”) Tonight, Sqürl will debut a new soundtrack — not to one of Jarmusch’s own films, but to four silent works from the surrealist Man Ray. The concerts are part of WNYC’s New Sounds Live series, Silent Films/Live Music, which pairs movies, both classic and contemporary, with performances from acclaimed musicians. (The current run of shows also features the composer Alfonso Villalonga and the Wordless Music Orchestra performing the score to the Spanish film “Blancanieves.”)', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/17/t-magazine/17jarmusch-reese/17jarmusch-reese-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/02/17/t-magazine/17jarmusch-reese/17jarmusch-reese-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/17/t-magazine/17jarmusch-reese/17jarmusch-reese-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/17/t-magazine/17jarmusch-reese/17jarmusch-reese-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/17/t-magazine/17jarmusch-reese/17jarmusch-reese-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard'