, {'abstract': 'The disqualification of a large number of images from this year’s World Press Photo contest has generated a debate over the need for more explicit rules on what is — and what isn’t — acceptable in digital photography.', 'web_url': 'https://lens.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/02/17/world-press-photo-manipulation-ethics-of-digital-photojournalism/', 'snippet': 'The disqualification of a large number of images from this year’s World Press Photo contest has generated a debate over the need for more explicit rules on what is — and what isn’t — acceptable in digital photography.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Significant questions have arisen after a large number of images were disqualified from this year’s World Press Photo competition because of excessive — and sometimes blatant — post-processing. After independent experts examined the images being considered for prizes in the final rounds, and presented their findings to the jury, 20 percent of the photos were disqualified by the judges. This was often because of significant addition or subtraction to the image content.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Debating the Rules and Ethics of Digital Photojournalism', 'kicker': 'Lens', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Contests and Prizes', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Photography', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Aranda, Samuel', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Campbell, David', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Contreras, Narciso', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McNally, Michele', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Press Photographers Assn', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'World Press Photo Foundation', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value