s', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Suicides and Suicide Attempts', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-02-17T08:27:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Letters', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Letter', '_id': 'nyt://article/a11b5fc5-e583-5f26-8496-bc0786bf430c', 'word_count': 396, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a11b5fc5-e583-5f26-8496-bc0786bf430c'}, {'abstract': 'The new chairman of the Senate Judiciary Committee opposes almost any reduction of mandatory minimum sentences.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/02/17/opinion/the-roadblock-to-sentencing-reform.html', 'snippet': 'The new chairman of the Senate Judiciary Committee opposes almost any reduction of mandatory minimum sentences.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For more than a year, members of Congress have been doing a lot of talking about the need to broadly reform harsh federal sentencing laws, which are a central factor in the explosion of the federal prison population. It’s an overdue conversation, and one of the few in which Democrats and Republicans find some agreement — but, so far, they have nothing to show for it.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': ' The Roadblock to Sentencing Reform', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Roadblock to Sentencing Reform', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sentences (Criminal)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Grassley, Charles E', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mandatory Sentencing', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Senate', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'House of Representatives', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Discrimination', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-02-17T08:27:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/ad42817d-553d-5588-b392-89a0edf926b3', 'word_count': 681, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ad42817d-553d-5588-b392-89a0edf926b3'}, {'abstract': 'The horrors of PTSD are more complex than most of us know. Sufferers feel exile, and healing must be moral as well as psychological.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/02/17/opinion/david-brooks-the-moral-injury.html', 'snippet': 'The horrors of PTSD are more complex than most of us know. Sufferers feel exile, and healing must be moral as well as psychological.', 'lead_paragraph': 'David J. Morris returned from Iraq with a case of post-traumatic stress disorder. The former Marine turned war correspondent was plagued by nightmares. His imagination careened out of control; he envisioned fireballs erupting while on trips to the mall. His emotions could go numb, but his awareness was hypervigilant. Images and smells from the war were tattooed eternally fresh on his brain, and he circled back to them remorselessly.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '23', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/01/opinion/brooks-circular/brooks-circular-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 588, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/11/01/opinion/brooks-circular/brooks-circular-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 588}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/01/opinion/brooks-circular/brooks-circular-jumbo-v5.jpg', 'height': 1003, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/01/opinion/brooks-circular/brooks-circular-superJumbo-v5.jpg', 'height': 1852, 'width': 1891, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/01/opinion/brooks-circular/brooks-circular-thumbStandard-v5.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/11/01/opinion/brooks-circular/brooks-circular-thumbStandard-v5.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/01/opinion/brooks-circular/brooks-circular-thumbLarge-v7.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Moral Injury', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Columnist', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Moral Injury', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Post-Traumatic Stress Disorder', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Morris, David J', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Veterans', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'The Evil Hours: A Biography of Post-Traumatic Stress Disorder (Book)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-02-17T08:27:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Brooks', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Brooks', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role':