taurant Shuko.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/02/18/dining/restaurant-review-shuko-in-the-east-village.html', 'snippet': 'The chefs Jimmy Lau and Nick Kim prepare elevated and memorable Japanese food at the new restaurant Shuko.', 'lead_paragraph': '“You like spicy?” Jimmy Lau asked from behind the counter at Shuko, the new restaurant just below Union Square where he and his partner, Nick Kim, prepare an elevated and memorable species of Japanese food. Before I could answer, he handed me a spicy tuna roll that would casually knock over my ideas about spicy tuna rolls, and spice, and tuna.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Restaurant Review: Shuko in the East Village', 'kicker': 'Restaurants', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Temple of Sushi for All Comers', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Restaurants', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Shuko (Manhattan, NY, Restaurant)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'East Village (Manhattan, NY)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kim, Nick', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lau, Jimmy', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-02-17T18:00:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'By Pete Wells', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Pete', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wells', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/76104f10-5072-5570-9b75-70242550ec61', 'word_count': 1109, 'uri': 'nyt://article/76104f10-5072-5570-9b75-70242550ec61'}, {'abstract': 'Cool, downtown versions of the unofficial hunter’s uniform graced the runways at Coach, Alexander Wang and 3.1 Phillip Lim.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/02/17/buffalo-plaid-trend-fall-winter-2015/', 'snippet': 'Cool, downtown versions of the unofficial hunter’s uniform graced the runways at Coach, Alexander Wang and 3.1 Phillip Lim.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Uniform dressing, from military greens to prep-school pleats, has always been a popular inspiration for designers, and this season, several have taken on the unofficial uniform of hunters: the oversize checks of buffalo plaid. First, at Coach, Stuart Vevers put a spin on the classic American print with pastel hues, balancing out the mostly black collection. Buffalo plaid also brightened another show consisting otherwise of almost entirely black looks: Alexander Wang’s, to which the designer added a splash of color with a red buffalo plaid coat shown halfway through. And the 3.1 Phillip Lim show featured the print expressed in multiple colorways: a classic black and white with red accents near the beginning, and an earthier version in beige, black and ochre near the end. Lim’s eye-catching interpretation, cool and a little tough, was perfect for his downtown girl.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/17/t-magazine/17trend-plaid-koh/17trend-plaid-koh-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 450, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/02/17/t-magazine/17trend-plaid-koh/17trend-plaid-koh-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 450}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/17/t-magazine/17trend-plaid-koh/17trend-plaid-koh-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 768, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/17/t-magazine/17trend-plaid-koh/17trend-plaid-koh-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 