.', 'web_url': 'https://carpetbagger.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/02/17/clothes-and-character-maleficent/', 'snippet': 'The costume designer was brought in late and then asked to do not one but eight looks for the main character. That’s when Team Maleficent was born.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Though nominated twice for an Oscar already, the costume designer Anna B. Sheppard was taken by surprise last month, she said, when her assistant interrupted a fitting with Morgan Freeman to announce it had happened again: she was up for her costume design for “Maleficent,” Disney’s “Sleeping Beauty” tale told from the antagonist’s point of view. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/17/arts/maleficent/maleficent-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/02/17/arts/maleficent/maleficent-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/17/arts/maleficent/maleficent-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 624, 'width': 936, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/17/arts/maleficent/maleficent-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 624, 'width': 936, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/17/arts/maleficent/maleficent-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/02/17/arts/maleficent/maleficent-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/17/arts/maleficent/maleficent-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Clothes and Character: ‘Maleficent’', 'kicker': 'Carpetbagger', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'u2018Maleficentu2019', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Costumes', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Baker, Rick', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Freeman, Morgan', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jolie, Angelina', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Walt Disney Company', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-02-17T18:01:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rachel Lee Harris', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rachel', 'middlename': 'Lee', 'lastname': 'Harris', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4de41552-a98c-5596-bc00-efaf41b8a90c', 'word_count': 1137, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4de41552-a98c-5596-bc00-efaf41b8a90c'}, {'abstract': 'Mr. Boorman’s new film picks up where “Hope and Glory” left off, with a young Briton as he comes into adulthood during the Korean War.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/02/18/movies/review-with-queen-and-country-john-boorman-continues-a-tale.html', 'snippet': 'Mr. Boorman’s new film picks up where “Hope and Glory” left off, with a young Briton as he comes into adulthood during the Korean War.', 'lead_paragraph': 'To appreciate “Queen and Country,” John Boorman’s gently nostalgic, quasi-autobiographical film about Britain in the early 1950s, it isn’t entirely necessary to have seen his earlier “Hope and Glory.” You should, of course, see it, if you haven’t already: One of a handful of great movies that look at World War II through the eyes of a child, “Hope and Glory” is distinguished by mischievous good humor and by the unashamed acknowledgment that war can be fun as well as horrible. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/18/arts/18QUEENSUB/18QUEENSUB-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 353, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/02/18/arts/18QUEENSUB/18QUEENSUB-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 353}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/18/arts/18QUEENSUB/18QUEENSUB-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 602, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/18/arts/18QUEENSUB/18QUEENSUB-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1205, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/18/arts/18QUEENSUB/18QUEENSUB-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/02/18/arts/18QUEENSUB/18QUEENSUB-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/18/arts/18QUEENSUB/18QUEENSUB-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Review: With ‘Queen and Country,’ John Boorman Continues a Tale', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_head