, 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/935008f5-5e5f-530d-bace-8d0b92ea7024', 'word_count': 871, 'uri': 'nyt://article/935008f5-5e5f-530d-bace-8d0b92ea7024'}, {'abstract': 'Joyce DiDonato stars in Rossini’s tale of Scottish rivals in love and politics.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/02/18/arts/music/review-a-la-donna-del-lago-with-melting-tenderness-at-the-met.html', 'snippet': 'Joyce DiDonato stars in Rossini’s tale of Scottish rivals in love and politics.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For years, the superb mezzo-soprano Joyce DiDonato has sung “Tanti affetti,” the final showpiece aria from Rossini’s “La Donna del Lago” (The Lady of the Lake), as a surefire encore in recitals. But on Monday night on the Metropolitan Opera stage, vocal display seemed the last thing on her mind.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/18/arts/18DONNAJP/18DONNAJP-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 433, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/02/18/arts/18DONNAJP/18DONNAJP-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 433}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/18/arts/18DONNAJP/18DONNAJP-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 740, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/18/arts/18DONNAJP/18DONNAJP-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1479, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/18/arts/18DONNAJP/18DONNAJP-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/02/18/arts/18DONNAJP/18DONNAJP-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/18/arts/18DONNAJP/18DONNAJP-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Review: A ‘La Donna del Lago’ With Melting Tenderness at the Met', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Noble Lady, Inspiring Love in Misty Climes', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Tommasini, Anthony', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Opera', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Metropolitan Opera', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rossini, Gioacchino', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Curran, Paul (1964- )', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mariotti, Michele', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Florez, Juan Diego', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'La Donna del Lago (Opera)', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'DiDonato, Joyce', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-02-17T22:35:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Anthony Tommasini', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Anthony', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Tommasini', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/9365de33-6a3a-52a6-adb5-71bfa88814f8', 'word_count': 1070, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9365de33-6a3a-52a6-adb5-71bfa88814f8'}, {'abstract': 'There was much to admire in “Backlight,” but it barely hinted at the sense of adventure and startling elements integral to much of Ms. Monk’s work.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/02/18/arts/music/review-ensemble-acjw-performs-meredith-monks-instrumental-backlight.html', 'snippet': 'There was much to admire in “Backlight,” but it barely hinted at the sense of adventure and startling elements integral to much of Ms. Monk’s work.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The composer Meredith Monk is known for her uncanny ability to coax the human voice into sonorities both ethereal and startling. Ms. Monk, also a dancer, singer, choreographer, director and filmmaker, has been honing this extended vocal technique since the 1960s, championed by her own ensemble. Her otherworldly vocal quilts are often a patchwork of noises, cries and ululations, interwoven with chanting and humming. Other works are more lyrical, with plaintive, folk-tinged vocal lines stretched over somber, spare accompaniments. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Review: Ensemble ACJW Performs Meredith Monk’s Instrumental ‘Backlight’', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'An Instrumental Work With a Vocal Touch', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Schweitzer, Vivien', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Monk, Meredith', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Ensemble ACJW', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-02-17T22:36:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Vivien Schweitzer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Vivien', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schweitzer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None