8-9c53-50f9-b2b8-16b81105e65f'}, {'abstract': 'A plan presented by Move NY includes the introduction of a toll for drivers within Manhattan — an idea rejected in Albany nearly seven years ago.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/02/18/nyregion/transit-group-would-add-tolls-to-four-new-york-bridges.html', 'snippet': 'A plan presented by Move NY includes the introduction of a toll for drivers within Manhattan — an idea rejected in Albany nearly seven years ago.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A transit advocacy group unveiled a proposal on Tuesday to remake the way tolls are set across New York City. Now comes the hard part — persuading lawmakers and drivers to embrace an idea that was defeated in Albany nearly seven years ago.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '17', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/18/nyregion/18TRAFFIC/18TRAFFIC-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/02/18/nyregion/18TRAFFIC/18TRAFFIC-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/18/nyregion/18TRAFFIC/18TRAFFIC-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/18/nyregion/18TRAFFIC/18TRAFFIC-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/18/nyregion/18TRAFFIC/18TRAFFIC-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/02/18/nyregion/18TRAFFIC/18TRAFFIC-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/18/nyregion/18TRAFFIC/18TRAFFIC-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Transit Group’s Next Challenge: Selling a New Version of Congestion Pricing  ', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Transit Group Is Seeking Changes to City’s Tolls', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Fitzsimmons, Emma G', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Roads and Traffic', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Move NY', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tolls', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bridges and Tunnels', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Congestion Pricing', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-02-18T03:33:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Emma G. Fitzsimmons', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Emma', 'middlename': 'G.', 'lastname': 'Fitzsimmons', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4b20fda7-80fb-57a9-8510-3bf1bb09813e', 'word_count': 819, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4b20fda7-80fb-57a9-8510-3bf1bb09813e'}, {'abstract': 'The announcement came hours before four women filed a lawsuit accusing Mohammad Abdullah Saleem of abuse dating back to the 1980s.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/02/18/us/illinois-imam-charged-with-sex-abuse.html', 'snippet': 'The announcement came hours before four women filed a lawsuit accusing Mohammad Abdullah Saleem of abuse dating back to the 1980s.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A Chicago-area imam was charged with sexual abuse on Tuesday in a case that has raised questions about whether a cloistered South Asian community’s conservative views on sex and purity had discouraged women from coming forward with accusations of abuse. The charge was announced hours before four women filed a lawsuit accusing the imam, Mohammad Abdullah Saleem, who founded a school called the Institute of Islamic Education, of a pattern of sexual abuse dating back to the 1980s. A 23-year-old woman who worked as a school secretary last year told the police that Mr. Saleem had repeatedly groped her and once pulled her onto his lap and held her there over her objections. “He categorically denies the allegations,” his lawyer, Thomas T. Glasgow, said after a court appearance. He said the school had investigated and found no evidence for the claims. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Illinois: Imam Charged With Sex Abuse ', 'kicker': 'National Briefing | Midwest', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Illinois: Imam Charged With Sex Abuse', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Saleem, Mohammad Abdullah', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sex Crimes', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Muslims and Islam', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Imams', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Chicago (Ill)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-02-18T03:33:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Matt Apuzzo', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Matt', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Apuzzo', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/330e4e0e-586d-5b37-bb5e-4649858407ad', 'word_count': 141, 'uri': 'nyt://article/330e4e0e-586d-5b37-bb5e-4649858407ad'}, {'abstract': 'Aides to Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu say they are being kept in the dark about details of the nuclear negotiations, but American officials say that is not true.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/02/18/world/fear-of-israeli-leaks-fuels-distrust-as-us-and-iran-hold-nuclear-talks.html', 'snippet': 'Aides to Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu say they are being kept in the dark about details of the nuclear negotiations, but American officials say that is not true.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — With the Obama administration racing to negotiate the outlines of a nuclear deal with Iran by the end of March, aides to Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu of Israel have charged in recent days that they are being deliberately left in the dark about the details of the talks. The Americans have said that is untrue, but even one of Washington’s closest negotiating partners reports being warned about being too open with the Israelis, “because whatever we say may be used in a selective way.”', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Fear of Israeli Leaks Fuels Distrust Over U.S. Talks With Iran', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Fear of Israeli Leaks Fuels Distrust as U.S. and Iran Hold Nuclear Talks', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Israel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iran', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Nuclear Weapons', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States International Relations', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Netanyahu, Benjamin', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-02-18T03:34:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By David E. Sanger', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': 'E.', 'lastname': 'Sanger', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f3c11cfc-0e13-575d-b750-0852650a2b55', 'word_count': 1183, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f3c11cfc-0e13-575d-b750-0852650a2b55'}, {'abstract': 'Authorities said a stampede on Tuesday left 16 people dead and 78 injured when a singer atop a Carnival float struck an overhead power line, igniting sparks and panic.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/02/18/world/americas/16-die-in-crush-at-carnival-in-haiti-capital.html', 'snippet': 'Authorities said a stampede on Tuesday left 16 people dead and 78 injured when a singer atop a Carnival float struck an overhead power line, igniting sparks and panic.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PORT-AU-PRINCE, Haiti — A stampede on Tuesday left 16 people dead and 78 injured when a singer atop a Carnival float struck an overhead power line, igniting sparks and panic, the authorities said.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '16 Die in Crush at Carnival in Haiti Capital', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '16 Die in Crush at Carnival in Haiti Capital', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Haiti', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Stampedes', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Archibold, Randal C', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Fatalities)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Carnival (Pre-L