ews_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Katrin Bennhold and Eric Schmitt', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Katrin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bennhold', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Eric', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schmitt', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/14a11bfa-a562-5b52-98fb-e3566710ef91', 'word_count': 2482, 'uri': 'nyt://article/14a11bfa-a562-5b52-98fb-e3566710ef91'}, {'abstract': 'A Moscow appeals court on Tuesday upheld a suspended three-and-a-half-year prison sentence against Aleksei A. Navalny, a leader of Russia’s opposition to President Vladimir V. Putin who was convicted last year of fraud in a case widely seen as politically motivated.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/02/18/world/europe/russia-court-upholds-activists-suspended-sentence.html', 'snippet': 'A Moscow appeals court on Tuesday upheld a suspended three-and-a-half-year prison sentence against Aleksei A. Navalny, a leader of Russia’s opposition to President Vladimir V. Putin who was convicted last year of fraud in a case widely seen as pol...', 'lead_paragraph': ' A Moscow appeals court on Tuesday upheld a suspended three-and-a-half-year prison sentence against Aleksei A. Navalny, a leader of Russia’s opposition to President Vladimir V. Putin who was convicted last year of fraud in a case widely seen as politically motivated. The court also released Mr. Navalny, an organizer of an opposition rally planned for March 1, from house arrest. A three-and-a-half-year prison sentence handed down to Mr. Navalny’s brother, who was convicted in the same case, remained unchanged. Mr. Navalny called his brother “a hostage.” ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Russia: Court Upholds Activist’s Suspended Sentence', 'kicker': 'World Briefing', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Russia: Court Upholds Activist’s Suspended Sentence', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Roth, Andrew', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Navalny, Aleksei A', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Putin, Vladimir V', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Russia', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sentences (Criminal)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Moscow (Russia)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-02-18T04:24:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew Roth', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Roth', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/a9f75a47-b885-5174-aa65-235c30a95a39', 'word_count': 86, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a9f75a47-b885-5174-aa65-235c30a95a39'}, {'abstract': 'Alice Rohrwacher’s “De Djess” is the ninth short film in the brand’s ongoing series.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/02/18/t-magazine/miu-miu-womens-tales-alice-rohrwacher-de-djess.html', 'snippet': 'Alice Rohrwacher’s “De Djess” is the ninth short film in the brand’s ongoing series.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For the latest installment of the Miu Miu short-film series Women’s Tales — an ongoing project that has included commissions by Miranda July, Ava DuVernay and Zoe Cassavetes — the brand enlisted Alice Rohrwacher, the writer and director of “Corpo Celeste” (2011) and the Cannes Grand Prix recipient “The Wonders” (2014). “In fact, it was my first short,” Rohrwacher says of her 15-minute-long piece, “De Djess.” “With a short film, you’re able to do some experimenting and still stay within formal guidelines.” That, and Miu Miu allowed Rohrwacher an enormous amount of artistic freedom; the house’s designer, Miuccia Prada, only asked to see the completed film, a rare occurrence in the movie-making realm.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/18/t-magazine/18moss-mm1/18moss-mm1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/02/18/t-magazine/18moss-mm1/18moss-mm1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/18/t-magazine/18moss-mm1/18moss-mm1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/18/t-magazine/18moss-mm1/18moss-mm1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/18/t-magazine/18moss-mm1/18moss-mm1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/02/18/t-magazine/18moss-mm1/18moss-mm1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/18/t-magazine/18moss-mm1/18moss-mm1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Miu Miu Women’s Tales Taps a Cannes Grand Prix Winner', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, '