5-02-18T08:27:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Letters', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Letter', '_id': 'nyt://article/a1688d38-17e4-5ea7-b554-8c11defd8fe3', 'word_count': 757, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a1688d38-17e4-5ea7-b554-8c11defd8fe3'}, {'abstract': 'The acting district attorney for Nassau County explains why she opposes a court disclosure order in the Jesse Friedman case.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/02/18/opinion/records-in-child-abuse-case-acting-da-responds.html', 'snippet': 'The acting district attorney for Nassau County explains why she opposes a court disclosure order in the Jesse Friedman case.', 'lead_paragraph': 'To the Editor:', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Records in Child Abuse Case: Acting D.A. Responds', 'kicker': 'Letter', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Records in Child Abuse Case: Acting D.A. Responds', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Friedman, Jesse', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sex Crimes', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Child Abuse and Neglect', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Singas, Madeline', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-02-18T08:27:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Letters', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Letter', '_id': 'nyt://article/b62335ca-e524-59a6-863f-81a298ff118e', 'word_count': 291, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b62335ca-e524-59a6-863f-81a298ff118e'}, {'abstract': 'Turkey’s drift away from democracy is part of a much larger trend around the world.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/02/18/opinion/thomas-friedman-democracy-is-in-recession.html', 'snippet': 'Turkey’s drift away from democracy is part of a much larger trend around the world.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Every month now we get treated to another anti-Semitic blast from Turkey’s leadership, which seems to be running some kind of slur-of-the-month club. Who knew that Jews all over the world were busy trying to take down President Recep Tayyip Erdogan? Last week, it was Prime Minister Ahmet Davutoglu’s turn to declare that Turkey would not “succumb to the Jewish lobby” — among others supposedly trying to topple Erdogan, the Hurriyet Daily News reported. This was after Erdogan had suggested that domestic opponents to the ruling Justice and Development Party, or A.K.P., were “cooperating with the Mossad,” Israel’s intelligence arm. So few Jews, so many governments to topple.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '21', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/01/opinion/friedman-circular/friedman-circular-jumbo-v2.png', 'height': 228, 'width': 228, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/01/opinion/friedman-circular/friedman-circular-superJumbo-v2.png', 'height': 228, 'width': 228, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/01/opinion/friedman-circular/friedman-circular-thumbStandard-v2.png', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/11/01/opinion/friedman-circular/friedman-circular-thumbStandard-v2.png', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/01/opinion/friedman-circular/friedman-circular-thumbLarge.png', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Democracy Is in Recession', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Columnist', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Democracy Is in Recession', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Turkey', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Friedman, Thomas L', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Erdogan, Recep Tayyip', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ANTI-SEMITISM', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Diamond, Larry', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Journal of Democracy', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Democracy (Theory and Philosophy)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-02-18T08:27:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Thomas L. Friedman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Thomas', 'middlename': 'L.', 'lastname': 'Friedman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/b7d32d12-8893-5397-b6db-a7d1327c2b84', 'word_count': 820, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b7d32d12-8893-5397-b6db-a7d1327c2b84'}, {'abstract': 'Lawmakers have a second chance to enact legislation that would bring more transparency to the workings of government.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/02/18/opinion/a-stronger-freedom-of-information-act.html', 'snippet': 'Lawmakers have a second chance to enact legislation that would bring more transparency to the workings of government.', 'lead_paragraph': '\xa0Congress came tantalizingly close last year to passing a bill to strengthen the Freedom of Information Act, which allows journalists and the public to access federal government records. The legislation, which would have brought more transparency, was blocked in December when the House speaker, John Boehner, refused to hold a vote on the Senate bill with no explanation. Two months later, lawmakers have a second chance.\xa0 ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Stronger Freedom of Information Act', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Stronger Freedom of Information Act', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Democratic Party', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'House of Representatives', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Senate', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Freedom of Information Act', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-02-18T08:27:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/c692019a-d134-5784-b6d2-8c58d9391283', 'word_count': 362, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c692019a-d134-5784-b6d2-8c58d9391283'}, {'abstract': 'I reconnected with my Shakespeare professor to get her thoughts on the humanities and higher education today.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/02/18/opinion/frank-bruni-college-poetry-and-purpose.html', 'snippet': 'I reconnected with my Shakespeare professor to get her thoughts on the humanities and higher education today.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PHILADELPHIA — Over four decades at two universities, Anne Hall has taught thousands of students, enough to know that they come to college for a variety of reasons, with a variety of attitudes. Many are concerned only with jobs. Some are concerned chiefly with beer.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '21', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/01/opinion/bruni-circular/bruni-circular-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 601, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/11/01/opinion/bruni-circular/bruni-circular-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 601}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/01/opinion/bruni-circular/bruni-circular-jumbo-v5.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 1023, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/01/opinion/bruni-circular/bruni-circular-superJumbo-v5.jpg', 'height': 1852, 'width': 1850, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/01/opinion/bruni-circular/bruni-circular-thumbStandard-v5.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/11/01/opinion/bruni-circular/bruni-circular-thumbStandard-v5.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/01/opinion/bruni-circular/bruni-circular-thumbLarge-v7.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'College, Poetry and Purpose', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Columnist', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'College, Poetry and Purpose', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Colleges and Universities', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hall, Anne (1945- )', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Humanities', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Poetry and Poets', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'University of North Carolina', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'University of Pennsylvania', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-02-18T08:27:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Frank Bruni', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Frank', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bruni', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/d982e6b6-c185-5b90-8e7e-95cefc47824a', 'word_count': 771, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d982e6b6-c185-5b90-8e7e-95cefc47824a'}, {'abstract': 'Euphemisms of the afterlife weren’t for us. Where she is now is in my mind.', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/02/18/my-mother-is-not-a-bird/', 'snippet': 'Euphemisms of the afterlife weren’t for us. Where she is now is in my mind.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I stood watching my mother’s last bellowing breaths. There were three of us holding her — me, my husband and my father — in the room we’d designed just for her. She was propped up in a rented hospital bed, lying on brown cotton sheets with the highest thread count I could find. My mother had been gasping like this for two days — a raspy, gurgling sound that I struggle to describe accurately with metaphors: a choking fish, a crackling microphone, a dying deer. But they all sidestep the truth. That was the sound of my 60-year-old mother dying of cancer.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/18/opinion/18theEndweb/18theEndweb-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 436, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/02/18/opinion/18theEndweb/18theEndweb-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 436}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/18/opinion/18theEndweb/18theEndweb-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 743, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/18/opinion/18theEndweb/18theEndweb-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1420, 'width': 1956, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/18/opinion/18theEndweb/18theEndweb-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/02/18/opinion/18theEndweb/18theEndweb-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/18/opinion/18theEndweb/18theEndweb-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'My Mother Is Not a Bird', 'kicker': 'The End', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Death and Dying', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-02-18T08:30:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Julienne Grey', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Julienne', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Grey', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organ