 588, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d38a7586-8e6c-55d5-b724-e636d66348e7'}, {'abstract': 'President Petro O. Poroshenko sought to cast the retreat from the strategic town in a positive light, but it was clearly a devastating defeat at the hands of the separatists.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/02/19/world/europe/ukraine-conflict-debaltseve.html', 'snippet': 'President Petro O. Poroshenko sought to cast the retreat from the strategic town in a positive light, but it was clearly a devastating defeat at the hands of the separatists.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ARTEMIVSK, Ukraine — Ukrainian soldiers were forced to fight their way out of the embattled town of Debaltseve in the early hours of Wednesday, casting further doubt on the credibility of a days-old cease-fire and eroding the promise of ending a war in Europe that has killed more than 5,000 people.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Ukrainian Soldiers’ Retreat From Eastern Town Raises Doubt for Truce', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Bloody Retreat Adds to Doubt for Ukraine Truce', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Ukraine', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Russia', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Debaltseve (Ukraine)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Poroshenko, Petro Olekseyevich', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Putin, Vladimir V', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-02-18T11:47:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew E. Kramer and David M. Herszenhorn', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': 'E.', 'lastname': 'Kramer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'David', 'm