 understanding of diseases and new ways to treat or cure them.', 'lead_paragraph': 'More than 200 scientists working on an ambitious federal project have begun to understand the complicated system of switches that regulates genes, turning some on and others off, making some glow brightly while others dim. They hope these discoveries, described in two dozen papers released on Wednesday, will eventually lead to a deeper understanding of diseases and new ways to treat or cure them.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '17', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Project Sheds Light on What Drives Genes ', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Project Sheds Light on What Drives Genes', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Genetics and Heredity', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kolata, Gina', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Nature (Journal)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'DNA (Deoxyribonucleic Acid)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Research', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lander, Eric S', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-02-18T12:00:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': 'By Gina Kolata', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Gina', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kolata', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0b9223a1-aa8b-56da-b3cd-32e67aacc830', 'word_count': 852, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0b9223a1-aa8b-56da-b3cd-32e67aacc830'}, {'abstract': 'The stalemate over Homeland Security funding grows more complicated.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/politics/first-draft/2015/02/18/today-in-politics-98/', 'snippet': 'The stalemate over Homeland Security 