ws', '_id': 'nyt://article/6511446a-9c5a-502b-9daf-9549a0c47413', 'word_count': 1404, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6511446a-9c5a-502b-9daf-9549a0c47413'}, {'abstract': 'Siem Reap, the gateway city to the temple ruins in Cambodia, is brimming with a clutch of stylish, recently opened boutiques.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/02/22/travel/khmer-inspired-shopping-by-angkor-wat.html', 'snippet': 'Siem Reap, the gateway city to the temple ruins in Cambodia, is brimming with a clutch of stylish, recently opened boutiques.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Siem Reap, the gateway city to Angkor, is renowned for a lot of things — more than 100 ancient temple ruins dot the surrounding jungles — but shopping isn’t one of them. It’s often an afterthought, with visitors snagging the prerequisite temple souvenir. But the heart of the city on the west side of the Siem Reap River is brimming with a clutch of stylish, recently opened boutiques carrying contemporary wares that often reference traditional Khmer culture. The shops are found along narrow lanes and well-trodden streets in a roughly 10-block radius, many owned by well-traveled expatriates breathing new energy into this tourist-oriented city. (Note: U.S. dollars are widely accepted.)', 'print_section': 'TR', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/22/travel/22FORAGING3/22FORAGING3-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/02/22/travel/22FORAGING3/22FORAGING3-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/22/travel/22FORAGING3/22FORAGING3-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/22/travel/22FORAGING3/22FORAGING3-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/22/travel/22FORAGING3/22FORAGING3-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/02/22/travel/22FORAGING3/22FORAGING3-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/22/travel/22FORAGING3/22FORAGING3-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Khmer-Inspired Shopping by Angkor Wat', 'kicker': 'Foraging', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Khmer-Inspired Contemporary Wares by Angkor’s Ancient Ruins', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Barone, Jeanine', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Cambodia', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Siem Reap (Cambodia)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ANGKOR WAT (CAMBODIAN TEMPLE)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Shopping and Retail', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Textiles', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'ANGKOR (CAMBODIA)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-02-18T14:03:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Travel', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jeanine Barone', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jeanine', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Barone', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reporte