015 Fashion Week in New York.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/02/18/rodarte-new-york-fashion-week-fall-2015-model-morph-anna-ewers/', 'snippet': 'The photographer Greg Kessler captures behind-the-scenes beauty transformations during Fall 2015 Fashion Week in New York.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The photographer Greg Kessler captures behind-the-scenes beauty transformations during Fall 2015 Fashion Week in New York. Here, the model Anna Ewers before (left) and after (right) makeup by James Kaliardos, hair by Odile Gilbert.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/18/t-magazine/18mm-rodarte/18mm-rodarte-jumbo.png', 'height': 563, 'width': 402, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/18/t-magazine/18mm-rodarte/18mm-rodarte-superJumbo.png', 'height': 563, 'width': 402, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/18/t-magazine/18mm-rodarte/18mm-rodarte-thumbStandard.png', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/02/18/t-magazine/18mm-rodarte/18mm-rodarte-thumbStandard.png', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/18/t-magazine/18mm-rodarte/18mm-rodarte-thumbLarge.png', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Anna Ewers Transforms at Rodarte', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2015-02-18T14:30:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Greg Kessler', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Greg', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kessler', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9e60054d-b21c-5e76-81f4-8917026f76ac', 'word_count': 65, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9e60054d-b21c-5e76-81f4-8917026f76ac'}, {'abstract': 'Joseph Haj, one of the few Arab-American artistic directors in the country, will take over at the Guthrie Theater in Minneapolis on July 1.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/02/18/new-artistic-director-for-guthrie-theater/', 'snippet': 'Joseph Haj, one of the few Arab-American artistic directors in the country, will take over at the Guthrie Theater in Minneapolis on July 1.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Guthrie Theater in Minneapolis has named its next artistic director: Joseph Haj, who currently leads PlayMakers Repertory Company in North Carolina. Mr. Haj, one of the few Arab-American artistic directors in the country, will take over the Guthrie on July 1, succeeding Joe Dowling, who is stepping down after 20 years. The Guthrie board’s chairman, Lee Skold, said Tuesday that the search team and board members – who spent a year looking for a leadership match – had been drawn to Mr. Haj’s “inspired vision, collaborative spirit, and standard of excellence.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'New Artistic Director for Guthrie Theater', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Appointments and Executive Changes', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Haj, Joseph', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Guthrie Theater', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Minneapolis (Minn)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-02-18T14:34:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Patrick Healy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Patrick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Healy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0d5fef1f-57df-5675-8777-1991819d13f4', 'word_count': 200, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0d5fef1f-57df-5675-8777-1991819d13f4'}, {'abstract': 'New Yorkers with a taste for Mr. Ives’s comedy can catch his latest collection of short plays.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/02/22/theater/david-ivess-lives-of-the-saints-from-primary-stages.html', 'snippet': 'New Yorkers with a taste for Mr. Ives’s comedy can catch his latest collection of short plays.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The playwright David Ives is all over the place. “The Metromaniacs,” his verse adaptation of an 18th-century play, has just opened at the Shakespeare Theater in Washington. His comedy “Venus in Fur,” seen widely at regional theaters, may get another goose from the movie release of a certain hugely popular series of novels about erotic transgression. It has also been announced that Mr. Ives will collaborate with Stephen Sondheim on a new musical adapted from a pair of Luis Buñuel films.', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/22/arts/22GUIDE4/22GUIDE4-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/02/22/arts/22GUIDE4/22GUIDE4-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/22/arts/22GUIDE4/22GUIDE4-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/22/arts/22GUIDE4/22GUIDE4-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/22/arts/22GUIDE4/22GUIDE4-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/02/22/arts/22GUIDE4/22GUIDE4-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/22/arts/22GUIDE4/22GUIDE4-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'David Ives&apos;s ‘Lives of the Saints’ From Primary Stages', 'kicker': 'The Week Ahead', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Theater: Short Shows From a Busy Man', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ives, David', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Primary Stages Co', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Lives of the Saints (Play)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-02-18T14:40:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Theater', 'byline': {'original': 'By Charles Isherwood', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Charles', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Isherwood', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b895576d-e066-57af-819d-7d4d7e5d5bb7', 'word_count': 186, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b895576d-e066-57af-819d-7d4d7e5d5bb7'}, {'abstract': 'Highlights from the International Herald Tribune archives: Italians demonstrate for war in 1915.', 'web_url': 'https://iht-retrospective.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/02/18/1915-italians-clamor-for-war/', 'snippet': 'Highlights from the International Herald Tribune archives: Italians demonstrate for war in 1915.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ROME — All adherents of the democratic parties had been convoked for to-day [Feb. 18] to the Piazza Monte Citorio for the purpose of a demonstration in favor of war. The square was barricaded by troops and police, but in the neighborhood of the Chamber a grave demonstration took place in spite of all precautions. Immense crowds gathered and clamored for war, interspersing their cries with shouts of ‘‘Down with Austria!’’ Processions of demonstrators marched through the streets with flags at their heads shouting against Germany and Austria. German and Austrian shops had all had their shutters put up. — The New York Herald, European Edition, Feb. 19, 1915', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '1915: Italians Clamor for War', 'kicker': 'IHT Retrospective', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Demonstrations, Protests and Riots', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'World War I (1914-18)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Italy', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Rome (Italy)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-02-18T14:43:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By International Herald Tribune', 'person': [{'firstname': 'International', 'middlename': 'Herald', 'lastname': 'Tribune', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/40e7fb03-f24d-5fa7-a6aa-9d5f66e5c6e1', 'word_count': 109, 'uri': 'nyt://article/40e7fb03-f24d-5fa7-a6aa-9d5f66e5c6e1'}, {'abstract': 'Peter Carey’s political thriller centers on cyber-saboteurs and the Australian left.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/02/22/books/review/peter-careys-amnesia.html', 'snippet': 'Peter Carey’s political thriller centers on cyber-saboteurs and the Australian left.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Now that the politics of hacking has \xadassumed an importance hitherto unknown, the theme Peter Carey has chosen for his latest novel seems especially timely. In many ways, it’s a departure from his previous work, although throughout “Amnesia” he maintains the temper and Rabelaisian fury of a prose we know all too well. You can pick any page at random and locate an energy that never seems to flag. His sentences hit their intended marks with an emotion that often feels like exasperated cruelty, and none of his characters are spared a little bloodletting.', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '17', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/22/books/review/0222-bks-Osborne/0222-bks-Osborne-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 575, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/02/22/books/review/0222-bks-Osborne/0222-bks-Osborne-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 575}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/22/books/review/0222-bks-Osborne/0222-bks-Osborne-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 981, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/22/books/review/0222-bks-Osborne/0222-bks-Osborne-superJumbo.jpg', 'height'