yt://article/73eeaeeb-b929-5e4f-a666-4f0f702189b4'}, {'abstract': 'The documentary makers John Maloof and Charlie Siskel tried to understand why Vivian Maier never showed her pictures.', 'web_url': 'https://carpetbagger.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/02/18/probing-the-mysteries-of-a-photographer-and-her-images/', 'snippet': 'The documentary makers John Maloof and Charlie Siskel tried to understand why Vivian Maier never showed her pictures.', 'lead_paragraph': 'One of the most fascinating art world stories of recent years is the discovery of the work of Vivian Maier and her rapid elevation to one of the great American photographers of the 20th century. It was John Maloof who found thousands of her negatives and undeveloped rolls of film at an auction house in Chicago, and paid $380 for them, and he is also the director, with Charlie Siskel, of “Finding Vivian Maier,” one of five films competing for the Oscar for best feature-length documentary.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/11/arts/maloof/maloof-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 750, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/02/11/arts/maloof/maloof-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 750}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/11/arts/maloof/maloof-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1000, 'width': 800, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/11/arts/maloof/maloof-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1000, 'width': 800, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/11/arts/maloof/maloof-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'su