ic and Protestant churches today [Feb. 18] reached a historic agreement to try to end their differences and achieve Christian unity. The first giant step toward a common understanding came during the unprecedented visit of a Roman Catholic cardinal to the World Council of Churches this morning. Augustin Cardinal Bea, on behalf of the Holy See, accepted the council’s proposal to establish a mixed committee to determine the principles and methods for future inter-church collaboration. — New York Herald Tribune, European Edition, Feb. 19, 1965', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/19/blogs/19iht-oldfeb19-churches/19iht-oldfeb19-churches-articleLarge.png', 'height': 439, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/02/19/blogs/19iht-oldfeb19-churches/19iht-oldfeb19-churches-articleLarge.png', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 439}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/19/blogs/19iht-oldfeb19-churches/19iht-oldfeb19-churches-jumbo.png', 'height': 750, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/19/blogs/19iht-oldfeb19-churches/19iht-oldfeb19-churches-superJumbo.png', 'height': 852, 'width': 1164, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/19/blogs/19iht-oldfeb19-churches/19iht-oldfeb19-churches-thumbStandard.png', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/02/19/blogs/19iht-oldfeb19-churches/19iht-oldfeb19-churches-thumbStandard.png', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 's