rop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/02/18/arts/18artsbeat-seuss1/18artsbeat-seuss1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/18/arts/18artsbeat-seuss1/18artsbeat-seuss1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'New Dr. Seuss Book, ‘What Pet Should I Get?’, Coming in July, With More to Come', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Book Showdown Looms: Harper Lee vs. Dr. Seuss', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Geisel, Theodor Seuss', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-02-18T16:23:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jennifer Schuessler', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jennifer', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schuessler', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6dea83b4-7be3-5fe9-8bab-dbf192195599', 'word_count': 264, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6dea83b4-7be3-5fe9-8bab-dbf192195599'}, {'abstract': 'Nick Hornby’s ingénue pursues her dream of fame in 1960s London.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/02/22/books/review/nick-hornbys-funny-girl.html', 'snippet': 'Nick Hornby’s ingénue pursues her dream of fame in 1960s London.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The unassuming title of Nick Hornby’s regular column about books for The Believer magazine perfectly matches its author’s conversational style: “Stuff I’ve Been Reading.” At a literary festival last October, Hornby spoke, not for the first time, in defense of taking the pain out of literature. Struggling through a book out of a sense of duty, he argued, is “reinforcing the \xadnotion that reading is something you should do but telly is something you want to do. It shouldn’t be like that. Novels should be like TV. It shouldn’t be hard work.”', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/22/books/review/0222-bks-WILLIAMS/0222-bks-WILLIAMS-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 732, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/02/22/books/review/0222-bks-WILLIAMS/0222-bks-WILLIAMS-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 732}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/22/books/review/0222-bks-WILLIAMS/0222-bks-WILLIAMS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 839, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/22/books/review/0222-bks-WILLIAMS/0222-bks-WILLIAMS-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1678, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/22/books/review/0222-bks-WILLIAMS/0222-bks-WILLIAMS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/02/22/books/review/0222-bks-WILLIAMS/0222-bks-WILLIAMS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/22/books/review/0222-bks-WILLIAMS/0222-bks-WILLIAMS-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Nick Hornby’s ‘Funny Girl’', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Laugh-In', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hornby, Nick', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Funny Girl (Book)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-02-18T16:24:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'BookReview', 'section_name': 'Books', 'subsection_name': 'Book Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By John Williams', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Williams', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/1f3a4de0-fed6-5bd7-a60a-a6be9580de5c', 'word_count': 1167, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1f3a4de0-fed6-5bd7-a60a-a6be9580de5c'}, {'abstract': 'Ms. Brown, a Democrat like her predecessor, John Kitzhaber, capped a long climb through the ranks of state government but also began what is certain to be a wrenching transition.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/02/19/us/kate-brown-replacing-john-kitzhaber-as-oregon-governor.html', 'snippet': 'Ms. Brown, a Democrat like her predecessor, John Kitzhaber, capped a long climb through the ranks of state government but also began what is certain to be a wrenching transition.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SALEM, Ore. — Kate Brown took the oath of office as governor here on Wednesday, capping a decades-long climb through the ranks of state government but also commencing what is certain to be a wrenching transition fraught with political risk. Her predecessor, John Kitzhaber, announced his resignation last week, just weeks into his fourth term, amid an onslaught of criminal and ethical investigations and a collapse of support from his own party.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Kate Brown, New Governor in Oregon, Seeks Public’s Trust', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'New Governor Seeks Public’s Trust in Oregon', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Johnson, Kirk', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Brown, Kate (1960- )', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Oregon', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kitzhaber, John', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hayes, Cylvia', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Governors (US)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-02-18T16:39:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kirk Johnson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kirk', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Johnson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ee5a591f-455f-5e92-a963-382ff28f3946', 'word_count': 1008, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ee5a591f-455f-5e92-a963-382ff28f3946'}, {'abstract': 'Amazon’s television production wing ordered full seasons of its pilot programs for “The Man in the High Castle,” “Mad Dogs,” “The New Yorker Presents,” “Just Add Magic” and “The Stinky & Dirty Show.”', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/02/18/amazon-orders-full-seasons-for-five-new-shows/', 'snippet': 'Amazon’s television production wing ordered full seasons of its pilot programs for “The Man in the High Castle,” “Mad Dogs,” “The New Yorker Presents,” “Just Add Magic” and “The Stinky & Dirty Show.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'In January, Amazon Studios, the online retail giant’s television production wing, posted 10 original pilots for viewers to watch and vote on. This morning, five of them were ordered to series: “The Man in the High Castle,” based on the Philip K. Dick novel that imagines an alternate reality in which the Axis powers won World War II; “Mad Dogs,” a dark comedy executive produced by Shawn Ryan (“The Shield,” “Terriers”); “The New Yorker Presents,” a docu-series overseen by Alex Gibney (“Taxi To the Dark Side,” “We Steal Secrets”); and the kids series “Just Add Magic” and “The Stinky & Dirty Show.”', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/19/arts/18HIGHCASTLEWEB/18HIGHCASTLEWEB-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 401, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/02/19/arts/18HIGHCASTLEWEB/18HIGHCASTLEWEB-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 401}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/19/arts/18HIGHCASTLEWEB/18HIGHCASTLEWEB-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 684, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/19/arts/18HIGHCASTLEWEB/18HIGHCASTLEWEB-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1368, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/19/arts/18HIGHCASTLEWEB/18HIGHCASTLEWEB-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/02/19/arts/18HIGHCASTLEWEB/18HIGHCASTLEWEB-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/19/arts/18HIGHCASTLEWEB/18HIGHCASTLEWEB-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Amazon Orders Full Seasons for Five New Shows', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Five Series Coming From Amazon Studios', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Web-Original Programming', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gibney, Alex', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'RYAN, SHAWN', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AMAZON.COM INC', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-02-18T16:44:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Gilbert Cruz', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Gilbert', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cruz', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d89cfcad-6b29-58c9-81c6-5a9e649a3610', 'word_count': 186, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d89cfcad-6b29-58c9-81c6-5a9e649a3610'}, {'abstract': 'One runner’s strategy and mind-set about the run-walk-run method during her road races and marathons.', 'web_url': 'https://well.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/02/18/real-runners-do-take-walk-breaks/', 'snippet': 'One runner’s strategy and mind-set about the run-walk-run method during her road races and marathons.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When a runner friend suggested I run my first distance race by adding walk breaks, the idea startled me. I didn’t think you were allowed to walk in races, not if you wanted to be a real runner. But the thought of running in New Jersey, all the way to the boardwalk in North Wildwood from Cape May in a single clip, seemed impossible, and I came around.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/18/health/18well_jen/18well_jen-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 