', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b5551d95-8f79-5e0e-9e98-eeba0ac89a9d', 'word_count': 938, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b5551d95-8f79-5e0e-9e98-eeba0ac89a9d'}, {'abstract': 'Tom Cross, the editor of “Whiplash,” discusses his work.', 'web_url': 'https://carpetbagger.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/02/18/below-the-line-editing-whiplash/', 'snippet': 'Tom Cross, the editor of “Whiplash,” discusses his work.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Those who have seen their fair share of films about musicians may go into a movie like “Whiplash” with certain expectations. But this best picture nominee is not your typical music drama. Instead, in its pacing,\xa0 acting and particularly\xa0 its editing, the film behaves more like “Bullitt” than, say, “Bird.” The focus is mainly on Andrew (Miles Teller), a jazz drum student at a prestigious music school, and his mentor, Fletcher (J.K. Simmons), an intense, strict and frequently verbally abusive\xa0 teacher. The film’s editor, Tom Cross, worked closely with the director, Damien Chazelle, to shape the cuts.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/18/arts/whiplash-image/whiplash-image-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 353, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/02/18/arts/whiplash-image/whiplash-image-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 353}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/18/arts/whiplash-image/whiplash-image-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 603, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/18/arts/whiplash-image/whiplash-image-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1206, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/18/arts/whiplash-image/whiplash-image-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/02/18/arts/whiplash-image/whiplash-image-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/18/arts/whiplash-image/whiplash-image-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Below the Line: Editing ‘Whiplash’', 'kicker': 'Carpetbagger', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Chazelle, Damien', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cross, Tom', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Simmons, J K', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Teller, Miles', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-02-18T17:01:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mekado Murphy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mekado', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Murphy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4bac425f-27fe-51b3-bd99-e5701ec3107e', 'word_count': 437, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4bac425f-27fe-51b3-bd99-e5701ec3107e'}, {'abstract': 'On the New York Fashion Week runways, all-black kilt-inspired bottoms are a chic upgrade from the tartan originals.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/02/18/new-york-fashion-week-fall-2015-trends-kilts-for-girls/', 'snippet': 'On the New York Fashion Week runways, all-black kilt-inspired bottoms are a chic upgrade from the tartan originals.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Designers have always loved borrowing from the boys for women’s collections; and for fall 2015, \u200bthey tapped into the structure of a kilt. At Coach, pleated, knee-length skirts, the default bottoms throughout the collection, added femininity to looks featuring structured shearling coats and heavy boots. Tim Coppens, who got his start in men’s wear,\u200b kept to his usual sporty aesthetic, topping kilt-inspired bottoms with boyish knits and bombers. And at Diesel Black Gold, Andreas Melbostad added texture to his all-black collection with lace, leather and, in this instance, layers of materials in a miniskirt version of the traditional Scottish garment. In all black, the trending color on this week’s runways, the new iterations are much chicer than the tartan originals.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/18/t-magazine/18trend-kilts-koh/18trend-kilts-koh-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 450, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/02/18/t-magazine/18trend-kilts-koh/18trend-kilts-koh-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 450}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/18/t-magazine/18trend-kilts-koh/18trend-kilts-koh-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 768, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/18/t-magazine/18trend-kilts-koh/18trend-kilts-koh-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1536, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/18/t-magazine/18trend-kilts-koh/18trend-kilts