ly primary states.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Vice President Joseph R. Biden Jr. on Wednesday continued his sweep through 2016 early primary states, stopping in Charleston, S.C., to deliver a broad speech on infrastructure as part of the administration’s “Grow America” tour. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '‘Infrastructure Joe’ Visits Another 2016 Early Primary State', 'kicker': 'First Draft', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2015-02-18T17:15:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nick Corasaniti', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Corasaniti', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/bad3a2aa-479a-5750-9c18-e97c7fd2078b', 'word_count': 300, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bad3a2aa-479a-5750-9c18-e97c7fd2078b'}, {'abstract': 'Millennials accustomed to ordering food for delivery on smartphones have come of legal drinking age, and niche start-ups are poised to take advantage.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/02/19/business/smallbusiness/same-day-delivery-resurges-adding-alcohol.html', 'snippet': 'Millennials accustomed to ordering food for delivery on smartphones have come of legal drinking age, and niche start-ups are poised to take advantage.', 'lead_paragraph': 'There are many bodies in the delivery graveyard. Webvan, Kozmo and Urbanfetch were all seen as the next big thing before crashing spectacularly.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/19/business/19sbiz1-web/19sbiz1-web-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'cro