nce of those interpretations at our peril: The Islamic State’s “intellectual genealogy” is intensely relevant to its political strategy, and its\xa0theology “must be understood to be combatted.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'In Defense of Islam', 'kicker': 'Ross Douthat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Christians and Christianity', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Muslims and Islam', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Religion and Belief', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Islamic State in Iraq and Syria (ISIS)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Middle East', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-02-18T20:50:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ross Douthat', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ross', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Douthat', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6407a2a7-ee24-5427-b499-07f2478be3e1', 'word_count': 1322, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6407a2a7-ee24-5427-b499-07f2478be3e1'}, {'abstract': 'A look at some of Ms. Chenoweth’s past performances.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/slideshow/2015/02/22/theater/20150222CHENOWETH.html', 'snippet': 'A look at some of Ms. Chenoweth’s past performances.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A look at some of Ms. Chenoweth’s past performances.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/22/theater/20150222CHENOWITH-slide-OHBE/20150222CHENOWITH-slide-OHBE-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 397, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/20