 Chausson in a recital at Zankel Hall.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/02/19/arts/music/review-jamie-barton-shows-that-shes-a-powerhouse-of-a-mezzo-soprano.html', 'snippet': 'Ms. Barton displayed her dramatic, voluptuous voice with songs by Dvorak and Chausson in a recital at Zankel Hall.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Pity the pianist who has to accompany Jamie Barton. It’s not that Ms. Barton, a dramatic mezzo-soprano who has found stardom in the opera world since her double first prize in the 2013 Cardiff Singer of the World Competition, treats her chamber music partners callously. During her recital debut at Zankel Hall on Tuesday evening, she exuded immense likability and down-to-earth charm. No, the predicament for Bradley Moore, her very able pianist on this occasion, was that next to the magnificent power of Ms. Barton’s voice, virtually everything he played came out sounding forlorn.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Review: Jamie Barton Shows That She’s a Powerhouse of a Mezzo-Soprano', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Power of Love and Lungs', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'da Fonseca-Wollheim, Corinna', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Barton, Jamie', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Carnegie Hall', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Classical Music', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-02-18T22:37:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Corinna da Fonseca-Wollheim', 'person': [{'firstname': '', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_ma