tion': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/671f9948-3f77-5a2e-ab11-f2aeebda57b2', 'word_count': 445, 'uri': 'nyt://article/671f9948-3f77-5a2e-ab11-f2aeebda57b2'}, {'abstract': 'Richard Linklater’s valentine to growing up, an early favorite, is now neck and neck with Alejandro G. Iñárritu’s wizardry in the best picture category.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/02/19/movies/awardsseason/oscar-ballots-in-best-picture-seems-to-narrow-to-boyhood-vs-birdman.html', 'snippet': 'Richard Linklater’s valentine to growing up, an early favorite, is now neck and neck with Alejandro G. Iñárritu’s wizardry in the best picture category.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Up until the fourth week of January it, seemed as if the race for the best picture Oscar was pretty much over except for the balloting. More than a dozen national and international critics organizations had anointed “Boyhood” the year’s best film and, with few exceptions, longtime awards season prognosticators forecast that the Academy of Motion Picture Arts and Sciences would do the same.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/19/arts/bagger1/bagger1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 402, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/02/19/arts/bagger1/bagger1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 402}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/19/arts/bagger1/bagger1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 685, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/19/arts/bagger1/bagger1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1371, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'sup