', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-02-19T03:28:50+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'New York', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Interactive Feature', '_id': 'nyt://interactive/f3c65805-dbfe-5c44-91ad-ad4c033e5b3c', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://interactive/f3c65805-dbfe-5c44-91ad-ad4c033e5b3c'}, {'abstract': 'France’s ultranationalist fringe party isn’t so fringe anymore.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/02/22/magazine/the-national-fronts-post-charlie-hebdo-moment.html', 'snippet': 'France’s ultranationalist fringe party isn’t so fringe anymore.', 'lead_paragraph': 'St.-Raphaël, a resort town on the French Riviera, is subdued in January, suspended in a state of waiting. Its seaside carousel is brilliantly lit but scarcely used, its hotels are mostly shuttered, its streets are nearly deserted by nightfall. On Jan. 16, however, just nine days after French jihadists stormed the Paris offices of the magazine Charlie Hebdo, a crowd gathered in the drizzling rain outside a small St.-Raphaël storefront. In summer days past, the shop sold cheap floppy sun hats to tourists on a table outside, but now a pole with a French flag stood there instead, and a banner had replaced the signs of commerce over the door. The space had been converted into a campaign office for two candidates running for local office, both of whom belonged to the National Front.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '144', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/22/magazine/22france1/22france1-articleLarge-v5.jpg', 'height': 351, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/02/22/magazine/22france1/22france1-articleLarge-v5.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 351}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/22/magazine/22france1/22france1-jumbo-v5.jpg', 'height': 599, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/22/magazine/22france1/22france1-superJumbo-v5.jpg', 'height': 1198, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/22/magazine/22france1/22france1-thumbStandard-v4.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/02/22/magazine/22france1/22france1-thumbStandard-v4.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/22/magazine/22france1/22france1-thumbLarge-v4.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The National Front’s Post-Charlie Hebdo Moment', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': "'Come as You Are'", 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Front (France)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Le Pen, Marine', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'France', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Immigration and Emigration', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Foreign Workers', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Charlie Hebdo', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-02-19T03:32:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Susan Dominus', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Susan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Dominus', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e4e419de-d083-56d7-91a9-10084c18860a', 'word_count': 6069, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e4e419de-d083-56d7-91a9-10084c18860a'}, {'abstract': 'A world-conquering start-up finds itself lost in translation in Tokyo.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/02/22/magazine/meet-the-unlikely-airbnb-hosts-of-japan.html', 'snippet': 'A world-conquering start-up finds itself lost in translation in Tokyo.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Let me introduce you to Yoppy. Yoppy is young and friendly and lives in a small apartment in the Shinagawa neighborhood of Tokyo. His full name is Yuhsuke Yoshimoto, but at least with visitors who come to stay with him through his listing on Airbnb, he prefers to go by Yoppy. He wears heavy-framed black glasses, has a boyish haircut and likes to talk to foreigners, even though his English is admittedly poor. In the one photo I’ve seen of him — his profile shot on Airbnb — he’s wearing a navy blazer, a collared shirt and a thin silver necklace. He smiles at the camera in a pleasant but not overbearing way. It would be hard, I imagine, not to like Yoppy if you were to meet him at a dinner party or at a gathering of pharmacists or financial planners (according to his profile, Yoppy is both a pharmacist and a financial planner), but still that says little about how you would feel when putting your toothbrush on the sink next to his late at night in a city that’s far, far from home.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '136', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/22/magazine/22airbnb2/22mag-22airbnb.t_CA1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/02/22/magazine/22airbnb2/22mag-22airbnb.t_CA1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/22/magazine/22airbnb2/22mag-22airbnb.t_CA1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/22/magazine/22airbnb2/22mag-22airbnb.t_CA1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/22/magazine/22airbnb2/22mag-22airbnb.t_CA1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/02/22/magazine/22airbnb2/22mag-22airbnb.t_CA1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/22/magazine/22airbnb2/22mag-22airbnb.t_CA1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Meet the Unlikely Airbnb Hosts of Japan', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': "'How Can We Find More People Like You?'", 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Colbert, Sara', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Airbnb', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Japan', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Renting and Leasing (Real Estate)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Tokyo (Japan)', 'rank': 6, 'majo