url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/02/22/magazine/the-great-divide.html', 'snippet': 'Finding human connection across walls and razor wire in Pakistan.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In Lahore, Pakistan, the city where I was born and where I once again live after two decades abroad, my experience of picking up my children from school has recently changed. As of this term, I can no longer enter my daughter’s kindergarten. I must show an ID card with her photograph at the fortified gate, a rectangular aperture in a high wall, and she is then brought out to me, emerging like a blue-clad fairy from some strange castle.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '100', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/22/magazine/22essay/22mag-22essay.t_CA0-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 371, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/02/22/magazine/22essay/22mag-22essay.t_CA0-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 371}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/22/magazine/22essay/22mag-22essay.t_CA0-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 632, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/22/magazine/22essay/22mag-22essay.t_CA0-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1265, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/22/magazine/22essay/22mag-22essay.t_CA0-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/02/22/magazine/22essay/22mag-22essay.t_CA0-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/22/magazine/22essay/22mag-22essay.t_CA0-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Great Divide', 'kicker': 'Essay', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Great Divide', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Lahore (Pakistan)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hamid, Mohsin', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Social Conditions and Trends', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Immigration and Emigration', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'School Shootings and Armed Attacks', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computer Security', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Airport Security', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Terrorism', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-02-19T04:14:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mohsin Hamid', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mohsin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hamid', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/74b1627e-292e-515e-9e77-62251349dc3b', 'word_count': 1917, 'uri': 'nyt://article/74b1627e-292e-515e-9e77-62251349dc3b'}, {'abstract': 'Selected by Natasha Trethewey.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/02/22/magazine/abide.html', 'snippet': 'Selected by Natasha Trethewey.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The poet Jake Adam York died of a stroke in 2012, when he was only 40. This poem calls to mind the hymn “Abide With Me,” a prayer for constancy: “In life, in death, O Lord, abide with me.” I have been in a plaintive mood recently, as I remember the many friends I’ve lost over the years, including Jake. When I read the poem now, I am struck by a kind of prescience in the elegiac lines, as if he were speaking his last words to the beloved, knowing how those of us who lost him must now abide. Poem selected by Natasha Trethewey.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '70', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/22/magazine/22poem/22poem-articleLarge-v3.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/02/22/magazine/22poem/22poem-articleLarge-v3.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/22/magazine/22poem/22poem-jumbo-v3.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/22/magazine/22poem/22poem-superJumbo-v3.jpg', 'height': 1154, 'width': 1732, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/22/magazine/22poem/22poem-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/02/22/magazine/22poem/22poem-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/22/magazine/22poem/22poem-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': '‘Abide’', 'kicker': 'Poem', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Abide', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'York, Jake Adam', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Trethewey, Natasha', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Trethewey, Natasha', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Poetry and Poets', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Death and Dying', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-02-19T04:14:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jake Adam York', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jake', 'middlename': 'Adam', 'lastname': 'York', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/20153b9d-ae73-50e8-aa3b-5ed5e347f4d6', 'word_count': 202, 'uri': 'nyt://article/20153b9d-ae73-50e8-aa3b-5ed5e347f4d6'}, {'abstract': 'Lessons on being emotional from a Mexican soap-opera star.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/02/22/magazine/how-to-cry-on-command.html', 'snippet': 'Lessons on being emotional from a Mexican soap-opera star.', 'lead_paragraph': '“If you are happy, having the best day ever, you still have to cry, because that is your job,” says Ana Brenda Contreras, a veteran of Mexican soap operas, or telenovelas. The genre’s operatic plotlines require high-volume, wet-cheeked waterworks, and Contreras, who recently played the lead in 162 episodes of “Corazón Indomable” (“Wild at Heart”), weeps on camera almost every day during production. “TV screens are small — people need to see that tear to feel the emotion,” the 28-year-old actor says.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '78', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/22/magazine/22tip/22tip-articleLarge.png', 'height': 574, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy'