n_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sam Roberts', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Roberts', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Obituary (Obit)', '_id': 'nyt://article/f21c3ad6-238e-52a5-a91e-f035b944a28c', 'word_count': 1147, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f21c3ad6-238e-52a5-a91e-f035b944a28c'}, {'abstract': 'Exchanges exhibited Mr. Bush’s comfort with using email as a tool for governing and with discussing policy with the news media.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/02/19/upshot/emails-to-florida-reporters-show-a-jeb-bush-eager-to-engage.html', 'snippet': 'Exchanges exhibited Mr. Bush’s comfort with using email as a tool for governing and with discussing policy with the news media.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The email that a Los Angeles Times reporter sent to Gov. Jeb Bush of Florida in April 2006 asked how his early years in Midland, Tex., had shaped him. Attached was an article the reporter had written about the immigration policies of Mr. Bush’s brother, President George W. Bush.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/19/upshot/19up-jebmail/19up-jebmail-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 422, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/02/19/upshot/19up-jebmail/19up-jebmail-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 422}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/19/upshot/19up-jebmail/19up-jebmail-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 720, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/19/upshot/19up-jebmail/19up-jebmail-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1440, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/19/upshot/19up-jebmail/19up-jebmail-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/02/19/upshot/19up-jebmail/19up-jebmail-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/19/upshot/19up-jebmail/19up-jebmail-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Emails to Florida Reporters Show a Jeb Bush Eager to Engage', 'kicker': 'On the Record', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Emails to Reporters Show a Jeb Bush Eager to Engage', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'E-Mail', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Willis, Derek', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'News and News Media', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bush, Jeb', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Florida', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2016', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-02-19T05:30:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'The Upshot', 'byline': {'original': 'By Derek Willis', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Derek', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Willis', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8079633e-33ca-5143-873a-0e6025b77298', 'word_count': 1182, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8079633e-33ca-5143-873a-0e6025b77298'}, {'abstract': 'Television highlights.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/02/19/arts/television/whats-on-tv-thursday.html', 'snippet': 'Television highlights.', 'lead_paragraph': '8:30 P.M. (CBS) THE ODD COUPLE Matthew Perry stars as Oscar Madison, a slovenly sports radio host, and Thomas Lennon is Felix Unger, an avowed neat freak, in this remake of the ’70s Jack Klugman-Tony Randall sitcom about roommates struggling to survive their divorces. Wendell Pierce plays Oscar’s agent; Leslie Bibb lives in their building and is willing to date Oscar, but only for sex; and Lauren Graham is his ex-wife. “The new show updates the surface details without dissolving the central bond between the two friends,” Alessandra Stanley wrote in The New York Times. “This is Mr. Perry’s third attempt at sitcom success after a decade on ‘Friends,’ and there is an uneasiness to his performance — in some scenes he looks startled, even frightened — that makes it hard to play off Mr. Lennon, who seems very comfortable as a nervous nelly. That chemistry could come with time, but even if the show flops, it’s an interesting experiment.” In “The Big Bang Theory,” leading in at 8, Wolowitz (Simon Helberg) gets some startling news as the gang prepares to help Stuart (Kevin Sussman) celebrate the reopening of his comic book store. And in the finale of “Two and a Half Men,” at 9, rumor has it that Charlie Harper, the character played by Charlie Sheen, may still be alive.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What’s on TV Thursday', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'What’s On TV Thursday', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2015-02-19T06:00:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kathryn Shattuck', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kathryn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shattuck', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Schedule', '_id': 'nyt://article/fe9e72b6-93f8-577b-afe6-dee18ceb1689', 'word_count': 695, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fe9e72b6-93f8-577b-afe6-dee18ceb1689'}, {'abstract': 'Quotation of the Day for Thursday, February 19, 2015.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/02/19/pageoneplus/quotation-of-the-day.html', 'snippet': 'Quotation of the Day for Thursday, February 19, 2015.', 'lead_paragraph': '“You have to understand, I am in pain. My son is gone.”', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Quotation of the Day', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Quotation of the Day', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2015-02-19T06:51:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Summary', 'section_name': 'Corrections', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Quote', '_id': 'nyt://article/6c6f359e-15ac-597e-9992-ad764b30b7b3', 'word_count': 47, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6c6f359e-15ac-597e-9992-ad764b30b7b3'}, {'abstract': 'Corrections appearing in print on Thursday, February 19, 2015.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/02/19/pageoneplus/corrections-february-19-2015.html', 'snippet': 'Corrections appearing in print on Thursday, February 19, 2015.', 'lead_paragraph': 'FRONT PAGE', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Corrections: February 19, 2015', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Corrections', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2015-02-19T06:51:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Summary', 'section_name': 'Corrections', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt: