, 'kicker': 'Letter', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Lynching in America: A Grim History', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Lynching', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Blacks', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Black People', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Race and Ethnicity', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Southern States (US)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-02-19T08:27:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Letters', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Letter', '_id': 'nyt://article/173df147-d465-5d80-80aa-f73c640f6023', 'word_count': 700, 'uri': 'nyt://article/173df147-d465-5d80-80aa-f73c640f6023'}, {'abstract': 'I am now face to face with dying. But I am not finished with living.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/02/19/opinion/oliver-sacks-on-learning-he-has-terminal-cancer.html', 'snippet': 'I am now face to face with dying. But I am not finished with living.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A MONTH ago, I felt that I was in good health, even robust health. At 81, I still swim a mile a day. But my luck has run out — a few weeks ago I learned that I have multiple metastases in the liver. Nine years ago it was discovered that I had a rare tumor of the eye, an ocular melanoma. The radiation and lasering to remove the tumor ultimately left me blind in that eye. But though ocular melanomas metastasize in perhaps 50 percent of cases, given the particulars of my own case, the likelihood was much smaller. I am among the unlucky ones.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '25', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/19/opinion/19sacks-copy/19sacks-copy-articleLarge-v6.jpg', 'height': 797, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/02/19/opinion/19sacks-copy/19sacks-copy-articleLarge-v6.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 797}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/19/opinion/19sacks-copy/19sacks-copy-jumbo-v6.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 771, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/19/opinion/19sacks-copy/19sacks-copy-superJumbo-v6.jpg', 'height': 1890, 'width': 1422, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/19/opinion/19sacks-copy/19sacks-copy-thumbStandard-v7.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/02/19/opinion/19sacks-copy/19sacks-copy-thumbStandard-v7.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/19/opinion/19sacks-copy/19sacks-copy-thumbLarge-v7.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'My Own Life', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Contributor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'My Own Life', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sacks, Oliver', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hume, David (1711-76)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Death and Dying', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Philosophy', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cancer', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'My Own Life (Book)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-02-19T08:27:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Oliver Sacks', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Oliver', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sacks', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/d05e29cb-e02e-5048-8d66-1ee8b6635e66', 'word_count': 889, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d05e29cb-e02e-5048-8d66-1ee8b6635e66'}, {'abstract': 'Proposals from New York’s chief judge would be a step toward restoring public trust in the justice system.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/02/19/opinion/a-judges-idea-for-grand-jury-reform.html', 'snippet': 'Proposals from New York’s chief judge would be a step toward restoring public trust in the justice system.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The latest idea for reforming the grand-jury system in cases involving police brutality — from New York State’s top judge, Jonathan Lippman — is one of several that have drawn attention in the two months since grand juries in Ferguson, Mo., and Staten Island declined to indict a local police officer who had killed an unarmed man. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '24', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/19/opinion/19thu3web/19thu3-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 440, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/02/19/opinion/19thu3web/19thu3-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 440}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/19/opinion/19thu3web/19thu3-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 750, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': No