': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/22/travel/22THAILAND3/22THAILAND3-articleLarge-v3.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/02/22/travel/22THAILAND3/22THAILAND3-articleLarge-v3.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/22/travel/22THAILAND3/22THAILAND3-jumbo-v3.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/22/travel/22THAILAND3/22THAILAND3-superJumbo-v3.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/22/travel/22THAILAND3/22THAILAND3-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/02/22/travel/22THAILAND3/22THAILAND3-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/22/travel/22THAILAND3/22THAILAND3-thumbLarge-v3.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': '‘Old Thailand’ Found on Sleepy Islands', 'kicker': 'Next Stop', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Glorious Islands, Where Nothing Happens', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lindt, Naomi', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Thailand', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Koh Mak (Thailand)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-02-19T13:31:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Travel', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By Naomi Lindt', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Naomi', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lindt', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0b536e51-8a22-5c0a-94df-1f8b2b1f4210', 'word_count': 1398, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0b536e51-8a22-5c0a-94df-1f8b2b1f4210'}, {'abstract': 'A New Year’s video directed by Zhou Xiaoping shows negative scenes in addition to positive images: polluted air and sunny skies, corrupt officials and meritorious leaders, poor villages and gleaming buildings.', 'web_url': 'https://sinosphere.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/02/19/from-blogger-endorsed-by-chinas-president-a-little-bit-of-the-countrys-dark-side/', 'snippet': 'A New Year’s video directed by Zhou Xiaoping shows negative scenes in addition to positive images: polluted air and sunny skies, corrupt officials and meritorious leaders, poor villages and gleaming buildings.', 'lead_paragraph': '“Hi, I’m China” is a New Year’s video directed by Zhou Xiaoping, a blogger praised last year by President Xi Jinping as a positive influence for the future of arts and culture in the country. Mr. Zhou is known for harsh criticism of the United States and diatribes against people he deems unduly critical of China.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'From Blogger Endorsed by China’s President, a Little Bit of the Country’s Dark Side', 'kicker': 'Sinosphere', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Blogs and Blogging (Internet)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Xi Jinping', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Zhou Xiaoping', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Communist Party of China', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-02-19T13:34:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Austin Ramzy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Austin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ramzy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d100a718-6d31-57b3-88ca-3c1be06e9c53', 'word_count': 396, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d100a718-6d31-57b3-88ca-3c1be06e9c53'}, {'abstract': 'If new Broadway and Off Broadway offerings are any indication, the road to amour is paved with politics, prejudice and the straitjacket of tradition.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/02/22/theater/cupids-arrows-wound-in-wolf-hall-skylight-an-octoroon-and-big-love.html', 'snippet': 'If new Broadway and Off Broadway offerings are any indication, the road to amour is paved with politics, prejudice and the straitjacket of tradition.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The lyricist Lorenz Hart, a star-struck cynic on the subject of human coupling, regularly itemized the painful symptoms that accompany affairs of the heart, like “the sleepless nights, the daily fights/The quick toboggan when you reach the heights.” And as most of us can testify, love isn’t easy under the best of circumstances.', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/22/arts/22BRANTLEY1/22BRANTLEY1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 390, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'leg