, 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/19/multimedia/jordan-extremism-summit/jordan-extremism-summit-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/02/19/multimedia/jordan-extremism-summit/jordan-extremism-summit-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/19/multimedia/jordan-extremism-summit/jordan-extremism-summit-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Jordan Stakes Role Against Terrorism', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Jordan', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Terrorism', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-02-19T21:44:02+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'Reuters', 'person': [], 'organization': 'Reuters'}, 'type_of_material': 'Video', '_id': 'nyt://video/69ffaaf5-ccf7-5a1e-a8eb-98f84e566059', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://video/69ffaaf5-ccf7-5a1e-a8eb-98f84e566059'}, {'abstract': 'In two shows, the excellent British artist Lucy Skaer covers much ground in several mediums with uneven results.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/02/20/arts/design/lucy-skaer-sticks-stones-and-random-house.html', 'snippet': 'In two shows, the excellent British artist Lucy Skaer covers much ground in several mediums with uneven results.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In two shows, the excellent British artist Lucy Skaer covers much ground in several mediums with uneven results. The repurposing and recycling of objects, images and forms — from other art, her own work, her life — are prominent in Ms. Skaer’s work, as with many artists today. The strategy yields outstanding results in the five related sculptures at Murray Guy. The tone is set by a low-lying sculpture: two thick, rough-edged slices of mahogany inlaid with smaller objects found around her studio — a tiny prototype, parts of other sculptures, a small lithography stone and an oblong blue ceramic tile. The piece, which evokes sculptures by Carl Andre and Bruce Nauman, is itself a prototype for the next four: an all-ceramic version; one in marble with touches of malachite; another in aluminum with gunmetal; and, finally, an all-wood version (including veneer). Together they form a stunning meditation on processes, materials and craft, on mutating details and textural contrasts, on looking, achieving an almost cosmic scope. I doubt each would seem quite so rich on its own.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '21', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/20/arts/20LUCYSKAERGALLERY3/20LUCYSKAER-GALLERY3-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 429, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/02/20/arts/20LUCYSKAERGALLERY3/20LUCYSKAER-GALLERY3-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 429}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/20/arts/20LUCYSKAERGALLERY3/20LUCYSKAER-GALLERY3-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 731, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/20/arts/20LUCYSKAERGALLERY3/20LUCYSKAER-GALLERY3-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1463, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/20/arts/20LUCYSKAERGALLERY3/20LUCYSKAER-GALLERY3-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/02/20/arts/20LUCYSKAERGALLERY3/20LUCYSKAER-GALLERY3-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/20/arts/20LUCYSKAERGALLERY3/20LUCYSKAER-GALLERY3-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Lucy Skaer: ‘Sticks & Stones’ and ‘Random House’', 'kicker': 'Art in Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Lucy Skaer: ‘Sticks & Stones’ and ‘Random House’', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Skaer, Lucy', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-02-19T21:44:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Art & Design', 'byline': {'original': 'By Roberta Smith', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Roberta', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Smith', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/f1838f3a-22e2-58b1-bf06-d6a2aeea56cd', 'word_count': 285, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f1838f3a-22e2-58b1-bf06-d6a2aeea56cd'}, {'abstract': 'The Afro-futurist artist Saya Woolfalk conjures a better tomorrow in which women create a consciousness free of the present day’s social ills.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/02/20/arts/design/saya-woolfalk-chimatek-hybridity-visualization-system.html', 'snippet': 'The Afro-futurist artist Saya Woolfalk conjures a better tomorrow in which women create a consciousness free of the present day’s social ills.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Saya Woolfalk’s engagingly imaginative exhibition evokes the lobby for a New Age boutique. It includes paintings of psychedelic kimonos, digital animations of archetypal iconography and exotic avatars and colorful mannequin heads decorated with bones and jewelry. Like the young video artist Jacolby Satterwhite among others, Ms. Woolfalk extends the genre known as Afro-futurism, which includes the music of Sun Ra and George Clinton and science-fiction novels by Samuel R. Delany and Octavia Butler.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '21', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/20/arts/20SAYA-GALLERY5/20SAYA-GALLERY5-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 894, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/02/20/arts/20SAYA-GALLERY5/20SAYA-GALLERY5-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 894}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/20/arts/20SAYA-GALLERY5/20SAYA-GALLERY5-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 687, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/20/arts/20SAYA-GALLERY5/20SAYA-GALLERY5-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1374, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/20/arts/20SAYA-GALLERY5/20SAYA-GALLERY5-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/02/20/arts/20SAYA-GALLERY5/20SAYA-GALLERY5-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/20/arts/20SAYA-GALLERY5/20SAYA-GALLERY5-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Saya Woolfalk: ‘ChimaTEK: Hybridity Visualization System’', 'kicker': 'Art in Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Saya Woolfalk: ‘ChimaTEK: Hybridity Visualization System’', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Woolfalk, Saya', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-02-19T21:46:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Art & Design', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ken Johnson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ken', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Johnson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/5a6fb395-294f-5531-ab3d-740efa8e5b5e', 'word_count': 215, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5a6fb395-294f-5531-ab3d-740efa8e5b5e'}, {'abstract': 'Mayor Rahm Emanuel of Chicago, who was the president’s first chief of staff, joined Mr. Obama at a ceremony Thursday proclaiming the city’s Pullman district a national monument.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/politics/first-draft/2015/02/19/first-draft-focus-a-reunion-of-sorts/', 'snippet': 'Mayor Rahm Emanuel of Chicago, who was the president’s first chief of staff, joined Mr. Obama at a ceremony Thursday proclaiming the city’s Pullman district a national monument.', 'lead_paragraph': '', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/19/us/politics/19firstdraft-obama-pullman/19firstdraft-obama-pullman-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'im