 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2547b321-4c63-5a50-8239-1a74be5c4d1c', 'word_count': 1, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2547b321-4c63-5a50-8239-1a74be5c4d1c'}, {'abstract': 'In time, Mr. Lang may become as forward-looking in his art as he was in his fashion design.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/02/20/arts/design/helmut-lang-at-sperone-westwater.html', 'snippet': 'In time, Mr. Lang may become as forward-looking in his art as he was in his fashion design.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In time, Helmut Lang may become as forward-looking in his art as he was in his fashion design. Right now, he only looks back, content with making standard-issue Post-Minimalism derived from ideas and materials pioneered more than 40 years ago by artists like Richard Van Buren, Keith Sonnier, Lynda Benglis, Eva Hesse and Hannah Wilke. Mr. Lang has long been acquainted with contemporary art, but this work evinces an all-too-typical amnesia about the recent past and a seeming disdain for the rigors of finding your own art rather than settling for a pastiche of the achievements of others.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '21', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/20/arts/20HELMUTLANGGALLERY1/20HELMUTLANG-GALLERY1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 439, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/02/20/arts/20HELMUTLANGGALLERY1/20HELMUTLANG-GALLERY1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 439}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/20/arts/20HELMUTLANGGALLERY1/20HELMUTLANG-GALLERY1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 749, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/20/arts/20HELMUTLANGGAL