us ways to celebrate the Lunar New Year in New York’s neighborhoods.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Chinatown is whatever you make of it. There is the strange blend of chain restaurants and knockoff clothing outlets on Canal Street. There are the popular restaurants, like Joe’s Shanghai or Golden Unicorn, where an hour’s wait is the price of authenticity. Then there are the narrow side streets and uninviting storefronts where the real treats lie: feasts that reward the adventuresome and often cost less than an appetizer anywhere else. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '26', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Chinese New Year Returns With Bargain Meals, Music and Parades', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Chinese New Year Returns With Bargain Meals, Music and Parades', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Lunar New Year', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Chinatown (Manhattan, NY)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-02-19T22:09:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Joshua Barone', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Joshua', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Barone', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b5b655bd-5e80-53ad-96d1-981bb9ed2e37', 'word_count': 524, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b5b655bd-5e80-53ad-96d1-981bb9ed2e37'}, {'abstract': 'Weekend entertainments from the archives of The New York Times.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/02/20/nyregion/friday-file.html', 'snippet': 'Weekend entertainments from the archives of The New York Times.', 'lead_paragraph': '62 YEARS AGO', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '26', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type'