: None}, 'type_of_material': 'Slideshow', '_id': 'nyt://slideshow/c1492456-3f8b-500e-bf8d-c8625ac11313', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://slideshow/c1492456-3f8b-500e-bf8d-c8625ac11313'}, {'abstract': 'Students and faculty at the university, one of the nation’s pre-eminent historically black higher education institutions, set out Thursday to expand entries and create new ones.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/02/20/us/at-howard-a-historically-black-university-filling-in-wikipedias-gaps-in-color.html', 'snippet': 'Students and faculty at the university, one of the nation’s pre-eminent historically black higher education institutions, set out Thursday to expand entries and create new ones.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — Wikipedia is a vast ocean of erudition, with entries on virtually every subject, obscure to earth-shattering, and, it may seem, every human being of even vague renown. It is also, its leaders concede, very white.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Howard University Fills in Wikipedia’s Gaps in Black History', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'At a Historically Black University, Filling in Wikipedia’s Gaps in Color', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Colleges and Universities', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Smith, Jada F', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Blacks', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Black People', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Wikipedia', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Howard University', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Wikimedia Foundation', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-02-20T01:14:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jada F. Smith', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jada', 'middlename': 'F.', 'lastname': 'Smith', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b0fd5136-e7b5-5c73-9232-7939079ddd40', 'word_count': 647, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b0fd5136-e7b5-5c73-9232-7939079ddd40'}, {'abstract': 'This Argentine anthology, an Oscar nominee for best foreign-language film, looks at human behavior when pushed to the extremes.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/02/20/movies/review-wild-tales-explores-the-blurred-limits-of-morality.html', 'snippet': 'This Argentine anthology, an Oscar nominee for best foreign-language film, looks at human behavior when pushed to the extremes.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As high-spirited as its title suggests, “Wild Tales” opens on a savage note and ends, well, that’s for you to find out. In between its shocker start and equally startling windup, this Argentine anthology offers up a scabrous, often unsettlingly funny look at human behavior in extremis. It’s a mad, mad social Darwinian world, churning with men and women who, whether pushed a lot or just a little, are all eager to do the worst to one another. They pounce and then they pummel, engaging in drag-down fights that leave them black and blue and sometimes stone-cold dead.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/20/arts/20WILDTALES1/20WILDTALES1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 399, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/02/20/arts/20WILDTALES1/20WILDTALES1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 399}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/20/arts/20WILDTALES1/20WILDTALES1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 681, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/20/arts/20WILDTALES1/20WILDTALES1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1363, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/20/arts/20WILDTALES1/20WILDTALES1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/02/20/arts/20WILDTALES1/20WILDTALES1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/20/arts/20WILDTALES1/20WILDTALES1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Review: ‘Wild Tales’ Explores the Blurred Limits of Morality', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Pushed to Edge, and Into a Blurred Morality', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Szifron, Damian', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-02-20T01:15:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Manohla Dargis', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Manohla', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Dargis', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/aa271837-27ae-5025-b077-9204333f7540', 'word_count': 779, 'uri': 'nyt://article/aa271837-27ae-5025-b077-9204333f7540'}, {'abstract': 'As the latest high-profile driver to switch racing teams, Carl Edwards may be the competitor to watch in this year’s Sprint Cup title hunt.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/02/20/sports/autoracing/carl-edwards-may-be-the-driver-to-watch-in-the-sprint-cup-title-chase.html', 'snippet': 'As the latest high-profile driver to switch racing teams, Carl Edwards may be the competitor to watch in this year’s Sprint Cup title hunt.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When Kyle Busch was dropped by Hendrick Motorsports after 2007 and signed to race for Joe Gibbs Racing, few could have predicted what happened next. Busch went from one win with Hendrick in 2007 to eight victories with Gibbs in 2008.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/20/sports/Y-NASCAR/Y-NASCAR-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 409, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/02/20/sports/Y-NASCAR/Y-NASCAR-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 409}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/20/sports/Y-NASCAR/Y-NASCAR-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 698, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/20/sports/Y-NASCAR/Y-NASCAR-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1397, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/20/sports/Y-NASCAR/Y-NASCAR-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/02/20/sports/Y-NASCAR/Y-NASCAR-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/20/sports/Y-NASCAR/Y-NASCAR-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'For Nascar Drivers, Switching Teams Has Paid Off Before', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'For Drivers, Switching Teams Has Paid Off Before', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobile Racing', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Edwards, Carl (1979- )', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Gibbs, Joe, Racing', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Roush Fenway Racing', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-02-20T01:21:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Auto Racing', 'byline': {'original': 'By Viv Bernstein', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Viv', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bernstein', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ffccce59-dbba-54b6-ba3e-343406232401', 'word_count': 931, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ffccce59-dbba-54b6-ba3e-343406232401'}, {'abstract': 'The gangly antihero of the director Michael Johnson’s first feature is a teenage misfit stumbling is way through tragedy and isolation to companionship.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/02/20/movies/review-all-the-wilderness-a-tale-of-a-teenage-outsider.html', 'snippet': 'The gangly antihero of the director Michael Johnson’s first feature is a teenage misfit stumbling is way through tragedy and isolation to companionship.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The kind of kid who’s a dinner bell for bullies, James (Kodi Smit-McPhee), the gangly antihero of “All the Wilderness,” wears the teenage-misfit badge on his bony frame like a romantic totem. A recent tragedy has exacerbated James’s already ingrowing personality, and now his quirks — quoting Carl Sandburg; drawing pictures of dead houseflies — have acquired a morbid cast that neither his therapist (Danny DeVito) nor his concerned single mother (Virginia Madsen) can pierce.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/20/arts/20ALLTHEWILDERNESS/20ALLTHEWILDERNESS-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 900, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/02/20/arts/20ALLTHEWILDERNESS/20ALLTHEWILDERNESS-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 900}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/20/arts/20ALLTHEWILDERNESS/20ALLTHEWILDERNESS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 683, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/20/arts/20ALLTHEWILDERNESS/20ALLTHEWILDERNESS-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1366, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/20/arts/20ALLTHEWILDERNESS/20ALLTHEWILDERNESS-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/02/20/arts/20ALLTHEWILDERNESS/20ALLTHEWILDERNESS-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/20/arts/20ALLTHEWILDERNESS/20ALLTHEWILDERNESS-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Review: ‘All the Wilderness,’ a Tale of a Teenage Outsider', 'kicker': None, 'co