', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cohn', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8e4aa026-44f1-59da-9f8f-75bb2797bf85', 'word_count': 1179, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8e4aa026-44f1-59da-9f8f-75bb2797bf85'}, {'abstract': 'The move is to reduce the influence of the governors of New York and New Jersey in the agency, among other changes announced by the Port Authority.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/02/20/nyregion/addressing-dysfunction-port-authority-plans-to-install-nonpolitical-ceo.html', 'snippet': 'The move is to reduce the influence of the governors of New York and New Jersey in the agency, among other changes announced by the Port Authority.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For decades, the Port Authority of New York and New Jersey has been a house divided, an agency overseen by people who owed loyalty to one governor or another. The internal division often devolved into dysfunction and has occasionally led to misfeasance, such as the move in 2013 to close some traffic lanes leading to the George Washington Bridge.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '24', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Addressing Dysfunction, Port Authority Plans to Install ‘Nonpolitical’ C.E.O.', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Port Agency Is Creating C.E.O. Job', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McGeehan, Patrick', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Port Authority of New York and New Jersey', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Governors (US)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York State', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New Jersey', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Christie, Christopher J', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons