cusing President Obama of not loving his country.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/politics/first-draft/2015/02/19/giuliani-obama-had-a-white-mother-so-im-not-a-racist/', 'snippet': 'Rudolph W. Giuliani defended his remarks accusing President Obama of not loving his country.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Former Mayor Rudolph W. Giuliani of New York on Thursday defended his assertion that President Obama did not love America, and said that his criticism of Mr. Obama’s upbringing should not be considered racist because the president was raised by “a white mother.”', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Giuliani: Obama Had a White Mother, So I’m Not a Racist', 'kicker': 'First Draft', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Giuliani Stands By Remarks on Obama', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Discrimination', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Giuliani, Rudolph W', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-02-20T02:06:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Maggie Haberman and Nicholas Confessore', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Maggie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Haberman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Nicholas', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Confessore', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/081b85f5-23c4-54f1-8e04-9f005d417048', 'word_count': 512, 'uri': 'nyt://article/081b85f5-23c4-54f1-8e04-9f005d417048'}, {'abstract': 'Turkey and the United States signed an agreement to train and equip moderate Syrian rebels to fight militants from the Islamic State, Foreign Minister Mevlut Cavusoglu said, according to the Anadolu News Agency.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/02/20/world/europe/turkey-deal-set-to-aid-syrian-rebels.html', 'snippet': 'Turkey and the United States signed an agreement to train and equip moderate Syrian rebels to fight militants from the Islamic State, Foreign Minister Mevlut Cavusoglu said, according to the Anadolu News Agency.', 'lead_paragraph': ' After months of talks, Turkey and the United States on Thursday signed an agreement to train and equip moderate Syrian rebels to fight militants from the Islamic State, Foreign Minister Mevlut Cavusoglu said, according to the Anadolu News Agency. Mr. Cavusoglu also suggested that the fighters could join the rebellion against the Syrian government, although American officials have emphasized that the primary goal is to combat the Islamic State, also known as ISIS or ISIL. Turkey, along with Jordan and Saudi Arabia, will provide training sites for the program, which is scheduled to begin in March and is expected to train about 15,000 fighters over three years, Turkish and American officials have said. The United States has said that it plans to send about 400 soldiers and other military personnel to train the fighters. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Turkey: Deal Set to Aid Syrian Rebels', 'kicker': 'World Briefing', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Help in Fight Against ISIS', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Turkey', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Islamic State in Iraq and Syria (ISIS)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-02-20T02:11:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sebnem Arsu', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sebnem', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Arsu', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/ed7eb909-e526-5cb5-aa0b-405a72a9244d', 'word_count': 134, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ed7eb909-e526-5cb5-aa0b-405a72a9244d'}, {'abstract': 'A panel in North Carolina has recommended closing three academic centers, including a poverty center and one dedicated to social change, sparking outrage among liberals.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/02/20/us/ideology-seen-as-factor-in-closings-in-university-of-north-carolina-system.html', 'snippet': 'A panel in North Carolina has recommended closing three academic centers, including a poverty center and one dedicated to social change, sparking outrage among liberals.', 'lead_paragraph': 'An advisory panel of the University of North Carolina’s Board of Governors has recommended closing three academic centers, including a poverty center and one dedicated to social change, inciting outrage among liberals who believe that conservatives in control of state government are targeting ideological opponents in academia.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Ideology Seen as Factor in Closings in University of North Carolina System', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Ideology Seen as Factor in Closings at University', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Colleges and Universities', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'North Carolina', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Shutdowns (Institutional)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 