onday.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/20/sports/CITY-RANGERS/CITY-RANGERS-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 410, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/02/20/sports/CITY-RANGERS/CITY-RANGERS-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 410}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/20/sports/CITY-RANGERS/CITY-RANGERS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 700, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/20/sports/CITY-RANGERS/CITY-RANGERS-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1401, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/20/sports/CITY-RANGERS/CITY-RANGERS-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/02/20/sports/CITY-RANGERS/CITY-RANGERS-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/20/sports/CITY-RANGERS/CITY-RANGERS-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Rangers, Again Prolific Late in Game, Are Beaten at Their Own Game ', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Rangers, Again Prolific Late in Game, Are Beaten at Their Own Game', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hockey, Ice', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Pickens, Pat', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hagelin, Carl', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'St Louis, Martin', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Vancouver Canucks', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Rangers', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-02-20T04:12:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Hockey', 'byline': {'original': 'By Pat Pickens', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Pat', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pickens', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1c9bd4ea-c323-551b-8b8b-3a4bfaec4295', 'word_count': 619, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1c9bd4ea-c323-551b-8b8b-3a4bfaec4295'}, {'abstract': 'The Chicago Cubs can proceed with a construction project at Wrigley Field, a federal judge ruled Thursday, but the project’s future remains uncertain as a lawsuit continues by property owners.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/02/20/us/illinois-cubs-allowed-to-continue-renovations.html', 'snippet': 'The Chicago Cubs can proceed with a construction project at Wrigley Field, a federal judge ruled Thursday, but the project’s future remains uncertain as a lawsuit continues by property owners.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Chicago Cubs can proceed with a construction project at Wrigley Field, a federal judge ruled Thursday, but the project’s future remains uncertain as a lawsuit continues by property owners who say the renovations will block their views of the stadium. Owners of properties across the street from the outfield have long sold tickets to spectators who watch from their rooftops. Some owners have argued in federal court that a renovation project underway at the stadium, which includes large signs that would be placed in the outfield, violates a contract between them and the team. Judge Virginia M. Kendall of United States District Court in Chicago said Thursday that she did not have the evidence needed for a temporary restraining order to stop construction, as the rooftop owners requested. Both sides will be back in court next month for a hearing on a preliminary injunction that could derail the renovations. “We’ve got Opening Day on April 5,” Judge Kendall said. “I’m going to get my job done before then.” ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Illinois: Cubs Allowed to Continue Renovations', 'kicker': 'National Briefing | Midwest', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Illinois: Cubs Allowed to Continue Renovations', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Wrigley Field (Chicago)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Chicago Cubs', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Chicago (Ill)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-02-20T04:13:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mitch Smith', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mitch', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Smith', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/fd4900b7-0af4-5524-8e4a-b12346581631', 'word_count': 169, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fd4900b7-0af4-5524-8e4a-b12346581631'}, {'abstract': 'The Hung Sing Kwoon Kung Fu and Lion Dance Club stopped at Jade Asian Restaurant in Flushing, Queens, on Thursday to celebrate the Chinese Lunar New Year.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/02/19/big-hello-for-the-year-of-the-yang/', 'snippet': 'The Hung Sing Kwoon Kung Fu and Lion Dance Club stopped at Jade Asian Restaurant in Flushing, Queens, on Thursday to celebrate the Chinese Lunar New Year.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Hung Sing Kwoon Kung Fu and Lion Dance Club stopped at Jade Asian Restaurant in Flushing, Queens, on Thursday to celebrate the Chinese Lunar New Year, symbolized this year by a zodiac animal whose Mandarin name, yang, is translated into English variously as sheep, goat or ram.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/20/nyregion/20CHINESENEWYEARFLOATER/20CHINESENEWYEARFLOATER-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 382, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/02/20/nyregion/20CHINESENEWYEARFLOATER/20CHINESENEWYEARFLOATER-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 382}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/20/nyregion/20CHINESENEWYEARFLOATER/20CHINESENEWYEARFLOATER-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 652, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/20/nyregion/20CHINESENEWYEARFLOATER/20CHINESENEWYEARFLOATER-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1304, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/20/nyregion/20CHINESENEWYEARFLOATER/20CHINESENEWYEARFLOATER-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/02/20/nyregion/20CHINESENEWYEARFLOATER/20CHINESENEWYEARFLOATER-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/20/nyregion/20CHINESE