holiday and its cultural significance and traditions.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '6 Q’s About the News | The Year of the Goat', 'kicker': 'The Learning Network', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2015-02-20T09:59:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By Katherine Schulten', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Katherine', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schulten', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c23fb222-ea8e-5811-ab81-b6c5d7ff9f2e', 'word_count': 247, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c23fb222-ea8e-5811-ab81-b6c5d7ff9f2e'}, {'abstract': 'Does a higher minimum wage lift families out of poverty? Or would it force employers to hire fewer workers?', 'web_url': 'https://learning.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/02/20/is-the-minimum-wage-too-low/', 'snippet': 'Does a higher minimum wage lift families out of poverty? Or would it force employers to hire fewer workers?', 'lead_paragraph': 'About half of all workers in the United States who are at or below the federal minimum wage of $7.25 an hour are ages 16 to 24. Would a higher minimum wage help young people get ahead? Would it help lift families out of poverty? Or would it unintentionally have the opposite effect by dampening hiring? Economists disagree about the effects of a higher minimum wage. What do you think?', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/01/01/business/jpWAGE-LN/jpWAGE-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 424, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/01/01/business/jpWAGE-LN/jpWAGE-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 424}}, {'rank': 0, 'su