rts in the Dardanelles in 1915.', 'web_url': 'https://iht-retrospective.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/02/20/1915-dardanelles-forts-bombarded/', 'snippet': 'Highlights from the International Herald Tribune archives: The Allied fleet bombards forts in the Dardanelles in 1915.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON — The Admiralty announces that yesterday [Feb. 19] morning a British fleet of battleships and battle cruisers accompanied by flotillas and aided by a strong French squadron, the whole under the command of Vice-Admiral Sackville Hamilton Carden, began an attack upon the forts at the entrance of the Dardanelles. The forts at Cape Helles and Kum Kale were bombarded with deliberate long-range fire. Considerable effect was produced on two of the forts, and two others were frequently hit, but, being open earthworks, it was difficult to estimate the damage. The forts, being outranged, were not able to reply to the fire.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '1915: Dardanelles Forts Bombarded', 'kicker': 'IHT Retrospective', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Ships and Shipping', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'France', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Great Britain', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Turkey', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-02-20T14:57:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By International Herald Tribune', 'person': [{'firstname': 'International', 'middlename': 'Herald', 'lastname': 'Tribune', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f8035f58-a882-5d46-a79b-700acce7007f', 'word_count': 169, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f8035f58-a882-5d46-a79b-700acce7007f'}, {'abstract': 'Haste, waste, and possibly avoidable disaster.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/02/20/europe-needs-to-stop-the-clock/', 'snippet': 'Haste, waste, and possibly avoidable disaster.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I’ve been in correspondence with various people trying to track the current Greece/euro crisis, and everyone seems to have reached the same conclusion I’ve reached — namely, that what’s needed above all right now is some way to stop the clock, call a time-out, whatever. We’re talking about weeks, maybe a month or two — but that pause is desperately needed, because otherwise it will be all too easy to stumble into a preventable disaster.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Europe Needs To Stop The Clock', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2015-02-20T15:05:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/37498339-504f-5fd2-a9aa-1d921451fd21', 'word_count': 351, 'uri': 'nyt://article/37498339-504f-5fd2-a9aa-1d921451fd21'}, {'abstract': 'Welcome to Motherlode’s weekly open thread. Do you have thoughts about the news this week, and how it affects families? A question to ask? A rant to share? This is your place. Go.', 'web_url': 'https://parenting.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/02/20/your-turn-a-weekend-thread-open-for-comments-45/', 'snippet': 'Welcome to Motherlode’s weekly open thread. Do you have thoughts about the news this week, and how it affects families? A question to ask? A rant to share? This is your place. Go.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Welcome to Motherlode’s weekly open thread. Do you have thoughts about the news this week, and how it affects families? A question to ask? A rant to share? This is your place. Go.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Your Turn: A Weekend Thread, Open for Comments', 'kicker': 'Motherlode', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2015-02-20T15:05:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Styles', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/486ef34b-6618-517f-9f1c-85855166dd64', 'word_count': 33, 'uri': 'nyt://article/486ef34b-6618-517f-9f1c-85855166dd64'}, {'abstract': 'The artist brings an exclusive new collection to the storied department stores.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/02/20/frederique-morrel-bergdorf-goodman/', 'snippet': 'The artist brings an exclusive new collection to the storied department stores.', 'lead_paragraph': '“My inspiration is life and all its aspects,” says the designer and artist Frédérique Morrel. That may sound like a particularly broad subject matter, but Morrel’s work, which is crafted\xa0by covering three-dimensional objects with vintage tapestries, does have an all-encompassing approach to its pastoral aesthetic. And beginning today, her newest pieces will be on view at Bergdorf Goodman’s 5th Avenue flagship store in New York —\xa0the result of an exclusive partnership with the department store (“We share the same values of exclusivity, rarity and the love of well done savoir-faire,” she says). The shoppable exhibition (prices range from $900 to $120,000) also marks her U.S. debut.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/20/t-magazine/20bergdorf-reese/20bergdorf-reese-articleLarge-v3.jpg', 'height': 674, 'width': 