, 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2e7f3f26-86fd-5882-8947-f6ee887484a0', 'word_count': 25, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2e7f3f26-86fd-5882-8947-f6ee887484a0'}, {'abstract': 'Highlights from the International Herald Tribune archives: King Gustav of Sweden refused military assistance to Finland in 1940.', 'web_url': 'https://iht-retrospective.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/02/20/1940-sweden-divided-over-aid-to-finland/', 'snippet': 'Highlights from the International Herald Tribune archives: King Gustav of Sweden refused military assistance to Finland in 1940.', 'lead_paragraph': 'STOCKHOLM — The domestic situation in Sweden tonight [Feb. 20] was tense as the result of King Gustav’s refusal to give military aid to Finland. Despite the King’s effort to keep Sweden at peace, as he has during the thirty-three years of his own reign and as it has been kept during more than a century, the undertone of discontent over official aloofness in the aggression on Finland was distinctly audible. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/21/blogs/21iht-oldfeb21-gustav/21iht-oldfeb21-gustav-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 781, 'width': 516, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/21/blogs/21iht-oldfeb21-gustav/21iht-oldfeb21-gustav-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 781, 'width': 516, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/21/blogs/21iht-oldfeb21-gustav/21iht-oldfeb21-gustav-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy'