': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-02-20T17:28:19+0000', 'document_type': 'audio', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Books', 'subsection_name': 'Book Review', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://audio/bf69b3b9-07d7-5a4a-ae14-fc967ede78e9', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://audio/bf69b3b9-07d7-5a4a-ae14-fc967ede78e9'}, {'abstract': 'Stewart O’Nan imagines Fitzgerald in Hollywood.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/02/22/books/review/west-of-sunset-by-stewart-onan.html', 'snippet': 'Stewart O’Nan imagines Fitzgerald in Hollywood.', 'lead_paragraph': 'F. Scott Fitzgerald was both a perfect and a terrible fit for Hollywood. His youthful fame gave him a shrewd perspective on that shallow, tinselly world. Yet while working there in the last three years of his life, he was a sad case: a debt-ridden genius, alcoholic, selling himself to collaborate on second-rate screenplays. Ever hear of “A Yank at Oxford”? No wonder his great, unfinished novel, “The Love of the Last Tycoon,” deals with the romance, illusion and tawdriness of the movie industry. ', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '15', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '‘West of Sunset,’ by Stewart O’Nan', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'This Gilded Shore', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': "O'Nan, Stewart", 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Fitzgerald, F Scott', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-02-20T17:29:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'BookReview', 'section_name': 'Books', 'subsection_name': 'Book Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Caryn James', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Caryn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'James', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/ad4051d1-9956-50dd-b663-368940b6553a', 'word_count': 593, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ad4051d1-9956-50dd-b663-368940b6553a'}, {'abstract': 'An analysis of PTSD and how the culture responds to it shows effects that extend well beyond the individual sufferer.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/02/22/books/review/the-evil-hours-by-david-j-morris.html', 'snippet': 'An analysis of PTSD and how the culture responds to it shows effects that extend well beyond the individual sufferer.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The field of psychiatric studies exploded during World War II because of an influx of traumatized soldiers. War is a kind of grand opening for studies of the mind. Historically, interest in trauma studies rises sharply during wartime, then wanes in its aftermath. But this time, even as the wars in Iraq and Afghanistan recede from public attention, rates of post-traumatic stress disorder have continued to increase. PTSD is currently the fourth-most-common psychiatric disorder in America.', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/22/books/review/22PERCY/0222-bks-PERCY-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 496, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/02/22/books/review/22PERCY/0222-bks-PERCY-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 496}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/22/books/review/22PERCY/0222-bks-PERCY-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 846, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/22/books/review/22PERCY/0222-bks-PERCY-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1266, 'width': 1532, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/22/books/review/22PERCY/0222-bks-PERCY-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/02/22/books/review/22PERCY/0222-bks-PERCY-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/22/books/review/22PERCY/0222-bks-PERCY-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': '‘The Evil Hours,’ by David J. Morris', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Wake of Grief', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Percy, Jennifer', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Morris, David J', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Post-Traumatic Stress Disorder', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'The Evil Hours: A Biography of Post-Traumatic Stress Disorder (Book)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-02-20T17:29:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'BookReview', 'section_name': 'Books', 'subsection_name': 'Book Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jen Percy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Percy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/604c58b5-eab7-56c4-b7de-aee0ccd5d0e3', 'word_count': 1307, 'uri': 'nyt://article/604c58b5-eab7-56c4-b7de-aee0ccd5d0e3'}, {'abstract': 'A journalist working in conflict zones becomes overwhelmed by the traumas she reports.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/02/22/books/review/irritable-hearts-by-mac-mcclelland.html', 'snippet': 'A journalist working in conflict zones becomes overwhelmed by the traumas she reports.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The American journalist Mac McClelland has reported from crisis zones like Myanmar and the Democratic Republic of Congo, but in her memoir “Irritable Hearts” she chronicles a crisis she can’t leave behind. ', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '19', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/22/books/review/22FALEIRO/22FALEIRO-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 835, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/02/22/books/review/22FALEIRO/22FALEIRO-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 835}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/22/books/review/22FALEIRO/22FALEIRO-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 737, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/22/books/review/22FALEIRO/22FALEIRO-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1473, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/22/books/review/22FALEIRO/22FALEIRO-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/02/22/books/review/22FALEIRO/22FALEIRO-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/22/books/review/22FALEIRO/22