men’s wear line 1205, Paula Gerbase has, until recently, maintained a profile as discreet as the clothes she creates. Last year, however, the Brazilian-born designer vaulted into the majors when she was named artistic director of John Lobb, the esteemed British footwear house. Though the appointment ruffled a few traditionalist feathers, to Gerbase, the pairing makes perfect sense: The designer, who studied at Central Saint Martins and spent several years training with tailors on Savile Row, retains a reverence for her adopted city’s customs even as she works to reinvent them. “The diversity and wealth of culture present in London is unparalleled and is endlessly inspiring,” she says. “There is also a unique freedom to it that allows you to express yourself creatively without boundaries.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/20/t-magazine/20beddie-gerbase1/20beddie-gerbase1-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/02/20/t-magazine/20beddie-gerbase1/20beddie-gerbase1-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/20/t-magazine/20beddie-gerbase1/20beddie-gerbase1-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/20/t-magazine/20beddie-gerbase1/20beddie-gerbase1-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/20/t-magazine/20beddie-gerbase1/20beddie-gerbase1-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/02/20/t-magazine/20beddie-gerbase1/20beddie-gerbase1-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/20/t-magazine/20beddie-gerbase1/20beddie-gerbase1-thumbLarge-v3.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Designer Paula Gerbase Shares Her Favorite London Haunts', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Food', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Shopping and Retail', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'London (England)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-02-20T19:15:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Eviana Hartman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Eviana', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hartman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1e97cfb4-1f94-5087-9cb9-fd602523741f', 'word_count': 696, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1e97cfb4-1f94-5087-9cb9-fd602523741f'}, {'abstract': 'New books examine the start of Mr. de Blasio’s tenure, case studies in participatory planning, and an early-20th-century fighter for socialist causes.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/02/22/nyregion/books-that-look-at-bill-de-blasios-first-year-as-mayor-urban-design-and-elizabeth-gurley-flynn.html', 'snippet': 'New books examine the start of Mr. de Blasio’s tenure, case studies in participatory planning, and an early-20th-century fighter for socialist causes.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Eric Alterman’s “Equality and One City: Bill de Blasio and the New York Experiment, Year One” (ebookNation) is a de Blasio booster’s handbook to how much the mayor has already accomplished and a sober reminder — no matter how many poor people vote for empathetic local candidates — of just how much Albany and Washington can scuttle his agenda. ', 'print_section': 'MB', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/22/nyregion/22BOOKSHELF/22BOOKSHELF-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 939, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/02/22/nyregion/22BOOKSHELF/22BOOKSHELF-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 939}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/22/nyregion/22BOOKSHELF/22BOOKSHELF-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 655, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/22/nyregion/22BOOKSHELF/22BOOKSHELF-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1565, 'width': 1000, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/22/nyregion/22BOOKSHELF/22BOOKSHELF-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/02/22/nyregion/22BOOKSHELF/22BOOKSHELF-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/22/nyregion/22BOOKSHELF/22BOOKSHELF-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline