56, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2a7e21c3-5be2-59f1-b083-c3d233831655'}, {'abstract': 'Mr. Gerhaher, set to perform at Alice Tully Hall, is considered one of the greatest proponents of the lied tradition since Dietrich Fischer-Dieskau.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/02/22/arts/music/christian-gerhaher-sings-winterreise-without-all-the-frills.html', 'snippet': 'Mr. Gerhaher, set to perform at Alice Tully Hall, is considered one of the greatest proponents of the lied tradition since Dietrich Fischer-Dieskau.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Schubert’s “Winterreise” (“Winter Journey”), an hourlong song cycle about heartbreak, loneliness and alienation published in 1828, is a masterpiece of austere beauty. In recent years, the work has been subjected to a flurry of stage adaptations, including one by the British director Katie Mitchell that weaves in poems by Beckett, and one, shown at the White Light Festival last November, with animated drawings by the South African artist William Kentridge. Theater and opera companies as far afield as Chicago, Anchorage and Melbourne have put on productions featuring actors, video art, sound design and dancers.', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/22/arts/22GERHAHER1/22GERHAHER1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/02/22/arts/22GERHAHER1/22GERHAHER1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/22/arts/22GERHAHER1/22GERHAHER1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/22/arts/22GERHAHER1/22GERHAHER1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1367, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/22/arts/22GERHAHER1/22GERHAHER1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/02/22/arts/22GERHAHER1/22GERHAHER1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/22/arts/22GERHAHER1/22GERHAHER1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Christian Gerhaher Sings ‘Winterreise’ Without All the Frills', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Art Songs Without All the Frills', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'da Fonseca-Wollheim, Corinna', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Classical Music', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Schubert, Franz', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gerhaher, Christian', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Chamber Music Society of Lincoln Center', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-02-20T20:46:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Corinna da Fonseca-Wollheim', 'person': [{'firstname': '', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/45b30d60-87c3-5f38-9c05-bca0d25c967d', 'word_count': 1606, 'uri': 'nyt://article/45b30d60-87c3-5f38-9c05-bca0