: '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Slideshow', '_id': 'nyt://slideshow/0875a95f-7043-55d9-b58a-622bcce04b0b', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://slideshow/0875a95f-7043-55d9-b58a-622bcce04b0b'}, {'abstract': 'By auctioning off the outfit he wore while meeting President Obama last month, Prime Minister Narendra Modi cauterized a political problem.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/02/21/world/asia/flap-in-india-over-narendra-modi-pinstripes.html', 'snippet': 'By auctioning off the outfit he wore while meeting President Obama last month, Prime Minister Narendra Modi cauterized a political problem.', 'lead_paragraph': 'NEW DELHI — Indian tycoons jockeyed on Friday to demonstrate their allegiance to Prime Minister Narendra Modi by bidding on a widely discussed item of clothing: the tailored suit that Mr. Modi wore last month to meet President Obama. The suit’s yellow pinstripes, upon closer examination, proved to be tiny lines of script spelling out Mr. Modi’s name.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/21/world/21MODI3/21MODI3-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 420, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/02/21/world/21MODI3/21MODI3-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 420}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/21/world/21MODI3/21MODI3-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 717, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/21/world/21MODI3/21MODI3-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1397, 'width': 1996, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None