rs are responding with more attractive balance-transfer offers, a new analysis finds.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Credit Card Balance Transfer Can Reap Savings if Done Cautiously', 'kicker': 'Your Money Adviser', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Credit and Debt', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Personal Finances', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Credit Cards', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Interest Rates', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-02-21T01:18:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Your Money', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ann Carrns', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ann', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Carrns', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c0761eee-27ee-5198-b261-7898cddd74fc', 'word_count': 611, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c0761eee-27ee-5198-b261-7898cddd74fc'}, {'abstract': 'The few residents left in the fiercely contested town, Debaltseve, emerged from basements and other refuges on Friday to a Dickensian scene of destruction and gloom.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/02/21/world/europe/ukraine-town-eases-back-into-life-after-deadly-week-of-fighting.html', 'snippet': 'The few residents left in the fiercely contested town, Debaltseve, emerged from basements and other refuges on Friday to a Dickensian scene of destruction and gloom.', 'lead_paragraph': 'DEBALTSEVE, Ukraine — While the Ukrainian government accused Russia of sending more tanks and troops into the country despite a cease-fire agreement, the few residents who remained in the fiercely contested town of Debaltseve emerged from basements and other refuges on Friday to a Dickensian scene of destruction and gloom.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/21/world/UKRAINE-2/UKRAINE-2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/02/21/world/UKRAINE-2/UKRAINE-2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/21/world/UKRAINE-2/UKRAINE-2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/21/world/UKRAINE-2/UKRAINE-2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/21/world/UKRAINE-2/UKRAINE-2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/02/21/world/UKRAINE-2/UKRAINE-2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/21/world/UKRAINE-2/UKRAINE-2-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Ukraine Town Eases Back Into Life After Deadly Week of Fighting', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Ukraine Town Eases Back Into Life After Deadly Week of Fighting', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Ukraine', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Debaltseve (Ukraine)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Russia', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-02-21T01:26:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew E. Kramer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': 'E.', 'lastname': 'Kramer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/880705e9-617c-54fb-aa28-93c614579695', 'word_count': 1125, 'uri': 'nyt://article/880705e9-617c-54fb-aa28-93c614579695'}, {'abstract': 'A new virus appears to have caused the death last spring of a man in Kansas, the Centers for Disease Control and Prevention reported Friday in its journal Emerging Infectious Diseases.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/02/21/us/new-virus-suspected-in-death-of-kansas-man.html', 'snippet': 'A new virus appears to have caused the death last spring of a man in Kansas, the Centers for Disease Control and Prevention reported Friday in its journal Emerging Infectious Diseases.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A new virus appears to have caused the death last spring of a man in Kansas, the Centers for Disease Control and Prevention reported Friday in its journal Emerging Infectious Diseases. The virus, called Bourbon virus after the county where the man lived, is probably spread by ticks; the man was healthy before seeking treatment for fever and fatigue after getting a tick bite. Bourbon virus belongs to a group called thogotoviruses, the C.D.C. said. It is the first time a thogotovirus has been known to make an American ill; there have been seven cases in Africa, Europe and Asia, the report said. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'New Virus Suspected in Death of Kansas Man', 'kicker': 'National Briefing | Health', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'New Virus Suspected in Death of Kansas Man', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Kansas', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Belluck, Pam', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Ticks (Insects)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Viruses', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Centers for Disease Control and Prevention', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Emerging Infectious Diseases (Journal)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-02-21T01:27:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Pam Belluck', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Pam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Belluck', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/1474b8e5-44f9-5fd2-8075-8753d79ab4ad', 'word_count': 103, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1474b8e5-44f9-5fd2-8075-8753d79ab4ad'}, {'abstract': 'When Hormis Thaliath saw Devi Nampiaparampil’s profile on a dating site, he knew she was the one. At the time though, she wasn’t even aware she had a profile.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/02/22/fashion/weddings/shes-the-one-after-all.html', 'snippet': 'When Hormis Thaliath saw Devi Nampiaparampil’s profile on a dating site, he knew she was the one. At the time though, she wasn’t even aware she had a profile.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In 2010, Hormis Thaliath logged into the Indian dating site Shaadi.com for the first time. Dating online had always struck him as awkward, but he learned the process wasn’t half as dubious as it had seemed when his sister first told him she had created an account on his behalf. In fact, it was almost comically easy. After browsing only four profiles, he had found someone interesting enough to stop looking further.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'She’s the One, After All', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Weddings and Engagements', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-02-21T01:30:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Society', 'section_name': 'Fashion & Style', 'subsection_name': 'Weddings', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kenan Christiansen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kenan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Christiansen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0032bb8c-9f9c-5376-a8d3-ecae5ab94c93', 'word_count': 1036, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0032bb8c-9f9c-5376-a8d3-ecae5ab94c93'}, {'abstract': 'After a reporter chronicled Jamel Hunter’s birthday party, he received a gift from Stan Lee, one of the famous crime fighter’s creators.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/02/21/nyregion/spider-man-in-sketch-form-visits-an-8-year-old-fan-in-harlem.html', 'snippet': 'After a reporter chronicled Jamel Hunter’s birthday party, he received a gift from Stan Lee, one of the famous crime fighter’s creators.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The intercom was broken outside the front door at the Washington Houses project in East Harlem on Thursday. No way to buzz a visitor up. Finally, someone leaving held the door open.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/21/nyregion/21CRIMESCENE/21CRIMESCENE-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/02/21/nyregion/21CRIMESCENE/21CRIMESCENE-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheig