1c8a9c-bef9-5706-8eb8-3cf35572d7fb'}, {'abstract': 'An agreement to extend Greece’s bailout for four months also committed the nation to fiscal targets and other conditions that its new leadership had vowed to scrap.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/02/22/world/europe/a-deal-that-preserves-greeces-place-in-eurozone-and-fiscal-restraints.html', 'snippet': 'An agreement to extend Greece’s bailout for four months also committed the nation to fiscal targets and other conditions that its new leadership had vowed to scrap.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BRUSSELS — Just a month ago, after being propelled to power by a wave of anger at Greece’s economic miseries, Alexis Tsipras declared his left-wing Syriza party’s election victory the start of a Europe-wide revolt against austerity. “Europe is going to change,” he said before setting off on a tour of European capitals to rally support for a more relaxed new direction.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/22/world/GREECE/GREECE-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 399, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/02/22/world/GREECE/GREECE-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 399}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/22/world/GREECE/GREECE-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 681, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/22/world/GREECE/GREECE-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1362, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/22/world/GREECE/GREECE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height'