rifts from the property’s back-lot smoker; festooning the outer wall of the restaurant building is a painted mural in the shape of a swine. There might as well be a giant overhead neon sign, flashing Abandon Diets, All Ye Who Enter Here. ', 'print_section': 'CT', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/22/nyregion/22DINECT2/22DINECT2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 600, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/02/22/nyregion/22DINECT2/22DINECT2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 600}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/22/nyregion/22DINECT2/22DINECT2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/22/nyregion/22DINECT2/22DINECT2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/22/nyregion/22DINECT2/22DINECT2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/02/22/nyregion/22DINECT2/22DINECT2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/22/nyregion/22DINECT2/22DINECT2-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Nose Knows the Way to Barbecue ', 'kicker': 'Dining Review | Connecticut', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Nose Knows the Way to Barbecue', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Restaurants', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Bridgeport (Conn)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Walrus + Carpenter (Bridgeport, Conn, Restaurant)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-02-21T21:40:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sarah Gold', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sarah', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gold', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/c2639b92-76bc-5ce6-845e-67f33fa55670', 'word_count': 785, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c2639b92-76bc-5ce6-845e-67f33fa55670'}, {'abstract': 'C. C. Sabathia, who lost a career-high 13 games in a poor 2013 and had his velocity fall in 2014 before his season was cut short by knee surgery, acknowledged he had plenty to prove.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/02/22/sports/baseball/c-c-sabathiahopes-his-results-recover-with-his-knee.html', 'snippet': 'C. C. Sabathia, who lost a career-high 13 games in a poor 2013 and had his velocity fall in 2014 before his season was cut short by knee surgery, acknowledged he had plenty to prove.', 'lead_paragraph': 'TAMPA, Fla. — C. C. Sabathia looked as imposing as ever as he walked into the Yankees’ clubhouse Saturday morning. Whether he returns to being so imposing on the mound remains an open question. ', 'print_section': 'SP', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/22/sports/22sabathia-1/22sabathia-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 958, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/02/22/sports/22sabathia-1/22sabathia-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 958}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/22/sports/22sabathia-1/22sabathia-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 642, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/22/sports/22sabathia-1/22sabathia-1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1283, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/22/sports/22sabathia-1/22sabathia-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/02/22/sports/22sabathia-1/22sabathia-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/22/sports/22sabathia-1/22sabathia-1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'C. C. Sabathia\xa0Hopes His Results Recover With His Knee', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Sabathia Hopes His Results Recover With His Knee', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Witz, Billy', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sabathia, C C', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Yankees', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-02-21T21:45:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Billy Witz', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Billy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Witz', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a46ece3b-0a58-5126-88f6-631279fca265', 'word_count': 421, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a46ece3b-0a58-5126-88f6-631279fca265'}, {'abstract': 'Thanks to the success of acts like Florida Georgia Line, country is finally moving ever so slightly into the singles era.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/02/22/arts/music/little-bit-country-lots-of-other-stuff.html', 'snippet': 'Thanks to the success of acts like Florida Georgia Line, country is finally moving ever so slightly into the singles era.', 'lead_paragraph': 'At the peak of their powers, the country duo Florida Georgia Line took hip-hop attitude, retrofitted with rural twang and concerns, and stomped to the top of Nashville on the backs of the status-quo bros who came just before them. Florida Georgia Line — Brian Kelley and Tyler Hubbard — weren’t any good at the status quo, but it turned out they were positively great at tossing it out.', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/22/arts/22GUIDE6/22GUIDE6-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 693, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/02/22/arts/22GUIDE6/22GUIDE6-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 693}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/22/arts/22GUIDE6/22GUIDE6-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 887, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/22/arts/22GUIDE6/22GUIDE6-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1773, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/22/arts/22GUIDE6/22GUIDE6-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/02/22/arts/22GUIDE6/22GUIDE6-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/22/arts/22GUIDE6/22GUIDE6-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Little Bit Country, Lots of Other Stuff', 'kicker': 'The Week Ahead | Pop', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Little Bit Country, Lots of Other Stuff', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Florida Georgia Line (Music Group)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-02-21T21:48:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jon Caramanica', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jon', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Caramanica', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ef26963e-b48a-5e3b-81e0-5f11d167057d', 'word_count': 172, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ef26963e-b48a-5e3b-81e0-5f11d167057d'}, {'abstract': 'Cervantes’s comic masterpiece, “Don Quixote,” inspired many artworks, most notably tapestries by Charles Coypel.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/02/22/arts/design/art-scenes-inspired-by-don-quixote.html', 'snippet': 'Cervantes’s comic masterpiece, “Don Quixote,” inspired many artworks, most notably tapestries by Charles Coypel.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Cervantes’s comic masterpiece, “Don Quixote,” inspired many artworks, most notably tapestries by Charles Coypel, Louis XV’s artist. Coypel created 28 tapestries woven at the Gobelins Manufactory in Paris. Starting on Wednesday, the Frick Collection will present a complete series of the scenes. The exhibition, “Coypel’s Don Quixote Tapestries: Illustrating a Spanish Novel in Eighteenth-Century France,” will include five of the original paintings they were based on; these have never been seen before in New York and are on loan from the Palais Impérial de Compiègne and the Musée Jacquemart-André, Paris. The museum will also show three Gobelins tapestry panels from the\xa0J. Paul Getty Museum and two Flemish tapestries inspired by Coypel from the Frick Collection, which have not been on view in more than 10 years. The Frick’s tapestries — rarely seen, because they take so much room to display — were cleaned in 1999 and restored at the Textile Conservation Lab at the Cathedral of St. John the Divine. (Through May 17, frick.org.)', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/22/arts/22GUIDE1/22GUIDE1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 371, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/02/22/arts/22GUIDE1/22GUIDE1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 371}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/22/arts/22GUIDE1/22GUIDE1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 633, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/22/arts/22GUIDE1/22GUIDE1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1266, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/22/arts/22GUIDE1/22GUIDE1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/02/22/arts/22GUIDE1/22GUIDE1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/22/arts/22GUIDE1/22GUIDE1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Art: Scenes Inspired by ‘Don Quixote’', 'kicker': 'The Week Ahead | Art', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Scenes Inspired by ‘Don Quixote’', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-02-21T21:48:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Art & Design', 'byline': {'original': 'By Robin Pogrebin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Robin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pogrebin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2d4b45d7-b075-55f4-93fb-c366d03b849a', 'word_count': 164, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2d4b45d7-b075-55f4-93fb-c366d03b849a'}, {'abstract': 'The pianist Leif Ove Andsnes and the Mahler Chamber Orchestra present Beethoven concertos.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/02/22/arts/music/for-this-musician-the-time-has-come.html', 'snippet': 'The pianist Leif Ove Andsnes and the Mahler Chamber Orchestra present Beethoven concertos.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The excellent Norwegian pianist Leif Ove Andsnes waited until his 40s — when he said he felt emotionally ready to perform Beethoven — to begin recording the Beethoven concertos with the Mahler Chamber Orchestra. Judging by the result, the wait has paid off. On Monday, Mr. Andsnes and the ensemble offer Beethoven’s second, third and fourth concertos, with Mr. Andsnes conducting from the keyboard. On Wednesday, they perform the first and fifth concertos. (8 p.m. Monday and Wednesday, Carnegie Hall, carnegiehall.org.)', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/22/arts/22GUIDE5/22GUIDE5-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/02/22/arts/22GUIDE5/22GUIDE5-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/22/arts/22GUIDE5/22GUIDE5-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/22/arts/22GUIDE5/22GUIDE5-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1366, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/22/arts/22GUIDE5/22GUIDE5-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/02/22/arts/22GUIDE5/22GUIDE5-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/22/arts/22GUIDE5/22GUIDE5-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'For This Musician, the Time Has Come', 'kicker': 'The Week Ahead | Classical', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'For This Musician, the Time Has Come', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Classical Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-02-21T21:48:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Vivien Schweitzer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Vivien', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schweitzer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/37005438-b938-5570-ad97-a0cc8d3459c7', 'word_count': 148, 'uri': 'nyt://article/37005438-b938-5570-ad97-a0cc8d3459c7'}, {'abstract': 'In the premiere of “Dinner at Tiffani’s,” the running gag is whether the show’s host, Tiffani Thiessen, actually ate the morsels she was shown scarfing down.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/02/22/arts/television/are-you-going-to-eat-that.html', 'snippet': 'In the premiere of “Dinner at Tiffani’s,” the running gag is whether the show’s host, Tiffani Thiessen, actually ate the morsels she was shown scarfing down.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Shocker: actors consuming food. Or are they? In the premiere of “Dinner at Tiffani’s,” Wednesday night on the Cooking Channel, the running gag is whether the show’s host, Tiffani Thiessen, late of “White Collar,” and her friends Nathan Fillion, Willie Garson and Lindsay Price actually ate the morsels they were shown scarfing down on their hit shows, or even from the catering table off screen. On “Sex and the City,” Mr. Garson reports, cast members had carte blanche at any New York restaurant, with food guaranteed in their trailers in 20 minutes. In “Beverly Hills 90210,” Ms. Price says, no one dared eat. (Bikini bodies, duh.) On the screen in “Castle,” Mr. Fillion prefers to wave his fork around and mime chewing. Whether Ms. Thiessen’s guests applied their sleight of hand to her roasted chicken, brussels sprouts with pancetta and fresh figs drizzled in lavender honey is anyone’s guess. But food isn’t really the point when you’re promising a walk down memory lane with Jason Priestley, Lance Bass, Elizabeth Berkley and Jonathan Silverman.', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/22/arts/22GUIDE2/22GUIDE2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/02/22/arts/22GUIDE2/22GUIDE2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/22/arts/22GUIDE2/22GUIDE2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/22/arts/22GUIDE2/22GUIDE2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1366, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/22/arts/22GUIDE2/22GUIDE2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/02/22/arts/22GUIDE2/22GUIDE2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/22/arts/22GUIDE2/22GUIDE2-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Are You Going to Eat That?', 'kicker': 'The Week Ahead | Television', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Are You Going to Eat That?', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-02-21T21:48:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kathryn Shattuck', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kathryn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shattuck', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8593ef95-44fb-555b-954c-b2e5baad3dcf', 'word_count': 173, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8593ef95-44fb-555b-954c-b2e5baad3dcf'}, {'abstract': '“Vivacious Lady” is a good place to start when contemplating the charms of Ginger Rogers.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/02/22/movies/watch-that-lady-and-see-a-star.html', 'snippet': '“Vivacious Lady” is a good place to start when contemplating the charms of Ginger Rogers.', 'lead_paragraph': '“Vivacious Lady” (1938) is a good place to start when contemplating the charms of Ginger Rogers, the subject of a MoMA Acteurism series. First there’s that title, a reminder of Rogers’s always welcome presence, whether dancing with Fred Astaire or falling in love, as she does in this movie with Jimmy Stewart, whose own acteurism is also nicely on display. And then there’s the story, which gets at what made Rogers such an invaluable star. ', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/22/arts/22GUIDE3/22GUIDE3-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 791, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/02/22/arts/22GUIDE3/22GUIDE3-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 791}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/22/arts/22GUIDE3/22GUIDE3-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 778, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 