ww.nytimes.com/2015/02/22/world/asia/polluted-air-cuts-years-off-lives-of-millions-in-india-study-finds.html', 'snippet': 'Altogether, 660 million Indians could lose 2.1 billion years in life expectancy as a result of air pollution, at enormous cost to the country’s economy, researchers found.', 'lead_paragraph': 'COLOMBO, Sri Lanka — More than half of India’s population lives in places with such polluted air that each person loses an average of 3.2 years in life expectancy, according to a recent study by researchers from the University of Chicago, Yale and Harvard.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Polluted Air Cuts Years Off Lives of Millions in India, Study Finds', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Polluted Air Cuts Years Off Lives of Millions in India, Study Finds', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Air Pollution', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'India', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Longevity', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Research', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'World Health Organization', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-02-21T21:57:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Gardiner Harris', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Gardiner', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Harris', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8cdf2f24-9d03-5627-b965-ebcee2d9c7c5', 'word_count': 286, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8cdf2f24-9d03-5627-b965-ebcee2d9c7c5'}, {'abstract': 'Pamela Chatterton-Purdy’s gilded panels portraying influential figures like the Rev. Dr. Martin Luther King Jr. and Rosa Parks can be seen at Les Beaux Arts Gallery, in Round Hill Community Church in Greenwich.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/02/22/nyregion/in-greenwich-art-focusing-on-civil-rights-figures.html', 'snippet': 'Pamela Chatterton-Purdy’s gilded panels portraying influential figures like the Rev. Dr. Martin Luther King Jr. and Rosa Parks can be seen at Les Beaux Arts Gallery, in Round Hill Community Church in Greenwich.', 'lead_paragraph': 'One day in the summer of 1955, when the artist Pamela Chatterton-Purdy was 15 years old, her father got a call from Jackie Robinson, the Brooklyn Dodgers’ second baseman and the first black man to play Major League Baseball in the modern era. Robinson was planning to buy a home in North Stamford, Conn., near where her family lived, and he wanted to hire her father’s van company for the move. ', 'print_section': 'CT', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/22/nyregion/22ARTSCTCOMBO/22ARTSCTCOMBO-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 652, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/02/22/nyregion/22ARTSCTCOMBO/22ARTSCTCOMBO-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 652}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/22/nyregion/22ARTSCTCOMBO/22ARTSCTCOMBO-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 942, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/22/nyregion/22ARTSCTCOMBO/22ARTSCTCOMBO-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1968, 'width': 1810, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/22/nyregion/22ARTSCTCOMBO/22ARTSCTCOMBO-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/02/22/nyregion/22ARTSCTCOMBO/22ARTSCTCOMBO-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/22/nyregion/22ARTSCTCOMBO/22ARTSCTCOMBO-thumbLarge-v3.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Icons in the Struggle for Racial Equality', 'kicker': 'Arts | Connecticut', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Icons in the Struggle for Racial Equality', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Risen, Clay', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Greenwich (Conn)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Race and Ethnicity', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Chatterton-Purdy, Pamela', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Blacks', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Black People', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Civil Rights Movement (1954-68)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-02-21T22:02:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Clay Risen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Clay', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Risen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/139e9827-6658-5281-b6ec-3d6b08b7bbb4', 'word_count': 731, 'uri': 'nyt://article/139e9827-6658-5281-b6ec-3d6b08b7bbb4'}, {'abstract': 'Mr. Rosenblat, a survivor of Nazi camps, wrote a tale of a kind girl and an apple that turned out to be false.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/02/22/business/media/herman-rosenblat-85-dies-made-up-holocaust-love-story.html', 'snippet': 'Mr. Rosenblat, a survivor of Nazi camps, wrote a tale of a kind girl and an apple that turned out to be false.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The first curse on mankind was imposed because of an apple, and for all that happened to Herman Rosenblat in his 85 years — the horrors inflicted in Nazi concentration camps, the gunshot wound he suffered when his Brooklyn television repair shop was robbed, the global fame bestowed by two appearances on “The Oprah Winfrey Show” — it is an apple for which he will be most remembered. That first bite of the fruit was built on a lie.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/22/business/22OBITSROSENBLAT/22OBITSROSENBLAT-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/02/22/business/22OBITSROSENBLAT/22OBITSROSENBLAT-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/22/business/22OBITSROSENBLAT/22OBITSROSENBLAT-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/22/business/22OBITSROSENBLAT/22OBITSROSENBLAT-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/22/business/22OBITSROSENBLAT/22OBITSROSENBLAT-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/0