egan the process of gradually reducing her dosages. In Going Off, a series of Anxiety posts in the coming weeks, she will chronicle the challenges she faces from both the drugs and the withdrawal in her pursuit of a drug-free life. ', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Fear and Withdrawal', 'kicker': 'Anxiety', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Fear and Withdrawal', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Anxiety and Stress', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Depression (Mental)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Drugs (Pharmaceuticals)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mental Health and Disorders', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Yoga', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-02-21T22:16:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Diana Spechler', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Diana', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Spechler', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/931ef81b-bfd6-563b-b8fb-da77f9b51262', 'word_count': 1173, 'uri': 'nyt://article/931ef81b-bfd6-563b-b8fb-da77f9b51262'}, {'abstract': 'Lawson Pub, having put the damage of hurricanes behind it, remains a welcoming Oceanside staple.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/02/22/nyregion/a-review-of-lawson-pub-in-oceanside.html', 'snippet': 'Lawson Pub, having put the damage of hurricanes behind it, remains a welcoming Oceanside staple.', 'lead_paragraph': 'There should be no doubt that the setting for the life story of Joseph Bonacore, the owner and chef of Lawson Pub, would be Oceanside. He was born and raised here, and when he was a teenager, he worked in the kitchen of a restaurant on the s