'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/55232518-a33a-568e-b63b-f1872dc2048f', 'word_count': 151, 'uri': 'nyt://article/55232518-a33a-568e-b63b-f1872dc2048f'}, {'abstract': 'Security companies are doing a better job at surrounding computers with defenses. Now the fight has moved far inside the machine, where unwanted or malicious software is nearly impossible to detect.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/02/22/lenovo-and-superfish-penetrate-the-heart-of-a-computers-security/', 'snippet': 'Security companies are doing a better job at surrounding computers with defenses. Now the fight has moved far inside the machine, where unwanted or malicious software is nearly impossible to detect.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The same week researchers reported that the National Security Agency had been embedding surveillance tools in the guts of thousands of machines in Iran, Russia and other countries, it was revealed that the world’s largest personal computer company had been doing something similar to its customers.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Lenovo and Superfish Penetrate the Heart of a Computer’s Security', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Spyware in Lenovo PCs Is Placed at Core of System ', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computer Security', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Surveillance of Citizens by Government', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Horne, Peter', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Lenovo Group', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Security Agency', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-02-22T10:30:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nicole Perlroth', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nicole', 'middlename': Non