et': 'Highlights from the International Herald Tribune archives: The American Club gathers to celebrate George Washington’s birthday in Paris in 1940.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Americans in Paris, celebrating Washington’s Birthday in the capital of a country at war, joined in a spontaneous enthusiastic ovation for heroic Finland at the banquet given by the American Club of Paris at the Grand Hotel yesterday evening [Feb. 22]. Rising from their seats, 300 members and guests of the club acclaimed Harri Holma, Finnish Minister, who was one of many foreign diplomats present. Sir Ronald Campbell, British Ambassador, was also given an ovation. It was the largest gathering the American Club has seen for a long time, and oldtimers recalled that during the World War the club rarely mustered 100 members at its function. Representing the French government, Camille Chautemps, Vice-President of the Council, paid tribute to the victims of Nazi aggression and recalled that George Washington was not only a victorious general, but a liberator and hero of democracy, defending individual liberty.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/23/blogs/23iht-Paris/23iht-Paris-jumbo.png', 'height': 582, 'width': 558, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/23/blogs/23iht-Paris/23iht-Paris-superJumbo.png', 'height': 582, 'width': 558, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/23/blogs/23iht-Paris/23iht-Paris-thumbStandard.png', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/02/23/blogs/23iht-Paris/23iht-Paris-thumbStandard.png', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailh