: {'original': 'By Viv Bernstein', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Viv', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bernstein', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4abddb2e-039b-526f-8d0e-011306233957', 'word_count': 965, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4abddb2e-039b-526f-8d0e-011306233957'}, {'abstract': 'Geza Ottlik and Hugh Kelsey wrote “Adventures in Card Play” in 1979. It is generally considered to be the toughest bridge book ever published.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/02/23/crosswords/bridge/a-deal-for-the-player-who-likes-a-challenge.html', 'snippet': 'Geza Ottlik and Hugh Kelsey wrote “Adventures in Card Play” in 1979. It is generally considered to be the toughest bridge book ever published.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Geza Ottlik and Hugh Kelsey wrote “Adventures in Card Play” in 1979. It is generally considered to be the toughest bridge book ever published. The deals were provided by Ottlik, from Hungary, and the text written by Kelsey, from Scotland. (Kelsey told me that Ottlik had found one analytical error in the book, but he refused to tell me in which deal. If you find it, please write in.)', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/23/crosswords/bridge/23card/23card-jumbo.gif', 'height': 1024, 'width': 560, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/23/crosswords/bridge/23card/23card-superJumbo.gif', 'height': 1059, 'width': 579, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/23/crosswords/bridge/23card/23card-thumbStandard.gif', 'height': 75, 'widt