: 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/22/education/22OREVIEW4_STONE/22OREVIEW4_STONE-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Farewell, Mani Cam. On the Red Carpet, Things Turn Serious.', 'kicker': 'Fashion Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Farewell, Mani Cam. On the Red Carpet, Things Turn Serious.', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Academy Awards (Oscars)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'E! Entertainment Television', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cotillard, Marion', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'ARQUETTE, PATRICIA', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Blanchett, Cate', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Dern, Laura', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Washington, Kerry', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Stone, Emma', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Witherspoon, Reese', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Watts, Naomi', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-02-23T05:13:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'subsection_name': 'Awards Season', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alexandra Jacobs', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alexandra', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Jacobs', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/98bfeae0-2c60-5044-839b-e566b2613502', 'word_count': 662, 'uri': 'nyt://article/98bfeae0-2c60-5044-839b-e566b2613502'}, {'abstract': 'Quotation of the day for Monday, February 23, 2015.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/02/23/pageoneplus/quotation-of-the-day-for-monday-february-23-2015.html', 'snippet': 'Quotation of the day for Monday, February 23, 2015.', 'lead_paragraph': '“Maybe in healthier times for the music business there would be a little more human compassion. But now, the business is in a really troubled place, and people have other responsibilities, like their own livelihood.”', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Quotation of the Day for Monday, February 23, 2015', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Quotation of the Day', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2015-02-23T05:20:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Summary', 'section_name': 'Corrections', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Quote', '_id': 'nyt://article/57cc3964-4e01-5aab-b880-8595389e73ff', 'word_count': 59, 'uri': 'nyt://article/57cc3964-4e01-5aab-b880-8595389e73ff'}, {'abstract': 'Television highlights.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/02/23/arts/whats-on-tv-monday.html', 'snippet': 'Television highlights.', 'lead_paragraph': '9 P.M. (HBO) CITIZENFOUR (2014) Laura Poitras had been working on a film about surveillance for two years when Edward J. Snowden, the National Security Agency whistle-blower, contacted her in January 2013, using the name “Citizenfour.” When Mr. Snowden let Ms. Poitras know that he would not conceal his identity as the source of information about N.S.A. surveillance, she persuaded him to let her film their encounter. This Oscar-nominated documentary chronicles the encounter in a Hong Kong hotel room of Ms. Poitras; Glenn Greenwald, the Pulitzer Prize-winning journalist who first wrote about Mr. Snowden’s revelations; and Mr. Snowden as he hands over classified documents that provide evidence of the N.S.A.’s invasion of privacy and copes with the resulting media storm. “Cinema, even in the service of journalism, is always more than reporting, and focusing on what Ms. Poitras’s film is about risks ignoring what it is,” A. O. Scott wrote in The New York Times. “It’s a tense and frightening thriller that blends the brisk globe-trotting of the ‘Bourne’ movies with the spooky, atmospheric effects of a Japanese horror film. And it is also a primal political fable for the digital age, a real-time tableau of the confrontation between the individual and the state.” He added: “Thinking about the issues Ms. Poitras raises can induce a kind of epistemological vertigo. What do we know about what is known about us? Who knows it? Can we trust them? These questions are terrifying, and so is ‘Citizenfour.’\xa0”', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What’s on TV Monday', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'What’s On TV Monday', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-02-23T05:29:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kathryn Shattuck', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kathryn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shattuck', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1a1a3e76-b592-5fb9-8116-081f867ea95c', 'word_count': 697, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1a1a3e76-b592-5fb9-8116-081f867ea95c'}, {'abstract': 'A new exhibit features three Bronx-born photographers whose work explores the idea of community while challenging outdated, lingering notions.', 'web_url': 'https://lens.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/02/23/complicating-the-picture-of-urban-life/', 'snippet': 'A new exhibit features three Bronx-born photographers whose work explores the idea of community while challenging outdated, lingering notions.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The 1980 image of Paul Newman, taken in the South Bronx during the filming of “Fort Apache, the Bronx,” could be a production still or a publicity photo. But the photograph was taken on location for more consequential reasons: Its photographer, Joe Conzo Jr., the teenage son of activists, was there to document a film that many in the community believed would hurt and embarrass it.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Complicating the Picture of Urban Life', 'kicker': 'Lens', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Blacks', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Black People', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Civil Rights and Liberties', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Civil Rights Movement (1954-68)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Photography', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Race and Ethnicity', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Berger, Maurice', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Frank, Robert', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Frazier, LaToya Ruby', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Bronx Museum of the Arts', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Lincoln Hospital', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'AFRICA', 'rank': 13, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Boston (Mass)', 'rank': 14, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'East Harlem (Manhattan, NY)', 'rank': 15, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Lower East Side (Manhattan, NY)', 'rank': 16, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'valu