 'lead_paragraph': '', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/21/opinion/rfdmosquitoes/rfdmosquitoes-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 414, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/02/21/opinion/rfdmosquitoes/rfdmosquitoes-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 414}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/21/opinion/rfdmosquitoes/rfdmosquitoes-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 707, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/21/opinion/rfdmosquitoes/rfdmosquitoes-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1414, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/21/opinion/rfdmosquitoes/rfdmosquitoes-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/02/21/opinion/rfdmosquitoes/rfdmosquitoes-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/21/opinion/rfdmosquitoes/rfdmosquitoes-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Can Genetically Modified Bugs Save Lives?', 'kicker': 'Room for Debate', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2015-02-23T12:50:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/120302a7-94ad-58f4-baa4-0f4305cade09', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://article/120302a7-94ad-58f4-baa4-0f4305cade09'}, {'abstract': 'Government recommendations on how much fat and salt you should eat weren’t always based on the best available evidence. That may be changing.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/02/24/upshot/behind-new-dietary-guidelines-better-science.html', 'snippet': 'Government recommendations on how much fat and salt you should eat weren’t always based on the best available evidence. That may be changing.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For decades, many dietary recommendations have revolved around consuming a low percentage of your daily calories from fat. It has been widely thought that doing so would reduce your chance of having coronary heart disease. Most of the evidence for that recommendation has come from epidemiologic studies, which can be flawed.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/24/upshot/24up-health/24up-health-articleLarge.gif', 'height': 338, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/02/24/upshot/24up-health/24up-health-articleLarge.gif', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 338}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/24/upshot/24up-health/24up-health-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/24/upshot/24up-health/24up-health-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/24/upshot/24up-health/24up-health-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/02/24/upshot/24up-health/24up-health-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/24/upshot/24up-health/24up-health-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Behind New Dietary Guidelines, Better Science', 'kicker': 'The New Health Care', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Diet and Nutrition', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Research', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cholesterol', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Salt', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Open Heart (Journal)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-02-23T12:55:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Upshot', 'section_name': 'The Upshot', 'byline': {'original': 'By Aaron E. Carroll', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Aaron', 'middlename': 'E.', 'lastname': 'Carroll', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/25286b17-ff94-540e-8b41-8c95b0bed70c', 'word_count': 1379, 'uri': 'nyt://article/25286b17-ff94-540e-8b41-8c95b0bed70c'}, {'abstract': 'The overestimates on rates for government bonds seem to be systemic, and we may be demanding more budget restraint than necessary.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/02/24/upshot/we-keep-flunking-forecasts-on-interest-rates-distorting-the-budget-outlook.html', 'snippet': 'The overestimates on rates for government bonds seem to be systemic, and we may be demanding more budget restraint than necessary.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Government economists try to predict the future of lots of indicators, including G.D.P., unemployment and inflation. Their record isn’t great, whether here or overseas. No less a figure than the Queen of England said to scholars at the London School of Economics about the deep recession in 2008: “Why did no one see it coming?”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/20/upshot/21up-forecast-1424385796135/21up-forecast-1424385796135-articleLarge-v2.png', 'height': 374, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/02/20/upshot/21up-forecast-1424385796135/21up-forecast-1424385796135-articleLarge-v2.png', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 374}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/20/upshot/21up-forecast-1424385796135/21up-forecast-1424385796135-jumbo-v2.png', 'height': 638, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/20/upshot/21up-forecast-1424385796135/21up-forecast-1424385796135-superJumbo-v2.png', 'height': 1046, 'width': 1679, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/20/upshot/21up-forecast-1424385796135/21up-forecast-1424385796135-thumbStandard.png', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/02/20/upshot/21up-forecast-1424385796135/21up-forecast-1424385796135-thumbStandard.png', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/20/upshot/21up-forecast-1424385796