cle', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alexandra Waespi', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alexandra', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Waespi', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/aaf9ae18-5d6e-5bcc-a222-e823331f10ec', 'word_count': 40, 'uri': 'nyt://article/aaf9ae18-5d6e-5bcc-a222-e823331f10ec'}, {'abstract': 'From the International Herald Tribune archives: Greenwich has a large factory fire in 1890.', 'web_url': 'https://iht-retrospective.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/02/23/1890-great-fire-at-greenwich/', 'snippet': 'From the International Herald Tribune archives: Greenwich has a large factory fire in 1890.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON— \xa0A conflagration, which involved buildings nearly one hundred yards square, of a field of barrels of petroleum and over a dozen barges, all blazing at the same time, broke out at an early hour this morning [Feb. 23], and is still burning to-night. The scene of the outbreak was the Ordnance Wharf, Blackwall Lane, East Greenwich. Several engines were soon at the scene. Even then the flames were visible as far away as Southwark. The factory is about seventy yards long and fifty yards wide, and was used by the firm for general manufacturing purposes, and was crammed with thousands of tons of stock of the most inflammable description. How it originated is a mystery. — The New York Herald, European Edition, Feb. 24, 1890', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/24/blogs/24iht-oldfeb24-greenwich/24iht-oldfeb24-greenwich-jumbo.png', 'height': 580, 'width': 395, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/24/blogs/24iht-oldfeb24-greenwich/24iht-oldfeb24-greenwich-superJumbo.png', 'height': 580, 'width': 395, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/24/blogs/24iht-oldfeb24-greenwich/24iht-oldfeb24-greenwich-thumbStandard.png', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/02/24/blogs/24iht-oldfeb24-greenwich/24iht-oldfeb24-greenwich-thumbStandard.png', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/24/blogs/24iht-oldfeb24-greenwich/24iht-oldfeb24-greenwich-thumbLarge.png', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': '1890: Great Fire at Greenwich', 'kicker': 'IHT Retrospective', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Factories and Manufacturing', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fires and Firefighters', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Greenwich (England)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-02-23T14:52:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By International Herald Tribune', 'person': [{'firstname': 'International', 'middlename': 'Herald', 'lastname': 'Tribune', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ccb84ad9-b7a1-5a47-acfe-44a9c60758f7', 'word_count': 126, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ccb84ad9-b7a1-5a47-acfe-44a9c60758f7'}, {'abstract': 'From the International Herald Tribune archives: Russians advance in the Carpathians in 1915.', 'web_url': 'https://iht-retrospective.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/02/23/1915-russians-in-north-poland/', 'snippet': 'From the International Herald Tribune archives: Russians advance in the Carpathians in 1915.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PETROGRAD — The Germans have swept through Augustowo and are now fighting a fresh Russian column between Lypsk and Grodno, but they are being held at bay on the right banks of the Narew and Bebrz, they have not been able to invest either Osowiec or Lomza, and the Muscovites have resumed the offensive on the north bank of the Vistula, where Marshal von Hindenburg’s forces were most threatening to the safety of Warsaw. — The New York Herald, European Edition, Feb. 24, 1915', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '1915: Russians in North Poland', 'kicker': 'IHT Retrospective', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'World War I (1914-18)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Germany', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Poland', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Russia', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-02-23T14:56:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By International Herald Tribune', 'person': [{'firstname': 'International', 'middlename': 'Herald', 'lastname': 'Tribune', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7a8a2e93-acb5-578b-b372-14010ea152b5', 'word_count': 84, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7a8a2e93-acb5-578b-b372-14010ea152b5'}, {'abstract': 'Prime Minister Tony Abbott of Australia announced national security revisions, including tighter immigration laws, and the revoking of citizenship or curbing rights of those involved in terrorism.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/video/world/asia/100000003529957/security-crackdown-