': 'Turtles and Tortoises', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Nova Scotia (Canada)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-02-23T16:14:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Science', 'section_name': 'Science', 'byline': {'original': 'By James Gorman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'James', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gorman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ba406164-bf84-523a-ba24-88cc5441d8f8', 'word_count': 527, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ba406164-bf84-523a-ba24-88cc5441d8f8'}, {'abstract': 'It was while I was in a country where the names “Roe” and “Wade” are virtually unknown that I have learned the most about their legacy.', 'web_url': 'https://kristof.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/02/23/the-engel-macher/', 'snippet': 'It was while I was in a country where the names “Roe” and “Wade” are virtually unknown that I have learned the most about their legacy.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The end of January marked an important anniversary for those of us who work in women’s health care: the 42nd anniversary of Roe v. Wade. This eponymous Supreme Court decision carries a great deal of emotional weight, and once a year, much of this emotion boils over into a week of protests, both for and against it. The names “Roe” and “Wade” inspire passionate opinions in even the most apolitical of Americans; and yet, ironically, it was in a country where these two names are virtually unknown that I have learned the most about their legacy.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/20/opinion/20kristof_hospital/20kristof_hospital-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 450, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/02/20/opinion/20kristof_hospital/20kristof_hospital-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 450}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/20/opinion/20kristof_hospital/20kristof_hospital-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 768, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/20/opinion/20kristof_hospital/20kristof_hospital-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1536, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/20/opinion/20kristof_hospital/20kristof_hospital-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/02/20/opinion/20kristof_hospital/20kristof_hospital-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/20/opinion/20kristof_hospital/20kristof_hospital-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Engel Macher', 'kicker': 'Nicholas Kristof', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ABORTION', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kristof, Nicholas D', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Guttmacher Institute', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Supreme Court (US)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'AFRICA', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-02-23T16:15:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Carolynn Dude', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Carolynn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Dude', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b3f4250b-3bd3-52b3-9cbb-a4f9928d7e12', 'word_count': 800, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b3f4250b-3bd3-52b3-9cbb-a4f9928d7e12'}, {'abstract': 'The Academy’s ways — including resistance to critical praise like that for “Boyhood” — made all the difference.', 'web_url': 'https://carpetbagger.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/02/23/how-it-came-to-be-birdmans-night/', 'snippet': 'The Academy’s ways — including resistance to critical praise like that for “Boyhood” — made all the difference.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Well, there you go. With the Academy Awards, sometimes you just never know. Or, rather you do, if you know where to look. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/23/arts/inarritu/inarritu-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/02/23/arts/inarritu/inarritu-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/23/arts/inarritu/inarritu-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/23/arts/inarritu/inarritu-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/23/arts/inarritu/inarritu-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/02/23/arts/inarritu/inarritu-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/23/arts/inarritu/inarritu-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'How It Came to Be ‘Birdman’s’ Night', 'kicker': 'Carpetbagger', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Academy Awards (Oscars)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Desplat, Alexandre (1961- )', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Inarritu, Alejandro G', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Linklater, Richard', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-02-23T16:15:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Cara Buckley', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Cara', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Buckley', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/629a05fa-0553-5ff3-998a-339012a75250', 'word_count': 418, 'uri': 'nyt://article/629a05fa-0553-5ff3-998a-339012a75250'}, {'abstract': 'A London strip now boasts shops as British as afternoon tea.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/02/23/london-duke-street/', 'snippet': 'A London strip now boasts shops as British as afternoon tea.', 'lead_paragraph': 'London’s quiet Duke Street, a few blocks from the international megastores on Mount Street, has seen an influx of boutiques with a decidedly local bent. The new location from the quirky-chic shoemaker Penelope Chilvers includes a studio for custom “dandy slippers,” and Philip Treacy’s protégée Laura Apsit Livens, a milliner to Rita Ora and the Duchess of Westminster, has set up her atelier inside a repurposed Victorian stairwell. Meanwhile, the historic men’s wear label E. Tautz — founded in 1867 and recently revived by the Norton & Sons designer Patrick Grant — just moved their first store into the neighborhood, with tailoring in the basement and the debut women’s collection on the racks. These boutiques join the recently opened Duke Street Emporium, a two-level concept store offering emerging fashion labels, beauty products and books amid exhibits from hometown artists.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '62', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/03/09/t-magazine/09mens-look-duke/09mens-look-duke-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 429, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/03/09/t-magazine/09mens-look-duke/09mens-look-duke-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 429}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/03/09/t-magazine/09mens-look-duke/09mens-look-duke-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 731, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/03/09/t-magazine/09mens-look-duke/09mens-look-duke-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1463, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/03/09/t-magazine/09mens-look-duke/09mens-look-duke-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/03/09/t-magazine/09mens-look-duke/09mens-look-duke-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type':