', 'value': 'Immelt, Jeffrey R', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Vestager, Margrethe', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Europe', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-02-23T20:58:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'DealBook', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Jolly', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Jolly', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ea2f3839-9236-5522-8965-b3ce08404dab', 'word_count': 421, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ea2f3839-9236-5522-8965-b3ce08404dab'}, {'abstract': 'Marc Jacobs, Erdem and Burberry all offered new twists on leopard print for the upcoming season.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/02/23/fall-2015-leopard-marc-jacobs-erdem-burberry/', 'snippet': 'Marc Jacobs, Erdem and Burberry all offered new twists on leopard print for the upcoming season.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The virtues of leopard print as a neutral are undersung. It goes with everything and is almost always in fashion — decade after decade, the print continues to find relevance, from Bettie Page’s midcentury pin-up swimsuits to Kate Moss’s signature vintage leopard coat. For fall/winter 2015, designers are revisiting leopard in new ways. First, in New York, Marc Jacobs used the print as trim on the collar and pockets of a metallic belted jacket, as well as on a matching bag. Across the pond at Erdem, the designer showed a ladylike leopard skirt suit, in homage to his Hitchcockian muses. Lastly, at Burberry, a demure midcalf-length leopard coat was toughened up with a built-in harness — Page would approve.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/23/t-magazine/23trend-leo