 Kakutani', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michiko', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kakutani', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/de5729d4-f113-51e0-8c01-5bb652929bb6', 'word_count': 754, 'uri': 'nyt://article/de5729d4-f113-51e0-8c01-5bb652929bb6'}, {'abstract': 'Before Sunday night, Polish movies had been nominated for best foreign language film nine times but never won an Academy Award.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/02/24/movies/as-ida-wins-an-oscar-poland-ends-a-losing-streak.html', 'snippet': 'Before Sunday night, Polish movies had been nominated for best foreign language film nine times but never won an Academy Award.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WARSAW — The utter tenacity with which the director Pawel Pawlikowski talked and talked and refused to be shooed off stage by the Oscar orchestra has been matched only by the Polish film industry’s own persistent, decades-long pursuit of international recognition.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/24/arts/23IDA/23IDA-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 515, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/02/24/arts/23IDA/23IDA-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 515}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/24/arts/23IDA/23IDA-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 879, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/24/arts/23IDA/23IDA-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1758, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption