as been a movie (directed by and starring Robert De Niro) and a Broadway solo show (directed by the Tony Award winner Jerry Zaks). Now it’s coming back again as a musical – with Mr. De Niro and Mr. Zaks teaming up as directors. The Paper Mill Playhouse in Millburn, N.J., announced on Monday that the world premiere of “A Bronx Tale” musical will be one of five shows in its 2015-16 season, running Feb. 4-March 6, 2016. “A Bronx Tale” features music by the Tony winner Alan Menken (“Newsies”), lyrics by Glenn Slater, and a book by Mr. Palminteri (who will not be a member of the cast this time around); Sergio Trujillo is the choreographer.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/24/arts/23artsbeat-chazz1/23artsbeat-chazz1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 389, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/02/24/arts/23artsbeat-chazz1/23artsbeat-chazz1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 389}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/24/arts/23artsbeat-chazz1/23artsbeat-chazz1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 665, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/24/arts/23artsbeat-chazz1/23artsbeat-chazz1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1329, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/24/arts/23artsbeat-chazz1/23artsbeat-chazz1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/02/24/arts/23artsbeat-chazz1/23artsbeat-chazz1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/24/arts/23artsbeat-chazz1/23artsbeat-chazz1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': '‘A Bronx Tale’ Musical to Debut at Paper Mill Playhouse in New Jersey', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Palminteri, Chazz', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Paper Mill Playhouse', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-02-24T00:05:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Patrick Healy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Patrick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Healy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c79bd467-359e-506b-a813-27abeb7babe1', 'word_count': 236, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c79bd467-359e-506b-a813-27abeb7babe1'}, {'abstract': 'The photographer’s work was made famous by Marlboro and Richard Prince. The photographer himself? Not so much.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/02/23/magazine/jim-krantzs-wild-west.html', 'snippet': 'The photographer’s work was made famous by Marlboro and Richard Prince. The photographer himself? Not so much.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Chicago-based commercial photographer Jim Krantz’s work has been famous in the art world for years. Krantz himself has been less so — a fact that perhaps requires some explanation. In the 1990s, Krantz, who had been documenting the cinematic vistas of the American West and its people with his camera for 20 years, went to Texas to photograph cowboys for a Marlboro advertising campaign. The final product caught the eye of Richard Prince, the “appropriation artist” who had achieved renown by photographing ads and presenting the resulting images in galleries and museums. Beginning in the 1980s, Prince reproduced images from Marlboro ads for his “Cowboys” series. One such print, at the time of its sale in 2005, was the most expensive photograph ever sold at auction.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/23/magazine/23mag-look-krantz-slide-53GR/23mag-look-krantz-slide-53GR-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 399, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/02/23/magazine/23mag-look-krantz-slide-53GR/23mag-look-krantz-slide-53GR-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 399}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/23/magazine/23mag-look-krantz-slide-53GR/23mag-look-krantz-slide-53GR-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/23/magazine/23mag-look-krantz-slide-53GR/23mag-look-krantz-slide-53GR-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1363, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/23/magazine/23mag-look-krantz-slide-53GR/23mag-look-krantz-slide-53GR-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/02/23/magazine/23mag-look-krantz-slide-53GR/23mag-look-krantz-slide-53GR-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/23/maga