ject', 'value': 'Memorabilia and Souvenirs', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Therapy and Rehabilitation', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Harvey, Matt', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Parnell, Bobby', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Mets', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-02-24T02:54:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tim Rohan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tim', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rohan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/700f3623-9c2d-5216-a10b-4fd99dbcc348', 'word_count': 997, 'uri': 'nyt://article/700f3623-9c2d-5216-a10b-4fd99dbcc348'}, {'abstract': 'The new owners of the Pawtucket Red Sox, a Class AAA team that has sent many future stars to the majors, said they intended to move the club to Providence.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/02/24/sports/baseball/rhode-island-city-may-lose-its-red-sox-and-mayor-says-its-heart.html', 'snippet': 'The new owners of the Pawtucket Red Sox, a Class AAA team that has sent many future stars to the majors, said they intended to move the club to Providence.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For decades, the Pawtucket Red Sox have been a minor league team as familiar to baseball fans as the Toledo Mud Hens, the Memphis Redbirds, the Durham Bulls or the Birmingham Barons. Playing at McCoy Stadium, which opened during World War II, the Rhode Island team, commonly known as the PawSox, has sent future stars such as Jim Rice, Carlton Fisk, Nomar Garciaparra, Roger Clemens, Mo Vaughn and Jacoby Ellsbury to the big club in Boston.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'cre