rkets, according to interviews with lawyers and a review of federal records. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Morning Agenda: Power Couple Ties Up S.E.C.', 'kicker': 'News', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2015-02-24T12:13:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Blogs', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sydney Ember', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sydney', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ember', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/050950d7-c26b-5aa1-bdf3-cf53f2e5fbed', 'word_count': 1941, 'uri': 'nyt://article/050950d7-c26b-5aa1-bdf3-cf53f2e5fbed'}, {'abstract': 'Rahm Emanuel did not receive enough votes to win a second term as mayor outright, so he will face Jesus Garcia, who took second place, on April 7.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/02/25/us/politics/chicago-votes-on-giving-rahm-emanuel-a-second-term-as-mayor.html', 'snippet': 'Rahm Emanuel did not receive enough votes to win a second term as mayor outright, so he will face Jesus Garcia, who took second place, on April 7.', 'lead_paragraph': 'CHICAGO — Rahm Emanuel, who was easily elected mayor of this city four years ago, was dealt a setback Tuesday. Though he came in first among five candidates, Mr. Emanuel failed to seal a second term by winning support from enough voters to avoid a riskier runoff election this spring.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/25/us/CHICAGO-sub/CHICAGO-sub-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 390, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/02/25/us/CHICAGO-sub/CHICAGO-sub-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlarge