st customers.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Deutsche Bank Hires Hewlett-Packard to Upgrade Systems', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Banking and Financial Institutions', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Hewlett-Packard Company', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Deutsche Bank AG', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Frankfurt (Germany)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-02-24T13:52:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'DealBook', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jack Ewing', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jack', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ewing', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/83ba4b2c-a9b6-5374-ab4a-559113108978', 'word_count': 346, 'uri': 'nyt://article/83ba4b2c-a9b6-5374-ab4a-559113108978'}, {'abstract': 'Despite economic concerns, Europeans have a number things going in their favor, including generally being happier people, private equity leaders say.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/02/25/business/dealbook/private-equity-leaders-make-case-for-european-investments.html', 'snippet': 'Despite economic concerns, Europeans have a number things going in their favor, including generally being happier people, private equity leaders say.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BERLIN — Private equity leaders made their case on Tuesday for investing in Europe despite concerns about the region’s economy and a potential exit by Greece from the eurozone.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Private Equity Leaders Make Case for European Investments', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Private Equity Leaders Make Case for European Investments', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Cinven Ltd', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Europe', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Private Equity', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-02-24T13:59:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'DealBook', 'byline': {'original': 'By Chad Bray', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Chad', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bray', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6a687c8c-2502-5c0d-8efd-83924cc93a5d', 'word_count': 350, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6a687c8c-2502-5c0d-8efd-83924cc93a5d'}, {'abstract': 'From new rinks for skating and, yes, curling, and even ice biking, to ice festivals, the city is enjoying its cold weather.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/03/01/travel/buffalo-embraces-winters-chill.html', 'snippet': 'From new rinks for skating and, yes, curling, and even ice biking, to ice festivals, the city is enjoying its cold weather.', 'lead_paragraph': 'At Buffalo’s newest outdoor rink, Canalside, teenage couples skated hand in hand, while a few stumbling toddlers nearly pulled their parents down. From a pedestrian bridge above the ice, spectators drank Flying Bison beer and bit into hot sandwiches from nearby food trucks. Stereos pumped Bob Marley, although the tropical beat belied the 20-degree temperatures. All around the double-sized rink, market vendors under striped awnings sold jewelry, hockey sticks and sweatshirts printed with “We Made Snow Famous” and “Buffalonians Never Say Die.”', 'print_section': 'TR', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'ra