rint_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Elliott Management Corp', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Juniper Networks Inc', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Shareholder Rights and Activism', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Singer, Paul E', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-02-24T14:46:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'DealBook', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael J. de la Merced', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'de la Merced', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0e453589-43f3-544b-b8ab-ab3ad9ff5e6b', 'word_count': 227, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0e453589-43f3-544b-b8ab-ab3ad9ff5e6b'}, {'abstract': 'There is so much effort and love in all these packages; so much support in all the inquiries. It’s shocking, humbling and fantastic.', 'web_url': 'https://parenting.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/02/24/an-outpouring-of-love-and-onesies/', 'snippet': 'There is so much effort and love in all these packages; so much support in all the inquiries. It’s shocking, humbling and fantastic.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Possibly because I’m a guy, I never really thought too hard about giving people baby gifts. It was just something that did not often cross my mind. When one of my friends or family members said that they were having a baby, I might have halfheartedly found them something off their registry that wasn’t too cheap, or just sent them a gift card, figuring that they may need it for diapers. If I found myself cruising the baby aisles of Target, it tended to be so overwhelming that I found the first age-appropriate toy I could, whether I thought the child could use it or not. Let’s just say that gift receipts were key.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/24/us/motherlode-joelwords/motherlode-joelwords-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 800, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/02/24/us/motherlode-joelwords/motherlode-joelwords-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 800}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/24/us/motherlode-joelwords/motherlode-joelwords-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 768, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/24/us/motherlode-joelwords/motherlode-joelwords-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1536, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/24/us/motherlode-joelwords/motherlode-joelwords-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/02/24/us/motherlode-joelwords/motherlode-joelwords-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/24/us/motherlode-joelwords/motherlode-joelwords-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'An Outpouring of Love and Onesies', 'kicker': 'Motherlode', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Babies and Infants', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parenting', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-02-24T14:48:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Styles', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Joel Keller', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Joel', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Keller', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8f20787b-3eb7-55ae-bb2c-ca0fe8b23266', 'word_count': 773, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8f20787b-3eb7-55ae-bb2c-ca0fe8b23266'}, {'abstract': 'Highlights from the International Herald Tribune archives: A dam near Prescott, Ariz., burst causing major damage in 1890.', 'web_url': 'https://iht-retrospective.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/02/24/1890-arizonas-catastrophe/', 'snippet': 'Highlights from the International Herald Tribune archives: A dam near Prescott, Ariz., burst causing major damage in 1890.', 'lead_paragraph': 'NEW YORK — The disaster at the dam on the Hassayampa River, near Prescott, Arizona, is the most fearful catastrophe in the history of the territory. The valley for miles below the dam was swept clean. The first intimation of the appalling disaster was a sound resembling thunder, and at the same instant a perpendicular wall of water, fully 50 feet high, came rushing down the narrow valley. The valley widens above Wickenburg, and much of the town lies upon lowlands close to the course of the stream, and it was almost certain that the vast body of water which rushed out of the reservoir had carried away many houses at that place. — The New York Herald, European Edition, Feb. 25, 1890', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/25/blogs/25iht-oldfeb25-arizona/25iht-oldfeb25-arizona-jumbo.png', 'height': 847, 'width': 512, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'image