e Voice celebrates the women he knew but is less forthcoming about major figures in the early years of rock.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/02/25/books/review-robert-christgau-reflects-on-his-career-as-a-rock-critic.html', 'snippet': 'A memoir by an authority on popular music who spent three decades with The Village Voice celebrates the women he knew but is less forthcoming about major figures in the early years of rock.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Here’s a cardinal rule of book criticism: Never blame someone for writing a book that’s different from the one you wanted him to write. But Robert Christgau’s memoir, “Going Into the City: Portrait of a Critic as a Young Man,” is so far from what I wanted that I can’t pretend I’m not crestfallen. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/25/arts/25christgaujacket/25christgaujacket-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 883, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/02/25/arts/25christgaujacket/25christgaujacket-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 883}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/25/arts/25christgaujacket/25christgaujacket-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 697, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/25/arts/25christgaujacket/25christgaujacket-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1393, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/25/arts/25christgaujacket/25christgaujacket-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_