tive Son,” which was published 75 years ago.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Each week in Bookends, two writers take on questions about the world of books. This week, Ayana Mathis and Pankaj Mishra discuss James Baldwin’s reaction to Richard Wright’s “Native Son,” which was published 75 years ago.', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '31', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/03/01/books/review/01bookends-promo/01bookends-promo-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 296, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/03/01/books/review/01bookends-promo/01bookends-promo-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 296}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/03/01/books/review/01bookends-promo/01bookends-promo-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 504, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/03/01/books/review/01bookends-promo/01bookends-promo-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 600, 'width': 1218, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/03/01/books/review/01bookends-promo/01bookends-promo-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/03/01/books/review/01bookends-promo/01bookends-promo-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/03/01/books/review/01bookends-promo/01bookends-promo-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'James Baldwin Denounced Richard Wright’s ‘Native Son’ As a ‘Protest Novel.’ Was He Right?', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'James Baldwin Denounced Richard Wright’s ‘Native Son’ as a ‘Protest Novel.’ Was He Right?', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mathis, Ayana', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mishra, Pankaj', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wright, Richard', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Writing and Writers', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Baldwin, James (1924-87)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-02-24T15:00:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'BookReview', 'section_name': 'Books', 'subsection_name': 'Book Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ayana Mathis and Pankaj Mishra', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ayana', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mathis', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Pankaj', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mishra', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1a1852de-26c4-56be-b223-d08619de2e1e', 'word_count': 1495, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1a1852de-26c4-56be-b223-d08619de2e1e'}, {'abstract': 'Highlights from the International Herald Tribune archives: A state of siege is declared in Guatemala as guerrillas clash with the government in 1965.', 'web_url': 'https://iht-retrospective.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/02/24/1965-state-of-siege-is-declared/', 'snippet': 'Highlights from the International Herald Tribune archives: A state of siege is declared in Guatemala as guerrillas clash with the government in 1965.', 'lead_paragraph': 'GUATEMALA CITY — Col. Enrique Peralta Azurdia’s government suspended the constitution and decreed a state of siege throughout Guatemala today [Feb. 24] because of what was called an attempt to overthrow his regime. Col. Peralta said ‘‘several groups of armed men have attacked civilians and authorities as part of a widespread plan to spread terror.’’ The national radio broadcast the state of siege decree, saying that it would be in effect as long as necessary. There was no immediate information as to who the plotters Col. Peralta referred to might be. — New York Herald Tribune, European Edition, Feb. 25, 1965', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '1965: State of Siege Is Declared', 'kicker': 'IHT Retrospective', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Constitutions', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': "Coups D'Etat and Attempted Coups D'Etat", 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Guatemala', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-02-24T15:00:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By International Herald Tribune', 'person': [{'firstname': 'International', 'middlename': 'Herald', 'lastname': 'Tribune', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f26bf38a-2df6-596c-a3cb-b3bf7139d7bc', 'word_count': 101, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f26bf38a-2df6-596c-a3cb-b3bf7139d7bc'}, {'abstract': 'The exact number of hostages seized remained unclear, with estimates ranging from several dozen to more than 100.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/02/25/world/middleeast/monitoring-group-says-isis-has-abducted-90-christians-in-syria.html', 'snippet': 'The exact number of hostages seized remained unclear, with estimates ranging from several dozen to more than 100.', 'lead_parag