{'abstract': 'Robert Christgau, best known for his 37 years of short-form rock music reviews for The Village Voice, releases “Going Into the City” today.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/02/24/memoir-going-into-the-city-by-robert-christgau/', 'snippet': 'Robert Christgau, best known for his 37 years of short-form rock music reviews for The Village Voice, releases “Going Into the City” today.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As the half-jokingly self-designated Dean of American Rock Critics, Robert Christgau has appeared to readers in bite-size chunks for well over four decades. Throughout his storied career — he is best known for his 35 years as a rock critic and editor at The Village Voice, where he founded the annual Pazz & Jop poll and perfected the letter-graded rock album capsule review — Christgau’s name has become synonymous with pith; the album reviews he has written regularly since 1969 rarely exceed 150 words. (Christgau says he must have cribbed the format from the longtime New York Daily News writer Kay Gardella, but claims to be “the inventor of the good capsule review.”) The memoir he releases today, then, represents new territory in more ways than one; and on the phone to discuss it, the famously cantankerous Christgau is in a good mood.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/24/t-magazine/24christgau-hafford-1/24christgau-hafford-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 800, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/02/24/t-magazine/24christgau-hafford-1/24christgau-hafford-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 800}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/24/t-magazine/24christgau-hafford-1/24christgau-hafford-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 768, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/24/t-magazine/24christgau-hafford-1/24christgau-hafford-1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1056, 'width': 792, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/24/t-magazine/24christgau-hafford-1/24christgau-hafford-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/02/24/t-magazine/24christgau-hafford-1/24christgau-hafford-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/24/t-magazine/24christgau-hafford-1/24christgau-hafford-1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'In a New Memoir, the Famously Pithy ‘Dean of American Rock Critics’ Goes Long', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Rock Music', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Christgau, Robert', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rosen, Jody', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Daily News', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Village Voice', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Brooklyn (NYC)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-02-24T18:00:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael Hafford', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname