ident is a Christian?', 'lead_paragraph': 'Thrice in the past few weeks, Scott Walker, the Wisconsin governor and presumptive candidate for president, has delivered a non-answer to a prodding question:\xa0First on whether he believes in evolution, second on whether he would disassociate himself from Rudy Giuliani’s (since half-retracted) impugning of President Obama’s patriotism, and then finally on whether he believes the\xa0president\xa0is a Christian.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The “Is Obama Christian?” Question', 'kicker': 'Ross Douthat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2016', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Clinton, Hillary Rodham', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Giuliani, Rudolph W', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Huckabee, Mike', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kierkegaard, Soren', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Walker, Scott K', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Democratic Party', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-02-24T22:35:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ross Douthat', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ross', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Douthat', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f212e6d7-6997-54a3-8f3e-2509ad28cb95', 'word_count': 1747, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f212e6d7-6997-54a3-8f3