rement that parents sign a consent form before a Jewish ritual that has been linked to herpes infections in infants.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/02/25/nyregion/de-blasio-set-to-waive-rule-requiring-consent-form-for-circumcision-ritual.html', 'snippet': 'Under pressure from ultra-Orthodox leaders, New York City is seeking to waive a requirement that parents sign a consent form before a Jewish ritual that has been linked to herpes infections in infants.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The administration of Mayor Bill de Blasio, under pressure from ultra-Orthodox rabbis, is set to ease New York City’s regulations on a controversial circumcision ritual that has been linked to herpes infections in infants. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '19', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Mayor de Blasio Is Set to Ease Rules on Circumcision Ritual', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'De Blasio Set to Waive Rule Requiring Consent Form for Circumcision Ritual', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Jews and Judaism', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Circumcision', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Herpes Viruses', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'de Blasio, Bill', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-02-25T02:44:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael M. Grynbaum', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d4cb46a2-7ada-5f08-847f-690d093220bc', 'word_count': 645, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d4cb46a2-7ada-5f08-847f-690d093220bc'}, {'abstract': 'Human Rights Watch said Tuesday that the Syrian government had dropped so-called barrel bombs on hundreds of heavily populated rebel-held areas in the past year, flouting a United Nations Security Council measure.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/02/25/world/middleeast/syria-dropped-barrel-bombs-despite-ban-report-says.html', 'snippet': 'Human Rights Watch said Tuesday that the Syrian government had dropped so-called barrel bombs on hundreds of heavily populated rebel-held areas in the past year, flouting a United Nations Security Council measure.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Human Rights Watch said Tuesday that the Syrian government had dropped so-called barrel bombs on hundreds of sites in rebel-held towns and cities in the past year, flouting a United Nations Security Council measure. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Syria Dropped ‘Barrel Bombs’ Despite Ban, Report Says', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Syria: Rights Group Reports on Use of ‘Barrel Bombs’ by Assad Forces', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Syria', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bombs and Explosives', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Human Rights Watch', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Human Rights and Human Rights Violations', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United Nations', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'War Crimes, Genocide and Crimes Against Humanity', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-02-25T02:49:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Somini Sengupta', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Somini', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sengupta', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d22c6e80-7529-5f75-96ca-fbead091d03f', 'word_count': 269, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d22c6e80-7529-5f75-96ca-fbead091d03f'}, {'abstract': 'The new rule, which mainly affects workers from some Asian countries who have applied for permanent resident green cards, added to a debate over President Obama’s executive actions.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/02/25/us/rule-change-sought-by-tech-firms-will-allow-some-spouses-of-immigrants-to-work.html', 'snippet': 'The new rule, which mainly affects workers from some Asian countries who have applied for permanent resident green cards, added to a debate over President Obama’s executive actions.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Obama administration said on Tuesday that it will give work permits to some spouses of highly skilled immigrants who are in the United States on temporary visas, a change long sought by technology companies and other businesses that is part of a series of controversial executive actions by the president.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Rule Change Sought by Tech Firms Will Allow Some Spouses of Immigrants to Work', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Rule Change Sought by Tech Firms Will Allow Some Spouses of Immigrants to Work', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Foreign Workers', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Preston, Julia', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Immigration and Emigration', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Visas', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Executive Orders and Memorandums', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-02-25T02:49:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Julia Preston', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Julia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Preston', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4e431839-83c3-5ed4-9166-483e5dadf663', 'word_count': 705, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4e431839-83c3-5ed4-9166-483e5dadf663'}, {'abstract': 'More than once, Andy Partridge set his mind to proposing to his childhood friend Mandy Hicks, but the moment was always ruined by other couples — until the pair went on an eagle watch in Upper Manhattan.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/02/25/nyregion/with-eagles-sighted-a-proposal-takes-flight.html', 'snippet': 'More than once, Andy Partridge set his mind to proposing to his childhood friend Mandy Hicks, but the moment was always ruined by other couples — until the pair went on an eagle watch in Upper Manhattan.', 'lead_paragraph': 'At midlife, Mandy Hicks and Andy Partridge, childhood friends from North Yorkshire, England, struck up a romance. To celebrate her 52nd birthday last week, they made their first visit to New York, in time for some of the coldest weather on record. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/25/nyregion/ABOUT/ABOUT-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/02/25/nyregion/ABOUT/ABOUT-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/25/nyregion/ABOUT/ABOUT-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'