orture and mistreatment of people arrested for conflict-related activities points to a continued challenge for the new government.', 'lead_paragraph': 'KABUL, Afghanistan — The torture and mistreatment of people arrested for conflict-related activities remain widespread in Afghan prisons, the United Nations said in a report released on Wednesday, pointing to a continued challenge for the nation’s new government.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Prisoner Abuse Still Widespread in Afghanistan, U.N. Says ', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Prisoner Abuse Still Widespread in Afghanistan, U.N. Says', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Afghanistan War (2001-14)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ahmed, Azam', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'AFGHANISTAN', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United Nations', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Torture', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Human Rights and Human Rights Violations', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-02-25T12:57:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Azam Ahmed', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Azam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ahmed', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d7954182-96e3-54bb-8623-cf326041f4df', 'word_count': 720, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d7954182-96e3-54bb-8623-cf326041f4df'}, {'abstract': 'Ms. Moss is returning to Broadway, portraying a successful professional wondering if she can have it all in this 1988 Tony Award- and Pulitzer Prize-winning play.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/03/01/theater/elisabeth-moss-a-career-woman-in-the-heidi-chronicles.html', 'snippet': 'Ms. Moss is returning to Broadway, portraying a successful professional wondering if she can have it all in this 1988 Tony Award- and Pulitzer Prize-winning play.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Elisabeth Moss’s mint-colored dressing room, on the second floor of the Music Box Theater, has a wall of windows that face the Gerald Schoenfeld Theater across 45th Street. “The Audience” is playing there now, and as Ms. Moss sat, dressed in sweatpants and scarfing down a half-frozen egg salad sandwich, the steely eyes of Helen Mirren, who stars as Queen Elizabeth II, glared at her from the opposite marquee. ', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/03/01/arts/01ELISABETH1/01ELISABETH1-articleLarge-v3.jpg', 'height': 800, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/03/01/arts/01ELISABETH1/01ELISABETH1-articleLarge-v3.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 800}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/03/01/arts/01ELISABETH1/01ELISABETH1-jumbo-v3.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 768, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/03/01/arts/01ELISABETH1/01ELISABETH1-superJumbo-v3.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1536, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/03/01/arts/01ELISABETH1/01ELISABETH1-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/03/01/arts/01ELISABETH1/01ELISABETH1-thumbStandard-v3.jpg