: 'Quentin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hardy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e9090c73-a8c6-5a89-91d6-698ec56104af', 'word_count': 494, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e9090c73-a8c6-5a89-91d6-698ec56104af'}, {'abstract': 'Highlights from the International Herald Tribune archives: British to sacrifice shirt-tails in 1940.', 'web_url': 'https://iht-retrospective.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/02/25/1940-british-to-sacrifice-shirt-tails/', 'snippet': 'Highlights from the International Herald Tribune archives: British to sacrifice shirt-tails in 1940.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON — British shirt-tails, noted for their length, must be sacrificed to the national welfare and curtailed for the duration of the war, according to Herbert Kay, Secretary of the Shirt Manufacturers’ Federation of Great Britain. The current demand for army overalls is absorbing a large proportion of the available cotton, he explained. ‘‘I don’t think it will come to such a drastic step as tailless shirts,’’ Mr. Kay said. ‘‘But the problem has to be solved somehow.’’ — New York Herald Tribune, European Edition, Feb. 26, 1940', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '1940: British to Sacrifice Shirt-Tails', 'kicker': 'IHT Retrospective', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Uniforms', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'World War II (1939-45)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Great Britain', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-02-25T15:05:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By International Herald Tribune', 'person': [{'firstname': 'International', 'middlen