 'The Moment', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Men and Boys', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McQueen, Alexander', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'van Noten, Dries', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Gucci Group NV', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Lanvin', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Louis Vuitton', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-02-25T15:30:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By T Magazine', 'person': [{'firstname': '', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2a9749b2-832c-5298-9969-a6ad72e97bcc', 'word_count': 15, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2a9749b2-832c-5298-9969-a6ad72e97bcc'}, {'abstract': 'By means of a nasty cyberattack, my three Sudan-related websites became unusable to all who visited my Facebook page on February 21, 2014. I believe the Khartoum (Sudan) regime is responsible.', 'web_url': 'https://kristof.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/02/25/i-have-been-silenced/', 'snippet': 'By means of a nasty cyberattack, my three Sudan-related websites became unusable to all who visited my Facebook page on February 21, 2014. I believe the Khartoum (Sudan) regime is responsible.', 'lead_paragraph': 'By means of a nasty cyberattack, my three Sudan-related websites became unusable to all who visited my Facebook page on February 21, 2014. I believe the Khartoum (Sudan) regime is responsible. Many Facebook visitors subsequently going to my Sudan sites immediately found innumerable and highly aggressive “pop-up” ads. Nothing could be accessed, by me or by my 1,200+ Facebook “friends,” mainly Sudanese from both Sudan and South Sudan. They had received as a “message” from me pornographic videography (purportedly including me) containing potent malware; the message was sent to both my daughters as well as other family members. Other visitors experienced various difficulties and anomalies in accessing their own Facebook page; other consequences may as yet be undiscovered (my computer has been behaving very peculiarly since then, and is now with technicians).', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'I Have Been Silenced', 'kicker': 'Nicholas Kristof', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Embargoes and Sanctions', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bashir, Omar Hassan Al-', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Facebook Inc', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Darfur (Sudan)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-02-25T15:40:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Eric Reeves', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Eric', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Reeves', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a13b6757-95c4-500f-b976-a1dd42fadada', 'word_count': 733, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a13b6757-95c4-500f-b976-a1dd42fadada'}, {'abstract': 'My college freshman’s summer plans are keeping her up nights. If she fails to earn a spot supplying free labor, she might have to resort to a paid job.', 'web_url': 'https://parenting.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/02/25/the-internship-that-looks-good-vs-the-job-that-pays/', 'snippet': 'My college freshman’s summer plans are keeping her up nights. If she fails to earn a spot supplying free labor, she might have to resort to a paid job.', 'lead_paragraph': 'My daughter, a college freshman, is stressed — but not about her coursework. What’s keeping her up at night is her summer plan: specifically, landing the perfect unpaid internship. She is worried that if she fails to earn a spot supplying free labor, she may have to resort to earning several thousand dollars as a camp counselor. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/25/us/motherlode-intern-words2/motherlode-intern-words2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 416, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/02/25/us/motherlode-intern-words2/motherlode-intern-words2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 416}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/25/us/motherlode-intern-words2/motherlode-intern-words2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 554, 'width': 800, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/25/us/motherlode-intern-words2/motherlode-intern-words2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 554, 'width': 800, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/25/us/motherlode-intern-words2/motherlode-intern-words2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/02/25/us/motherlode-intern-words2/motherlode-intern-words2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/25/us/motherlode-intern-words2/motherlode-intern-words2-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'th