’s Less-Than-Stellar Plan to Bolster Earnings', 'kicker': 'Breakingviews', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'JPMorgan Chase’s Less-Than-Stellar Plan to Bolster Earnings', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Banking and Financial Institutions', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'JPMorgan Chase & Company', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Dimon, James', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lake, Marianne', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-02-25T17:07:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dealbook', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'DealBook', 'byline': {'original': 'By Antony Currie', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Antony', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Currie', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/51459911-3823-5ff6-835d-f8bdea30724e', 'word_count': 356, 'uri': 'nyt://article/51459911-3823-5ff6-835d-f8bdea30724e'}, {'abstract': 'Highlights from the International Herald Tribune archives: U.S. jets hit Viet Cong in 1965.', 'web_url': 'https://iht-retrospective.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/02/25/1965-u-s-jets-hit-viet-cong/', 'snippet': 'Highlights from the International Herald Tribune archives: U.S. jets hit Viet Cong in 1965.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SAIGON — U.S. Air Force jets bearing secret antipersonnel weapons today blasted Viet Cong ambush positions north and east of Saigon. Sixteen of the jets hammered Viet Cong positions in the Mang Yang Pass, about 280 miles north of Saigon, to help out an ambushed Special Forces company. The pass is on a road between Pleiku and Qui Nhon, both the scene of recent terrorist attacks on U.S. installations. The guerrillas have severed the main road from coastal Qui Nhon to the Cambodian-Laotian frontier in a dozen places in an evident effort to knock out all of central Vietnam. ‘‘I don’t think we’ll ever get the road open,’’ a U.S. Engineer officer said. ‘‘The main difficulty is getting in there to repair it.’’ — New York Herald Tribune, European Edition, Feb. 26, 1965', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '1965: U.S. Jets Hit Viet Cong', 'kicker': 'IHT Retrospective', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Vietnam War', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United States Air Force', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-02-25T17:07:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By International Herald Tribune', 'person': [{'firstname': 'International', 'middlename': 'Herald', 'lastname': 'Tribune', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/907fe5fa-f58c-560a-b633-89d880fdfa46', 'word_count': 133, 'uri': 'nyt://article/907fe5fa-f58c-560a-b633-89d880fdfa46'}, {'abstract': 'It’s hip for the fashion crowd to hate the city, but some fans are trying to change opinions.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/02/26/fashion/cheerleading-for-milan-fashion-week-2015.html', 'snippet': 'It’s hip for the fashion crowd to hate the city, but some fans are trying to change opinions.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MILAN — Twice a year (four times for the durable souls who cover both men’s and women’s collections), international fashion professionals in pack formation wend their way to Milan, the home base of the Italian fashion industry. For many of these visitors, it is a trip accepted with the grim resignation that typically accompanies dental visits. Complaints, never absent from the industry even at its most celebratory, rise to a crescendo. The cause of consternation: Gray, unbeautiful, unwelcoming Milan.', 'print_section': 'E', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/26/fashion/26fmilan-A/26fmilan-A-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 387, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/02/26/fashion/26fmilan-A/26fmilan-A-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 387}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/26/fashion/26fmilan-A/26fmilan-A-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 661, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/26/fashion/26fmilan-A/26fmilan-A-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1322, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/26/fashion/26fmilan-A/26fmilan-A-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/02/26/fashion/26fmilan-A/26fmilan-A-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/26/fashion/26fmilan-A/26fmilan-A-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Cheerleading for Milan', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'In Milan, Winning Over the City’s Doubters', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Schneier, Matthew', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Milan Fashion Week', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Milan (Italy)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Martin, J J', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-02-25T17:16:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Styles', 'section_name': 'Fashion & Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Matthew Schneier', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Matthew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schneier', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/30debca7-2fa5-5635-bd54-af16459a74fa', 'word_count': 1030, 'uri': 'nyt://article/30debca7-2fa5-5635-bd54-af16459a74fa'}, {'abstract': 'Liz Alderman, the chief European business correspondent for the International New York Times, reflects on the Greek economic crisis.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/times-insider/2015/02/25/reflections-on-the-greek-economic-crisis-reporters-notebook/', 'snippet': 'Liz Alderman, the chief European business correspondent for the International New York Times, reflects on the Greek economic crisis.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I’ve been writing about the economic and political crisis in Greece since 2012, when it looked as if the country might exit the euro monetary union if a young leftist maverick politician, Alexis Tsipras, came to power during a pivotal double-election that was being held that summer. He lost, just barely. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/25/blogs/Greece2/Greece2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 441, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/02/25/blogs/Greece2/Greece2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 441}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/25/blogs/Greece2/Greece2-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 753, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_na