ng', 'height': 446, 'width': 533, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/25/travel/36-hours-lake-tahoe-interactive-map-1424887176028/36-hours-lake-tahoe-interactive-map-1424887176028-thumbStandard.png', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/02/25/travel/36-hours-lake-tahoe-interactive-map-1424887176028/36-hours-lake-tahoe-interactive-map-1424887176028-thumbStandard.png', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/25/travel/36-hours-lake-tahoe-interactive-map-1424887176028/36-hours-lake-tahoe-interactive-map-1424887176028-thumbLarge.png', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': '36 Hours in Lake Tahoe', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Maps', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Lake Tahoe (Nev)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-02-25T18:11:09+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Travel', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Interactive Feature', '_id': 'nyt://interactive/b27aae04-352c-5b4a-8df7-0b17fb7459f7', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://interactive/b27aae04-352c-5b4a-8df7-0b17fb7459f7'}, {'abstract': 'The cobalt blue lake straddling California and Nevada offers cowboy-chic in the north, casinos and clubs in the south, and plenty of skiing in between.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/03/01/travel/what-to-do-in-36-hours-lake-tahoe.html', 'snippet': 'The cobalt blue lake straddling California and Nevada offers cowboy-chic in the north, casinos and clubs in the south, and plenty of skiing in between.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Straddling the Nevada-California border, Lake Tahoe’s immense cobalt blue oval — unfrozen thanks to the lake’s depth — stands out against the snow-covered mountains like a colossal eye staring into heaven. This May, Tahoe’s wilderness will be even more accessible with JetBlue beginning daily direct flights between J.F.K. and Reno-Tahoe International Airport. The lake’s vastness can be absorbed only by being there — or better yet, skiing the dozen resorts surrounding it, their trails like frozen white waterfalls cutting through the fir-lined mountains. Lake Tahoe has two distinctive areas: the north side, where cowboy-chic cabins and semi-isolated shops and cafes overlook a quiet shoreline; and South Tahoe, which glitters with casinos, clubs and a slew of new upscale boutique hotels hovering above the lake. Skiing both sides in one weekend is an ambitious undertaking, but the lake’s wilderness spirit and surprising contrasts are compelling enough to pull you into its adventurous orbit.', 'print_section': 'TR', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '36 Hours in Lake Tahoe', 'kicker': '36 Hours', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jones, Finn-Olaf', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Lake Tahoe (Nev)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Skiing', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Restaurants', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ALPINE SKIING', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Casinos', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-02-25T18:11:19+0000', 'document_ty