ample of his ability to state his case and stick to it.', 'lead_paragraph': 'DES MOINES — As Gov. Scott Walker of Wisconsin struggled to respond to questions about the president’s patriotism and religion last week, some saw an unprepared presidential hopeful in the national glare — not ready for “the N.F.L.,” as one participant in a Sunday morning talk show put it.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/25/us/26WALKERweb/26WALKERweb-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 418, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/02/25/us/26WALKERweb/26WALKERweb-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 418}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/25/us/26WALKERweb/26WALKERweb-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 713, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/25/us/26WALKERweb/26WALKERweb-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1427, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/25/us/26WALKERweb/26WALKERweb-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/02/25/us/26WALKERweb/26WALKERweb-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/25/us/26WALKERweb/26WALKERweb-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'For Scott Walker, a Consistent Approach Under Tough Questioning', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Walker, Scott K', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2016', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Wisconsin', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-02-25T18:45:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Trip Gabriel', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Trip', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gabriel', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1bd39661-5ae4-5fdf-b103-6bc53759c069', 'word_count': 927, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1bd39661-5ae4-5fdf-b103-6bc53759c069'}, {'abstract': 'The movie-style attack near the Strait of Hormuz appeared to be a show of might and an expression of displeasure at the American presence in the region.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/02/26/world/middleeast/in-mock-attack-iranian-navy-blasts-away-at-replica-us-aircraft-carrier.html', 'snippet': 'The movie-style attack near the Strait of Hormuz appeared to be a show of might and an expression of displeasure at the American presence in the region.', 'lead_paragraph': 'TEHRAN — Iran’s navy may pale in comparison to that of the United States, but on Wednesday it inflicted serious damage on an American aircraft carrier — a mock-up of one, to be exact.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Iran’s Navy Blasts Away at a Mock U.S. Carrier', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Iran’s Navy Blasts Away at a Mock U.S. Carrier', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iran', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Nuclear Weapons', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Islamic Revolutionary Guards Corps', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Strait of Hormuz', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Aircraft Carriers', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-02-25T18:53:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Thomas Erdbrink', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Thomas', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Erdbrink', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/28a3b5ab-894a-539e-914e-1cd296abd376', 'word_count': 583, 'uri': 'nyt://article/28a3b5ab-894a-539e-914e-1cd296abd376'}, {'abstract': 'The hairstylist Guido Palau created a coiffure to match the designer’s romantic fall 2015 collection.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/02/25/alberta-ferretti-fall-2015-beauty/', 'snippet': 'The hairstylist Guido Palau created a coiffure to match the designer’s romantic fall 2015 collection.', 'lead_paragraph': '“Mrs. Ferretti loves romance, so there’s always that thing,” said the stylist Guido Palau backstage at the designer’s fashion show today in Milan. To add extra enchantment to the fall Alberta Ferretti runway, Palau used extensions to make sure the models had long, even strands, which he blow-dried simply and then arranged into a loose ponytail, achieved by pulling the elastic down to let the hair out around the face a little (as\xa0Orlando Pita did\xa0at Michael Kors). Like Ferretti’s new collection, the resulting coiffure has a flowing, classical quality that’s meant to enhance each ensemble. “It has a kind of purity to it, which is so Ferretti,” he said, “but it will have a slightly old-fashioned take which feels very right for this collection.” Palau also notes that the hairstyle hides the models’ ears, adding to its timeless appeal and giving it an “untouched” and “painterly” look.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/25/t-magazine/25beauty-ferretti/25beauty-ferretti-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 800, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/02/25/t-magazine/25beauty-ferretti/25beauty-ferretti-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 800}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/25/t-magazine/25beauty-ferretti/25beauty-ferretti-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 768, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/25/t-magazine/25beauty-ferretti/25beauty-ferretti-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1536, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/25/t-magazine/25beauty-ferretti/25beauty-ferretti-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/02/25/t-magazine/25beauty-ferretti/25beauty-ferretti-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/25/t-magazine/25beauty-ferretti/25beauty-ferretti-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Enchanting, Loose Ponytails at Alberta Ferretti', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Models (Professional)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ferretti, Alberta', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Palau, Guido', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Milan (Italy)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-02-25T19:00:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nathan Reese', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nathan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Reese', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/88cf5cf6-9598-5934-8f16-ebb41b52c84c', 'word_count': 190, 'uri': 'nyt://article/88cf5cf6-9598-5934-8f16-ebb41b52c84c'}, {'abstract': 'At 12:01 a.m. recreational marijuana will become semi-legal in the district .', 'web_url': 'https://takingnote.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/02/25/marijuana-legalizationnot-the-drug-itselfsows-confusion-in-d-c/', 'snippet': 'At 12:01 a.m. recreational marijuana will become semi-legal in the district .', 'lead_paragraph': 'At 12:01 a.m. on Thursday, recreational marijuana will become semi-legal in the District of Columbia under a patchwork blanket of no-go zones, threats of prosecution from congressional overseers and confusion about enforcement by overlapping city and federal police agencies. There won’t be any clouds of smoke, though. The pot law, approved by 70 percent of city voters last November, is so tightly restricted to home use that this social revolution may be largely invisible in the city at large.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Marijuana Legalization—Not the Drug Itself—Sows Confusion in D.C.', 'kicker': 'Taking Note', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Marijuana', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bowser, Muriel E', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Washington (DC)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-02-25T19:15:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Francis X. Clines', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Francis', 'middlename': 'X.', 'lastname': 'Clines', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/895de625-d7b1-5c11-a341-9b534bd04e03', 'word_count': 315, 'uri': 'nyt://article/895de625-d7b1-5c11-a341-9b534bd04e03'}, {'abstract': 'Mr. Draghi, president of the European Central Bank, said member countries might need to give up some independence and create more Pan-European institutions.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/02/26/business/mario-draghi-warns-of-risky-future-for-eurozone.html', 'snippet': 'Mr. Draghi, president of the European Central Bank, said member countries might need to give up some independence and create more Pan-European institutions.', 'lead_paragraph': 'FRANKFURT — In a contentious appearance before the European Parliament on Wednesday, the president of the European Central Bank said that the future of the eurozone was at risk unless member countries gave up some independence and created more Pan-European government institutions.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/26/business/26draghi-web/26draghi-web-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 395, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/02/26/business/26draghi-web/26draghi-web-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 395}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption'