'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/790db19e-8009-548a-8658-c6fe017927a3', 'word_count': 643, 'uri': 'nyt://article/790db19e-8009-548a-8658-c6fe017927a3'}, {'abstract': 'Two recent examples of anonymous quotation in The Times deserve notice.', 'web_url': 'https://publiceditor.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/02/25/anonywatch-on-port-authority-restrooms-and-jeb-bushs-adviser/', 'snippet': 'Two recent examples of anonymous quotation in The Times deserve notice.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I’d never want to stand in the way of someone fulfilling her ambitions, so I’m inclined to laugh — although it is a bitter laugh — about the most recent example of gratuitous anonymous quotation in The Times. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'AnonyWatch: On Port Authority Restrooms and Jeb Bush’s Adviser', 'kicker': 'The Public Editor&#039;s Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2015-02-25T19:25:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Margaret Sullivan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Margaret', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sullivan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c20582ef-17ad-5020-88d5-9fb012c92248', 'word_count': 505, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c20582ef-17ad-5020-88d5-9fb012c92248'}, {'abstract': 'In this Text to Text, we feature an Op-Ed written by Malcolm’s daughter Ilyasah Shabazz, in which she asks “What would Malcolm X think?” about today’s violence and activism. We pair it with an excerpt from one of Malcolm X’s final speeches, when he addresses many of these same issues.', 'web_url': 'https://learning.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/02/25/text-to-text-what-would-malcolm-x-think-and-after-the-bombing/', 'snippet': 'In this Text to Text, we feature an Op-Ed written by Malcolm’s daughter Ilyasah Shabazz, in which she asks “What would Malcolm X think?” about today’s violence and activism. We pair it with an excerpt from one of Malcolm X’s final speeches, when h...', 'lead_paragraph': 'Malcolm X was assassinated (PDF) 50 years ago this month, cutting short a powerful voice demanding justice and equality for African-Americans. When he died in 1965 there were still two Americas — one for whites and another for blacks. And while the nation has experienced a remarkable transformation in racial justice in the decades since his death, just in the past year we witnessed echoes of that stubborn divide with police shootings, protests and anger around St. Louis, New York City and elsewhere. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/21/opinion/21shabazzWEB-LN/21shabazzWEB-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 507, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/02/21/opinion/21shabazzWEB-LN/21shabazzWEB-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 507}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/21/opinion/21shabazzWEB-LN/21shabazzWEB-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 865, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/21/opinion/21shabazzWEB-LN/21shabazzWEB-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1730, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/21/opinion/21shabazzWEB-LN/21shabazzWEB-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/02/21/opinion/21shabazzWEB-LN/21shabazzWEB-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/21/opinion/21shabazzWEB-LN/21shabazzWEB-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Text to Text | ‘What Would Malcolm X Think?’ and ‘After the Bombing’', 'kicker': 'The Learning Network', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2015-02-25T19:30:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael Gonchar', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gonchar', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/43e912e1-8a10-5a58-a802-6c9f1d1694a6', 'word_count': 3042, 'uri': 'nyt://article/43e912e1-8a10-5a58-a802-6c9f1d1694a6'}, {'abstract': 'Artsy types are increasingly leaving the confines of the city center in favor of adopting a country life nearby.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/02/25/berlin-brandenburg-design-and-arts-scene-thrives/', 'snippet': 'Artsy types are increasingly leaving the confines of the city center in favor of adopting a country life nearby.', 'lead_paragraph': 'That Berlin has one of Europe’s most vibrant contemporary arts scenes is hardly news — but now, a key group of creators are moving outside the city center to build ethically motivated, innovatively designed retreats, concert venues and private homes. Native Berliners often describe a quest for gemütlichkeit — German for a space that inspires cheerful serenity — as a defining element in Berlin’s characteristic aesthetic and life-philosophy. When placed outside the city’s famously spacious old apartments, this sense of tranquility is supposedly achieved through considerate and conscientious design that fits into, rather than overpowers, the surrounding environment.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/05/t-magazine/05berlin-honigman/05berlin-honigman-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/02/05/t-magazine/05berlin-honigman/05berlin-honigman-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/05/t-magazine/05berlin-honigman/05berlin-honigman-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/05/t-magazine/05berlin-honigman/05berlin-honigman-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/05/t-magazine/05berlin-honigman/05berlin-honigman-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/02/05/t-magazine/05berlin-honigman/05berlin-honigman-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/05/t-magazine/05berlin-honigman/05berlin-honigman-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Just Outside Berlin, a Design and Arts Scene Thrives', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline'