tname': 'Bilton', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/af27a255-0317-5acd-954a-7db74a8f4cd3', 'word_count': 985, 'uri': 'nyt://article/af27a255-0317-5acd-954a-7db74a8f4cd3'}, {'abstract': 'The first full-length album from the Future Brown production collective emphasizes melody while fluently borrowing structural elements from a host of styles.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/02/26/arts/music/future-brown-confident-song-collective-cooks-new-stews.html', 'snippet': 'The first full-length album from the Future Brown production collective emphasizes melody while fluently borrowing structural elements from a host of styles.', 'lead_paragraph': 'We were supposed to have reached the singularity by now, no? That place where the underground scenes that were born in opposition to the mainstream excess of the 1980s and 1990s and 2000s would, through the Internet, come to rest comfortably next to, and inside of, pop. The old distinctions were meant to be relics; now that anyone can get anything at any time, hierarchies were doomed. Right?', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/26/arts/26FUTUREBROWN/26FUTUREBROWN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 388, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/02/26/arts/26FUTUREBROWN/26FUTUREBROWN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 388}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/26/arts/26FUTUREBROWN/26FUTUREBROWN-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 661, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/26/arts