[{'firstname': 'Monica', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Davey', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Mitch', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Smith', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2976bb22-977c-5127-97c1-06941663d362', 'word_count': 1007, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2976bb22-977c-5127-97c1-06941663d362'}, {'abstract': 'The United States Embassy in Jordan on Wednesday warned American citizens to avoid high-end shopping malls in Amman, the capital, because of credible threats of terrorist attacks.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/02/26/world/middleeast/jordan-us-warns-of-threat-to-malls.html', 'snippet': 'The United States Embassy in Jordan on Wednesday warned American citizens to avoid high-end shopping malls in Amman, the capital, because of credible threats of terrorist attacks.', 'lead_paragraph': ' The United States Embassy in Jordan on Wednesday warned American citizens to avoid high-end shopping malls in Amman, the capital, because of credible threats of terrorist attacks. The embassy’s statement contained no information about the type or timing of any possible attack, but it advised Americans in the country and embassy employees and their families to avoid the malls in the next few days. “Extremist groups have repeatedly expressed interest in attacking so-called soft targets, such as malls and restaurants in Jordan,” it said. The spokesman for Jordan’s government, Mohammad Momani, said security measures had already been stepped up because of “regional events.” Jordan is taking part in the campaign against the Islamic State group, which recently killed a captured Jordanian pilot and released a video showing his grisly death. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Jordan: U.S. Warns of Threat to Malls', 'kicker': 'World Briefing', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Jordan: U.S. Warns of Threat to Malls', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Jordan', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sweis, Rana F', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Diplomatic Service, Embassies and Consulates', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Terrorism', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-02-26T02:32:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rana F. Sweis', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rana', 'middlename': 'F.', 'lastname': 'Sweis', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/02d764b4-51e4-5aa2-a2f1-1aa871760990', 'word_count': 130, 'uri': 'nyt://article/02d764b4-51e4-5aa2-a2f1-1aa871760990'}, {'abstract': 'Long before “Jaws,” Dr. Clark rode a 40-foot whale shark, met great whites while scuba diving, studied “sleeping” sharks in undersea caves and witnessed a shark’s birth.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/02/26/us/eugenie-clark-scholar-of-the-life-aquatic-dies-at-92.html', 'snippet': 'Long before “Jaws,” Dr. Clark rode a 40-foot whale shark, met great whites while scuba diving, studied “sleeping” sharks in undersea caves and witnessed a shark’s birth.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Eugenie Clark, whose childhood rapture with fish in a New York City aquarium led to a life of scholarly adventure in the littorals and depths of the Seven Seas and to a global reputation as a marine biologist and expert on sharks, died on Wednesday at her home in Sarasota, Fla. She was 92.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'imag