ich Caleb Emmons asks for a raise.', 'web_url': 'https://wordplay.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/02/25/its-all-a-plot/', 'snippet': 'In which Caleb Emmons asks for a raise.', 'lead_paragraph': 'THURSDAY PUZZLE — I think Caleb Emmons is asking for a raise. You might not have picked up on this, but I did. I became a big believer in subliminal messages after majoring in Strategic Guessing in college. The university insisted on calling it “Marketing,” but guessing — as in, “We’re pretty sure consumers won’t sue us for selling them this product” — was much closer to the truth.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'It’s All a Plot', 'kicker': 'Wordplay', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Crossword Puzzles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-02-26T03:00:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Crosswords & Games', 'byline': {'original': 'By Deb Amlen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Deb', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Amlen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4204e1c6-0c78-58d6-9f36-ab2c4b52cb89', 'word_count': 684, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4204e1c6-0c78-58d6-9f36-ab2c4b52cb89'}, {'abstract': 'Successive governments in Israel have failed to address the lack of reasonably priced housing, the state comptroller found.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/02/26/world/as-vote-nears-watchdog-agency-criticizes-netanyahu-on-housing-costs.html', 'snippet': 'Successive governments in Israel have failed to address the lack of reasonably priced housing, the state comptroller found.', 'lead_paragraph': 'JERUSALEM — In another potential blow to Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu, who faces his country’s voters in less than three weeks, Israel’s government watchdog issued a harsh report on Wed