 would secure the necessary funding to forestall what transit experts were warning about — a slump in service, overflowing subway trains and more frequent delays.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '25', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'M.T.A. Chief Tries to Ease Alarm on Budget Gap, but Warns of Risks to Projects', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'M.T.A. Leader Tries to Ease Alarm on Budget Gap, but Warns of Risks to Projects', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Metropolitan Transportation Authority', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Prendergast, Thomas F', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Transit Systems', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Budgets and Budgeting', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-02-26T03:13:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Benjamin Mueller', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Benjamin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mueller', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0cb49841-b538-51f0-9e54-1114e1291e65', 'word_count': 560, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0cb49841-b538-51f0-9e54-1114e1291e65'}, {'abstract': 'Duodenoscopes are difficult to disinfect, and there is no expert consensus on the best way to do so now that standard methods have been called into question.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/02/26/us/after-deadly-infections-fda-asks-device-makers-about-cleaning-methods.html', 'snippet': 'Duodenoscopes are difficult to disinfect, and there is no expert consensus on the best way to do so now that standard methods have been called into question.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Food and Drug Administration never reviewed data from manufacturers regarding the procedures needed to clean the complex medical devices that recently infected seven patients with drug-resistant bacteria, an agency official acknowledged on Wednesday.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '17', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/26/science/26endoscope/26endoscope-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 719, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/02/26/science/26endoscope/26endoscope-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 719}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/26/science/26endoscope/26endoscope-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 854, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/26/science/26endoscope/26endoscope-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1708, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/26/science/26endoscope/26endoscope-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/02/26/science/26endoscope/26endoscope-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/26/science/26endoscope/26endoscope-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'After Deadly Infections, F.D.A. Asks Device Makers About Cleaning Methods', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline