: 'subject', 'value': 'Poaching (Wildlife)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Endangered and Extinct Species', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Convention on International Trade in Endangered Species', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'AFRICA', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-02-26T20:33:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dan Levin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Levin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8d7cdb4a-d2a9-510c-9c36-826698c769f9', 'word_count': 681, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8d7cdb4a-d2a9-510c-9c36-826698c769f9'}, {'abstract': 'The makeup artist took cues from the designer’s fall 2015 ladylike collection to create a look for today’s show.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/02/26/pat-mcgrath-prada-milan-fall-2015-fashion-week/', 'snippet': 'The makeup artist took cues from the designer’s fall 2015 ladylike collection to create a look for today’s show.', 'lead_paragraph': 'This year Prada gave the legendary makeup artist Pat McGrath two words to work with: New Elegance. “We used a little bit of a kind of a soft chestnut color on the eyes in the sockets, and then the brow was softly groomed,” said McGrath backstage before today’s show. For the lips, she chose similarly muted hues: “a pale pink” and “a pale orange.” (She also noted that she used “a little bit of blush” over the lightly applied foundation to complete the look.) It was a stark contrast to the brand’s bold spring/summer 2015 look, which involved bleached eyebrows with striking cat-eye makeup. “It was very funny because last season was a nod to punk — and for Miu Miu we had bad girls,” she said, referring to her work with another Prada S.p.A.-owned label. “But this year it seems like they’re good girls.” And it’s true — the fall beauty look has a refinement that matches the ladylike air of the collection. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/26/t-magazine/26beauty-prada/26beauty-prada-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 800, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/02/26/t-magazine/26beauty-prada/26beauty-prada-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 800}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/26/t-magazine/26beauty-prada/26beauty-prada-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 768, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/26/t-magazine/26beauty-prada/26beauty-prada-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1536, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/26/t-magazine/26beauty-prada/26beauty-prada-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/02/26/t-magazine/26beauty-prada/26beauty-prada-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/26/t-magazine/26beauty-prada/26beauty-prada-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Pat McGrath’s ‘New Elegance’ Beauty for Prada', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 