'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6d708afd-0b3f-55a3-928b-76b062c2c018', 'word_count': 264, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6d708afd-0b3f-55a3-928b-76b062c2c018'}, {'abstract': 'The ensemble played a sold-out set consisting of a mix of jazz standards and selections from a new album that recalibrates songs by other artists.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/02/27/arts/music/review-the-robert-glasper-trio-presents-moody-covers-at-the-village-vanguard.html', 'snippet': 'The ensemble played a sold-out set consisting of a mix of jazz standards and selections from a new album that recalibrates songs by other artists.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The pianist Robert Glasper pitches his tent at the junction of coolheaded logic and digressive caprice. Not long into his sold-out first set at the Village Vanguard on Wednesday night, he tossed off a staccato solo interlude, notes clacking like marbles out of a bag onto the floor. A melodic shape emerged, and bass and drums hit a single, sudden downbeat — thump! — as Mr. Glasper kept extemporizing with chromatic flair. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/27/arts/27glasper-2/27glasper-2-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/02/27/arts/27glasper-2/27glasper-2-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/27/arts/27glasper-2/27glasper-2-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/27/arts/27glasper-2/27glasper-2-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJ