tion-sets-off-a-chain-of-misery.html', 'snippet': 'In this film set in a Maine logging town, a school-bus driver deals with the repercussions of a tragic mistake.', 'lead_paragraph': '“Blown by wind, kissed by the snow, all that’s left is the dark below.” Heard over the end titles of Lance Edmands’s “Bluebird,” those words from the Fleetwoods’ 1961 hit “Tragedy” distill the film’s desolate mood. Set during winter in Millinocket, a fading Maine logging town, this polar vortex of a movie opens with a quotation from Thoreau’s “The Maine Woods” that evokes human helplessness in the face of chaotic natural forces. Then it segues to shots of snow-covered logs transported by conveyor belt for conversion into pulp. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/27/arts/27BLUEBIRD/27BLUEBIRD-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 341, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/02/27/arts/27BLUEBIRD/27BLUEBIRD-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 341}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/27/arts/27BLUEBIRD/27BLUEBIRD-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 582, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/27/arts/27BLUEBIRD/27BLUEBIRD-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1163, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/27/arts/27BLUEBIRD/27BLUEBIRD-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/02/27/arts/27BLUEBIRD/27BLUEBIRD-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnail