'In a free-speech case that could bolster whistle-blowers, a federal appeals court ruled on Thursday in favor of a New York City police officer who said his commanders retaliated against him after he complained to them about what he believed to be a quota system that resulted in unjustified stops and arrests.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '23', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Appellate Ruling Supports a Police Whistle-Blower in New York', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Appellate Ruling Supports a Police Whistle-Blower', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Whistle-Blowers', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Vega, Tanzina', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Police Department (NYC)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Matthews, Craig', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Search and Seizure', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-02-27T04:39:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tanzina Vega', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tanzina', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Vega', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/50c4abcf-440f-5794-a670-5ffabcb2874a', 'word_count': 620, 'uri': 'nyt://article/50c4abcf-440f-5794-a670-5ffabcb2874a'}, {'abstract': 'Mr. Smith plays a seasoned con man who schools a novice (Margot Robbie) in more sophisticated scams.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/02/27/movies/review-in-focus-a-grifter-will-smith-as-life-coach.html', 'snippet': 'Mr. Smith plays a seasoned con man who schools a novice (Margot Robbie) in more sophisticated scams.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A silky high-end caper about a pair of good-looking con artists, “Focus” is a movie blessedly free of self-importance. It constructs a seductive fantasy world out of actual places (New Orleans, Buenos Aires) and milieus (Super Bowl skyboxes, Formula One racing) and generously grants V.I.P. access to the audience. You may be a few steps behind as the big scams unfold, but you feel more like a player than a sucker. The preposterousness of the story doesn’t seem like a rip-off, since the twists in the plot, for the most part, pay off nicely.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/27/arts/27FOCUS1/27FOCUS1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 432, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/02/27/arts/27FOCUS1/27FOCUS1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 432}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/27/arts/27FOCUS1/27FOCUS1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 737, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/27/arts/27FOCUS1/27FOCUS1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1474, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/27/arts/27FOCUS1/27FOCUS1-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/02/27/arts/27FOCUS1/27FOCUS1-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/27/arts/27FOCUS1/27FOCUS1-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Review: In ‘Focus,’ a Grifter (Will Smith) as Life Coach', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Graduating to the Big Con, After a Romantic Crash Course', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ficarra, Glenn', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Requa, John', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Smith, Will', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Robbie, Margot', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Focus (Movie)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-02-27T04:41:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By A.O. Scott', 'person': [{'firstname': 'A.', 'middlename': 'O.', 'lastname': 'Scott', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/c27f729b-333f-5881-9a4f-877d14639abe', 'word_count': 672, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c27f729b-333f-5881-9a4f-877d14639abe'}, {'abstract': 'Johnny Hincapie, who says he was wrongly convicted of murder in the killing of Utah tourist Brian Watkins in 1990, faced tough questioning at a hearing on Thursday.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/02/27/nyregion/in-trip-to-past-a-false-confession-claim-meets-skepticism-of-another-sort.html', 'snippet': 'Johnny Hincapie, who says he was wrongly convicted of murder in the killing of Utah tourist Brian Watkins in 1990, faced tough questioning at a hearing on Thursday.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The video monitor switched off. Seated on the witness stand, Johnny Hincapie, 42, took off his eyeglasses and began to weep. Everyone around him in the seventh-floor courtroom in Manhattan fell silent. After 40 seconds or so, a phone rang, and a court clerk answered, whispering, “Part 73.” The sobbing continued. Mr. Hincapie had just finished watching a video of himself at age 18, confessing to being part of a group that had mugged a family of tourists in a Midtown Manhattan subway station and killed the valiant son who had resisted.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/27/nyregion/27ABOUT1/27ABOUT1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 401, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/02/27/nyregion/27ABOUT1/27ABOUT1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 401}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/27/nyregion/27ABOUT1/27ABOUT1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 685, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/27/nyregion/27ABOUT1/27ABOUT1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1370, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/27/nyregion/27ABOUT1/27ABOUT1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/02/27/nyregion/27ABOUT1/27ABOUT1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/27/nyregion/27ABOUT1/27ABOUT1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'In Trip to Past, a False Confession Claim Meets Skepticism of Another Sort', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'In Trip to Past, a False Confession Claim Meets Skepticism of Another Sort', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hincapie, Johnny', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Dwyer, Jim', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Confessions', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Murders, Attempted Murders and Homicides', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Watkins, Brian', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Midtown Area (Manhattan, NY)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-02-27T04:56:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jim Dwyer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jim', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Dwyer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/be1a86b9-920f-54c9-a3c7-ec8816e2b3ba', 'word_count': 812, 'uri': 'nyt://article/be1a86b9-920f-54c9-a3c7-ec8816e2b3ba'}, {'abstract': 'A Portland resident’s mission: to change the way sake is brewed in America. Meet Gordon Heady.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/02/27/t-magazine/gordon-heady-sake.html', 'snippet': 'A Portland resident’s mission: to change the way sake is brewed in America. Meet Gordon Heady.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Gordon Heady likens the taste of American sake to “jet fuel,” something he intends to change by becoming the country’s first master brewer. The Portland native was introduced to rice wine in college — the Japanese students he tutored in English paid him in bottles — and in 2012, he visited the southern island of Kyushu and fell in love with the 316-year-old brewery Wakatakeya Shuzo. Heady, who speaks about sake with reverence — “it’s the drink of the gods” — has since returned as an apprentice for about six months each year during brewing season. “The brewers are wizards who use fermentation to bring rice to its highest purpose,” he says. Fittingly, the blend he brews there — with notes of cooked citrus and wet wool — is called A Zen Ai Koshu, or “Love.”', 'print_section': 'M2', 'print_page': '64', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/03/08/t-magazine/08mens-look-sake/08mens-look-sake-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/03/08/t-magazine/08mens-look-sake/08mens-look-sake-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/03/08/t-magazine/08mens-look-sake/08mens-look-sake-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/03/08/t-magazine/08mens-look-sake/08mens-look-sake-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/03/08/t-magazine/08mens-look-sake/08mens-look-sake-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/03/08/t-magazine/08mens-look-sake/08mens-look-sake-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/03/08/t-magazine/08mens-look-sake/08mens-look-sake-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Sake Evangelist ', 'kicker': 'Food Matters', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Sake Evangelist', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2015-02-27T05:00:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TLiving', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Julia Payne', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Julia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Payne', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/49fca91b-da75-5ab8-925b-2729e70e2468', 'word_count': 138, 'uri': 'nyt://article/49fca91b-da75-5ab8-925b-2729e70e2468'}, {'abstract': 'This word has appeared in 529 New York Times articles in the past year.', 'web_url': 'https://learning.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/02/27/word-of-the-day-optional/', 'snippet': 'This word has appeared in 529 New York Times articles in the past year.', 'lead_paragraph': 'optional • \\ˈäp-shnəl, -shə-nəl\\ • adjective ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Word of the Day | optional', 'kicker': 'The Learning Network', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2015-02-27T05:03:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Learning Network', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Learning Network'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5f27f6fa-2d35-5b29-b209-d5ed53d2f029', 'word_count': 222, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5f27f6fa-2d35-5b29-b209-d5ed53d2f029'}, {'abstract': 'Dieterle’s 1942 film emphasized jazz as an intrinsically African-American art form, even as it played loosely with some of the music’s history.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/03/01/movies/homevideo/william-dieterles-syncopation-on-dvd-bending-notes-and-jazz-history.html', 'snippet': 'Dieterle’s 1942 film emphasized jazz as an intrinsically African-American art form, even as it played loosely with some of the music’s history.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Motion pictures and jazz were both born around the dawn of the 20th century. But did Hollywood ever get the music right? Take “Syncopation” (1942), a snappily titled, wildly ambitious jazz chronicle that might be the last thing you’d expect from Warner Bros.’ German-born workhorse, William Dieterle (1893-1972).', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/03/01/arts/01HOBERMAN/01HOBERMAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 438, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/03/01/arts/01HOBERMAN/01HOBERMAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 438}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/03/01/arts/01HOBERMAN/01HOBERMAN-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 748, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/03/01/arts/01HOBERMAN/01HOBERMAN-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1080, 'width': 1478, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/03/01/arts/01HOBERMAN/01HOBERMAN-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/03/01/arts/01HOBERMAN/01HOBERMAN-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/03/01/arts/01HOBERMAN/01HOBERMAN-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'William Dieterle’s ‘Syncopation’ on DVD: Bending Notes and Jazz History', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Bending Notes and Jazz History', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Jazz', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Video Releases (Entertainment)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'William Dieterle (1893-1972)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Clarke, Shirley', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Syncopation (Movie)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'The Connection (Movie)', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-02-27T05:12:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'subsection_name': 'DVD', 'byline': {'original': 'By J. Hoberman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'J.', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hoberman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/98956834-66f7-573b-858c-8e7dca46bc93', 'word_count': 1267, 'uri': 'nyt://article/98956834-66f7-573b-858c-8e7dca46bc93'}, {'abstract': 'The writer and director’s deadpan comedies have followed a man-child on the skids.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/03/01/movies/joel-potrykuss-film-buzzard-is-inspired-by-dead-end-jobs.html', 'snippet': 'The writer and director’s deadpan comedies have followed a man-child on the skids.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Marty, the abrasive antihero of “Buzzard,” is not out to win employee of the month — quite the opposite. A temporary worker in the mortgage department of a Midwestern bank, he closes his checking account and opens a new one to take advantage of a $50 promotional offer. He returns office supplies for profit. After cutting himself in a poorly conceived attempt to attach Freddy Krueger blades to a Nintendo Power Glove, he fakes an injury at work to get the medical costs covered.', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/03/01/arts/01BUZZARD1/01BUZZARD1-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 338, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/03/01/arts/01BUZZARD1/01BUZZARD1-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 338}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/03/01/arts/01BUZZARD1/01BUZZARD1-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 576, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/03/01/arts/01BUZZARD1/01BUZZARD1-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1080, 'width': 1920, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/03/01/arts/01BUZZARD1/01BUZZARD1-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/03/01/arts/01BUZZARD1/01BUZZARD1-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/03/01/arts/01BUZZARD1/01BUZZARD1-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Joel Potrykus’s Film ‘Buzzard’ Is Inspired by Dead-End Jobs', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'He’s Going Nowhere. Care to Follow?', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{