e/27526e4d-b7ff-554f-b8dd-766456e13f47'}, {'abstract': 'Specimen libraries are vital for biology. So why are museums being forced to cut their funding?', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/02/27/opinion/libraries-of-life.html', 'snippet': 'Specimen libraries are vital for biology. So why are museums being forced to cut their funding?', 'lead_paragraph': 'HIDDEN behind the popular displays at many of your favorite natural history museums — in their basements, back rooms and, increasingly, off-site facilities — sit humanity’s most important libraries of life, holding not books but preserved animal and plant specimens, carefully collected over centuries by thousands of scientist explorers. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '25', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/27/opinion/27lujan/27lujan-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 370, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/02/27/opinion/27lujan/27lujan-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 370}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/27/opinion/27lujan/27lujan-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 632, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/27/opinion/27lujan/27lujan-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1264, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/27/opinion/27lujan/27lujan-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/02/27/opinion/27lujan/27lujan-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 7