urse is constrained by layers of censorship and self-censorship, Kong Qingdong, a neo-Maoist literary scholar at Peking University and an avid blogger, has long attracted attention with his vociferous commentaries.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Beijing Courts Address the Right to Criticize Public Figures', 'kicker': 'Sinosphere', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Censorship', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Libel and Slander', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Suits and Litigation (Civil)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bo Xilai', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Confucius', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kong Qingdong', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Peking University', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-02-27T10:26:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Patrick Boehler', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Patrick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Boehler', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ffc90ffe-465c-5d42-9e14-86a9286c79c9', 'word_count': 878, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ffc90ffe-465c-5d42-9e14-86a9286c79c9'}, {'abstract': 'The agreement emerged as a judge was believed to be close to ruling on damages for the contamination and loss of use of more than 1,500 acres of wetlands, marshes, meadows and waters.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/02/28/nyregion/exxon-mobil-settles-with-new-jersey-over-environmental-damage.html', 'snippet': 'The agreement emerged as a judge was belie