onary era, for just a few dollars.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/03/01/travel/5-ways-to-time-travel-and-party-in-new-york.html', 'snippet': 'Anyone with a passion for the past can plunge into almost any historical period, from the Jazz Age to the Revolutionary era, for just a few dollars.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When William Faulkner famously mused on the power of history — “The past is never dead. It’s not even past,” he wrote — he probably didn’t have New York foremost in mind. The city, not known for its ability to hold on to old and historic spaces, has often directed its energy manically to the future. But in 2015, a contrarian spirit lives on in the city, and anyone with a passion for the past can plunge into almost any historical period for just a few dollars — and, in some of the more theatrical parties, by also investing in some decent vintage duds. We’ve covered how to enjoy Gilded Age decadence, but if your preferences lie in different eras, here are some events to seek out.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/03/01/travel/01GILDEDSIDEBAR-copy/01GILDEDSIDEBAR-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/03/01/travel/01GILDEDSIDEBAR-copy/01GILDEDSIDEBAR-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/03/01/travel/01GILDEDSIDEBAR-copy/01GILDEDSIDEBAR-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/03/01/travel/01GILDEDSIDEBAR-copy/01GILDEDSIDEBAR-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype