fier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ed573eb1-4e34-56a1-982f-49bc27e81632', 'word_count': 40, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ed573eb1-4e34-56a1-982f-49bc27e81632'}, {'abstract': 'Highlights from the International Herald Tribune archives: Russians fear cholera in 1890.', 'web_url': 'https://iht-retrospective.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/02/27/1890-cholera-in-persia/', 'snippet': 'Highlights from the International Herald Tribune archives: Russians fear cholera in 1890.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Rigorous measures are being taken by the Russian Government, says the St. Petersburg correspondent of the Times, to prevent the spread of cholera from Persia and Mesopotamia into the Trans- caucasus. The Official Messenger publishes a long account of the progress of the disease towards the Russian frontier, with the opinions of Russian Consuls. The Consul at Bagdad states that, in his opinion the cessation of the epidemic in Mesopotamia at the end of 1889 was only temporary, and that it will soon reappear. Various arrangements of a sanitary and preventive character are ready to be put into force on the frontiers of the first warning. All vessels from the infected countries will have to submit to ten days’ quarantine and disinfection at Batoum and Theodosia. All pilgrims and travelers from Persia and Turkey are to be sent on through Batoum and Baku, where they will undergo quarantine and have their luggage disinfected. — The New York Herald, European Edition, Feb. 28, 1890', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/28/blogs/28iht-oldfeb28-cholera/28iht-oldfeb28-cholera-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 391, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/02/28/blogs/28iht-oldfeb28-cholera/28iht-oldfeb28-cholera-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 391}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/28/blogs/28iht-oldfeb28-cholera/28iht-oldfeb28-cholera-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 667, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/28/blogs/28iht-oldfeb28-cholera/28iht-oldfeb28-cholera-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1335, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/28/blogs/28iht-oldfeb28-cholera/28iht-oldfeb28-cholera-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/02/28/blogs/28iht-oldfeb28-cholera/28iht-oldfeb28-cholera-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/28/blogs/28iht-oldfeb28-cholera/28iht-oldfeb28-cholera-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': '1890: Cholera in Persia', 'kicker': 'IHT Retrospective', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cholera', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Persian Gulf', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'St Petersburg (Russia)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-02-27T15:23:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By International Herald Tribune', 'person': [{'firstname': 'International', 'middlename': 'Herald', 'lastname': 'Tribune', 'qualifier': None, 'ti