': 'Mr. Brown’s dance troupe brings the warmth of the islands in a program of recent and vintage works.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/02/28/arts/dance/review-ronald-k-brown-evidence-heats-up-at-the-joyce.html', 'snippet': 'Mr. Brown’s dance troupe brings the warmth of the islands in a program of recent and vintage works.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It’s a treat to wrap yourself up in some vintage Ronald K. Brown on a cold winter night. Leading off Evidence’s second program at the Joyce Theater on Thursday was Mr. Brown’s 1999 “Gatekeepers,” originally created for Philadanco. In a program note, he describes his dancers as “soldiers walking toward heaven, searching for the wounded and looking out to make a safe haven for others to follow.” \xa0', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/28/arts/28EVIDENCE/28EVIDENCE-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 884, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/02/28/arts/28EVIDENCE/28EVIDENCE-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 884}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/28/arts/28EVIDENCE/28EVIDENCE-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 696, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/28/arts/28EVIDENCE/28EVIDENCE-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1391, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/28/arts/28EVIDENCE/28EVIDENCE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/02/28/arts/28EVIDENCE/28EVIDENCE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/28/arts/28EVIDENCE/28EVIDENCE-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Review: Ronald K. Brown/Evidence Heats Up at the Joyce', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Searching, Swiveling and Heating Things Up', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dancing', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Joyce Theater', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Brown, Ronald K', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Brown, Ronald K/Evidence', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-02-27T23:25:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Dance', 'byline': {'original': 'By Gia Kourlas', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Gia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kourlas', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/06cec525-31ad-573a-88e5-c7b056a78b3f', 'word_count': 388, 'uri': 'nyt://article/06cec525-31ad-573a-88e5-c7b056a78b3f'}, {'abstract': 'This string quartet, founded in Budapest in 1975, performed on Thursday night, offering a program of Schubert, Mozart and Beethoven.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/02/28/arts/music/review-takacs-quartet-and-the-viennese-masters-play-at-alice-tully-hall.html', 'snippet': 'This string quartet, founded in Budapest in 1975, performed on Thursday night, offering a program of Schubert, Mozart and Beethoven.', 'lead_paragraph': 'From even the most prominent of string quartets, a program of Schubert, Mozart and Beethoven might come across as stolid. After all, there are so many foursomes around now that scoff at every kind of boundary, from the JACK  and the Kronos to the Ébène and the Danish. But the Takacs Quartet always shows that there is, and must be, room for insightful, intense performances of major works. That was its achievement in a superb appearance at Alice Tully Hall on Thursday: revealing the familiar as unfamiliar, making the most traditional of works feel radical once more.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/28/arts/28TAKACS/28TAKACS-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 405, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/02/28/arts/28TAKACS/28TAKACS-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 405}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/28/arts/28TAKACS/28TAKACS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 691, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/28/arts/28TAKACS/28TAKACS-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1383, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/28/arts/28TAKACS/28TAKACS-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/02/28/arts/28TAKACS/28TAKACS-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/28/arts/28TAKACS/28TAKACS-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Review: Takacs Quartet and the Viennese Masters Play at Alice Tully Hall', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Going for Wrenching, Unstable and Disoriented', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Allen, David', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Classical Music', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Alice Tully Hall (Manhattan, NY)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Takacs Quartet', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-02-27T23:26:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Allen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Allen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/4a77ca8b-a528-567b-8721-84239c2b054b', 'word_count': 399, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4a77ca8b-a528-567b-8721-84239c2b054b'}, {'abstract': 'The war in Syria has blurred the line between armchair jihadists and real combatants.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/02/27/magazine/how-serious-was-the-brooklyn-isis-plot.html', 'snippet': 'The war in Syria has blurred the line between armchair jihadists and real combatants.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The radicalization of three Central Asian immigrants living in Brooklyn, who were arraigned yesterday in a federal court for allegedly plotting to aid ISIS, seems to have taken place with surprising speed. According to the 23-page affidavit unsealed Wednesday night, federal agents began watching Abdurasul Hasanovich Juraboev, a 24-year-old gyro-shop employee from Uzbekistan, and Akhror Saidakhmetov, a 19-year-old Kazakh employed at a cellphone repair kiosk, six months ago, shortly after the two men began posting to a website sympathetic to ISIS. The investigation culminated on Wednesday when federal agents arrested Juraboev at his apartment and Saidakhmetov at John F. Kennedy International Airport, where he was attempting to board a flight to Turkey; each man allegedly had plans to cross the border and fight — and, they hoped, to die — in Syria. (A third man, Saidakhmetov’s 30-year-old boss, Abror Habibov, is alleged to have raised money for the trip.)', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/27/magazine/27mag-isis/27mag-isis-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 396, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/02/27/magazine/27mag-isis/27mag-isis-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 396}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/27/magazine/27mag-isis/27mag-isis-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 676, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/27/magazine/27mag-isis/27mag-isis-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1352, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/27/magazine/27mag-isis/27mag-isis-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/02/27/magazine/27mag-isis/27mag-isis-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/27/magazine/27mag-isis/27mag-isis-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name'