k': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Target Corporation', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Walmart Stores Inc', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-02-28T02:58:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/540a4ba6-ee56-562e-8ea3-c6f5fb415bae', 'word_count': 365, 'uri': 'nyt://article/540a4ba6-ee56-562e-8ea3-c6f5fb415bae'}, {'abstract': 'A Saturday brain twister by Barry C. Silk.', 'web_url': 'https://wordplay.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/02/27/british-bit-of-headwear/', 'snippet': 'A Saturday brain twister by Barry C. Silk.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SATURDAY PUZZLE — A good crossword puzzle will always remind you that you don’t know everything, and that goes double for Saturdays. No matter how much you think you might be up on your lingo, eventually someone will pull a TITFER on you out of nowhere and you’ll realize that there is still much to learn. Some people will find that unfair, but I think it makes life worth living. It’s also why I color my hair.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'British Bit of Headwear', 'kicker': 'Wordplay', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Crossword Puzzles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-02-28T03:00:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Crosswords & Games', 'byline': {'original': 'By Deb Amlen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Deb', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Amlen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/34e017cd-6d74-5441-a012-d46ae068e665', 'word_count': 401, 'uri': 'nyt://article/34e017cd-6d74-5441-a012-d46ae068e665'}, {'abstract': 'Mayor Bill de Blasio wants to stop regulating a practice that could infect babies with herpes.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/02/28/opinion/a-bad-call-on-risky-circumcisions.html', 'snippet': 'Mayor Bill de Blasio wants to stop regulating a practice that could infect babies with herpes.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The herpes simplex virus, common and relatively harmless in adults, can be deadly to babies. Such infections in newborns are blessedly rare, but one thing is known to increase the risk significantly: the circumcision ritual called metzitzah b’peh, practiced by many ultra-Orthodox and some Orthodox Jews, in which a circumciser, or mohel, sucks blood from a newly cut penis with his mouth.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/28/opinion/28sat4web/28sat4web-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 342, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/02/28/opinion/28sat4web/28sat4web-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 342}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/28/opinion/28sat4web/28sat4web-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 584, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/28/opinion/28sat4web/28sat4web-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1066, 'width': 1868, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/28/opinion/28sat4web/28sat4web-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/02/28/opinion/28sat4web/28sat4web-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/28/opinion/28sat4web/28sat4web-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Bad Call on Risky Circumcisions', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Bad Call on Risky Circumcisions', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Circumcision', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Herpes Viruses', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Jews and Judaism', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'de Blasio, Bill', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-02-28T03:11:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/f25329b4-8508-5dc1-a78d-a975da885fbf', 'word_count': 398, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f25329b4-8508-5dc1-a78d-a975da885fbf'}, {'abstract': 'The psychiatrist, testifying at the trial of Pedro Hernandez, said Mr. Hernandez was “praying for God to forgive him” as he told her he killed a boy in a bodega.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/02/28/nyregion/psychiatrist-says-etan-patz-suspect-gave-a-2nd-confession.html', 'snippet': 'The psychiatrist, testifying at the trial of Pedro Hernandez, said Mr. Hernandez was “praying for God to forgive him” as he told her he killed a boy in a bodega.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A man on trial for the murder of 6-year-old Etan Patz confessed to killing a child in an interview with a psychiatrist at Rikers Island a month after his arrest, according to the doctor’s testimony on Friday. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Psychiatrist Says Etan Patz Suspect Gave a 2nd Confession', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Psychiatrist Says Patz Suspect Gave a 2nd Confession', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Patz, Etan', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hernandez, Pedro (1961- )', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Confessions', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Murders, Attempted Murders and Homicides', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Robotti, Flavia', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-02-28T03:12:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By James C. McKinley Jr', 'person': [{'firstname': 'James', 'middlename': 'C.', 'lastname': 'McKinley', 'qualifier': 'Jr', 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a34eaddd-cecb-560c-bd5c-68c345caf54b', 'word_count': 691, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a34eaddd-cecb-560c-bd5c-68c345caf54b'}, {'abstract': 'The former mayor of New York suggests that the Obama administration negotiate directly with Canada on a climate pact.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/02/28/opinion/joe-nocera-bloomberg-sees-a-way-on-keystone.html', 'snippet': 'The former mayor of New York suggests that the Obama administration negotiate directly with Canada on a climate pact.', 'lead_paragraph': 'No one can question Michael Bloomberg’s climate change bona fides. As mayor of New York, he declared that cities had to lead the way in reducing the threat of climate change, and he strove to make New York greener. He has donated millions of dollars to the effort to shut down coal-fired power plants. He endorsed President Obama for re-election in 2012 primarily because the president, he said, “has taken major steps to reduce our carbon consumption.” Most recently, he was named the United Nations secretary general’s special envoy for cities and climate change, a position he appears to be taking quite seriously.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '17', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/01/opinion/nocera-circular/nocera-circular-jumbo-v2.png', 'height': 228, 'width': 228, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/01/opinion/nocera-circular/nocera-circular-superJumbo-v2.png', 'height': 228, 'width': 228, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/01/opinion/nocera-circular/nocera-circular-thumbStandard-v2.png', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/11/01/opinion/nocera-circular/nocera-circular-thumbStandard-v2.png', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/01/opinion/nocera-circular/nocera-circular-thumbLarge-v4.png', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Bloomberg Sees a Way on Keystone', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Columnist', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Bloomberg Sees a Way on Keystone', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Nocera, Joseph', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Keystone P