}, 'type_of_material': 'Question', '_id': 'nyt://article/c318e742-29d9-580c-a94e-f3daf52d397d', 'word_count': 993, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c318e742-29d9-580c-a94e-f3daf52d397d'}, {'abstract': 'Men with even one past conviction on their résumés are having trouble finding jobs, and that is taking a toll on the overall labor market.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/03/01/business/out-of-trouble-but-criminal-records-keep-men-out-of-work.html', 'snippet': 'Men with even one past conviction on their résumés are having trouble finding jobs, and that is taking a toll on the overall labor market.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Michael Hugh Mirsky landed a temporary job in December rolling stacks of crated milk and orange juice to the loading docks at a commercial dairy in central New Jersey. He’s not making much, and he doesn’t know how long it will last, but after 30 months of unemployment, he counts himself lucky. Mr. Mirsky is a convicted criminal, and work is hard to find.', 'print_section': 'BU', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/03/01/business/1-CRIMINAL-JP1/1-CRIMINAL-JP1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 449, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/03/01/business/1-CRIMINAL-JP1/1-CRIMINAL-JP1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 449}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/03/01/business/1-CRIMINAL-JP1/1-CRIMINAL-JP1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 766, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/03/01/business/1-CRIMINAL-JP1/1-CRIMINAL-JP1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1532, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thum