'web_url': 'https://iht-retrospective.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/02/28/political-cartoons-during-the-great-war/', 'snippet': 'The work of William Allen Rogers, a prolific cartoonist for The Herald during World War I, eventually earned him the French Legion of Honor.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The New York Herald’s cartoons during World War I reflected shifting attitudes as events progressed. James Gordon Bennett Jr., the paper’s publisher, never made a secret of his political views: The Herald initially supported the Allies morally, but lauded America’s “strict neutrality.” The full page illustration, above, by Ridgeway Knight shows Lady Columbia as she comforts the French Liberty, surrounded by the ruins of the first battles. “Brave France, you have my grateful and sisterly sympathy,” reads the caption.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/25/blogs/25iht-cartoons-columbia/25iht-cartoons-columbia-jumbo-v2.png', 'height': 644, 'width': 527, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/25/blogs/25iht-cartoons-columbia/25iht-cartoons-columbia-superJumbo-v2.png', 'height': 644, 'width': 527, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/25/blogs/25iht-cartoons-columbia/25iht-cartoons-columbia-thumbStandard.png', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/02/25/blogs/25iht-cartoons-columbia/25iht-cartoons-columbia-thumbStandard.png', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/25/blogs/25iht-cartoons-columbia/25iht-cartoons-columbia-t