 Company', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Economy', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Regulation and Deregulation of Industry', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Bank for International Settlements', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Economic Conditions and Trends', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Income Inequality', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Colleges and Universities', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lake, Marianne', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cecchetti, Stephen G', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kharroubi, Enisse', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-02-28T19:17:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'SundayBusiness', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Economy', 'byline': {'original': 'By Gretchen Morgenson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Gretchen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Morgenson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7e8b774a-05c6-585b-a2b5-82d1e6d9af88', 'word_count': 1059, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7e8b774a-05c6-585b-a2b5-82d1e6d9af88'}, {'abstract': 'Santina, tucked under the High Line and enclosed in a glass box designed by Renzo Piano, seems like a mirage.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/03/01/nyregion/where-wind-chill-is-not-a-factor.html', 'snippet': 'Santina, tucked under the High Line and enclosed in a glass box designed by Renzo Piano, seems like a mirage.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Never has a restaurant opened at a more opportune time, hell having frozen over and over. Santina, tucked under the High Line and enclosed in a glass box designed by Renzo Piano, seems like a mirage. Yet the palm and orange trees are real, as are the Murano glass sunflower chandeliers. Waiters dress in pastel polo shirts, white pants and sneakers, like deckhands on a yacht. Corny Italian music wafts over the birds of paradise perched in giant vases atop a Carrara marble bar brimming with fashionistas, food bloggers and financial types. On folksy pottery direct from the Amalfi coast come Mario Carbone’s creations of vegetables, nuts and seafood: comfort food without the weight. No wonder Santina, named for Mr. Carbone’s Sicilian grandmother, and the newest venture from the Parm team of Mr. Carbone, Rich Torrisi and Jeff Zalaznick, has been hot since it opened five weeks ago. It’s a culinary spray tan, only healthier. LIZ ROBBINS ', 'print_section': 'MB', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/03/01/nyregion/01TABLE1/01TABLE1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/03/01/nyregion/01TABLE1/01TABLE1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/03/01/nyregion/01TABLE1/01TABLE1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/03/01/nyregion/01TABLE1/01TABLE1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/03/01/nyregion/01TABLE1/01TABLE1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/03/01/nyregion/01TABLE1/01TABLE1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/03/01/nyregion/01TABLE1/01TABLE1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Taste of Summer Under the High Line ', 'kicker': 'At the Table', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Taste of Summer Under the High Line', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Restaurants', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Robbins, Liz', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'High Line (Manhattan, NY)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Santina (Manhattan, NY, Restaurant)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-02-28T19:21:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Liz Robbins', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Liz', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Robbins', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/be35874f-5678-5966-99e9-afd7316ce9d9', 'word_count': 544, 'uri': 'nyt://article/be35874f-5678-5966-99e9-afd7316ce9d9'}, {'abstract': 'The Russian opposition tries to make sense of Friday’s shooting and a deadly new reality.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/02/28/magazine/after-boris-nemtsovs-assassination-there-are-no-longer-any-limits.html', 'snippet': 'The Russian opposition tries to make sense of Friday’s shooting and a deadly new reality.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On Friday evening, Boris Nemtsov, a Russian opposition leader and former first deputy prime minister under Boris Yeltsin, went on a prominent Moscow radio station to exhort his fellow citizens to come out to protest President Vladimir Putin’s policies. There would be a rally on Sunday, a spring march, to demonstrate against the deepening economic crisis and Russia’s involvement in Ukraine. The most prominent Russian opposition leader, Aleksei Navalny, had been put in jail for 15 days, which just happened to be long enough to keep him from attending the rally. Nemtsov, who was older and, by now, less influential, had handed out leaflets in the metro and encouraged people to come anyway.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/28/magazine/28mag-nemtsov/28mag-nemtsov-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/02/28/magazine/28mag-nemtsov/28mag-nemtsov-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/28/magazine/28mag-nemtsov/28mag-nemtsov-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/28/magazine/28mag-nemtsov/28mag-nemtsov-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/28/magazine/28mag-nemtsov/28mag-nemtsov-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/02/28/magazine/28mag-nemtsov/28mag-nemtsov-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/28/magazine/28mag-nemtsov/28mag-nemtsov-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'After Boris Nemtsov’s Assassination, ‘There Are No Longer Any Limits’', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Assassinations and Attempted Assassinations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Investigative Committee (Russia)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Nemtsov, Boris Y', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Putin, Vladimir V', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romanova, Olga', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Yashin, Ilya', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Moscow (Russia)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Ukraine', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Russia', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-02-28T19:21:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Julia Ioffe', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Julia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ioffe', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/aa8624ef-ae3c-5f10-af50-eae1926a4242', 'word_count': 1504, 'uri': 'nyt://article/aa8624ef-ae3c-5f10-af50-eae1926a4242'}, {'abstract': 'Surreptitious monitoring of conversations did not begin with the revelations recounted in “Citizenfour,” but rather has long been conducted by the authorities, private detectives, armies and criminals.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/03/01/nyregion/a-short-history-of-wiretapping.html', 'snippet': 'Surreptitious monitoring of conversations did not begin with the revelations recounted in “Citizenfour,” but rather has long been conducted by the authorities, private detectives, armies and criminals.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Q. When “Citizenfour,” Laura Poitras’s film about Edward Snowden’s revelations of government electronic monitoring, won the Oscar for best documentary,', 'print_section': 'MB', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/03/01/nyregion/01FYI/01FYI-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 707, 'width': 500, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/03/01/nyregion/01FYI/01FYI-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 707, 'width': 500, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/03/01/nyregion/01FYI/01FYI-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/03/01/nyregion/01FYI/01FYI-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/03/01/nyregion/01FYI/01FYI-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Short History of Wiretapping', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Surveillance of Citizens by Government', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wiretapping and Other Eavesdropping Devices and Methods', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Police Department (NYC)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Citizenfour (Movie)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-02-28T19:26:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael Pollak', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pollak', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Question', '_id': 'nyt://article/05bde422-a58f-5cfc-8622-fa30f2e89d12', 'word_count': 502, 'uri': 'nyt://article/05bde422-a58f-5cfc-8622-fa30f2e89d12'}, {'abstract': 'A Jewish family whose son was killed feels betrayed.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/03/01/opinion/sunday/roger-cohen-did-israel-put-money-over-justice.html', 'snippet': 'A Jewish family whose son was killed feels betrayed.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ON April 17, 2006, a Palestinian suicide bomber killed 11 people near the old Tel Aviv bus station. Among the victims was Daniel Wultz, a bright and determined 16-year-old from Florida who fought for his life for 27 days before succumbing to severe injuries. His father, Yekutiel, who was wounded in the attack, watched the terrorist detonate himself. “I decided to do anything and everything I could,” he told me, “never again to have that helpless feeling.”', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/01/opinion/cohen-circular/cohen-circular-articleLarge-v2.png', 'height': 300, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/11/01/opinion/cohen-circular/cohen-circular-articleLarge-v2.png', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 300}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/01/opinion/cohen-circular/cohen-circular-jumbo-v4.png', 'height': 512, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/01/opinion/cohen-circular/cohen-circular-superJumbo-v4.png', 'height': 1000, 'width': 2000, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/01/opinion/cohen-circular/cohen-circular-thumbStandard-v4.png', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/11/01/opinion/cohen-circular/cohen-circular-thumbStandard-v4.png', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/01/opinion/cohen-circular/cohen-circular-thumbLarge-v6.png', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Did Israel Put Money Over Justice? ', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Columnist', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Did Israel Put Money Over Justice?', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wultz, Daniel Cantor (1989-2006)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cohen, Roger', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wultz, Yekutiel', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cantor Wultz, Sheryl', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Israel', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Netanyahu, Benjamin', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iran', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Suits and Litigation (Civil)', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Terrorism', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-02-28T19:27:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'subsection_name': 'Sunday Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Roger Cohen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Roger', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cohen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/2a8fb428-ddac-51cf-b68e-9d4d909308ce', 'word_count': 1579, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2a8fb428-ddac-51cf-b68e-9d4d909308ce'}, {'abstract': 'For the fall 2015 fashion show today, the makeup and hair artists created a decidedly un-girly look.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/02/28/pat-mcgrath-guido-palau-jil-sander-androgynous-beauty-milan-fashion-week/', 'snippet': 'For the fall 2015 fashion show today, the makeup and hair artists created a decidedly un-girly look.', 'lead_paragraph': 'While the fall/winter 2015 Jil Sander collection was splashed with vibrant patterns and electric pops of color, the makeup artist Pat McGrath and hair stylist Guido Palau kept things understated — and decidedly un-girly. “It’s an androgynous look,” McGrath told T today before the show. “It’s all about the brows.” To make them stand out, McGrath said she “put pencil and shadows into the brow and brushed them through for a natural feel.” The result was a clean look, which aligned nicely with Palau’s take on the hair, which he described as “boyish, simple, very minimal.” To get the uncomplicated style, Palau used Redken Satinwear 02 Prepping Blow-Dry Lotion to achieve a smooth blowout and Forceful 23 Super Strength Finishing Spray to keep the bangs in place. Finally, Wind Blown 05 Dry Finishing Spray completed the coiffure and added some texture. Palau said the completed look was quintessential Sander, embodying “masculine femininity” rather than “feminine femininity.” And to top it all off, Palau threw in a small quirk: “a bobby pin on the side to add a bit of charm.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/02/28/t-magazine/28bbr/28bbr-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 900, 'width': 600, 'sub