, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Perry, Rick', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Texas', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Pence, Mike', 'rank': 13, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Indiana', 'rank': 14, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-02-28T19:30:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'subsection_name': 'Sunday Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/3cd4afbd-07e4-5018-a0f1-4ffc09bb020c', 'word_count': 528, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3cd4afbd-07e4-5018-a0f1-4ffc09bb020c'}, {'abstract': 'Effective rules imposing a fiduciary duty on all retirement account advisers should quickly be put in place.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/03/01/opinion/sunday/protecting-fragile-retirement-nest-eggs.html', 'snippet': 'Effective rules imposing a fiduciary duty on all retirement account advisers should quickly be put in place.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A new study by the White House Council of Economic Advisers has found that financial advisers seeking higher fees and commissions drain $17 billion a year from retirement accounts by steering savers into high-cost products and strategies rather than comparable lower-cost ones. ', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/03/01/opinion/01sun3web/01sun3web-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 473, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/03/01/opinion/01sun3web/01sun3web-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 473}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/03/01/opinion/01sun3web/01sun3web-jumbo.jpg', 'height'