'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/9eb50446-f57c-520a-97f6-798df0e147ac', 'word_count': 359, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9eb50446-f57c-520a-97f6-798df0e147ac'}, {'abstract': 'Marcus Trappaud Bjorn, a freelance photographer from Copenhagen, created an award-winning series of portraits of passengers taking the Staten Island Ferry.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/03/01/nyregion/the-faces-on-the-ferry.html', 'snippet': 'Marcus Trappaud Bjorn, a freelance photographer from Copenhagen, created an award-winning series of portraits of passengers taking the Staten Island Ferry.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For many commuters, taking the Staten Island Ferry means that “you’re sitting on the ferry and can’t do anything,” Marcus Trappaud Bjorn observed. He speaks from experience.', 'print_section': 'MB', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Faces on the Ferry', 'kicker': 'Album', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Faces on the Ferry', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bjorn, Marcus Trappaud', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Photography', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Staten Island Ferry', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Transit Systems', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-02-28T19:42:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Corey Kilgannon', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Corey', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kilgannon', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/809af84f-ea1e-5b2d-9e21-10a546f80cc2', 'word_count': 469, 'uri': 'nyt://article/809af84f-ea1e-5b2d-9e21-10a546f80cc2'}, {'abstract': 'What was it about those late 1970s classes?', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2015/02/28/empire-of-the-institute/', 'snippet': 'What was it about those late 1970s classes?', 'lead_paragraph': 'Not long ago I received a copy of MIT and the Transformation of American Economics, a collection of essays on how American economics became model- and math-oriented after World War II, and of the special role played by the department Paul Samuelson built. There was a lot in there I didn’t know, despite the many years I spent at MIT first as a student, then as faculty. So I found it — as Spock would say — fascinating.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Empire of the Institute', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2015-02-28T19:42:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d9438e93-f1ba-596d-93f2-2fb1a59da253', 'word_count': 979, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d9438e93-f1ba-596d-93f2-2fb1a59da253'}, {'abstract': 'The House narrowly met a midnight deadline to continue funding the Department of Homeland Security, an embarrassment to Republican leadership, who will discuss it on the Sunday shows.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/politics/first-draft/2015/02/28/what-were-watching-sunday-shows-17/', 'snippet': 'The House narrowly met a midnight deadline to continue funding the Department of Homeland Security, an embarrassment to Republican leadership, who will discuss it on the Sunday shows.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Late Friday, the House passed a one-week extension of funding for the Department of Homeland Security, narrowly meeting its midnight deadline. The House had rejected an earlier version of the bill, which would have extended funding for three weeks, dealing a humiliating blow to the Republican leadership.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What We’re Watching: Sunday Shows', 'kicker': 'First Draft', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Boehner, John A', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Feinstein, Dianne', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McCarthy, Kevin (1965- )', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Perry, Rick', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Scalise, Steve', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Walker, Scott K', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Conservative Political Action Conference', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-02-28T19:48:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Elena Schneider', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Elena', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schneider', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ecd17adf-7e7f-57b2-a5c8-cc58859a8b84', 'word_count': 259, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ecd17adf-7e7f-57b2-a5c8-cc58859a8b84'}, {'abstract': 'Kevin Gleeson performs in a Rolling Stones tribute band and also works for the New York Police Department.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/03/01/nyregion/like-a-rolling-stone.html', 'snippet': 'Kevin Gleeson performs in a Rolling Stones tribute band and also works for the New York Police Dep