cle', 'news_desk': 'Letters', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Letter', '_id': 'nyt://article/d6b0c526-bbe3-573d-94f7-c27a7db92a03', 'word_count': 2079, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d6b0c526-bbe3-573d-94f7-c27a7db92a03'}, {'abstract': 'Re-entering the workplace after 20 years, a homemaker wages an uphill battle trying to teach anatomy and physiology to students in a beauty class.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/03/01/jobs/attack-of-the-student-hairdressers.html', 'snippet': 'Re-entering the workplace after 20 years, a homemaker wages an uphill battle trying to teach anatomy and physiology to students in a beauty class.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When my two eldest girls went off to college, I began to look for a part-time job. Through the grapevine, I heard of an opening for a part-time substitute teacher at a high school near home. I applied and was hired right away. What great good luck, I thought. Not only could I help pay my daughters’ tuition, but the job would be a nice transition back into the workplace after 20 years as a homemaker.', 'print_section': 'BU', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/03/01/business/1-ONWORKSUB/1-ONWORKSUB-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 413, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/03/01/business/1-ONWORKSUB/1-ONWORKSUB-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 413}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/03/01/business/1-ONWORKSUB/1-ONWORKSUB-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 705, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/03/01/business/1-ONWORKSUB/1-ONWORKSUB-superJumbo.jpg