oundational movie that helped establish the industry are rare.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/03/01/movies/d-w-griffith-a-new-perspective.html', 'snippet': 'Hollywood usually loves an anniversary, yet even in the centennial of “The Birth of a Nation,” theatrical screenings of this foundational movie that helped establish the industry are rare.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Hollywood usually loves an anniversary, yet even in the centennial of “The Birth of a Nation,” theatrical screenings of this foundational movie that helped establish the industry are rare. It’s no secret why: D. W. Griffith’s three-hour blockbuster of the Civil War and Reconstruction, while a giant leap forward for cinema, is also art in service to racist propaganda, promoting the Ku Klux Klan as defenders of the South from predatory freed blacks.\xa0 ', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/03/01/arts/01GUIDE1/01GUIDE1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 520, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/03/01/arts/01GUIDE1/01GUIDE1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 520}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/03/01/arts/01GUIDE1/01GUIDE1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 888, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/03/01/arts/01GUIDE1/01GUIDE1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1776, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/03/01/arts/01GUIDE1/01GUIDE1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/03/01/arts/01GUIDE1/01GUIDE1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/03/01/arts/01GUIDE1/01GUIDE1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'D. W. Griffith, A New Perspective ', 'kicker': 'The Week Ahead', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Film: D. W. Griffith, a New Perspective', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2015-02-28T21:32:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Daniel M. Gold', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Daniel', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4a7d51cf-ea7e-55a9-b293-412bc882da74', 'word_count': 158, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4a7d51cf-ea7e-55a9-b293-412bc882da74'}, {'abstract': 'The rigorous, even-toned Chicago clarinetist James Falzone takes the role of his instrument in the history of improvised music seriously.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2015/03/01/arts/music/six-clarinetists-in-a-circle.html', 'snippet': 'The rigorous, even-toned Chicago clarinetist James Falzone takes the role of his instrument in the history of improvised music seriously.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The rigorous, even-toned Chicago clarinetist James Falzone takes the role of his instrument in the history of improvised music seriously — and also the practice of balancing tight composition with open improvisation, extending outward from jazz into European classical and devotional traditions. He doesn’t come to New York often, and he comes to Roulette this week with a special new group, the Renga Ensemble, playing from a careful, bracing, provocative album, “The Room Is” (Allos Documents). It’s a set of pieces written for six clarinetists in a circle, with no rhythm section; it was inspired by renga, a centuries-old Japanese form of collaborative poetry, with a protocol to weave together individual voices into a coherent whole. The musicians on the record, and in the concert on Wednesday, are high-powered improvisers: Aside from Mr. Falzone, there’s Ned Rothenberg, Ken Vandermark, Keefe Jackson, Jason Stein and Ben Goldberg. Within the design of the compositions, each will get his say. (8 p.m., 509 Atlantic Avenue, Brooklyn, roulette.org.) ', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/03/01/arts/01GUIDE8/01GUIDE8-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 399, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/03/01/arts/01GUIDE8/01GUIDE8-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 399}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/03/01/arts/01GUIDE8/01GUIDE8-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 680, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/03/01/arts/01GUIDE8/01GUIDE8-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1361, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/03/01/arts/01GUIDE8/01GUIDE8-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/03/01/arts/01GUIDE8/01GUIDE8-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge